'I know I ought not to be here. The Kindred swore us away. I saw three of them though. They pulled their launches up on the shore and entered this tunnel with their crews. They went straight on ahead.

'I know I'm not supposed to be here, but I know a bit about the temple. I used to work a dock here in my younger days. If you need to get deeper into the ruins, I can help you.

'If you can tell me the last room you entered, I can show you a shortcut through the nearby tunnels.'

<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest tracks your progress for the Tier 5 difficulty of 'Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo'. While underway, it allows you to resume adventuring in 'Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo' at the furthest checkpoint you have reached in each reset cycle. Upon entering 'Depths of Mâkhda Khorbo', any player with this quest underway can open the door to take hidden tunnels to the furthest checkpointed progression. This quest will automatically reset every Thursday.</rgb>Artar Ildarthos asks you to break the Ordâkhai fortifications at Ghât Lor.Destroy fortifications at Ghât Lor. Ghât Lor can be found to the east of Vartúlin.Destroy fortifications at Ghât Lor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Artar Ildarthos at Vartúlin.Return to Artar Ildarthos at Vartúlin'We Kintai have a saying, outsider. "When the tree resists the wind, it is the wood that cracks, never the wind." We all must be in balance with nature, never resisting its flow. These southern Men - these Men of Ordâkh - they are always out of balance, destroying the natural way of things. They have built great fortifications at Ghât Lor, further destroying our forests and sometimes even using the husks of our sacred Veróthi to protect themselves.

'Break their fortifications, destroy this blasphemy against nature and the Kintai. It will weaken them, and may make them think twice before they again twist nature to their corrupted will. We Kintai know that when the tree resists the wind, it is the wood that cracks. It is past time these Men of Ordâkh learn the same.''The wood has broken and so, hopefully, has the spirit of the southern Men. It is a severe lesson, but one the Ordakhai must learn, sooner or later. My thanks for your efforts, ${PLAYER}. You are like the wind, guiding the natural way of things.'Defeat jackals (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Were you not set upon by wild dogs upon your journey to Jirush, traveller? These desert hounds have grown bold of late. Many a would-be visitor has found himself beset by jackals. If these fierce scavengers pose no threat to you, I would thank you for your aid in making these roads safe from the beasts.''I cannot recall the last I went for a stroll with my faithful companion here without fear of encountering a less-friendly hound! Thank you, brave adventurer. The sole dog I need see in the Khûd is this one beside me.'Defeat many jackals in Khûd Zagin.Defeat many jackals in Khûd Zagin.Defeat many jackals in Khûd ZaginDefeat a great many jackals in Khûd Zagin.Defeat many jackals in Khûd Zagin.Defeat a great many jackals in Khûd Zagin.Defeat a great many jackals in Khûd ZaginDefeat many jackals in Urash Dâr.Defeat many jackals in Urash Dâr.Defeat many jackals in Urash DârDefeat a great many jackals in Urash Dâr.Defeat many jackals in Urash Dâr.Defeat a great many jackals in Urash Dâr.Defeat a great many jackals in Urash DârUsakâr's favourite walking stick was taken from him by a marsh-strider in Zahûmakh. Recover the walking stick from the boorish marsh-striders.Recover Usakâr's favourite walking stick from a marsh-strider in Zahûmakh.Recover Usakâr's favourite walking stick from a marsh-strider in ZahûmakhRecover Usakâr's favourite walking stick from a marsh-strider in Zahûmakh.Recover Usakâr's favourite walking stick from a marsh-strider in ZahûmakhReturn to Usakâr near Dag Usakâra with the walking stick.Return to Usakâr near Dag Usakâra with the walking stick'For me? Why, yes, I suppose there is something you could do for me. My favourite walking stick was taken from me. Brutal thing. I was walking through the marshes south of here, when suddenly these marsh-striders appeared. Very rude chaps, wouldn't take no for an answer, and stripped me of my walking stick. I tried to tell them it was my favourite, but they weren't hearing it, for some reason.

'I would very much appreciate it if you would have a word with them. May be more likely to listen to you. Anyway, I was walking near Zahûmakh when I was accosted. I expect the stick is still there, possibly in the possession of one of those boorish marsh-striders.''Ah, there it is. Wherever did you find it? That's right, the marsh. I can tell from the smell. I think this just became my second favourite walking stick. Bit ripe, isn't it? Still, thank you for finding it.'Defeat many kergrim in Urash Dâr.Defeat many kergrim in Urash Dâr.Defeat many kergrim in Urash DârDefeat a great many kergrim in Urash Dâr.Defeat many kergrim in Urash Dâr.Defeat a great many kergrim in Urash Dâr.Defeat a great many kergrim in Urash DârPhâredar received a message from Keteph asking for assistance. You can find Keteph at the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl.Make your way to the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl and speak with Keteph. He requires assistance and thinks you are the person for the job.'Greeting, ${PLAYER}.

'It is good to see you again; auspicious as well. You see, just as the sun set yesterday, I received a missive from my patron, Keteph. Weeks of silence and then a wordy letter explaining that the aristocracy keeps him busy in Umbar Baharbêl.

'It seems that he needs assistance and he asked that I send you along if I saw you again. He took a liking to you and your thoroughness and knows well of the continued efforts you afforded him.

'You will find him in the Swain's Guild-hall in Umbar Baharbêl.''Ah, my friend, you arrive at the very moment of my need. I am pleased that Phâreda informed you of my plight.

'You see, my dishes continue to prove evocative and enticing to the discerning palette of the aristocrats in Umbar Baharbêl. This is good. I am busy and well-engaged, but they grow tired of a taste so quickly it does not long stay on their plates or in their minds. So I must constantly design new dishes for their consumption. This is why I request you visit me.

'I have a notion that requires another discerning individual, like yourself.'Amalíbi, pleased with your assistance, suggests there are still more in Shagâna to assist. While she would rather you remain in Khûd Zagin, she suggests moving on to Imhûlar to aid the Shagâna there.Amalíbi suggests you cross the Bridge of Danagír and seek Numûru. Numûru is the first lieutenant of a rising force who is rumoured among the Shagâna to be a warrior-queen of old reborn.'Whether you stay in Khûd Zagin or move onward, know your efforts in our land will be remembered and spoken of, as is our tradition.'

She pauses.

'For all you've done here, I wonder, will you do more for the Shagâna?

'To the east, in Imhûlar, a warlord rises above all others. She presses the enemy at Kûr Anzar and consolidates forces to her banner like a warrior-queen of old.

'She stirs the hearts of the oppressed, and I would go to her were I not pledged to avenge my fallen family.

'If you still seek to aid the Shagâna, go east across the Bridge of Danagír and find Numûru, first lieutenant to the woman who would unite us. He will welcome your aid.''We have heard of your exploits in Khûd Zagin. Are you here to lend your mettle to us now? If so, you are most welcome.'Your standing with the Adúrhid improves and earns you a gift from the Ikorbâni Elves.Your continued assistance with the goals and objective of the Kintai Elves earns you merit among them. They wish to honour your efforts with a gift at Shonith.Reach Kindred tier with the AdúrhidYour continued assistance with the goals and objective of the Kintai Elves earns you merit among them. They wish to honour your efforts with a gift at Shonith.Visit Thridarlan at Shonith to receive a giftYour continued efforts to aid the Kintai Elves brings great joy to them. You should visit Thridarlan at Shonith to receive a gift from the Elves of the oasis.'We are beyond calling you friend or ally. Were you of our blood we would call you family.

'Thank you for all you have done for the Adúrhid. Please, know this gift is given with the greatest grace we can call upon.'You continue to prove your valour, nerve, and measured assistance to the Hunter's Guild of Mûr Ghala.You must earn Kindred standing with the Hunter's Guild of Mûr GhalaYour standing among the Ikorbâni earns you a gift. Return to Kildûg at Iridír to claim your reward.You have honoured your word to assist the Ikorbâni in their efforts to restore their lands. You should return to Kildûg at Iridír to receive a reward for your continued assistance.Reach Kindred tier with the IkorbâniYou have honoured your word to assist the Ikorbâni in their efforts to restore their lands. You should return to Kildûg at Iridír to receive a reward for your continued assistance.Visit Kildûg at Iridír to claim a giftYour efforts to assist the Ikorbâni are noted among the people. To recognize your efforts, the leaders of the Shagâni at Iridír wish to honour you with a gift and thanks.'For all you have done for our people we are pleased to call you kindred. Your arrival brought us concern. Now we have seen the truthfulness of your words and the nobility of your spirit.

'We will thrive because of your assistance.

'Please, visit Nêkhur after choosing your gift.'You continue to prove your value, honesty, and measured assistance to the Kintai Elves of Ikorbân.You must earn Kindred standing with the KintaiYou continue to prove your value, honesty, and measured assistance to the Kintai Elves of Sul Madásh.You must earn Kindred standing with the Kintai of Sul MadáshYour standing among the Tale-wardens earns you a gift. Return to one of their members' quartermasters to be rewarded.Visit the Tale-warden Assistant, Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate, or any of the other Phetekâri quartermasters at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a gift from the Tale-wardens of Umbar.Reach Kindred tier with the PhetêkariVisit the Tale-warden Assistant, Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate, or any of the other Phetekâri quartermasters at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a gift from the Tale-wardens of Umbar.Visit Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate to claim your giftVisit a Tale-warden's assistant at Iridír, Jirush, or UrmâkhYour standing with the Phetekâri grows. You should visit one of their assistants at Telperiën's Gate, Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a well-earned gift.'I did not expect such engagement from the people of the North. You have proven an invaluable ally and resource to us.

'Please accept one of these gifts from Captain Rothog and speak with Shulêga for any other you may desire. I shall ensure your name is recognized throughout the Phetekâri.

'You are truly a kindred spirit.''Please accept one of these gifts from Captain Rothog and speak with a quartermaster for any other you may desire. I shall ensure your name is recognized throughout the Phetekâri.

'You are truly a kindred spirit.'Your continued efforts in Shagâna inform the Tale-wardens of the people, history, and tribulations of the land. The records of the Ikorbân Valley's history grow due to your efforts.You must earn Kindred standing with the Tale-wardens.Your continued efforts to support Shâra Mizâdi and her forces in Idagâl earn you greater favour with Hamât Renewed.You must earn Kindred standing with Hamât RenewedYour continued efforts to support Kighân earns you greater favour with the City of Zajâna.You must earn Kindred standing with the City of ZajânaYour continued efforts to support the Ikorbân Valley earn you greater favour with the Shagâni people.You must earn Kindred standing with the IkorbâniYour continued efforts to support An Shêru earns you greater favour with the Temámir of Jiret-menêsh.You must earn Kindred standing with the Temámir of Jiret-menêshSomeone has posted a task to collect pitted axes. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire pitted axes.Wanted: pitted axes from Umbar or the outer reaches of Gondor.Wanted: pitted axes from Umbar and the outer reaches of Gondor. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: pitted axes from Gondor. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Reach Level 30 with the Ledger-keepers: Umbar BarharbêlReach Level 30 with the Ledger-keepers: Umbar Barharbêl AllegianceYou have turned over every stone, discovered every encampment, and defeated every foe in the Umbar-môkh.Complete quests in the Umbar-môkh.Complete Slayer of the Umbar-môkhComplete Explorer of the Umbar-môkhComplete Tales of the Umbar-môkhDefeat Ordâkhai soldiers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'You are known to me through a particular shared network, wanderer, and I know the Ordâkhai are no friend of yours. I and my fellows grow wary of their patrols so near to our own. We true of the Khûd would welcome your assistance in limiting their hunting grounds.''The Ordâkhai continue to nip at our heels. Have you had much trouble ridding these wastes of their like? The sooner their numbers dwindle, the safer Ghalburu becomes.''It is not just I and my fighters that have noticed fewer Ordâkhai sniffing about our home. Our families, sick, injured, and children back home in Ghalburu have all felt relief from the yoke of their oppression. Thank you for sending those vile invaders a message that we will not accept their presence lying down.'Ildarthos, Artar of the remaining Adúrhid warriors in Vartúlin, has asked for your help in bringing peace to the many wrathful Curthádi at Róthirin.Bring peace by force to the restless Curthádi spirits at Róthirin.Defeat Curthádi at Róthirin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Report back to Artar Ildarthos at Vartúlin that you've brought peace to many Curthádi at Róthirin.Report back to Artar Ildarthos at Vartúlin'It grieves me greatly, but I have a task for you, outsider, if you're willing. There are many of our kind that cannot find peace, even in death. It is this forest, Favrathór, cursed as it has become. Wherever the Lâg Dávrit struck the Favrathór, Curthádi were borne out of that imbalance in nature. Curthádi are Adúrhid spirits of hatred and anger, who roam this land, never finding peace.

'It is the solemn duty of the Adúrhid warriors to bring peace by force to those among my kin who become Curthádi. You have helped Thórvilon greatly, and so you seem to be someone we Adúrhid can trust. I will be honest, I have so few warriors left - I cannot spare any currently to deal with the Curthádi. The southern Men make war on us. Ever has it been, and ever it will be. We cannot find peace. Yet our duty to the Curthádi remains.

'Will you go in my stead? This is a sacred duty I give to you. We are responsible for tending all of our dead, peaceful and otherwise. This extends even to the odious few who become Curthádi. Go to Róthirin - there the Pale Blight has corrupted the Veróthi of the grove, and many spirits of the grove have spilled out, angry and hateful, becoming Curthádi. Give them the final peace they deserve.''It is a hard thing, bringing peace to those who do not want it. Thank you for executing this duty in my stead. There is much that is out of balance in Favrathór this day. I must admit, I often long for the great boughs and peaceful green copses of the old Emerald Wood, of Laithór.'Cultists within Jâx Ugikh are said to have collected a series of befouled artifacts from the area. Locate these objects and destroy them.Seek out and destroy relics that are said to be corrupting the ground near Jâx Ugikh.Destroy corrupted relics (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Kên Taghlim and inform Azrât that the corrupted relics have been destroyed.Talk to Azrât in Kên Taghlim'While exploring the area, I noticed that the cultists near Jâx Ugikh seem to have some sort of objects that seem to be exuding corruptive energies. These corrupted relics might spread their influence throughout the region.

'Could you travel to Jâx Ugikh and destroy any of these objects that you find?''With these corrupted relics destroyed, the influence from these cultists will not spread further throughout the region. While it was dangerous work, you have made it safer for the denizens of this place.

'Thanks again for all of your help.'Amarêkh, one of the Temámir guards stationed in Mekab-kuphâr, has asked you to leave offerings of food for the "little spirits" throughout Khabârkhad.Amarêkh, one of the Temámir guards stationed in Mekab-kuphâr, has asked you to leave offerings of food for the "little spirits" throughout Khabârkhad. 

The first location is west of Mekab-kuphâr, near Sektakhâb, where the Dead walk.Leave food offerings near Sektakhâb (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The second location is north of Mekab-kuphâr, near Nishabêt, home of monstrous spiders.Leave food offerings near Nishabêt (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The third location is north-west of Mekab-kuphâr, near Lôkhalel, where tomb robbers keep their council.Leave food offerings near Lôkhalel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to the Temámir Guard Amarêkh in Mekab-kuphâr in southern Khabârkhad.Return to the Temámir Guard Amarêkh in Mekab-kuphâr'Could I have a moment of your time? I have a bit of a problem.'

The guard seems reticent to share her secret.

'It's, well, promise you won't laugh, will you?'

She leans in close to whisper something to you.

'It's the little spirits. Spirits of the dead. They've been coming after our patrols, throwing stones at our helmets, knocking our legs when we're not looking. It's bad for morale. Some of the guards are scared to patrol now, for fear the spirits will get more violent and do worse.

'I've been leaving food for them, little offerings over the past few weeks. It seems to have mollified them. But now I've been stationed here and I'm not to leave or go on patrols for a fortnight or more. I'm worried the spirits will start growing agitated. Could you leave food for them, in my stead?

'I know it seems a mite odd, but things have gotten more peaceful in the past few weeks. I can mark the locations down for you. Can you help?''Thank you. I know it seems strange, but I really do think the food helps. And anyway, someone is eating a little better because of us.'Raphûz and Ashâmi in Ub Nishir help to coordinate attacks against the myriad enemies in Urash Dâr. They are warriors now, having faced their fears and overcome the pressures of their past.Raphûz thanked you for your guidance and camaraderie through his journey. He aspires to be like you now. He added that you should speak with Ashâmi, also in Ub Nishir, as she wants to speak with you too.Speak with Ashâmi at her post near Raphûz in Ub NishirAshâmi credits you with making her a better person and guiding her and Raphûz into the relationship and fate they have chosen. Raphûz had mentioned you should return to him at Ub Nishir after speaking with Ashâmi.Speak with Raphûz at his post near Ashâmi in Ub Nishir'When we met, ${PLAYER}, I was a directionless young man. I expected to toil as a Tale-warden and fulfil the promise to my mother and father. I had no plan for my life. I was content in completing theirs.

'You opened my eyes in a way I did not know was possible. Your selflessness and fortitude is an example of how to live the fullest life.

'I intend to follow a path like yours. There is a threat here. Ashâmi and I can make a difference here.

'Speak with her and then return to me. I am finishing my gift to you.''I am pleased to see you again, ${PLAYER}.'

She shifts her weight.

'When I saw you come to our land, I feared you came as another subjugator.

'I witnessed your caring nature in rescuing Mashûli, and I began to think otherwise.

'All my life, I was told you, from the North, were all evil. A menace to the world set upon forcing us to kneel to your whims and blades.

'In a short time, you proved these tales to be lies.

'You are genuine and good. You are a teacher. You live your life for a purpose greater than you.

'I am a better person knowing you.'

She smiles.

'Raphûz and I are together because of you. We found our purpose. The evil growing around us will consume everything if people like you and us do not fight the swelling darkness.

'We will fight. I know you will.''We appreciate you, ${PLAYER}.

'Please, take this journal. It contains our discussions and adventures together across Shagâna.

'If you want to recall how we became allies and friends, all you need do is leaf through these pages and recall our journeys.

'Let us keep working together to make the world better for us all.

'Friend.'Kiga has asked that you find her expedition leader, Edâkhi, near the Falls of Ilûritu because she has yet to return to Ub Nishir.Kiga has asked you to search for the leader of her group, Edâkhi, near the Falls of Ilûritu.Search for Edâkhi near the Falls of IlûrituSpeak to Edâkhi and tell her that Kiga is worried about her.Speak with EdâkhiReturn to Kiga in Ub Nishir to the north of Maurûsh and let her know about Edâkhi.Return to Kiga in Ub Nishir'I have not seen you before, you must be the one of which Galâmka spoke?

'I am Kiga, and I ask for your help. I fear someone dear to me may be in danger. You see, I am part of an expedition group who has been researching the Falls of Ilûritu to the north, and searching for the river-maiden, Enârshan, who is said to reside there.

'When Utug-bûr opened, we fled from the Orcs roaming the land and came across Ub Nishir and Galâmka, who offered us safety.

'The leader of our expedition, Edâkhi, went back to our camp near the falls to retrieve our research that we had to leave behind. She has not yet returned and so I must ask that you travel to the falls and see if you can find her. I ask that you return to me with any discoveries you can, good or bad. I must know of her fate.''And who are you, ${CLASS}?'

Edâkhi looks at you and stands ready to fight, unsure if you are friend or foe as you explain that Kiga sent you.

'Ah, dear Kiga. I am glad you found me. Please return to Ub Nishir and tell her that I am safe. The Falls of Ilûritu are truly wondrous, and I wish to learn more of its secrets. As Kiga told you, we are searching for Enârshan, the river-maiden who is said to be here.

'I am only finishing what I can, then I will return when the roads are safe.''You have returned, and without Edâkhi.'

You explain to Kiga that you found Edâkhi at the camp near the falls and told her of Kiga's concerns. She said she will return to Ub Nishir when she can.

'Oh! What a true relief. I am so glad that she is safe. I can not thank you enough! We are all dedicated to our work, but there is a reason she is the leader of our group. So I will understand her needing to get all that she needs before returning.

'Again, thank you, ${CLASS}. A weight has been lifted and I will await Edâkhi's return.'Galâmka has asked you to retrieve supplies that were left behind in Maurush and bring them to Ub Nishir.Gather the lost supplies for Galâmka from within Maurûsh.Collect lost supplies in Maurûsh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Deliver the recovered supplies to Galâmka in Ub Nishir to the north of Maurûsh.'Ah, good, you have returned. There is still much I need to learn from the reports that you brought back. I have another task that needs your help, as we are beginning to run low on supplies in our camp here at Ub Nishir.

'I believe I know where we can get some more, but I warn you: it may be dangerous.

'When the Orcs flooded into Maurûsh and we were forced to flee, we left behind much of our stores. I believe that these stores remain intact, we only need someone to reclaim them. I ask for that someone to be you ${CLASS}. Go to these stores and bring back what supplies you can.''Were you able to find success in Maurûsh?'

You give the supplies you had recovered to Galâmka.

'Aha! You have! This will be a great relief for the people here. I thank you for this, ${CLASS}.

'If you wish to help more, I have made our plans with the information gathered from the scouting reports you retrieved. Return to me when you are ready and we can discuss them further.'Dashên has had a shipment of trade-goods stolen by bandits. He has asked for your help in getting them back.The bandits attacked the waggon along the Road of Riches to the east of Iridír. You should defeat the bandits in that area and recover the lost trade-goods.Defeat bandits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Recover stolen trade-goods (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated the bandits and recovered the stolen trade-goods. You should return to Iridír and speak to Dashên.'Hashtal-gûr, traveller. Tell me, are you looking for work? I have been waiting for a new shipment of trade-goods from the south. My carrier made it here, but the goods did not. He said he was waylaid by bandits on the road and was greatly outnumbered. He gave them the goods in exchange for his life. It was the right decision, but I still need my trade-goods back or I cannot pay my debts. Please, would you lend me your aid?

'He said he was stopped along the road between here and the Wrackwade to the east. I will pay you what I am able for their return.''The carrier said he was robbed along the road between here and the Wrackwade to the east. I will pay you what I am able for the return of my trade-goods.''Níkhu! My goods! Thank you so much ${PLAYER}, you have saved my business. I do hope peace is restored to Ambarûl soon. Many bandits are Ordâkhai deserters, and the sooner the Dumûri can make them leave, the better.'Meliri insists that no food should go to waste and has asked you to pick up any perfectly good oranges off of the ground before they can go bad.Meliri wants you to collect any perfectly good oranges you find lying on the ground. They are found in the orange groves of Burukíri in Ambarûl.Collect perfectly good oranges (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You collected the perfectly good oranges you found lying on the ground. You should return to Meliri at Burukíri in Ambarûl.'Say, while you are out there running about the orange trees, there is another useful thing you could be doing. Sometimes oranges fall off of the trees before we are able to harvest them. If you get them off the ground quickly enough, they are still perfectly good. No food should be left to go to waste. If you see any perfectly good oranges on the ground, pick them up, will you? I will pay you for the work, of course.''If you dally too long, those perfectly good oranges will not be so good anymore!''You see, these oranges are perfectly good! Nothing wrong with them at all. Some may be a little ugly, but it all tastes the same. It is good they will not go to waste. Thank you for your hard work.'Shukûri in the Gorge of Woe has asked you to help her with thinning the number of wasps and sandstorms in the area.Shukûri has asked you to thin the numbers of wasps and sandstorms within the Gorge of Woe.Defeat Urâshi sandstorms (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Urâshi wasps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Shukûri in the Gorge of Woe and let her know that you have thinned the number of enemies in the area.Return to Shukûri'If you can spare the effort, I could use your help to clear out the Gorge of Woe.

'I am making my preparations to leave this place, and the path is no longer safe now that it has become infested with dangers. I ask that you rid the area of the wasps and sandstorms that reside here while I finish what I must do.''I see you have returned from the Gorge of Woe.

'I thank you for your help with this, ${CLASS}. My journey is now much safer because of your actions this day. I must finish my preparations now as I have a long road ahead.'Tibira has need of someone to travel to Ambarûl and make a trade for her.Tibira has asked you to take her copper ingot to Dashên at Iridír in Ambarûl and trade it for fresh produce.Tibira has asked you to take her copper ingot to Dashên at Iridír in Ambarûl and trade it for fresh produce. You should talk to Dashên.Talk to DashênYou have traded Tibira's copper ingot to Dashên at Iridír in Ambarûl for fresh produce. You should return to Tibira at Western Khanâg in Khûd Zagin with the crate.'If you are available, I am in need of someone who can brave the roads. As you can see, we do not have much in the way of farmland here. Most fruits and vegetables must be imported from other areas through trade.

'Take this copper bar to Iridír. It is in Ambarûl, to the north, across the Ikorbân. Find the man called Dashên, and give him the copper bar for as much fresh produce as he will give for it, and then return here.

'I hope you will do this, as you would not only be helping my business but also helping my customers have access to a variety of foods.''Hashtal-gûr! Back again, are we?'

You tell Dashên that you are trading on behalf of Tibira in Western Khanâg and would like to buy produce.

'One moment!''${PLAYER}, you have the produce?'

You give her the crate.

'Dashên was kind to us today. It seems copper is fetching a fine price. Thank you for your help once again.'Dashên takes the copper ingot and hands you a crate loaded with a generous variety of fruits, vegetables, nuts, and a jar of honey.

'There we are. Give Tibira my thanks for her business.'Sûlmur has offered to walk you through making papyrus.Collect reeds from the pile across the yard at Mehêtur, and bring them to the workbench.Pick up a pile of papyrus reedsYou have a pile of papyrus reeds. Take them to the workbench, remove the green skin, and cut them into strips.Use the workbench to prepare the reedsYou have peeled the papyrus and cut the inside of the reeds into thin strips. Now you should weave them together at the workbench.Use the workbench to weave the strips togetherYou have woven the papyrus strips together. The next step is to press them under a heavy weight.Use the workbench to press the woven reeds under a weightYou have completed all the steps of making papyrus. You should talk to Sûlmur.Talk to Sûlmur'I have stacked some reeds on the other side of the yard. Pick up a bundle and bring it to the workbench. First, you will use a knife to remove the green skin and then slice the inside of the reed into thin strips. Next, weave the strips together in a crosshatch pattern. Once that is done, with cloth on either side, the papyrus is pressed beneath a heavy weight.

'Do you think you will remember all that? Get to it!''Skilfully done! However, I must admit that if you return in three days you will not have usable papyrus. Once cut, the strips of reeds need to be soaked in water for three days to release the gum in the fibres that allow the papyrus to stick together. Your papyrus will fall apart.'

She gives you an amused laugh.

'But now you know how it is made. You are not angry, I hope.'Mark weaknesses in Jirush's walls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'You have labelled that many, eh? Well, it is not near so many as I had feared, but certainly more than I had hoped. I suppose I should thank you for this. I may be busy, but someone like you, well.... You are doubtless occupied with your tasks, too. Thank you for helping make this ragged city safer.'Zamína wishes to write a song honouring people who have fallen in the assaults led by Bârshud II. She would like your help in gathering stories from displaced warriors and citizens nearby.Zamína wishes to write a song honouring people who have fallen in the assaults led by Bârshud II. She would like your help in gathering stories from displaced warriors and citizens nearby.Gather stories for Zamína (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Zamína with the stories you have gathered from the people in Iridír.'Hello, ${CLASS}. I am sure you have heard of the assaults led by that monster, Bârshud II, here in Ambarûl.

'I wish to help however I can, but my talents are in music. I would like to write a melody to honour the fallen and the injured. Can I ask you to help me speak with people here who have been displaced and try to gather their stories? I can use the tales they tell craft my song.''These stories are heart-breaking, but will be valuable in my work.

'I thank you for your help. I will now do my best to craft a song worthy of these words to properly honour them.'The wheelwright, Aranbir, says he will make time to fix Khâmi's wheel if you fill in for his absent apprentice.Aranbir has asked you to go to the crafter's wharf in Iridír and bring him a sack of coal that can be found near the oven.Collect a sack of coal and bring it to AranbirYou have brought Aranbir the sack of coal for which he asked. You should talk to him to learn of your next task.Talk to AranbirAranbir has asked you to go to the fishing dock in Iridír, find a tub of water, and return with it in hand.Bring a tub of water to AranbirYou have brought Aranbir the tub of water for which he asked. You should talk to him to learn of your next task.Talk to AranbirAranbir has sent you on one last errand for him - to pick up his lunch. You should talk to Endunâm the cook on the crafter's wharf in Iridír.Talk to EndunâmYou have gotten lunch from Endunâm. You should bring it to Aranbir.'Getting to this wheel should not be difficult if I have meaningful help. The first thing I need is more coal to stoke the fire. There is a stockpile of coal on the crafter's wharf near the cooks' oven. Go there and bring a sack of coal to me.''I need more coal to stoke the fire. Bring me coal from the stockpile on the crafter's wharf, near the oven.''Very good. Thank you for the coal. Next, I need more water for quenching the iron. You should be able to get a tub of water from the fishing dock.''Fetch me a tub of water from the fishing dock. I will need it to quench the iron.''Thank you for the water. It looks like hardly any of it was spilt. Impressive. The last task I have for you is the most important. Go to Endunâm and pick up my lunch. I am less productive when I am hungry.''Go to Endunâm and pick up my lunch.''Oh, hoi! What is this, Aranbir sent you to get him some lunch? Ah yes, a man cannot work on an empty stomach!'

Endunâm puts together a plate of food and hands it to you.

'There you are. No nibbling! Buy your own if you are hungry.''Lunch! The highlight of my day. Other than breakfast and supper, anyway. Thank you so much for helping me today. While you were gone I repaired your wheel. It is sitting just there by the hut. Help yourself.'Bâdarul has requested that you assist in delivering letters explaining their loss to the families of soldiers who have fallen in battle here in Iridír.Bâdarul has requested that you assist in delivering letters explaining their loss to the families of soldiers who have fallen in battle here in Iridír.Return to Bâdarul in Iridír and let him know that you have given the letters to the grieving families.Return to Bâdarul in Iridír'I am glad to see you. We have suffered losses here in Iridír from the assault led by Bârshud II and now the families must be informed.

'These letters contain the news as well as personal sentiments for the ones affected. I know it will not be enough but we have to at least be sure they know what happened to their loved ones.

'Would you assist me in delivering them? I do not feel I can take them myself as I need to grieve for the loss as they were all beloved friends and I can not face their families yet.''I trust you have delivered the terrible news to the families. I hope that they are able to find peace.

'Thank you for your help, ${PLAYER}. I will not forget this act of kindness.'Raphûz was invited to speak with Igbâl. He asked you to attend the meeting with him for support.Raphûz asked you to meet him at Igbâl's home in Jirush. He is to meet the merchant for his role in Ardub's rescue.Make your way to Igbâl's home in JirushWhen you arrived at Igbâl's home, it appeared that Raphûz was engaged in conversation with the man. Galamê, Igbâl's translator, summoned you to speak with him.Speak with Galamê at Igbâl's home in JirushGalamê asked if you knew Raphûz's intent and suggested he needed to speak with Igbâl. Galamê then suggested you speak with Raphûz.Speak with Raphûz at Igbâl's home in JirushAfter speaking with Raphûz, Galamê motioned and called for you to return and speak with him at Igbâl's home in Jirush.Speak with Galamê at Igbâl's home in JirushAshâmi watched with great interest as you spoke with Galamê and Raphûz spoke with her father, Igbâl. She motioned you to come speak with her at her father Igbâl's home in Jirush.Speak with Ashâmi at Igbâl's home in JirushAshâmi asked you to dissuade Raphûz from whatever path her father, Igbâl, set him upon. She is concerned that the young man will be slain attempting whatever task her father set before him. She wants you to speak with Raphûz.Speak with Raphûz at Igbâl's home in JirushRaphûz did not want to discuss what Igbâl asked of him at his home. He requested that you return to his camp in Jirush and speak to him there.Speak with Raphûz at his camp in Jirush'My friend, you met with this man, his family, and the translator. You have been by my side for much of my journey. I ask you to join me again. I could use your support.

'Meet me at Igbâl's home in Jirush so we can see what he offers.

'Yes?''Your friend is curious, ${PLAYER}. He speaks with a passion about Ashâmi, Igbâl's youngest daughter. He regaled us with a tale of saving her deer and acquiring gifts you and he collected.

'He asked to court Ashâni. Did you know of this?'

You explain what you know.

'Very well. Speak with your friend. I must explain all this to Igbâl.'Raphûz looks a bit shaken.

'Am I showing how nervous I am, my friend?

'I told the translator everything: your assistance, my reasoning for asking more of you. He looked at me incredulously and said we should wait for your arrival. What did he ask?'

You explain that you confirmed Raphûz's story.

'Thank you.'Raphûz attends Lord Igbâl as you speak with Galamê.

'Know this, Lord Igbâl intends to send Raphûz to a place of great terror in Khûd Zagin. He will send him to Nirgambâr. The Dead have walked there for years. Until recently, they dwelled only within the halls of the great tombs. Something changed in the past few months that draws them from the tombs onto the sands. Your friend should be wary.'Ashâmi looks over your shoulder as she speaks.

'What is this fool doing? My father will get him killed. Reason with him and turn him from whatever path my father sets before him.

'Do it quickly. I will not let Raphûz's blood stain my hands.'Before you can protest and speak on Ashâmi's behalf, Raphûz holds up a hand and quietly states, 'Not here, my friend. Meet me back at my encampment.''I am to prove my value to Ashâmi's father by collecting a treasure from the Tombs of Nirgambâr. It does not sound like a place one should trespass into lightly.'

You explain the warnings from Galamê and Ashâmi.

'A warning, yes. Do you see? Her protest is also an admission that she cares. I shall think on this.'To the South, the Nêpharai have made a small encampment known as Harkhaphâr. The Nêpharai possess supplies that have been taken from Hulzidâr. Enter the camp and reclaim these supplies.The Nêpharai have stolen needed supplies from Hulzidâr. Travel south to Harkhaphâr, locate the supplies, and reclaim them.Gather supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return the supplies to Bâkhadir, located just north of Harkhaphâr.Talk to Bâkhadir outside of the camp'A short time ago, several former gladiators attempted an uprising here, and when that failed, fled to Harkhaphâr. These Nêpharai stole supplies and have been intercepting supply shipments from the south. 

'They chose to betray our encampment because we took in Rothog's people, and those who sought protection from the dangers of the catacombs.

'Could you travel to Harkhaphâr, secure these much needed supplies, and return them to Bâkhadir, who is located outside of the camp.''Ah good! These supplies should allow our people to survive for several months.  Your work will lessen the suffering of the refugees that we protect.'Ashâmi desires to rid herself of her father and Raphûz wants to help her achieve her independence as a way to prove to her that his missteps were only due to his not understanding the culture.Ashâmi accepted Raphûz's apology and seems genuinely concerned about him. She asked you to speak with him while she prepares a message for her father.Ashâmi asked that you speak with Raphûz at ShonithRaphûz suggests an alternate plan and wants you to share it with Ashâmi. He asked you to speak to her at the oasis Shonith.Speak with Ashâmi at the oasis of ShonithAshâmi realized what Raphûz delivering the message to her father would mean. She accepted the offer. You should return to Raphûz at the oasis Shonith and inform him.Speak with Raphûz at the oasis ShonithRaphûz plans to deliver the Aladi head to Igbâl at the merchant's home in Jirush. He asked you to meet him there to bear witness and to support the ruse he and Ashâmi concocted.Make your way to Igbâl's home in JirushYou arrived at Igbâl's home after Raphûz delivered the news of Ashâmi and provided the "proof" of the Alad's death. The mood is somber. Galamê stands ready to speak with you.Speak with the translator, Galamê, at Igbâl's home in JirushGalamê explained that Igbâl believes his daughter is dead and that you and Raphûz avenged her death by slaughtering the Alad. The ruse was successful. Raphûz waits for you to speak with him at Igbâl's home.Speak with Raphûz at Igbâl's home in JirushRaphûz said Igbâl cited portents in the sky and on the earth that reinforced the story you shared. He wants you to return to Shonith to tell Ashâmi what occurred.Talk to Ashâmi in Shonith'I admit I was impressed by how well you and Raphûz handled yourselves against the Alad.

'Not many keep their sanity who encounter the fabled Shagâni demons. Perhaps there is more to him, and you than I expect.

'I am preparing the head and a message for my father. I spoke with Raphûz. He is sincere in his apology.

'I will speak with him more when I complete this task. Can you comfort him? He looks like a jackal pup in search of its mother.''A jackal pup?

'She's goading me.'

He looks in Ashâmi's direction.

'Even now, she glances at us and smirks. What does it mean, friend?'

He shakes his head.

'The Aladi head may show that she is free of its power, but if her father believes she is alive he will pursue her, no?'

He thinks.

'My friend, tell her we will take the head to her father. See how she reacts.''Raphûz would take the head?'

She smirks.

'Capable and not squeamish. These are good qualities to have.

'Tell me, for what purpose? I wish to confront my father directly and burn the foolish notions and superstitions from him.

'If I am not present-'

She stops mid-sentence.

'He will think me dead. He will keep his superstitions, but I will be free to pursue my fate. Let us add wisdom to the qualities Raphûz possesses.

'Very well. Deliver the head to Raphûz and tell him to return to Jirush and gain an audience with my father.

'He saves me the strain of writing half-learned letters to Igbâl.''Raphûz seems full of surprises. I will not forget his gesture. Though I know my father will mourn my loss and believe my spirit transferred into some desert beast, it is better he not be shamed by my outward rejection of his parentage.

'Raphûz is wise and good.''She understood the subtext of my concern without exposition. We are very much alike and also very different.'

He sighs.

'Do not lecture me on the little cruelty this does to the man. It is no worse than caging a bird meant to fly free. One may cause a short period of sorrow, the other a lifetime.

'I will take her package to Jirush and spin a tale of my own for her father.'

He claps you on the shoulder.

'Meet me there, and we shall see how well it went, friend.''You arrive at a sober moment, ${PLAYER}. Your friend Raphûz informed my lord, Igbâl, of your victory over the Alad that took his daughter.

'He takes comfort in the desert demon's demise and mourns the loss of his youngest.

'He believes her spirit is in the newborn fawn her fallow deer birthed this morning. He believes you and Raphûz were meant to avenge his daughter and is grateful you pursued her.

'Raphûz has awaited your arrival.''Have you delivered the message to my father yet? Please, make haste. He almost never leaves his home in Jirush. You will find him there.'Raphûz offers a weak smile as you approach.

'It is strange, ${PLAYER}. Igbâl shed no tears. He mentioned a sign he witnessed in the sky last evening and the birth of the fawn this morning as proof to corroborate my tale.

'It is as if he would prefer her to be dead than suffer the ignominy of being defied.'

He chuckles.

'Or I weave such a compelling tale the man had no choice but to believe. We should return to Shonith and share our news.''As I said before, my father's beliefs are profound.'

She manages a smile.

'Raphûz recounted the tale. It was a good story. I fought against the demon and nearly won. You both arrived to find the Alad gravely wounded, rending my body to restore itself. Together, you levied blows against it until it stirred no more.

'You took the head. Alas, there was nothing left of me.

'Raphûz said my father accepted his words, cited portents he had seen, and called a fawn a sign of my rebirth.

'I am freed to my fate, thanks to you both.'Edâkhi has asked you to help her investigate the Falls of Ilûritu for signs of Enârshan, the river-maiden.Edâkhi has asked you to look for clues to Enârshan's whereabouts near along the river.Discover clues along the river (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Look for additional clues to Enârshan's whereabouts along the river for Edâkhi.Discover additional clues along the river (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Look for clues to Enârshan's whereabouts near the waterfall for Edâkhi.Discover additional clues near the Falls of Ilûritu (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Edâkhi and tell her about what you have learned about the river-maiden, Enârshan.Return to Edâkhi with what you learned'Greetings, adventurer. What brings you to the Falls of Ilûritu?

'I am here to recover research from my expedition group that we had to leave behind when we fled from the Orcs.

'We are searching for signs of Enârshan. The Idâmi, or river-maiden as you may say, who is said to dwell within the Ilûritu waterfall. Many men and women have perished seeking her. They are said to be drawn by her song and vanish somewhere within the falls.

'I wish to finish what research I can while I am here and I would be very grateful for your help if you can spare the time.

'Would you travel to the falls to the north-west and see if you can discover any signs of Enârshan? I will remain here and scour our notes for anything of use.''I am glad for your return. What were you able to find?'

You tell Edâkhi about the large footprints you found along the river and at the base of the waterfall.

'Ah! It seems you have found true signs of the Idâmi! Our research was correct!

'These footprints you describe sound as though they could not belong to any Man and lead to the waterfall of Ilûritu? That is what the tales speak of, but we could not find a dwelling around the falls.

'I must take some time to read over our research again with this new information. Please return when you can... and thank you for your help.'We have discovered a dangerous cult of usan-kûni worshippers hiding in our own back-yard. They call themselves Anâkhi, and have made their home inside Ashunûg, a salt mine in northern Ambarûl that has long been abandoned. We are only recently freed of Sauron, the All-seeing, and must not allow this new cult to take hold. The Anâkhi scorpion worshippers must be driven from our lands.Complete 'Ashunûg, the Fane of the Accursed -- Tier 1'Complete 'Ashunûg, the Fane of the Accursed -- Tier 2'Complete 'Ashunûg, the Fane of the Accursed -- Tier 3'Complete 'Ashunûg, the Fane of the Accursed -- Anâkhi'A hungry dog whines and begs at Zidek's butcher shop.Zidek is trying to send the hungry dog away. You should talk to Zidek.Talk to ZidekZidek tried sending the hungry dog away, but you took pity upon the animal and bought some meat for the dog. You should give it to him.Give food to the hungry dogYou have given meat you bought from Zidek to the hungry stray and can see that he is a gentle and intelligent dog. You should give him some pats.Give the dog a <rgb=#00FF00>pat</rgb>.You have given meat you bought from Zidek to the hungry stray and can see that he is a gentle and intelligent dog. Afterward, you gave the good dog some pats that did not go unappreciated. You should talk to Zidek.Talk to ZidekZidek said he would feed the dog if he serves as the protector and companion of Ubdun the goatherd. He has pointed to a large, juicy steak on the table, and asked you to take it and see if the dog will follow you to Ubdun.Carry the steak to Ubdun outside JirushThe dog has followed you, or rather the steak, to Ubdun's location, near Jirush. You should talk to Ubdun.Talk to UbdunThe dog is whining, staring at the meat Zidek has for sale.

'Off with you, you pest!'

Zidek looks about, presumably for something to throw at the dog.You hold the meat out to the dog, and he takes it from you, careful not to bite your hand. He wags his tail and continues to lick your hand long after the food is gone.'That accursed beast has been coming around a lot lately. I have no meat to spare on a beggar, much less a beggar that is a mangy cur.'

You look at the dog who has soft, sad eyes, and he doesn't look like a mangy cur to you. You ask the butcher if you can buy some meat for the dog.

'Well.. as long as it is paid for.'

You pay him and he reluctantly gives you some meat.You can see that the expression in Zidek's eyes has softened since he watched you interact with the hungry stray dog.

'You know, now that I think about it, it is possible I can spare some meat for the beast. If he works for it, that is. It seems that Ubdun could use a companion and protector while herding the goats, and this fellow looks like he needs a companion in addition to something to eat.

'Here, take that steak on the table and see if the dog will follow you to Ubdun.''What a wonderful idea! Zidek is so kind and smart. This is the perfect solution. No brigand dare attack me now! It will be good to have both a protector and a new friend. Thank you once again ${PLAYER}, for everything you have done. For all of us.'Mizâdi has asked that you speak with residents of Urmâkh to help with their daily needs.Mizâdi has asked that you speak with residents of Urmâkh to help with their needs. Specifically, she's asked you speak with Girnada, Mushêndu, Entârshul and Nukûsh in Urmâkh.Speak with Girnada, Quartermaster of UrmâkhSpeak with Mushêndu, a farmer in UrmâkhSpeak with EntârshulSpeak with Nukûsh, Blacksmith of UrmâkhReturn to Mizâdi in Urmâkh now that you have heard the needs of the people of Urmâkh.Speak with Mizâdi in Urmâkh'Hashtal-gûr, outsider. I am Mizâdi, Shâra of Renewed Hamât.

'You come at a fortuitous time. There is much to do here in Urmâkh, but my gaze is fixed on Kûr Anzar. It was there that my forces and many innocents were driven out recently by the forces of the All-seeing, those accursed Barkhûshim, false prophets to a dead lord. Many were killed or captured in the battle, including my husband, Eshtali. I will see them driven from Kûr Anzar, and they will drown in the river of blood I spill from them.

'But with my focus there, the people of Urmâkh here have many every day concerns with which I am unable to assist. You should talk with some of the locals if you wish to help. Recently Girnada, Mushêndu, Entârshul and Niriga have all come to me with concerns. Go and hear their concerns. If you wish to help me, help them.''Mizâdi sent you? I'm glad someone is listening to my concerns, even if it is a lûbara. Yes, we have a real problem feeding everyone here in Urmâkh, particularly with the influx from Kûr Anzar. We need more food and provisions, and quickly.''Hashtal-gûr, friend. Yes, there is something concerning to me. Our local well, right over there. The well has run dry, we are unable to draw water from it. And without the well, we don't have a good local source of water. Residents must trek many miles to the river, encountering all manner of beast and dangers to obtain water now.''Thank you. Mizâdi is kind, as are you, to think of us with so many other troubles befalling us. I care for the local children while the rest of the town works. I wonder if you could help me by calling the children in for their meal?''Ehh? Speak up now! You want to help? About time someone did. My apprentice has left to aid the war effort for Mizâdi. I could use all the help I can get. You can gather some ore and wood for the forge to start.''Thank you. I trust I can expect you to follow up with their tasks and help as you are able. As for me, we have need of those with bravery and talent in the fight to retake Kûr Anzar. I have a task that is well suited to someone of your talents.'Your continued efforts to support Shâra Mizâdi and her forces in Idagâl earn you favour with Hamât Renewed.You must earn Neutral standing with Hamât RenewedYour continued efforts to support Mûr Ghala earns you greater favour with the City of Zajâna.You must earn Neutral standing with the City of ZajânaYou continue to prove your valour, nerve, and measured assistance to the Hunter's Guild of Mûr Ghala.You must earn Neutral standing with the Hunter's Guild of Mûr GhalaYour continued efforts to support the Ikorbân Valley earn you greater favour with the Shagâni people.You must earn Neutral standing with the IkorbâniYou continue to prove your value, honesty, and measured assistance to the Kintai Elves of Ikorbân.You must earn Neutral standing with the KintaiYou continue to prove your value, honesty, and measured assistance to the Kintai Elves of Sul Madásh.You must earn Neutral standing with the Kintai of Sul MadáshYour continued efforts to support An Shêru earns you greater favour with the Temámir of Jiret-menêsh.You must earn Neutral standing with the Temámir of Jiret-menêshExplore enemy camps, settlements, and lairs in Adagím in Mûr Ghala.Explore enemy camps, settlements, and lairs in Adagím in Mûr Ghala.Find HordíridFind Thor LhîgFind HadrudádFind OgultáthFind DathrudúshFind NarcháshFind Thalat TîrFind the Pits of ChortáthFind MautharkFind Mokh GrazádhFind LhámuthFind the Lair of the ShadlúgaiFind Saig HathílFind Fushaum SûlmSlay many Ordâkhai foes throughout Mûr Ghala.Slay many Ordâkhai foes throughout Mûr Ghala.Complete Ordâkhai-bane of Kighân (Advanced)Complete Ordâkhai-bane of An Shêru (Advanced)Complete Ordâkhai-bane of Idagâl (Advanced)Defeat restless dead within Nirgambâr, the Restless Tomb.Defeat restless dead within Nirgambâr, the Restless Tomb.Defeat the restless dead within NirgambârIn a sheltered valley in the north of Khûd Zagin stand ancient, crumbling ziggurat-tombs of pale stone collectively known as Nirgambâr. Scouts have reported that one of the Zidemel's men, Andur, is said to have entered Nirgambâr drawn there by dark whispers. Locate and stop Andur before he can unleash what lurks in this cursed place.Explore the ancient, crumbling ziggurat-tombs of pale stone known as Nirgambâr. Follow Andur's path deeper within the ancient tomb.Defeat SakhârshagAndur's path leads you deeper into Nirgambâr. Who knows what might lie in wait next?Defeat Imanak-tûrTravelling deeper within Nirgambâr has revealed several ancient creatures. Who or what lies in the central chamber?Defeat AratûgIn a sheltered valley in the north of Khûd Zagin stand ancient, crumbling ziggurat-tombs of pale stone collectively known as Nirgambâr. Scouts have reported that one of the Zidemel's men, Andur, is said to have entered Nirgambâr drawn there by dark whispers. Locate and stop Andur before he can unleash what lurks in this cursed place.Explore the ancient, crumbling ziggurat-tombs of pale stone known as Nirgambâr. Follow Andur's path deeper within the ancient tomb.Defeat SakhârshagAndur's path leads you deeper into Nirgambâr. Who knows what might lie in wait next?Defeat Imanak-tûrTravelling deeper within Nirgambâr has revealed several ancient creatures. Who or what lies in the central chamber?Defeat AratûgIn a sheltered valley in the north of Khûd Zagin stand ancient, crumbling ziggurat-tombs of pale stone collectively known as Nirgambâr. Scouts have reported that one of the Zidemel's men, Andur, is said to have entered Nirgambâr drawn their by dark whispers. Locate and stop Andur before he can unleash what lurks in this cursed place.Complete 'Nirgambâr, the Restless Tomb -- Tier 1'In a sheltered valley in the north of Khûd Zagin stand ancient, crumbling ziggurat-tombs of pale stone collectively known as Nirgambâr. Scouts have reported that one of the Zidemel's men, Andur, is said to have entered Nirgambâr drawn there by dark whispers. Locate and stop Andur before he can unleash what lurks in this cursed place.Explore the ancient, crumbling ziggurat-tombs of pale stone known as Nirgambâr. Follow Andur's path deeper within the ancient tomb.Defeat SakhârshagAndur's path leads you deeper into Nirgambâr. Who knows what might lie in wait next?Defeat Imanak-tûrTravelling deeper within Nirgambâr has revealed several ancient creatures. Who or what lies in the central chamber?Defeat AratûgIn a sheltered valley in the north of Khûd Zagin stand ancient, crumbling ziggurat-tombs of pale stone collectively known as Nirgambâr. Scouts have reported that one of the Zidemel's men, Andur, is said to have entered Nirgambâr drawn their by dark whispers. Locate and stop Andur before he can unleash what lurks in this cursed place.Complete 'Nirgambâr, the Restless Tomb -- Tier 2'In a sheltered valley in the north of Khûd Zagin stand ancient, crumbling ziggurat-tombs of pale stone collectively known as Nirgambâr. Scouts have reported that one of the Zidemel's men, Andur, is said to have entered Nirgambâr drawn there by dark whispers. Locate and stop Andur before he can unleash what lurks in this cursed place.Explore the ancient, crumbling ziggurat-tombs of pale stone known as Nirgambâr. Follow Andur's path deeper within the ancient tomb.Defeat SakhârshagAndur's path leads you deeper into Nirgambâr. Who knows what might lie in wait next?Defeat Imanak-tûrTravelling deeper within Nirgambâr has revealed several ancient creatures. Who or what lies in the central chamber?Defeat AratûgIn a sheltered valley in the north of Khûd Zagin stand ancient, crumbling ziggurat-tombs of pale stone collectively known as Nirgambâr. Scouts have reported that one of the Zidemel's men, Andur, is said to have entered Nirgambâr drawn their by dark whispers. Locate and stop Andur before he can unleash what lurks in this cursed place.Complete 'Nirgambâr, the Restless Tomb -- Tier 3'In a sheltered valley in the north of Khûd Zagin stand ancient, crumbling ziggurat-tombs of pale stone collectively known as Nirgambâr. Scouts have reported that one of the Zidemel's men, Andur, is said to have entered Nirgambâr drawn their by dark whispers. Locate and stop Andur before he can unleash what lurks in this cursed place.Complete 'Nirgambâr, the Restless Tomb -- Tier 3'Sigênik sent you to Nangar, who, in turn, directs you to assist the other Elders of Jirush to gain their trust and respect.Sigênik directed you to return to Nangar. You will likely need to assist Nangar with some tasks involving the other elders in Jirush to ensure your trustworthiness to the outpost.Find and speak with Nangar in JirushNangar asked you to work with the other elders in Jirush to gain their favour and respect. You are to visit Zidemel, Malgat, and Igbâl and undertake whatever assistance they require.Complete all the requests Zidemel has for youComplete all the requests Malgat has for youComplete all the requests Igbâl has for youHaving completed all the requests for the elders in Jirush you should return to Nangar at his home and tell him of all you have done. Nangar's home is south-west of the northern entrance to Jirush.Speak with Nangar at his home in Jirush'You have proven your ability to perceive one of our members. I am pleased by this. Now, however, I must ask you to assist our outpost in a manner which appeases the different elders and ingratiates you to each.

'Return to Nangar and ask him what you can do to aid the outpost of Jirush.''You have done well. Continue to prove yourself to Nangar. In time, you may yet be able to help us more directly. For now, friend, keep our contact to a minimum.''It is good to have another set of hands in these trying times.'

He offers a genuine smile.

'Do not worry. I shall not set you to tasks that directly confront our enemy, not yet.

'I think assisting the other elders to prove your value and intention will suffice.

'Igbâl is as stubborn as a sated camel. He will not speak with you. You will work through his intermediary Galamê. Malgat is a forthright man with honourable intent. His needs are varied, and though they seem selfish, they are not. Zidemel is an odd sort. He hears voices, as do his followers. Humour them. It should mean no harm to anyone to do so.

'Return to me when they are satisfied.''While each of the elders does not directly support the rebellion, they do make efforts to assist the outpost and indirectly aid the cause. Please work with them, earn their favour and trust, and then return to me.''Your efforts ingratiate you to the elders. Forgive our further subterfuge. Our position is tenuous, and confrontation with the Ordâkhai will bring unease to the other elders. A few more measured moves, and I can assure the other elders of your intentions.'Grove-warden Avadhril asks for your help in spreading Cúridwan's salve throughout Vartúlin.Apply Cúridwan's salve to copses and soil plots afflicted with Lâg Dávrit in Vartúlin.Apply Cúridwan's salve to copses afflicted with Lâg Dávrit (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Apply Cúridwan's salve to soil plots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Avadhril in Vartúlin.'This is quite the blessing Cúridwan has bestowed upon us. We must not waste any of it. You were the one who sought her out and helped heal Vartúlin. It should then be your honour to heal greater Vartúlin.

'There are many soil plots and tree copses throughout Vartúlin. Spread a small but judicious amount of the salve on each. We will use Vartúlin as a staging point to heal greater Adagím. It is my intention to see Laithór, the Emerald Wood, reborn before I leave this place and undergo the Wearying.''This is a large step, ${PLAYER}. We have created a fortification of nature against the Lâg Dávrit. Soon, we will push these bounds out further and further. The Emerald Wood will once more be real again, not just a memory of old Kinta like me.'Fallow deer have been damaging the fields more than usual this year. Urama has asked you to hunt deer and bring her the venison.The destructive Ikorbâni harts and hinds can be found in the rice fields of Ekagar in Ambarûl.Hunt deer and collect venison (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have hunted deer and collected venison. You should bring the meat to Urama.'Are you any good at hunting game? The fallow deer have been just dreadful this year. We always have a little problem with them eating the crops, but of late they have been overmuch! Hunting some deer would do us much good, and the meat would not be unwelcome. It could be used to make a tasty stew that would keep my son and myself fed for quite some time.''Hunting Ikorbâni harts and hinds will help protect the fields from destruction. If you bring me the venison when you are done, I will use it to make a hearty stew.''Oh, that meat... just look at it! Thank you, my son and I will eat well for a stretch.'Brave adventurers have been summoned to complete missions across Middle-earth.Missions can be completed across Middle-earth.

You should complete missions.Complete missions (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have completed many missions across Middle-earth.CompletedYou should complete missions.You have completed many missions and done much to aid the peoples of Middle-earth!Brave adventurers have been summoned to complete missions across Middle-earth.Missions can be completed across Middle-earth.

You should complete missions.Complete missions (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have completed many missions across Middle-earth.CompletedYou should complete missions.You have completed many missions and done much to aid the peoples of Middle-earth!Amâsu believes there is still a chance of finding the Dubarâkh, the lost Ambarûli library, and suggested looking for a way to enter other salt mine tunnels.Amâsu has asked you to attempt to enter the other mine tunnels in the hills north of Iridír. She believes one of them may be the location of the lost library, Dubarâkh.Return to the salt minesAmâsu believes one of the other mine tunnels may be the location of the lost archive, Dubarâkh. You should check the gates to see if you can get into them.Check the gate on the nearby mine tunnelAmâsu believes one of the other mine tunnels may be the location of the lost archive, Dubarâkh. You should check the gates to see if you can get into them.Check the gate across the bridgeAmâsu believes one of the other mine tunnels may be the location of the lost archive, Dubarâkh. You have found a mine tunnel with a rusted gate that you are able to open. You should enter the tunnel.Enter the abandoned mine tunnelYou have found a mine tunnel with a rusted gate that you were able to open. Inside, dangerous scorpions are present. You should defeat them.Defeat usan-kûni (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Explore the mine tunnelsYou have found a mine tunnel with a rusted gate that you were able to open. While exploring the tunnels, you found a wall that struck you as odd.Examine the wallWhile exploring another salt mine tunnel, you noticed an unusual wall. You should tell Amâsu.Talk to Amâsu'It is unfortunate that you found nothing but danger on your outing. I had thought it quite possible that Khûldim was telling the truth. It would make sense if the archive were in the old salt mines. It would be well hidden, protected from the elements, and the salt would keep the papyrus dry, allowing the scrolls to remain intact for centuries if not ages.'

The venerable woman looks thoughtful for a moment.

'I now wonder if Khûldim led us in the correct direction by accident. There are other mine tunnels in the hills to the north. ${PLAYER}, if you do not mind, return to that area and see if you can get into the other tunnels. If so, it may be worth exploring.''Oh, this is interesting indeed! Thank you for looking. You have given me new hope!'The wall here seems unusually flat and different from the other walls in the tunnels. You aren't entirely sure, but you can imagine a hidden door here. You feel that it is information worth sharing with Amâsu.Ahûd, a guard that has been sent to help secure the sewers beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl, asked you to defeat a giant crocodile named Imkhâlam by the people of the city.Ahûd suggests collecting bog-lurker meat to lure the giant crocodile Imkhâlam to you. You can find sewer-lurkers throughout Ilmabiri; the Wells.Collect sewer-lurker meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ahûd suggests collecting bog-lurker meat to lure the giant crocodile Imkhâlam to you. Find a good location in the sewers under the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl to place the bait.Find a good place for the baitAhûd suggests collecting bog-lurker meat to lure the giant crocodile Imkhâlam to you. Place the bait to lure Imkhâlam to you. Imkhâlam is in the sewers beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.Place the meat to set the trapSummon and defeat ImkhâlamAhûd suggests collecting bog-lurker meat to lure the giant crocodile Imkhâlam to you. Place the bait to lure Imkhâlam to you. Imkhâlam is in the sewers beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.Summon and defeat ImkhâlamYou have summoned and defeated Imkhâlam the giant crocodile. Return to Ahûd at Kruha-sûrja, the guard post in the northern part of the sewers beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.Talk to Ahûd'Greetings! Are you offering to help? I do happen to have a task you could help with if you are willing.

'There is an unusually large crocodile reported to be down here in the sewers. The people have named it Imkhâlam. I am not one to flee from danger, mind you, but I have no desire to meet Imkhâlam! If you are willing to take him on, I may suggest first collecting some meat with which to lure the behemoth out. I hear he is fond of bog-lurker meat.''${PLAYER}, you have returned! Is Imkhâlam no more? I am very impressed with your bravery as well as your skills, thank you!'The overworked apprentice of The Din of Arms would like opinions on his new drink.Tûphik has asked you to give Xêrba drink samples to wandering citizens so you can get their opinions.

You can find them around the gardens outside The Din of Arms.You have no more samples of Xêrba to give!

You should report back to Tûphik at The Din of Arms.'Psst! You there! Quickly, before I am caught talking while working!

'I want to collect opinions on this drink I brewed. I named it Xêrba! No alcohol in here, I promise. -- just fruit and spices. Could you offer samples to people wandering the gardens and see what they have to say?

'I swear, there is never enough time for me to do anything other than work....''Oh! I almost thought you would just run off and drink all of the Xêrba yourself... it would not be the first time!

'Thank you, this is all very useful information! Ah -- sorry, I must get back to work!'Defeat many Orcs in Urash Dâr.Defeat many Orcs in Urash Dâr.Defeat many Orcs in Urash DârDefeat a great many Orcs in Urash Dâr.Defeat many Orcs in Urash Dâr.Defeat a great many Orcs in Urash Dâr.Defeat a great many Orcs in Urash DârDefeat many Orcs in Imhûlar.Defeat many Orcs in Imhûlar.Defeat many Orcs in ImhûlarDefeat a great many Orcs in Imhûlar.Defeat many Orcs in Imhûlar.Defeat a great many Orcs in Imhûlar.Defeat a great many Orcs in ImhûlarDefeat many Ordâkhai in Ambarûl.Defeat many Ordâkhai in Ambarûl.Defeat many Ordâkhai in AmbarûlDefeat a great many Ordâkhai in Ambarûl.Defeat many Ordâkhai in Ambarûl.Defeat a great many Ordâkhai in Ambarûl.Defeat a great many Ordakhai in AmbarûlDefeat many Ordâkhai in Imhûlar.Defeat many Ordâkhai in Imhûlar.Defeat many Ordâkhai in ImhûlarDefeat a great many Ordâkhai in Imhûlar.Defeat many Ordâkhai in Imhûlar.Defeat a great many Ordâkhai in Imhûlar.Defeat a great many Ordâkhai in ImhûlarDefeat many Ordâkhai in Khûd Zagin.Defeat many Ordâkhai in Khûd Zagin.Defeat many Ordâkhai in Khûd ZaginDefeat a great many Ordâkhai in Khûd Zagin.Defeat many Ordâkhai in Khûd Zagin.Defeat a great many Ordâkhai in Khûd Zagin.Defeat a great many Ordâkhai in Khûd ZaginReach Level 30 with the Order of the EagleReach Level 30 with the Order of the Eagle AllegianceRaphûz and Ashâmi resolve that their purpose together is to fight alongside one another against whatever the great evil threatening Shagâna.Ashâmi told you she and Raphûz intend to fight alongside one another against whatever the great evil stirring in Shagâna proves to be. She hopes you will visit them at their home in Urmâkh.Visit Ashâmi and Raphûz at their home in UrmâkhYour friends and their things are gone from the home. There is a note bearing your name left behind. You should collect and read the note you found.Collect your letter at Ashâmi and Raphûz's home in UrmâkhYou found a letter at the home once occupied by Raphûz and Ashâmi in the settlement of Urmâkh. You wonder what the letter might say.Read the letter left for you by your friends Ashâmi and RaphûzThough the letter did not say directly Ashâmi and Raphûz went on to Urash Dâr, all you know of the pair and your journeys lead to their taking the fight to the heart of the enemy. Should you find yourself in Urash Dâr, you should look there for your friends.Talk to Raphûz in Urash Dâr'Raphûz and I will make our way back toward Kûr Anzar. We will discuss along the way.

'Find us there, ${PLAYER}. We will be pleased to treat with you.''We were right to come here, ${PLAYER}. There is darkness spreading from the north-east. We joined this group of people who wish to stand against the rising evil there.

'If you can help, we could surely use your skills.'Ashâmi and Raphûz now reside in Urmâkh and they are becoming closer. They asked you to accompany them as they meet with a man named Numûru.Ashâmi is genuinely pleased to see you and told you to go and speak with Raphûz. She expects that he will be even more pleased. You can find him at their home in Urmâkh.Speak with Raphûz at his home in UrmâkhRaphûz and Ashâmi asked you to attend their meeting with Numûru, the right hand of Mizâdi Shâra-ingari. You should meet them at Numûru's post in Urmâkh.Speak with Raphûz at Numûru's post in UrmâkhSpeak with Ashâmi at Numûru's post in UrmâkhAshâmi and Raphûz both asked if you would speak with Numûru about their character. The soldier professed concern about their resolve. You can find Numûru at his post in Urmâkh.Speak with Numûru at his post in UrmâkhNumûru supplied you with two maps and asked you to give them to Ashâmi and Raphûz. Deliver the maps to Ashâmi and Raphûz at Numûru's post in Urmâkh.Ashâmi and Raphûz were provided orders from Numûru to prove their courage against their fears. They both reacted differently and asked you to meet them back at their home in Urmâkh.Speak with Ashâmi at her home in Urmâkh'I am not surprised to see you again ${PLAYER}. It appears you are the person Raphûz says you are. I think you are a rarity in this world, as is he.

'Our journey here was fraught, but we learn from each other and protect each other. Raphûz is not without skill, and his stories of Umbar and his family brighten the dull moments.

'You should go and see him. We are preparing to go and see Numûru, a personal guard of the leader here.

'He will think your arrival is kismet.'

She winks.

'So do I.''Hurry now, go say hello to Raphûz. He will be so glad to see you and to share our news.''${PLAYER}!

'Have you seen Ashâmi?'

You nod.

'Did she share our news?'

You tell him she mentioned Numûru.

'It is an auspicious day. We have learned much from one another. We have worked hard. We fight with a purpose, and when there is danger, we watch over each other.

'In the quieter moments, we share our stories, honestly. Our admiration and respect grow. She is as amazing as I assumed.

'I have you to thank.

'Listen, friend. We are to attend Numûru, the right hand of Mizâdi Shâra-ingari. She leads the forces to retake and restore Kûr Anzar. We hope to make an impression and join her elite guard.

'Please, meet us there. Perhaps you can speak on our behalf.''Your timing is impeccable. We just finished speaking with Numûru and mentioned you. He wishes you to speak on our character. We hope you do not mind.''The gall of this man. He needs to know of our character? It is an affront to me and to Raphûz. Still, Raphûz thinks that your words will sway the man. Will you speak for us?''Perhaps Raphûz is correct. Numûru must be cautious about who he lets near or around Mizâdi. Can you speak on our behalf?''Numûru seems to be a discerning man. Perhaps there is a reason he does not trust so readily. Still, I would prefer if we could contribute to the cause immediately.''You know these two, or so they say.

'I wish to know their weaknesses and their fears. If they join Mizâdi's guard, they must be without fear or weakness. Our enemy is fierce. Our defence must be resolute and stoic.'

You convey the stories of the boar and the serval injuring the two in their youth and they carry this fear. As you speak, he sketches two maps.

'Very good. Deliver these to Ashâmi and Raphûz. Tell them to return with the proof of their deeds.'

Numûru hands you two maps.Ashâmi looks at the map and sees a drawing of a serval.

'A serval.'

She looks closer.

'What is this marking? It looks like a cloud. Disease? I am tasked with killing a diseased serval.'

Ashâmi looks uneasy.

'This is a test I did not expect. We should take our leave and discuss at our quarters.'Raphûz looks at the map and sees a crude drawing of a boar.

'I am to kill a boar.

'I faced this fear before and overcame it. I will do so again. Let us retire to our home here in Urmâkh.'Ashâmi's face belies her unease.

'We must prepare for these challenges. Our purpose is clear. We both wish to serve alongside Mizâdi, and so we must overcome.'Ashâmi and Raphûz return to Numûru and provide proof of their success. The captain offers one more challenge to them both.Ashâmi is ready to return to Numûru at his post in Urmâkh. She wants you to ensure that Raphûz is also ready to return to Mizâdi's captain. You will find Raphûz at their home in Urmâkh.Speak with Raphûz at his home in UrmâkhRaphûz and Ashâmi are both ready to return to Numûru. They ask you to meet them at Numûru's post in Urmâkh to see the result of their efforts.Speak with Numûru about Ashâmi and Raphûz at his post in UrmâkhNumûru said there is one more task that Ashâmi and Raphûz must complete together. The two were surprised they had not done enough. He instructed you to speak to them at his post in Urmâkh.Speak with Raphûz at Numûru's post in UrmâkhSpeak with Ashâmi at Numûru's post in UrmâkhAshâmi and Raphûz returned to their home in Urmâkh to discuss how they will undertake the next challenge. They wish to speak to you at their home in Urmâkh before they go.Speak with Ashâmi at her home in Urmâkh'We are preparing to return to Numûru.

'We ask that you attend our discussion with him again. Your assistance and support are invaluable to us.

'Please, speak with Raphûz and inform him I am ready.''I am eager to present Numûru with proof of our success. I would like you to be present.

'I believe this will ensure we are made members of Mizâdi's forces and will realize our purpose in Imhûlar.

'We have you to thank for our relationship and our successes. It is only right we share.''Raphûz and Ashâmi did as I requested. They faced their fears and earned the right to prove their courage against the Ordâkhai of Imhûlar.'

Numûru pauses and looks at your friends.

'They were perplexed when I told them there was another challenge before them. 

'Mizâdi's guards are not tempered by only fighting beasts.

'They must hone their skills against the true enemy. Speak with them. I believe they are worthy, but I require further proof.''We are to engage the enemy directly. We will provide a distraction by attacking a smaller encampment while the main force pushes against the Ordâkhai at Kûr Anzar.''Numûru wants more proof of our devotion to the cause.'

She shakes her head.

'I do not like the words he chooses. We fight because it is noble. We fight because the cause is just. We fight because the plight of the people of Shagâna is extreme. We fight for our freedom and a future for the children of Shagâna.

'We fight for an ideal. Not a saviour.''I spoke with Raphûz. He is enamoured by Mizâdi's words, but he is not given to the superstitions of the Shagâni.

'I think it is his pragmatic view on Shagâna that endears me to him.

'We have discussed and will go to the encampment and prove our value to Numûru and Mizâdi's cause together.'Nangar's trust in you grows. He asks that you take the letter to Sigénik for more instruction. He cannot be gone from the outpost too long or questions will rise.Nangar returned the untranslated and translated letters to you with instruction to deliver them to Sigénik. He believes Sigénik is better fit to direct you than he.Read the letter home if you wishSigénik directed you to climb the crags to the east to find an oasis where the rebels, and their leader Amalíbi. You are to deliver the letters to her.Read the letter if you wish'Take the letter to Sigénik. He will direct you to someone better equipped to deal with this situation.

'My duties as Elder occupy too much time, and if I were to go missing from my post for too long, there would be questions.

'Thank you for all you did here in Jirush, ${PLAYER}. May we all find the peace we desire.''I can do no more without assistance from our leader. Return to Sigénik. If he feels, as I, that you are ready to meet our leader, he will send you on to the hidden location.'Sigénik takes the message and reads it slowly.

'There is an opportunity here, an opportunity we cannot squander. In your short time in Jirush, you have made inroads with the Elders, engaged our enemy directly, and aided our cause. I believe your intentions are earnest. I cannot leave my post here as others may come, and I must test them as I did you.'

He hands the message to you.

'To the east, in the craggy hills among the outcroppings, there is a small oasis where my fellow rebels make their home. Go there and find Amalíbi.

'Deliver this letter to her. She will know you are coming.''Amalíbi leads us from Ghalburu in the crags east of Jirush. She will welcome you. I have informed her of how much aid you have offered thus far. The path is not obvious, but it is there. Travel east from Jirush and you will find it.'The old woman looks you over as she takes the letter from your hand. She reads quietly and then meets your gaze.

'Forgive us. Our position in this land is tenuous. Your arrival required consideration and observation before we could be sure you were trustworthy.

'I am Amalíbi, I lead this rebellion. We welcome your assistance.'Angârmu has asked for your help to find his camel, Ishegir, that has wandered off near Malgâma.Angârmu has asked you to check for his camel, Ishegir, at his first favourte spot to the west, past the big rock.Reach Ishegir's first favourite spotUse the <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> emote to check for signs of Ishegir at his first favourite spot near big rock to the west of which Angârmu spoke.There was no sign of Ishegir at his first favourite spot. He may be at his second favourite spot near the river's edge to the east.Reach Ishegir's second favourite spotUse the <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> emote to check for signs of Ishegir at this location.There was no sign of Ishegir at his second favourite spot. Perhaps you will find him at his third favourite spot that Angârmu told you of, near the Pools of Kudím to the north of here.Reach Ishegir's third favourite spotUse the <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> emote to check for signs of Ishegir at this location.Return to Angârmu with news of Ishegir after having checked all of his favourite spots he had suggested.Return to Angârmu with news of Ishegir'Greetings visitor. My trusted camel, Ishegir, has wandered off and not yet returned.

'I fear the worst. You must help me find him!

'Go to his favourite resting spots and look for signs of him. His first is to the west of here, just past the big rock. If you do not find him there, travel to the east of here and find where the small river meets the big river. That is his second most favourite spot.

'If you fail in finding him at those spots, head east past the walls of Zikrum-dûl, then north until you find the Pools of Kudím. He enjoys watching the pools there.''You have come back to me! I trust that Ishegir is not far behind!'

You tell Angârmu that you saw no signs of his camel, Ishegir, in any of his favourite spots.

'I am not surprised. He is very hard to spot. I have been told that only I can see him which makes him very hard to find when he wanders off! I worry that he will be late for his supper now though.

'Thank you for looking, visitor. Ishegir is a stubborn one.'Defeat zealots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'The sounds of those zealots clashing with our most hated foes has been wracking my sleep. My night terrors would surely be eased if I knew there were fewer of them about!''My heart is much calmed by this news of those zealots' defeat, thank you. I do not wish to forbid any from following a leader of their choice, but I do not see why one should be so hostile towards innocent civilians. Thank you, friend. Some coin for the dangers you faced in easing a poor man's mind.'Avadhril the Grove-warden asks for your help in bearing water from the local stream to Veróthi in Vartúlin place of Sarnor, who has fallen ill.Speak with Sarnor near Vartúlin's upper path and gather his water buckets.Speak with Sarnor near Vartúlin's upper pathGather Sarnor's buckets. They are beside him on his left.Gather Sarnor's buckets (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect water from the upper stream and water the Veróthi near the bend in the path.Collect water from Vartúlin's upper stream near the bridgeCollect water from the upper stream and water the Veróthi at the edge of Vartúlin.Collect more water from Vartúlin's upper stream near the bridgeSpeak with Avadhril in Vartúlin.Speak with Avadhril'We have much to do in Vartúlin. Chief among them for myself is nurturing the Veróthi here, which contain our cherished ancestors. The streams running through Vartúlin feed most of the Veróthi, however there are several stands of Veróthi away from the river that require frequent watering. Unfortunately, Sarnor, our water-bearer, has fallen ill. Would you be able to aid us?

'The task is simple enough. Collect Sarnor's buckets from him, then go to the river and gather water. Lastly, water the stand of Veróthi at the bend at the top of the path above us, and at the edge of Vartúlin, to my right.''You are to be my replacement for the day, then?

'Yes, I am ashamed to say I have a fever and am unable to perform my duties. I tried, but both Thórvilon and Avadhril forbade my work this day. I suppose I am grateful for their kindness, and yours.

'The buckets are beside me there to my left. Thank you for this. I shall return to dreams, and hope they are of old Laithór, the Emerald Wood.''We Kintai aid one another when one of us weakens or falls ill. It appears you do the same. For that, you have my respect, and my gratitude.'Galâmka would like more information about the situation in Maurûsh and asks you to go and do additional scouting in the area.Galâmka has asked that you observe the northern entrance to the interior of Maurûsh.Reach the door to the northern interior in MaurûshUse the <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> emote to scout out the northern entrance to the interior of Maurûsh to gain information.Galâmka has asked that you observe the eastern entrance to the interior of Maurûsh.Reach the door to the eastern interior in MaurûshUse the <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> emote to scout out the eastern entrance to the interior of Maurûsh to gain information.Return to Galâmka in Ub Nishir to inform him of what you learned from your scouting mission.Return to Galâmka in Ub Nishir with the information gained'Greetings, ${PLAYER}.

'The scouting reports you gathered before and the trials you have overcome from the information they detailed have been a great boon to us all.

'People here are beginning to have real hope now. Hope that we can truly win back our homes from these monsters.

'With your help we have weakened our enemy, but we still need to know more before we can attack them head-on. We have little knowledge of the Orcs' movements regarding the interior of the stronghold, and I desire to send you on a scouting mission of your own. Go investigate the northern and eastern entrances and see what you discover there.''You return. With good tidings I hope?'

You explain what you observed at the entrances to Maurûsh.

'That is troublesome to hear. It appears that we must avoid these entrances and not risk attacking them directly. We must work on a new plan for now and find another point of attack.

'Thank you again, my friend, for the information you have brought me. I hope to see you again soon.'Tilmakhím is to the south of Tâkhdar.

Hármelak has asked you to discover where some traps for pests have been laid in Tilmakhím.Tilmakhím is to the south of Tâkhdar, but you know the traps are set along the northern walls of Khabârkhad.

Journey there to search for pest traps.Search for pest traps along the northern walls of KhabârkhadTraps for rats can be found along the northern walls of Khabârkhad.

Identify and remove the pest traps.Locate and remove traps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hármelak is in Dâr Laja.

You have found and removed the traps Hârmelak has said failed to capture pests and are a danger to her people. She will want to hear the good news.Return to Hármelak'I greet you, ${PLAYER}. Your travels have taken you to Tilmakhím in the depths of Takhdâr, so I hear. My sources have cautioned me that pests troubling Umbar-môkh are not under control. It is my understanding you are aware of this matter as well.

'I am told the traps are ensnaring my people, not pests. I ask you to take note of where these traps might be laid, and return to me with clear information regarding their locations.''I have heard you have been to Tilmakhím. Why have you not yet removed the pest's traps?''You have found all the traps, then? My people are safer for your actions; we thank you. I may have further use for your loyalty, and equal reward.'Akûshu worries about the scorpions and marsh-flies being a threat to the horses.Akûshu has requested you slay some of the usan-kûni scorpions to the south at a place called Nirikal, and scather-flies in the bog near the river-bank at Umûn Khab.Defeat scather-flies at at Umûn Khab (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat usan-kûni at Nirikal (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have slain many of the usan-kûni and scather-flies that posed a threat to the horses' safety. You should talk to Akûshu at Gha Nêkha, south of Eshadûr in Ambarûl.Talk to Akûshu'Thank you friend for stopping to help us. Though we have some shelter here, I am worried for the horses. Many beasts in Shâgana would happily make a meal of them. If you are able, would you slay some of wild beasts? I am particularly concerned about the usan-kûni to the south at a place called Nirikal and the scather-flies in the marsh along the river-bank at Umûn Khab.''Would you slay some of the usan-kûni to the south and the scather-flies in the marsh on the river-bank?''${PLAYER}, thank you so much for dealing with those horrid beasts. Do the horses seem more calm to you? I think I am more calm, anyway!'Mizâdi has asked you to destroy the siege weapons being built in Kûr Anzar, to prevent their use against her forces in the future.Mizâdi has asked you to sneak into Kûr Anzar and sabotage the Barkhûshim siege weapons intended for use in an assault on Urmâkh. Kûr Anzar can be found due east of Urmâkh.Destroy the Barkhûshim siege weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Mizâdi in Urmâkh with the good news.Return to Mizâdi in Urmâkh'I see that you can get things done. That bodes well for us, as I have great need of one such as you. Your talent for stealth seems matched only by Razâl.

'This next mission will require the same care and patience you undertook in rescuing Razâl. We know the All-seeing are constructing great siege engines. We believe it is with intention to destroy Urmâkh. We have intercepted several of their spies around the perimeter of Urmâkh, scouting our defences. I need you to go back to Kûr Anzar and destroy these weapons whilst they are still being built. There is often black powder stored around these great weapons. Set it ablaze and then quickly make your escape. The resulting conflagration should do the rest.''This is wonderful news. You have bought us a fortnight of time or more. Without those siege weapons, Urmâkh can repel any attack the Barkhûshim bring forth in the short term. In the long term, we will take the fight to their doorstep. Thank you for your valorous deeds in keeping Urmâkh and her people safe, ${PLAYER}.'A powerful creature stalks the halls of Ghâr Mejet. Destroy vile effigies in the area and confront the creature.A powerful creature stalks the halls of Ghâr Mejet. Destroy vile effigies in the area and then confront the creature.Destroy vile effigies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Confront Lâkhmar and drive the foul creature away.Defeat LâkhmarTalk to Yâshri and inform her that the creature has been felled.

Yâshri can be found just north of Ghâr Mejet.Talk to Yâshri'A powerful creature known as Lâkhmar stalks the halls of Ghâr Mejet. Destroying the vile effigies throughout the area will make him more vulnerable to harm.

'Seek out these objects, destroy them, and drive back the foul creature.''With Lâkhmar being dispatched, Ghâr Mejet may pose less of a threat to the people who dwell below the streets.

'Thank you for aiding in this most important task.'Assuming you came to her orchard looking for work, Meliri has tasked you with defeating the scather-flies in her orange groves.You have been asked to defeat scather-flies scattered throughout the orange groves of Burukíri in Ambarûl.Defeat scather-flies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have defeated scather-flies scattered throughout the orange groves of Burukíri in Ambarûl. You should return to Meliri.Talk to Meliri'Hashtal-gûr stranger. What could possibly bring a traveller to Ambarûl? Ah, you must be looking for work. You have come to the right place, my friend. We are always short on strong hands. Assuming you know how to use the weapons you carry, I have just the job for you. The biggest threat to our orange groves is insects. By 'big' I mean that literally. There are huge buzzing scather-flies flitting all about the orchard!

'Put those weapons to good use against those flies and I will pay you some coin. Do it well, and I will have more work for you.''You won't make any coin just standing around! Defeating scather-flies around the groves is what you should be doing.''The flies have been dealt with? Superb. They will probably just come right back, but in the meantime, I have more work for you. Here is the coin I promised.'Mizâdi has asked you to conduct a daring raid on Garash Kâru, the Ekhamâti encampment providing a foothold for Bârshud into Ambarûl.Travel to Garash Kâru in southern Ambarûl. Garash Kâru can be found south-west of Iridír, over the river Ikorbân.Enter Garash Kâru in southern AmbarûlDestroy barricades and defeat Ekhamâti at Garash Kâru in Ambarûl. Garash Kâru can be found due south of Iridír.Destroy barricades at Garash Kâru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ekhamâti look-outs at Garash Kâru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ekhamâti sorcerers at Garash Kâru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ekhamâti cat-keepers at Garash Kâru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Rumûza at Garash Kâru in Ambarûl.Defeat Rumûza at Garash KâruPlant Mizâdi's banner in the centre of Garash Kâru.Plant Mizâdi's banner in the centre of Garash KâruReturn to Mizâdi in Iridír with news of the fall of Garash Kâru.Return to Mizâdi in Iridír with news of your success'Now is the time for our counter-attack. Bârshud has driven his forces as far as Garash Kâru, at the southern border of Ambarûl. Before he finishes fortifying his position, I would ask you, ${PLAYER}, to go with some of the Subuzûri and sweep through the camp. Expel him from Ambarûl before he can dig in.

'This is our utmost priority at this moment, friend.''This is a great victory indeed, ${PLAYER}! Our first real victory since Kûr Anzar.

'Now with his forces pushed back, we have some needed breathing room to plan an assault on Bârshud's encampment, wherever that is. My scouts are currently scouring Khûd Zagin, looking for the source of his operations. But that is for another day. Today, I am heartened, friend.'Sângal is worried that the displaced people in Iridír have no place to sleep. He has asked that you help construct tents to be used as temporary shelters.Sângal is worried that the displaced people in Iridír have no place to sleep. You can gather supplies nearby to help construct the tents.Gather tent supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Help Sângal set up tents for the displaced people in Iridír.Construct tents (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Sângal in Iridír and let him know you have finished setting up the tents for the displaced people to use. They no longer have to sleep in the open weather and cold.Return to Sângal'Ah, adventurer. I could use your help!

'We have people arriving here in Iridír who have been driven from their homes by the assaults in Ambarûl. I worry for them having to sleep wherever they can find room and being exposed to the weather and cold. I have some supplies here. Would you please take them and set up some tents that they can stay in?''The tents will work flawlessly! Well done! Thank you, ${CLASS}! I will inform the people of your efforts and let them know they will no longer be forced to suffer the outdoors.'Raphûz is tasked with eliminating a boar in a camp near Urmâkh. He asked you to meet with him and assist him.Raphûz asks you to accompany him to find and defeat the boar Numûru tasked him with killing. The boar's lair is west from the settlement of Urmâkh.Find Raphûz near the boar camp west of UrmâkhRaphûz was waiting near the boars outside of Urmâkh. He signaled to you and looks ready to find and defeat the target of his task from Numûru.Complete Instance: Raphûz's ChallengeYou assisted Raphûz in completing his task to face his fear and defeat the boar near Urmâkh. You should meet him at his home in Urmâkh to determine what to do next.'When I heard Mizâdi speak to the people before an assault by the Ordâkhai, I was moved. Her candor and fearlessness against a powerful enemy is inspiring.

'The Shagâni of Imhûlar believe she is something greater, a saviour.

'Again, the superstitions of the people sway them. She is a woman, an inspiring woman.

'I wish to fight for this land. For Ashâmi and the people of Shagâna. If I must face my greatest fear again to serve among Mizâdi's elite forces, I shall.

'As before, will you meet me at the camp west of here, near the border of Khûd Zagin, my friend?''We should make our way into the ruins and find this beast. The sooner we are finished, the sooner Ashâmi and I can assist in Mizâdi's cause.''When Ashâmi completes her task as well, we will speak with you. We may need your aid with Numûru again.

'We have done well today. You remain my stoutest ally, ${PLAYER}.'Raphûz asks for assistance in acquiring the tusks from the largest boar in the wilds east of the Wrackwade. He has a fear of boars and a desire to overcome the fear.Raphûz told you he would make his way to the boar's camp and wait for you. Make your way to the east and find Raphûz outside of the boar camp.Find Raphûz near the boar's denRaphûz is prepared to enter the den and find the largest boar. Speak with him and see that he defeats the largest boar in Ambarûl.Complete Instance: Facing His FearAfter defeating the boar, Urushagân, Raphûz told you he would speak to you about your efforts within the safety of Wrackwade.'When I was a boy, I travelled with my father outside of Umbar. Even then, my curiosity earned me trouble.'

He chuckles.

'I found a piglet in the wild. Without thought, I approached the piglet, and its squeal tore through my ears and alerted its mother nearby.

'The matron closed on me, bit down on my leg, and dragged me over the rough terrain until a caravan archer brought it down.

'I learned to fear boars. It is only now, as I recall the story, I understand my actions led to two deaths that day.'

He looks at you solemnly.

'I wish to face my fear. I hear a singular of boars lies to the east. Will you meet me there and help me face my fear?''I am prepared if you are, my friend. Say the word and we will begin.''As I said after defeating the large boar, I understand bravery now better than before. It is not standing up to a moment of fear. It is embracing the fear and using the fear to fuel your actions. Incorporating all your body provides to enhance your performance and emerge triumphant over your fear. That is bravery.

'Thank you for helping me find mine.'Raphûz asks for assistance in hunting down a scorpion for its stinger north of Wrackwade. He learned the Ambarûli have an innate hatred of the scorpions.Raphûz told you he would make his way to the scorpion nest north of Wrackwade to wait for you. Make your way to the north and find Raphûz outside of the salt mine.Find Raphûz near the scorpion nest near the salt mineRaphûz is prepared to enter the nest to hunt the largest scorpion. Speak with him and see that he defeats the scorpion.Complete Instance: Proving His BraveryRaphûz said he would meet you back in Wrackwade to discuss the defeat of the scorpion.Return to Wrackwade and speak with Raphûz'When I enquired about Shagâni culture, I learned there is a shared hesitation about scorpions in these lands. There is something deeply-seated here about how they are revered and followed. I believe there is a cult threatening the people that revolves around the creatures.

'If I can claim the tail of one of these beasts, I think it is a fitting show of strength. Will you meet me at a scorpion nest north-east of here near an old salt mine and help me claim a stinger from such a beast?''We are very near the scorpion nest. I am prepared. Are you?''I am happy I remembered to craft some potions before we travelled into the nest, my friend. The venom those creatures inject could be deadly. I understand that some may revere those beasts, though I do not understand how. Thank you, again.'Defeat the Orcs who tracked you to Enârshan's home.Orcs have followed you back from Khûn Sagaz. Defeat them and protect Enârshan's home.Speak with Enârshan when you are ready to defend her homeYou have defeated the Orcs who followed your tracks. Speak with Enârshan to ensure her that the threat is gone.Speak with Enârshan'I believe with this our preparations are complete. Wait, what is that sound?'

Enârshan pauses for a moment.

'Do you hear that, ${CLASS}?'

Enârshan's eyes grow wide with anger.

'Orcs! There are Orcs here! They must have followed you from Khûn Sagaz!

'Remove these beasts from my home!''How dare those foul beasts enter into my home! They deserve the end you gave them. Thank you for your help, though you were the cause of it.

'We must bring an end to these Orcs who dare defile my waters.''How dare these Orcs come here. Come to my home!

'Make these Orcs pay for passing through the waterfall!'Defeat many rats in the Umbar-môkh.Defeat many rats in the Umbar-môkhDefeat rats in the Umbar-môkhDefeat a great many rats in the Umbar-môkh.Defeat many rats in the Umbar-môkh.Defeat a great many rats in the Umbar-môkh.Defeat a great many rats in the Umbar-môkhNisami, who cares for the outpost's food and the treasury, explains that brigands raided the outpost and stole several rations and a coffer containing the wealth. She asks that you deal with the brigands and recover the stolen goods.Nisami explained that brigands, south-west beyond, raided Jirush and stole food and coin from the outpost. She asked you to go to the brigand encampment to recover the stolen goods and to avenge the people of Jirush.Defeat brigands in their encampment (${NUMBER}/16)Recover ration packs for Jirush (${NUMBER}/6)Recover the coffer of coins stolen from JirushYou recovered the wealth and food for Jirush from the brigand camp south-west of Nirgambâr. Return the ration packs and the coffer to Nisami at Jirush in central Khûd Zagin.'Malgat sent you?

'I shall be brief. The Ordâkhai soldiers are the nearest enemy, but the brigands living in the shadow of Nirgambâr do worse damage to our people.

'They steal rations and what little wealth we have. They leave us hungry and destitute. While the elders do what they can, they are too few and consumed by the tenuous truce with the Ordâkhai to be bothered with these knaves.

'You can help with this. In a recent raid, the brigands stole a coffer and six ration packs I made for the weakest among us. Recover those items, and revisit the pain they unleashed on us tenfold.''As if the Ordâkhai threatening the outpost were not enough, brigands steal our food and wealth and then flee beyond the Tombs of Nirgambâr. Please, if you will, recover the stolen food and coin. If you can, revisit the suffering on the brigands there tenfold.''I am impressed. Perhaps the elders should offer you coins to stand against the Ordâkhai soldiers and the brigands. Though, I am certain the price you command is more than we can muster in Jirush. I will accept this grand effort as more than enough.

'Thank you, sincerely.'Kûzash has asked you to help him gather wood from trees in the area so that he can work to repair the lift.Kûzash has asked you to help him gather wood from trees at the bottom of the cliffs near Ashâgir so that he can work to repair the lift.Gather wood for repairs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bring the wood for the lift repairs back to Kûzash in the Ashâgir hideout.'Ah, you appear to be a capable adventurer. Perhaps you can provide some help.

'I am doing what I can to repair the lift here in Ashâgir. The path up is a treacherous one, and having the lift operational would be a great improvement.

'I could use some more wood for the repairs. You can find trees with suitable branches in the canyon below near the water. I ask that you gather some and return to me.''Welcome back, ${CLASS}. I see that you have gathered the wood that I requested.

'You have been a great help to me. Now I must return to work.'Explore camps, settlements, and other important points of interest in Dil-irmíz in the Umbar-môkh.Explore camps, settlements, and other important points of interest in Dil-irmíz in the Umbar-môkh.Find the DûlkarFind JadamborFind DeshûkhFind Dâr SêkhtaExplore camps, settlements, and other important points of interest in Ilmabiri in the Umbar-môkh.Explore camps, settlements, and other important points of interest in Ilmabiri in the Umbar-môkh.Find Kruha-sûrjaFind HêbatokhFind Nêb-jadirFind the Talaba-kênFind Môba IdedYou have turned over every stone, discovered every encampment, and defeated every foe in Imhûlar in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete quests in Imhûlar in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete Explorer of ImhûlarComplete Slayer of ImhûlarComplete Tales of ImhûlarExplore camps, settlements, and other important points of interest in Kamrabezûr in the Umbar-môkh.Explore camps, settlements, and other important points of interest in Kamrabezûr in the Umbar-môkh.Find Kên TaghlimFind HulzidârFind Jâx UgikhFind the HarkhaphârFind Ghâr MejetExplore camps, settlements, and other important points of interest in Khabârkhad in the Umbar-môkh.Explore camps, settlements, and other important points of interest in Khabârkhad in the Umbar-môkh.Find Itekh-kênFind Mekab-kuphârFind LôkhalelFind NishabêtFind SektakhâbExplore camps, settlements, and other important points of interest in Tâkhdar in the Umbar-môkh.Explore camps, settlements, and other important points of interest in Tâkhdar in the Umbar-môkh.Find Kheb HanûtFind TilmakhímFind IshadôkhFind Sâl BajatFind Shak PhêlexHow can one hope to wrest back the broken narrative of an entire city?Jihan has tasked you with interviewing three individuals in the Tor-gardens.

Imêna works at The Din of Arms to the south-west. Sophân waits by the Gate of Steps to the south. Nûr can be found to the south-east outside the Dahâl Huliz.Talk to Imêna at The Din of ArmsTalk to Nûr at the Dahâl HulizTalk to Sophân at the Gate of StepsYou have finished interviewing all three people and taken notes.

You should bring the notes to Jihan in the gardens outside Dâr Tabib.'May I have a moment of your time? You see, I am compiling accounts of Umbar's recent past. I have not finished this current interview, but I promised to talk to three others in the Tor-gardens today. It would not do to leave them waiting. If you would be willing to interview them and take notes, I could pay you.

'The old Harâph Imêna works at The Din of Arms to the south-west. Sophân waits by the Gate of Steps to the south. And you can find Nûr to the south-east outside the Dahâl Huliz.''My childhood memories before Mût Tadaul -- the Death of Light -- are hazy. But Mût Tadaul itself, I remember as clear as water.

'Ordâkh soldiers flooded the streets, tearing down banners of all colours as they went. The cries and the screams of people echoed around me. Umbar burned. My family ran to the docks in hopes of fleeing by water. When we beheld the burning remnants of ships that had attempted to do the same, we could only turn back.

'Many good people died that day. Some days, I am still there, and Umbar is still burning.

'As a Harâph, I have spun countless stories for eager listeners. This is not a story that I enjoy telling, but it is one that must be told. It must be remembered.''When the riots started, I joined along with other Hûliz. Too long had we been used as the Heirs' executioners. Perhaps it was the rush of finally fighting back, but I knew we would succeed. After all, we outnumbered those in power.

'Some of my fellows died believing they had helped change things. And they did. But I watch as the Kindred replace the Heirs. I watch as our most vulnerable citizens continue to suffer, just in different ways. And I wonder what the future holds in store for Umbar -- if anything else will change.

'I no longer fight as a Hûlaz. I cannot bear it.''The colourful banners around the city still surprise me, every day. When will I get used to it? I do not know. But I wish Mother and Father were here with me to see this.

'Worshippers took them from our home. If our neighbours had not found and hidden me, I would have burned along with them. I survived only because I was lucky. I hate feeling like that.

'The Church may be gone from Umbar, but its shadow still exists.''Thank you, traveller. These accounts are not the ancient texts that many of my colleagues seek, but they are just as important.

'History tells us of how Umbar was passed from empire to empire. The Church may have tried to purge the past, but simply look around and listen -- not everything was destroyed. The Númenórean and Hamâti architecture, the sounds of Umbari, Westron, and Ordâkhai words. The people and their stories. We were here. We still are.'You have turned over every stone, discovered every encampment, and defeated every foe in Khûd Zagin in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete quests in Khûd Zagin in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete Explorer of Khûd ZaginComplete Slayer of Khûd ZaginComplete Tales of Khûd ZaginYou have gone to every corner, defeated every foe, and been a champion for the peoples of the Ikorbân Valley.Go to every corner, defeat every foe, and be a champion for the peoples of the Ikorbân Valley.Complete Renewer of AmbarûlComplete Rejuvenator of Khûd ZaginComplete Rejuvenator of ImhûlarComplete Vanquisher of Urash DârCultists throughout Kamrabezûr have gathered valuable artifacts throughout the area. Gather these objects and return them, so that Azrât continue her research.Recover relics from cultists spread throughout Kamrabezûr.Collect relics from cultists in Kamrabezûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Azrât is at Kên Taghlim in Kamrabezûr.

Now that you have collected the relics, you should return them to her.Talk to Azrât in Kên Taghlim'${PLAYER}! During my time in the catacombs, I have learned that there are areas that contain information and objects that are impossible to find elsewhere. Some time ago, I travelled here and began establishing a small encampment to gather this information so that it can be put to good use.

'Sadly, many times, this information can be found in the most dangerous places. In this case, I believe that relics of a bygone age can be recovered from Jâx Ugikh.

'Could you recover some of these relics and return them to me so I could continue my research?'You present the relics to Azrât.

'My goodness, ${PLAYER}! These relics will provide a great deal of context and information about the ancient origins of Jâx Ugikh.

'Thank you for your help!'You have turned over every stone, discovered every encampment, and defeated every foe in Ambarûl in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete quests in Ambarûl in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete Explorer of AmbarûlComplete Slayer of AmbarûlComplete Tales of AmbarûlYou have turned over every stone, discovered every encampment, and defeated every foe along your journey to help restore Hamât and free the people of Shagâna with Mizâdi in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete tasks that aid Shagâna and Mizâdi as part of the Crown of Hamât in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete Dangers in ShagânaComplete Ekhamati-bane of Shagâna (Advanced)Complete Tales of the Crown of HamâtComplete Treasure-seeker of ShagânaDabôr the Breaker has requested that you assist Yâshri in gathering goods from Ghâr Mejet. When sold, these goods provide Harkhaphâr with much needed income to support the settlement.Seek out Yâshri, located near Ghâr Mejet, and see if you can lend her aid.Talk to Yâshri near Ghâr Mejet'Thank you kindly for offering aid to our small camp. Yâshri is a capable gatherer who locates and acquires bits and baubles that are sold and used to support our outpost.

'Travel west, seek her out, and see if you can assist her.''It is so kind for Dabôr to send an extra pair of hands to help me gather things in this area. Please note, it is quite dangerous as the restless Dead creep throughout the area.'Your standing among the Tale-wardens earns you a gift. Return to one of their members' quartermasters to be rewarded.Visit the Tale-warden Assistant, Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate, or any of the other Phetekâri quartermasters at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a gift from the Tale-wardens of Umbar.Reach Respected tier with the PhetêkariVisit the Tale-warden Assistant, Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate, or any of the other Phetekâri quartermasters at Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a gift from the Tale-wardens of Umbar.Visit Mashêm at Telperiën's Gate to claim your giftVisit a Tale-warden's assistant at Iridír, Jirush, or UrmâkhYour standing with the Phetekâri grows. You should visit one of their assistants at Telperiën's Gate, Iridír, Jirush, or Urmâkh to claim a well-earned gift.'You have proven to be one of the greatest contributors to our effort in Ikorbân. Lord Rothog wishes for you to choose a gift.

'As always, speak with Shulêga to purchase other offerings from our patron.''Accept this gift for everything you have done to provide us with insight into the Shagâni culture.

'As always, speak with our quartermaster to purchase other offerings from our patron.'Your continued efforts in Shagâna inform the Tale-wardens of the people, history, and tribulations of the land. The records of the Ikorbân Valley's history grow due to your efforts.You must earn Respected standing with the Tale-wardensYour continued efforts to support Shâra Mizâdi and her forces in Idagâl earn you great respect with Hamât Renewed.You must earn Respected standing with Hamât RenewedAshâmi and Raphûz ask you to share their time by a fire in Shonith to discuss the trials of the past several days.Raphûz and Ashâmi invited you to sit with them to discuss the events of your arrival in Shonith and the future.Complete Instance: Respite in ShonithYou allowed Raphûz and Ashâmi to speak without you at the advice of Lathagwid. You should return to Raphûz at the oasis Shonith to learn how the remainder of the night went.'Raphûz suggests a celebration for all of us. A meal, a smoke, and talk of the future.

'I hope you will join us.''We will be here this evening if you wish to join us. Please do.''We talked late into the night, my friend, long after you departed. Ashâmi convinced me our destinies lie east, toward Kûr Anzar.

'There is a warrior there, said to be a hero reborn. She fights for the future of this land.

'Since my arrival in Shagâna, this is the call I have heard. I have found my path. Now, I must walk it.

'Thank you for all your help along the way. I hope to see you again.'Eshéra has a plan to make some extra coin for you both by selling crocodile skins to a dealer at the market in Umbar-môkh.Eshéra has suggested you defeat crocodiles to collect their skins in Ilmabiri, beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.Collect Ilmabiri crocodile skins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected the skins of defeated crocodiles in the sewers beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. You should bring them to Eshéra at Hêbatokh, her camp in Ilmabiri.'There are many profitable things that can be found down here. If you are interested, the skins of crocodiles are also in demand. These I know they use to make shoes, bags and other items to sell to people in the Upper Ward with more money than sense. If you also bring me crocodile skins, there will be something in it for you.''Ah yes, these should fetch a fine price. Here is your cut. It is a pleasure doing business with you.'Eshéra has a plan to make some extra coin for you both by selling bat wings to a dealer at the market in Umbar-môkh.Eshéra has suggested you defeat bats to collect their wings in Ilmabiri, beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.Collect Ilmabiri bat wings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected the wings of defeated bats in the sewers beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. You should bring them to Eshéra at Hêbatokh, her camp in Ilmabiri.'You know friend, between your fighting skills and my connexions, we could make each other some extra coin.'

The woman gives you a sly smile.

'I happen to know someone in the markets of Umbar-môkh that will pay well for bat wings. Why? I have no idea, and neither do I care, as long as they pay the agreed-upon price.''Yes, these will do nicely. Very good, ${PLAYER}. Here is your cut.'Sigênik, a craftsman in Western Khanâg, has told you his plan to reuse the metal from lost swords in Shukabad.Sigênik has asked you to travel to  Shukabad, west of Western Khanâg, and collect time-worn swords there.Collect time-worn swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have gone to Shukabad and collected the time-worn swords there. You should bring them to Sigênik in Western Khanâg.'Hashtal-gûr, traveller. You look like the sort who can handle themselves. I can see in your eyes that danger is not unknown to you. Tell me, would you help a humble craftsman?

'In a land as unforgiving as the Khûd, nothing should go to waste if it can be helped. Over the ages, many soldiers have come to the Khûd, only to meet their end here. One would not have to look too hard to find their gear lost to time in the desert. For example, at the ruins of Shukabad, I have heard there are swords to be found, just lying about on the ground. Scavengers do not bother with them because they are rusted and unusable. They are still made of fine metals, however, and a skilled craftsman would be able to melt them down and reuse the metal.

'It is easier to pick up these scraps than it is to mine new ores. If you are good in a fight anyway, as many of these metals are in dangerous areas. Should you be willing to face the dangers, go to Shukabad, west of here, collect any time-worn swords you find there, and bring them to me.''Ah yes, ${PLAYER}, there is a good amount of useable metal here. Thank you!'Galâmka wishes to tell you of his plans to retake Maurûsh from the Orcs.Find Irkiri scouting to the east of Maurûsh and collect her scouting report for Galâmka.Locate Irkiri to the east of MaurûshRetrieve the scouting report from IrkiriRetrieve the scouting report from IrkiriFind Emlû scouting to the south of Maurûsh and collect his scouting report for Galâmka.Locate Emlû to the south of MaurûshSearch Emlû to see if you can find his scouting reportSearch Emlû for the scouting reportFind Zukhal scouting to the west of Maurûsh and collect her scouting report for Galâmka.Locate Zukhal to the west of MaurûshRetrieve the scouting report from Zukhal.Retrieve the scouting report from ZukhalBring the scouting reports back to Galâmka in Ub Nishir.'Welcome, ${PLAYER}. As we spoke of before, these Orcs have taken Maurûsh from us when the demon-pits opened, and we plan to reclaim it.

'I sent scouts to survey the Orcs' comings and goings in Maurûsh, and I need someone to retrieve their reports.'

Galâmka studies his map and gestures to points on it.

'You can find Irkiri near here, to the east of the stronghold. Emlû should be here, to the south. Then Zukhal, scouting here to the west.

'Find them and tell them I sent you. They should be expecting you.''I trust that since you have not attacked me, you must be the ${CLASS} that Galâmka sent.'

She hands you the scouting report.

'I have detailed the paths the Orcs take in this area while they themselves are scouting in my report. It worries me how close they are coming to our hideout, so we must deal with them soon. Bring this to Galâmka. I will remain here.''You have returned. I trust that you have gathered the reports I requested?'

You hand Galâmka the scouting reports retrieved and inform him of Emlû's fate.

'That is sad to hear of Emlû. He will be remembered. I am thankful you were able to retrieve these reports. Return to me when you have time and we can discuss what must be done with this information.''Aye, you must be the ${CLASS} of which Galâmka spoke.'

Zukhal hands you his scouting report.

'I have been tracking where the Orcs have been hiding their supplies. Their hiding locations have been noted in the report.'A Dumûri warrior is offering to escort you back to the Dubarâkh, should you desire it.Continue talking to the Dumûri warrior, should you wish to return to the Dubarâkh.Talk to the Dumûri warrior'Hashtal-gûr, ${PLAYER}. I have standing orders to escort you back to the Dubarâkh, if you wish to return there and study the documents. Please let me know if you would like me to take you there.''You would like to go then? This is wonderful news. Guard duty is so dull.'A Dumûri warrior is offering to escort you back to Girhâzi's Lodge in Iridír, should you desire it.Continue talking to the Dumûri warrior if you are ready to return to Iridír.Talk to the Dumûri warrior'Amazing, is it not? I wonder what knowledge is within all these scrolls. Are you finished here? I can lead you back to Iridír, if you would like.''Ready? Off we go.'The workers injured while working within Rakhatâb heard the tales of your service to the fort and your decision to not take part in the terrible game of chance that some enjoy. They have gathered rewards for your kindness.Marjadi wants to give you something for your nobility.Speak with Marjadi at Rakhatâb'I am glad you returned.''The workers continue to give me Ûr to provide you for the nobility you displayed in your discussion with Othax. Please accept this.'Enârshan has asked that you gather Sigêma and Bizgâr plants as well as defeat any Orcs near the Falls of Ilûritu.Enârshan has asked you to gather Sigêma and Bizgâr as well as defeat Orcs near the Falls of Ilûritu.Gather Sigêma flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather Bizgâr weeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Orcs near the Falls of Ilûritu (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Enârshan with the gathered ingredients in the Falls of Ilûritu.'I am in need of some plants for a concoction. It will be a potent weapon against the Orcs.

'Along the river flowing from these falls you will find flowers known as Sigêma, and Bizgâr, a weed. Gather any many as you can for me while I craft the rest.

'The river's edge has been tainted by the presence of Orcs as well. So dispose of any that you see.''Ah yes, these will do nicely.'

Enârshan takes the plants from you.

'And I trust that you disposed of any Orcs you saw tainting my waters? Good. We will drive them from these lands.

'I will finish the concoction shortly. Return to me when you are ready to travel back into Khûn Sagaz.'Some of Ashnân's livestock have been left out in the fields, and he needs your help sending them back home.Some of Ashnân's livestock have been left out in the fields, and he needs your help sending them back home. Find them near Burukíri and encourage them to return.Send cows back home (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Send horses back home (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have found the livestock that wandered off and sent them back home to Burukíri. Return to Ashnân and make sure he knows.Return to Ashnân in Burukíri'Greetings, ${CLASS}. Some of my livestock have wandered off and have not yet returned home. Might I trouble you with finding them in the surrounding fields and sending them back here?

'I would usually do this myself, but since my farm-hands left I do not have the time with all my other duties. I would gladly compensate you for the help.''I have been told that you found the animals and sent them home. I am grateful for your help. Please accept this for your troubles.'Make your way to Nâmbadir, the Span of Princes, and scout along it. Numûru fears the Orcs are increasing in number and streaming in from Urash Dâr.Go to Nâmbadir, the Span of Princes to the east of Kûr Anzar and search for signs of Orcs.Go to Nâmbadir, the Span of Princes and search for signs of OrcsGo a third of the way onto the span of Nâmbadir and scout south.Go a third of the way onto Nâmbadir and scout southGo half of the way onto the span of Nâmbadir and scout north.Go half of the way onto Nâmbadir and scout northGo two-thirds of the way onto the span of Nâmbadir and scout east, towards Urash Dâr.Go two-thirds of the way onto Nâmbadir and scout east, towards Urash DârReturn to Numûru in Urmâkh with your report.Return to Numûru in Urmâkh with your report'Mizâdi's spies have reported an Orc camp sighted near the crossing into Urash Dâr. However, it is not just the Orc encampment nearby that concerns us. Nâmbadir, the Span of Princes, has also been seen occupied by Orkish forces. Make your way to the bridge and let us know what you find. I fear this is only the tip of the spear, and we may soon have two sets of villains and dangers.''I had feared as much. The Orcs are moving from Urash Dâr into Imhûlar. We must bolster our defences to the east before we are over-run. Thank you, ${PLAYER}. This report may have saved countless lives, you have my thanks for your brave and selfless deeds.'Mizâdi has asked you to accompany Razâl and Numûru on a mission into Kûr Anzar to weaken the Barkhûshim.Speak with Mizâdi in Urmâkh when you are ready.Speak with Mizâdi when you are ready to goSpeak with Razâl near the tower in Kûr Anzar.Speak with Razâl near the tower in Kûr Anzar'We need to push aside grief. It grants us nothing, and threatens everything. A Shâra's burdens will not wait.

'I have need of your services once more, my friend. Razâl and Numûru have planned a raid into Kûr Anzar this night, to weaken the All-seeing fortifications and weapons, and take back some preciously needed supplies for our people here in Urmâkh. I would ask that you join them, as you can clearly handle yourself in combat.

'Meet with them outside Kûr Anzar this night. The time grows near for our assault on Kûr Anzar directly. This mission will help hasten that day, ${PLAYER}. Speak with me when you are ready to leave.'They've taken him into Angar Aragín. We must save him!''Be quick, be quiet and be careful. I will see you all again soon.'Thórvilon has requested your help in searching for a cure to the Lâg Dávrit, the Pale Blight afflicting Vartúlin and greater Imhûlar.Speak with Grove Elder Thórvilon and ascertain what is troubling him.Speak with Grove Elder Thórvilon and learn more of VartúlinSpeak with Grove-tender Ulthral about a poultice for Thórvilon's wife, Milingor. She can be found on the higher level of Vartúlin, near the bridge.Speak with Grove-tender Ulthral in Vartúlin about Milingor's poulticeSpeak with Milingor, Thórvilon's wife, in her Veróth across the bridge from Thórvilon in Vartúlin.Speak with Milingor in her VeróthPrune dead Sarláshi limbs from Milingor's Veróth.Prune dead Sarláshi limbs from Milingor's Veróth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak once more with Grove Elder Thórvilon at the edge of Vartúlin.Speak once more with Grove Elder ThórvilonSpeak with Avadhril to ascertain the details of contacting Usakâr the Hermit.Speak with Avadhril in VartúlinGo to the grove Avadhril mentioned east of Vartúlin and obtain some oranges for Usakâr.Pick up oranges from under dying orange trees (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find Dag Usakâra, Usakâr's home. Avadhril mentioned it was east of Vartúlin, where the mountain ridge meets an open meadow.Find Dag Usakâra, Usakâr's home east of VartúlinSpeak with Usakâr and offer him the oranges.Thórvilon greets you cautiously.

'Though you are an outsider, you have the look of someone capable. I am quite desperate, enough so that I would turn to a stranger for our salvation. This grove you see is dying. My people are dying. My wife... my wife is struggling. She is wearying, fading before my very eyes. I cannot bear it.

'These eyes have seen such sights... countless miracles over thousands of years. Never did I think I would see such nightmares as these. The land cursed, the ground parched, forests as dry and white as bone. All my friends, all those I love, destined to fade and be forgotten.

'I will not fade so easily. I will not let this grove crumble to dust. That is not my path. I have a desperate idea, and you seem capable. Will you help me - will you help our people?''There is a man who treats with us, Usakâr. His ways are strange, but I believe he may have a powerful friend - Cúridwan, the Golden Maiden. She is someone who could help us heal Vartúlin, this grove you see around you. Ever since the southern men made their way through our forests, the trees have started dying, turning hard and white as bone. We call it Lag Dávrit, the Pale Blight.

'I believe it is tied to the southern men, but I cannot be sure. Much of what they do is profane to nature, as they burn and cut the trees and brush they meet, rather than exist within it. I believe Usakâr knows more about the Lag Dávrit, as well as the knowledge of how to contact Cúridwan. She has the power to cure the Lag Dávrit, if she wishes it. I know it in my bones.

'Before you go after Usakâr, would you check on Milingor, my wife? She is behind me, half into the Veróth growing over the bridge. It pains me to see her so. I wish to help her, to stop her Wearying, as she feels it is not her time yet. But yet the Veróth still readily accepts her. I do not wish for her to go yet. Selfishly, I want more time with my beloved.

'Also, if there are any dead branches on her Veróth, please prune them. It is better for her. I cannot do it myself right now. I cannot bear it.

'Perhaps Grove-tender Ulthral has a poultice to comfort Milingor? You should stop there first. She is on the path above me.''Thorvilon asked you to check on me? He is sweet to ask. And thank Ulthral for me, for this poultice....

'I thought I would undergo the Trothúl, the Wearying, when I was ready to leave this place. I am not ready, little one. I don't want to go yet.

'There is much I would still see and do in this place, with Thórvilon. He tells me to save my energy, that I need to sustain my strength another season and that Cúridwan will soon help us. My strength is fleeting, little one. Each day I see a little less of this grove, my home. Each day I feel increasingly unmoored, less myself.

'I still feel the wind in my limbs, the dry, wheezing breeze. I feel the cold and the heat on my bark. I wish... I wish... I wish many things.

'I love Thórvilon very much. I will hold on for as long as I can.''Thank you for your kindness. It is hard some days, to bear all the burdens nature has placed upon us. I only wish for Milingor's safety, and the safety and health of all the Adúrhid in this grove. It seems a tall order this day, and most days, however.

'If we are to survive, we need you to convince Usakâr to tell you what he knows of Cúridwan. If you can find her, please, let her know how desperately we need a cure for this Pale Blight. Look around you. This was once Laithór, the Emerald Woods. It has been transformed in a Man's span into Favrathór, the Forest of Bone. So many plants and animals are afflicted with disease. We have held it off for as long as we can, however now it has crept into Vartúlin itself. We have nowhere left to go.

'Avadhril knows more about Usakâr. She often treats with him. She will know how to find him and what boons to bring with you. I believe the Golden Maiden can help us survive. We just need to find her.''Lidath mâd, outsider. I am fond of Thórvilon, as I believe his heart is fair, but I do not agree that there is a way to save our people. We are destined to all join in Milingor's fate, and soon, I believe. Nevertheless, Thórvilon is our leader, and I will follow his wishes. If he wishes you to treat with Usakâr, I will tell you how to do so.

'Usakâr is one of the few friends we count among Men. He has always been a loyal ally and friend to the Adúrhid. It is customary for us to send with our envoys to him a gift, part of nature's bounty. As you can see, nature has struggled and her bounty is little more than leaves and ash this season.

'There exists not far from here to the east, however, a small grove of orange trees. When last I walked this orchard, there still were a few oranges clinging to life on one of the orange trees. Bring him a gift of those oranges. I wish I could offer more, but as you can see we barely have anything to give. The southern men have cursed this land. I fear there is nothing we few who remain can do to reverse their savage violence on Favrathór, what was once Laithór, the Emerald Wood, but which is now the Forest of Bone.

'After you have the oranges, continue east along the mountain ridge. Where the mountain meets meadow, there you shall find Dag Usakâra, the home of Usakâr.''You bring oranges, so you must be an envoy of the Adúrhid. I keep telling them not to bother sending me fruit, I don't need it. But they, ah, keep to the old ways it seems.

'You are a strange envoy indeed, from the Adúrhid. What's that? Cúridwan? She is a myth! A legend! A terrible cook! Ah, perhaps the cat's out of the bag with that, I suppose. And cats seldom go back into bags once let out. Anyway!

'I have kept Cúridwan's location and identity jealously my own for a very long time. Still, this forest continues to worsen. I know the Adúrhid continue to worsen as well. As the forest goes, so they go. Perhaps it is time to pay Cúridwan a visit after all.

'Don't tell her I called her a terrible cook. She'll be feeding me her blackened chicken pie for months as a punishment. Alright, let's be off then, if you're ready! But keep close! These woods are quite dangerous to outsiders, and many have simply disappeared in them, never to be seen again. I long for the days when a burnt chicken pie was the most dangerous thing I had to dodge.''Milingor? Yes, she is Wearying. But we can make her transition comfortable! I have just the thing.

'Here, take this poultice to her. It is little more than tea, I confess, but sometimes tea is exactly what one needs! At the very least, it is warm and will comfort her.'Usakâr has agreed to show you the way to the home of Cúridwan, the Golden Maiden, to try to find a cure for the Lâg Dávrit, the Pale Blight sweeping through the woods of Imhûlar.Speak with Usakâr and he will mark your map with the route to Cúridwan's home.Speak with Usakâr at Dag Usakâra to mark your mapFind your way to the first point Usakâr has marked on your map.Find your way to the first point Usakâr has markedFind your way to the second point Usakâr has marked on your map.Find your way to the second point Usakâr has markedFind your way to the third point Usakâr has marked on your map.Find your way to the third point Usakâr has markedSpeak with Usakâr at the mouth of the cave.Speak with Usakâr at the mouth of the cave'If we are to be off, let's be quick about it! This is no time for idle wandering.

'Let me mark the important areas on your map. You must pass through these areas, and in this order or you won't get there at all. I will meet you there. I know several ancient paths that few men remember, and fewer men tread. There we are! I will meet you outside the cave to Kûgrun, Kugêmi's sanctuary.''Ah, here we are. And right on time, too.''You're ready? Hmm, that is good. You seem to be of stout heart and constitution, which is what this journey and any pies we eat shall require. All right, let's be off!'Enter the cave and find Cúridwan to ascertain whether she can help you cure the Lâg Dávrit.Speak with Usakâr by the cave door.Speak with Usakâr by the cave doorGo through the cave entrance and enter Kûgrun, home of Cúridwan.Go through the cave entrance and enter KûgrunSpeak with Cúridwan, the Golden Maiden by her cottage.Speak with Cúridwan, the Golden Maiden by her homeAsk Cúridwan about the ingredients necessary for the salve.Ask Cúridwan about the ingredients necessary for the salveSpeak with Usakâr in Kûgrun.Speak with Usakâr in KûgrunThank Cúridwan for her aid in the Kintai's plight.Thank Cúridwan for her aid in the Kintai's plightGather ingredients for Cúridwan: marsh-strider bark and bog flowers from the marsh at Zahûmakh to the east of Kûgrun, scorpion venom and berries from Dûlagig to the north of Kûgrun.Gather bog flowers from the marsh at Zahûmakh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather bark from marsh-striders at Zahûmakh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather wild berries from Dûlagig (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather scorpion venom from Dûlagig (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Cúridwan in Kûgrun with the ingredients you've gathered.'Here we are. I knew we'd make it. I know this cave like the back of my own hand.''Go quickly. Collect the ingredients and bring them straight back here. I believe that Cúridwan can do as she says. I have seen wondrous things from her before, things you would not believe if I told you. She can save the Kintai and reverse the Lâg Dávrit.''Are you ready? It's time to meet her. Go through the cave door behind me. She is waiting.''Cúridwan? Ah, yes, the Adúrhid do call me that. I have many names, but that one suits me as well any.

'The Lâg Dávrit? Yes, as you can see, I've been fighting it in my own way, and recently I've made a breakthrough of sorts. A salve I've made that I believe can reverse the Pale Blight and restore the natural way of things. But I have quite run out of ingredients.

'I can help you, and the Kintai, but I need your help in collecting more of the ingredients for this salve.''There are four ingredients I need you to gather in order to create this salve.

'I require marsh-strider bark, from the marshes of Zahumakh. I also need unblemished bog flowers that grow near there.

'I need scorpion venom, from the scorpion dens of Dûlagig. I also require unblemished berries that grow in the scrub brush near Dûlagig.''Let's see, do we have everything here? Venom, bark, berries, bog.... Seems so! Give me just a moment then....

'There. Those items have been fashioned together. Now it needs to sit for several hours and steep to properly finish it. While it does, I believe there is one more thing we must do in order for this salve to work permanently, and not merely be a passing hope for the Kintai.''I wish we had more time to talk, ${PLAYER}. I see great things in you.

'I believe our paths will cross again after this. But for now, gather these ingredients for me, and we may yet stop the Lâg Dávrit in its tracks. The Adúrhid of Imhûlar will not breathe their last if I can help it. Bring me those ingredients, and quickly, and the Adúrhid will have their miracle.'Cúridwan has tasked you with destroying three great founding stones brought to Imhûlar by the Ordâkhai.Curidwan has tasked you with destroying Ordâkhai founding stones at Ghât Lor. Ghât Lor can be found far to the east of Kûgrun.Destroy Ordâkhai founding stones at Ghât Lor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Cúridwan in Kûgrun.Return to Cúridwan in KûgrunTake Cúridwan's salve.Take Cúridwan's salveUse the first phial of salve on the river behind Cúridwan's cottage to heal Vartúlin.Use the salve on the river to heal VartúlinSpeak with Cúridwan before you leave.Speak with Cúridwan before you leaveSpeak with Usakâr in Kûgrun.'There is one more task we must accomplish, if we actually wish to defeat the Lâg Dávrit permanently. You were probably too young to remember, ${PLAYER}, but the Lâg Dávrit is a recent affliction. It's been here for a little longer than a man's span, afflicting Imhûlar. It came with the Men of Ordâkh, as they made their way north from their strongholds further south.

'I believe their founding stones may have something to do with the Lâg Dávrit. I have sensed a powerful, foreboding energy from them. I believe they must be broken, if the Lâg Dávrit is to be properly defeated, and not merely turned back for a season.

'This salve needs time to complete. The Men of Ordâkh make their camp at Ghat Lor. Destroy the founding stones there. I believe that will rob the Lâg Dávrit of its power. Return here when you are finished. Hopefully by then the salve and my chicken pie will both be done.''Perfect timing. The salve just finished, and so did the blackened chicken pie in the oven.'

Usakâr briefly looks panicked. Cúridwan leans in conspiratorially.

'He complains, but he loves my blackened chicken pie.'

She leans out again, and returns to her normal volume.

'I will get the salve for you. It's a shame you both can't stay for dinner.''Ah, yes. Here is the salve. I made sure you got enough for all of Vartúlin. This river you see behind me empties directly into Vartúlin. Take this first phial and dump all its contents in the river behind me. I have a second phial for you as well, to take back to Thórvilon, so he may start the rebuilding process in the forests of Adagím outside of Vartúlin.''You have done much this day for the Adúrhid. You are quite the potent ally for them. I hope you know I appreciate your efforts as well.

'Here is the other phial of the salve. Use it to purify areas untouched by the waters near Vartúlin, or give it to the Adúrhid for the same purpose.

'Our paths will cross again, my friend. I have seen it. Until then, may your travels be safe and your belly be full. We can scarcely ask for more.''This is wonderful news! Come, we must return to Vartúlin immediately. I will return with you to Thorvilon. He will be overjoyed - I know he has wished for this day to come for many years. It has been a long losing fight against the Lâg Dávrit for Thórvilon and the Adúrhid, until now.'With the salve applied to the waters that run into Vartúlin, Usakâr urges you to return there quickly, to tell Thórvilon and the other Kintai the good news.Speak with Usakâr to return to Vartúlin.Speak with Usakâr when you are ready to goUse Cúridwan's salve to heal areas afflicted with the Lâg Dávrit, the Pale Blight around Vartúlin.Use Cúridwan's salve to heal areas around Vartúlin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Thórvilon near the edge of Vartúlin.'Come, we must return quickly to Vartúlin to let Thórvilon know!''Thank you for everything you've done. We still have so much to do, but now we have hope because of you.

'You are welcome to come to Vartúlin and sit in our shade any season, my friend. Though there is still much to do, I am buoyed that the winds are turning and the emerald leaves will be returning to Favrathór. I wish so much that Milingor was here to see this. I - I wish so much. But thank you, truly, for all you've done for us.

'Avadhril would have your help, if you wish to further aid us.''We must make haste to let Thórvilon know the good news!'Speak with Thórvilon and let him know the good news about finding a cure for the Lâg Dávrit.Thórvilon has gathered with some others around Milingor's Veróth. You should join them.Join Thórvilon near Milingor's VeróthListen to Thórvilon.Listen to ThórvilonComfort Thórvilon.Comfort ThórvilonListen to Thórvilon and Usakâr's conversation.Listen to Thórvilon and Usakâr's conversationSpeak with Avadhril nearby.Speak with Avadhril nearby'I see now the strength Thórvilon possesses. He has set aside his grief to be present for his people. I don't believe in miracles or sorcerers, friend. There are far too few of both left in this world. But I believe in him. I believe in Thórvilon. I will give what strength I have to him, that Vartúlin might flourish again.'The fence, Rashâm, wishes to return the Ghôlkhas armour, and would like help in paying respects to the noble family from whom it was stolen.Kheb Hanût is in the north-western corner of Tâkhdar.

The fence, Rashâm, has suggested you search for fallen coins in the black market of Kheb Hanût. He wants to pay a symbolic token of apology for the Ghôlkhas tomb-robbing.Enter Kheb HanûtOld and forgotten coins will be found in Kheb Hanût, in the north-west of Tâkhdar.

Rashâm would like you to collect some keepsake coins in the black market that no one will miss to represent a funerary token.Look for fallen coins in Kheb Hanût (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})A good spot facing the sea is south of the Fisherfold in Umbar Baharbêl.

Rashâm has asked you to drop old coins into the ocean by the Fisherfold in remembrance of a fallen hero whose tomb was robbed.Drop the coins into the seaOkhtâr Ghôlkhas is waiting inside Dâr Laja.

You have paid your respects to the long-departed ancestor by dropping coins to the sea. Hopefully Rashâm has returned the Ghôlkhas armour by now. You should see if Okhtâr has news.Speak with Okhtâr Ghôlkhas'The armour Zulkhêma sold me was wrested from a wealthy family's mausoleum, you say? That conniving woman, selling me something at so high a price; I could not sell something so distinctive! I may deal in ill-gained goods, but I am no grave-robber, and I thank you for warning me away. Did this Ghôlkhas family member tell you the location of the tomb, by chance? No, of course not.

'I must find a way to express my apology and return the armour without being noticed. Please bestow some respects to this slain ancestor on my behalf, perhaps tossing them into the sea near the Fisherfold. Find some coins; it is our way.''I would not ask you to waste your own coin-purse on a sentimental errand. It cannot be too difficult to find other coins lying about here. You would be surprised what people allow to go missing.''Have you found any scuffed or faded old coins yet? Look around here. I am certain someone long ago might have lost some. I am of the mind we only require two. One for each eye of the departed.''I may be a fence, but I respect our funerary customs. The Fisherfold faces the sea. I would think it would be easy to find a good place in the water to respect the departed, even if we cannot place coins over their eyes ourselves.''So you have paid your respects? Then my conscience is clear. I will find my way inside the Ghôlkhas manor to return the armour. You do not need to know the particulars. By the time you speak with Okhtâr, I will have performed my task, I swear.''The most exciting individual crept past my guards, I am told. Do you know how rare it is for any such miscreant to evade my manor's defences? What a tale to tell! I do not much mind; whoever this character was, they seem to have returned my armour to me. This must have been your doing.

'As promised, your reward. Do not tell me of your adventures; I prefer to imagine them!'Defeat many sand-sifters in Khûd Zagin.Defeat many sand-sifters in Khûd Zagin.Defeat many sand-sifters in Khûd ZaginDefeat a great many sand-sifters in Khûd Zagin.Defeat many sand-sifters in Khûd Zagin.Defeat a great many sand-sifters in Khûd Zagin.Defeat a great many sand-sifters in Khûd ZaginWorking with Nimasi, you have traced the banner attacks to a large camp in southern Imhûlar. Investigate the camp without being seen to discover the source of these attacks.Speak with Nimasi outside the camp when you are ready to go.Speak with Nimasi when you are ready to goDeliver Shâr Bârshud's message to Mizâdi in Kûr Anzar.Deliver Shâr Bârshud's message to Mizâdi in Kûr Anzar'We must get inside that camp and get close to that main tent in the back. I am sure whoever is in charge will be in there. If we hope to save Surâsh and end these attacks, we need to know who these people are and what they are planning.

'We also must locate Surâsh, but we should only free her after we've scouted the enemy and found out all we can of their plans, as the noise and commotion may waylay any intelligence gathering.

'We must be stealthy as we move. There are too many of them for a frontal assault. Are you ready?''I cannot believe Nimasi turned on us. This is most troubling. Most troubling. And the danger to you was grave, I must be better about who I allow into the Subuzûri.'

Mizâdi appears to steel herself. A sudden coldness overtakes her face.

'I don't care how many soldiers the Hûl has proffered him. He has not yet felt the might of the Subuzûri.

'Very well. If it is a war he wants, then he shall have one.

'But I will not allow the people of Kûr Anzar to feel war's cold comforts once more. I will meet him in open battle. War is coming, ${PLAYER}. War is coming to Imhûlar.''Are you ready? Steel yourself, we are about to go into the lair of these monsters.'Nâmi has asked you thin out the number of scorpions in Dul Râkh to the west.Nâmi has asked you to travel to the cave in Dul Râkh and thin the number of scorpions in the area.Travel to Dul RâkhDefeat scorpions inside the cave at Dul Râkh for Nâmi at the Dumûri camp in Urash Dâr.Defeat scorpions in Dul Râkh cave (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Nâmi in Urash Dâr and let her know you have thinned the number of scorpions in Dul Râkh.Return to Nâmi'${CLASS}, I am glad to see you here. We here have been battling with the Anâkhi in their cave, Dul Râkh, nearby.

'I ask that you help us to turn the tide as we are needed in many places since Utug-bûr was opened. If you can, go to Dul Râkh and find their cave. Inside you must cleanse it of these vicious scorpions that the Anâkhi worship.''Greetings, ${CLASS}.

'I gather that you have returned from Dul Râkh successful in your task. I thank you for your help in this fight.

'The Anâkhi and their beasts will be less of a threat for now.'Defeat many scorpions in Imhûlar.Defeat many scorpions in Imhûlar.Defeat many scorpions in ImhûlarDefeat a great many scorpions in Imhûlar.Defeat many scorpions in Imhûlar.Defeat a great many scorpions in Imhûlar.Defeat a great many scorpions in ImhûlarDefeat many scorpions in Urash Dâr.Defeat many scorpions in Urash Dâr.Defeat many scorpions in Urash DârDefeat a great many scorpions in Urash Dâr.Defeat many scorpions in Urash Dâr.Defeat a great many scorpions in Urash Dâr.Defeat a great many scorpions in Urash DârDefeat many scorpions in Ambarûl.Defeat many scorpions in Ambarûl.Defeat many scorpions in AmbarûlDefeat a great many scorpions in Ambarûl.Defeat many scorpions in Ambarûl.Defeat a great many insects in Ambarûl.Defeat a great many scorpions in AmbarûlSlay many scorpions throughout the Ikorbân Valley.Slay many scorpions throughout the Ikorbân Valley.Complete Scorpion-slayer of Ambarûl (Advanced)Complete Scorpion-bane of Imhûlar (Advanced)Complete Scorpion-bane of Urash Dâr (Advanced)Explore friendly settlements, structures, tombs, and other important points of interest in Ambarûl in the Ikorbân Valley.Explore friendly settlements, structures, tombs, and other important points of interest in Ambarûl in the Ikorbân Valley.Find IridírFind SûruFind Telperiën's WallFind The Flood-spanFind the WrackwadeFind BurukíriFind Asha MûnFind MehêturFind EkagarFind GishtirFind ArwáthFind the DubarâkhFind Esh EnûnFind Gha NêkhaMizâdi asks you to scout the Orc camp near the Span of Danagír. If possible, destroy the Orkish weapons in their racks.Mizâdi has asked you to scout the Orc camp near the Span of Danagír, sabotaging the Orkish weapons racks as you go.Scout the entrance to the Orc campScout the bend in the Orc campScout deeper in the campDestroy Orkish weapons racks (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Scout the back of the Orc camp.Scout the back of the campDefeat the Utûgi Devastator.Defeat the Utûgi DevastatorReturn to Mizâdi in Urmâkh with your report.Return to Mizâdi in Urmâkh'It is not only the Barkhûshim we must contend with. It seems a Shâra can never rest, ${PLAYER}. We have been hearing rumours, reports of odd things near the Span of Danagír to the east. My scouts recount stories of Orcs and something larger... even more sinister. We know not how strong they are or where they come from, but these rumours are quite concerning.

'Go to the Span of Danagír. My spies tell me a band of Orcs has encamped near there. Scout the camp and count their number. If you have the opportunity, destroy their racked weapons so they cannot threaten Renewed Hamât. We have enough to deal with in the Barkhûshim in Kûr Anzar. I will not have another group of villains move towards us. Gather what information you can, and then report back to me. Do not take unnecessary risks. I fear for your safety if my scouts' reports are true.''How big was it? That is quite worrying. I fear that this incursion is only the tip of a great spear about to plunge into Renewed Hamât. I must think on this more. Nevertheless, thank you. Many would have run from such a sight. It is truly only the valorous that would fight such a beast and live to tell the tale.'Sûlmur has blank papyrus scrolls that need to be delivered.You have been asked to deliver blank papyrus scrolls to a woman named Amâsu, who is in Iridír, a town in Ambarûl east of Mehêtur.'I understand that you must continue your travels. Thank you for your company and for indulging me. Are you continuing east? In the village of Iridír there is an old woman called Amâsu. I owe her three scrolls. Would you deliver them for me?

'As busy as I appear, would you believe I have very few customers? Last year I had more work than time. The Great Southern Empire of Ordâkh ruled here until not long ago, and they were my only customers. Sadly, they did not allow our people to learn to read or write, so I am unsure what the future has in store for me.

'Amâsu is a kindly woman, and probably just bought some of my scrolls to be charitable.'

Sûlmur laughs again, but this time you sense discomfort.

'Well, whether she needs them or not, she paid, so the order will be fulfilled. Would you mind? The roads are perilous and I would prefer to stay here.''Would you deliver three scrolls for me? In the village of Iridír to the east, there is an old woman called Amâsu, who has already paid for them.'Hello lûkal, what is this?'

She takes the scrolls from you.

'Ah yes, from Sûlmur. Thank you for bringing these. How is Sûlmur, is she well? Has she gone after that handsome rice farmer yet?'

You tell her Sûlmur is well, but has not gone after Turizi yet. Amâsu sighs wistfully.

'Ah well, it is only a matter of time I suppose.'Khûldim Umûn has informed Girhâzi that the Dubarâkh is inside an abandoned salt mine. You are invited to join them as they search the caves for the lost library of Ambarûli culture and history.Talk to Girhâzi when you are ready to travel to the salt mine in search of the Dubarâkh.Complete Instance: Searching for HopeYou accompanied Girhâzi to explore the abandoned salt mine of Ashunûg in search of the Dubarâkh. Instead of a library, you found a cult and Khûldim Umûn found death at the hands of his would-be rescuers.Talk to GirhâziFrustrated at her failure to locate the Dubarâkh, Girhâzi needs a moment to herself and sent you to talk to Amâsu instead.Talk to Amâsu'I could not have gotten this information without you, ${PLAYER}. Would you like to come with us to search this salt mine? I will gather some Dumûri volunteers and get Khûldim ready to be moved. Let me know when you are ready and we will be on our way.''You are ready to go on this expedition? Then let us be off.''I am unsurprised that Khûldim lied to us. I only wish it had not been so. Curse it all, now we have no hope of finding the Dubarâkh! That coward got himself killed when he could have gone home to Ordâkh! What a fool! He lied to us for no reason but to deprive us of something we want.'

You can see her sadness shifting into anger.

'I will never understand why people hate us so. Leave me be, I need to think. Talk to Amâsu if you must talk to someone.''Please excuse Girhâzi's behaviour. I have noticed that when she does not wish to feel pain, she recasts it into anger. It has been so since Ukhâx and her boys were taken from her. Her pain is something she will eventually have to face, but let us not worry ourselves about it today.'Tibira gave a donkey and some supplies to Andur, formerly a soldier of Ordâkh and then a bandit, and sent him to collect some of the semi-precious gemstones that can be found in the desert. She says he should have returned by now and has asked for your help in finding what became of him.Andur is supposed to be in the hills east of Western Khanâg. You should go there and look for him.Find AndurYou have found Andur in the hills east of Western Khanâg, exactly where he is supposed to be. You should talk to Andur.Talk to AndurYou have found Andur exactly where he is supposed to be, but the donkey is wounded. Andur is caring for the donkey and has asked you to collect the semi-precious stones from the pebbles for him.Collect colourful stones from the loose gravel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have found Andur exactly where he is supposed to be, but the donkey is wounded. Andur is caring for the donkey and has asked you to collect the semi-precious stones from the pebbles for him. You have collected the stones, and should now talk to Andur.You have found Andur exactly where he is supposed to be, tending to the wounded donkey. You collected the semi-precious stones for him, which he said he will carry back to the town. You should return to Tibira and give her an update.Talk to Tibira in Western KhanâgYou have found Andur exactly where he is supposed to be, tending to the wounded donkey. You collected the semi-precious stones for him, which he said he will carry back to the town. You returned to Tibira and as you were giving her an update, Andur arrived. You should talk to Andur.Talk to AndurYou have found Andur exactly where he is supposed to be, tending to the wounded donkey. You collected the semi-precious stones for him, which he said he will carry back to the town. You returned to Tibira and as you were giving her an update, Andur arrived. You should continue talking to Tibira.Talk to Tibira'${PLAYER}, I had hired a man named Andur, who said he was your friend, to collect gemstone pebbles. I gave him a donkey and some supplies and sent him to an area east of here, where I know the colourful stones can be scooped up from the gravel.

'He has not yet returned, and I worry that he perhaps got lost or ran afoul of some beast in the desert. Would you mind looking to see what became of him?'

Though you want to think the best of Andur, you can't help but wonder if the man perhaps took Tibira's donkey, never to return.'${PLAYER}, what are you doing here? No matter, I could use your help. The donkey got stung by an usan-kûni, and I have been tending to the animal. The poor thing is in much pain, but I must try and keep her still to prevent the venom from spreading from her leg to other parts of her body. I think she will be fine, we only need a little more time to rest.

'I have not yet been able to collect any of the coloured stones for which Tibira sent us seeking. Since you are here, would you mind doing that while I keep the donkey calm? That way when she is ready to move on, we can head back to Western Khanâg immediately.''You have collected the stones? Thank you ${PLAYER}, we will be able to leave that much sooner now. She is almost better and will be fit to walk before long. Thank you once again for your help, ${PLAYER}. I will take the stones and will be off to Western Khanâg shortly.''Welcome back, ${PLAYER}, did you find Andur?'

You fill her in on recent events, secretly still not entirely sure if Andur can be trusted to not steal the stones and the donkey.

'Oh, speaking of, there he is now!''Did you only just get here, ${PLAYER}? It seems that I caught up to you very quickly!

'I give you my gratitude again for taking a chance and trusting me. Most people would have slain me where I stood in the desert. You have given me a second chance at life, and I will not squander it. Thank you, my friend.''It is good to see Andur has returned unharmed. I could use his help with many odd jobs and errands, and I will gladly employ him for as long as he would like to stay. Not to say that you were not good help, ${PLAYER}, but I imagine that you will soon be moving on.'Mizâdi has asked you to lead the charge to secure the lower ward of Kûr Anzar. Once successful, Mizâdi can set up a foothold outside Kûr Anzar.Ready yourself for battle, then move swiftly into Kûr Anzar and defeat the forces of the All-seeing. Find and defeat the loathsome Barkhûshim leading them, Rokóbu. Kûr Anzar is located east of Urmâkh.Defeat Barkhûshim champions in Kûr Anzar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Barkhûshim skirmishers in Kûr Anzar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat a Barkhûshim sorceress in Kûr AnzarFind and defeat Rokóbu in Kûr AnzarReport your success to Mizâdi in Urmâkh.Report your success to Mizâdi in Urmâkh'We are close to retaking Kûr Anzar and driving the loathsome Barkhûshim out. Soon we will reunite all of Hamât under our banner of hope. Kûr Anzar is the key.

'We need to seize a foothold in Kûr Anzar, from which we may strike at the heart of Okhíso and his twisted realm. You are to be the point of our spear, ${PLAYER}. It's time to make our move. We ask that you move through the lower portion of the city and drive their forces back in the lower ward. We know Okhíso's loathsome aide, Rokóbu to be leading them. If you get the chance, plunge your sword into his chest for me. Now is the time that Hamât rises again!''This is quite the day, my friend. Quite the triumph. And you killed Rokóbu?'

Mizadi lets out a long, loud whoop of triumph.

'That will prove to be a severe blow to Okhíso. We still have much to do before we can declare victory, but this is a huge first step. Without your bravery, I fear we would have been lost, ${PLAYER}. You have my thanks.Dilûsu has asked you to help him deal with another group of brigands nearby that have been attacking people trying to flee.Dilûsu has asked you to help him deal with a group of brigands near Zikrum-dûl who have been attacking people as they flee the Orcs.Defeat brigands in Zikrum-dûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Dilûsu now that you have made the area safer from the brigands.Return to Dilûsu near Zikrum-dûl'Ah, fortunate timing, ${CLASS}. You look like a capable adventurer.

'People here could use your help if you are willing. A group of brigands nearby in Zikrum-dûl has been preying on the weak as they flee the demons in the area.

'It is a step too far for them to be attacking and robbing folk who are trying to escape this cursed land. They must be stopped if you find yourself in the area.''I have reports that the fiends in Zikrum-dûl have been dealt with. I trust I have you to thank for that, ${CLASS}.

'This road will now be safer for people in need... for now, that is.'Mizâdi's trusted scout, Razâl, has gone missing. She has asked you to search the western outskirts of Kûr Anzar for signs of his whereabouts.Razâl, Mizâdi's trusted scout, hasn't reported back in a day. Investigate the eastern outskirts of Kûr Anzar for signs of Razâl. Kûr Anzar is located east of Urmâkh.Investigate the outskirts of Kûr Anzar for signs of RazâlFree Razâl from his bonds so you both can escape before the Barkhûshim notice you.Free Razâl from his bonds so you both can escapeFind the three locations Razâl mentioned on the western outskirts north of where he was captured and scout Kûr Anzar from each of them.Scout the first outlook into Kûr AnzarScout the second outlook into Kûr AnzarScout the third outlook into Kûr AnzarSpeak with Mizâdi in Urmâkh.Speak with Mizâdi in Urmâkh'Hashtal-gûr, ${PLAYER}. We are in need of someone with your rare talents. My best scout, Razâl, has not reported back to Numûru in the past day. He was scouting Kûr Anzar, and I fear the Barkhûshim, those twisted adherents to the Church of the All-seeing, may have captured him.

'You seem like you can handle yourself, perhaps better than some warriors I might send. Please, find Razâl for me. He was sent to the eastern outskirts of Kûr Anzar, to map the movements of the Barkhûshim. If he has been captured, it is likely there you may find him, or some clue to his whereabouts. We need every soldier we have, particularly one with Razâl's talent for burgling. Please, if you find him, order him to report back to me immediately. He is one of my best warriors, but he takes such foolish risks sometimes.''I am grateful to you. As you can see, Razâl made it back safely. Hopefully he is a bit wiser for the wear, but he escaped with his skin due to your valour, so for that I am in your debt. Thank you for seeing to this task. I have another, larger task for you when you are ready. One that is suitable for someone of such skill.'Amalíbi asks you to seek the wisdom and aid of the peculiar Elves living in an oasis in the south of Khûd Zagin. The Elves are secluded and do not often engage with Men.Amalíbi asks you to make your way south of Ghalbûru to a hidden oasis called Shonith, where Elves live and seclude themselves from the difficulties and trials of Man.Amilíbi appears frustrated.

'We hoped the response from Jombahok or Khadûr would be swift. Alas, both captains consolidate their positions rather than risking further hostility. Their inaction creates unease.

'We could ask you to press our enemies harder and push for all-out warfare. Or, we can seek more allies.

'We chose the latter.

'We wonder if you will act as our emissary to the Elves in the south at Shonith. They will no longer speak to us, and we do not know why.

'Their last oasis lies far to the south-west, deep within the crags. Will you seek them out?''We know the plight of the men who dwell in the wastes of Khûd Zagin. I cannot pledge to any cause of Man. Not while we struggle to maintain what little we can of the natural world.

'Do you not see the horror growing all around you? Do you not see that this is the last vestige of us in the world?

'No, we struggle to live our own lives. We can spend no effort to aid those men.'Porókho has told you that there are places in Ilmabiri where relics of ancient Númenor can still be found. He said that if you bring him some, he will give you coin for them.Porókho believes Númenórean relics may be found in the eastern part of Ilmabiri, beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. You should go there and collect them.Collect Númenórean relics (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected Númenórean relics found in the sewers. You should bring them to Porókho at Hêbatokh, his camp in Ilmabiri.'Listen, if you are not opposed to... acquiring items, I have a proposition for you.'

He scratches his beard thoughtfully as he considers you.

'These sewers are one of the oldest parts of the city. They were built by Men of Númenor, and the fact that they are still working today is a testament to their knowledge and skill. You can see their influence in much of the architecture. There are some areas of Ilmabiri where Númenorian relics can still be found. If you come across any, bring them to me, and I will give you some coin in exchange for them. I think you can find some to the east.''Oh thank you, my friend, these are in excellent condition. You have really come through for old Porókho today!'Amalíbi asks you to return to the Ordâkhai camp overlooking Jirush to post the false notice. She also supplied with the sounding horn to draw out the guards to see the note.Amalíbi provided the notice and a sounding horn and asked you to make your way to the Ordâkhai camp north of Jirush. You need to find a suitable location to post the notice and then find a suitable place to hide, and blow the horn.You posted the inciting letter. You should retreat to a location concealed from the entrance and blow the sounding horn to draw a guard to gate.A soldier emerged from the camp, took the note, and immediately called for Jombahok. Return to Amalíbi at Ghalbûru and tell her of the success.Return to Amalíbi with news from the Ordâkhai encampment'Our liberation is at hand. This letter will draw the two captains into a conflict that will weaken their number and provide us with the opening we need to lay them low.

'Go to the encampment north of Jirush. Post this on the gates. Then take this horn, find a place to hide, blow it, and wait for the reaction of the soldier who finds it.

'Then return to me with what you learn.'You recount the soldier's actions at the encampment.

'Nothing more than Jombahok's name?'

She looks concerned.

'I do not understand what this means. I do not know what reaction I expected, but our scouts say there is no movement from either encampment.'

She sighs.

'We have done all we can. Please accept this with my thanks. Return to me from time to time. Perhaps the anger will seethe and grow into something.'Mizâdi has received word from her spies that her missing husband, Eshtali, has been sighted near the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi. Make your way there and look for clues to his whereabouts.Search the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi south of Urmâkh for signs of Mizâdi's missing husband, Eshtali. Mizâdi said he would be wearing crimson robes.Search three spots around Esh-kimâkhi for clues as to Eshtali's whereaboutsContinue searching Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi south of Urmâkh for signs of Mizâdi's missing husband, Eshtali. Mizâdi said he would be wearing crimson robes.Search around Esh-kimâkhi for clues as to Eshtali's whereaboutsExamine the man to determine if he is Eshtali.Examine the man to determine if he is EshtaliGive Mizâdi in Urmâkh news of her husband's death.Give Mizâdi in Urmâkh news of her husband's death'I have a personal matter with which I would ask your assistance, ${PLAYER}.

'I have received word from my spies of a rumour that my husband, Eshtali, has recently been seen outside the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi to the south of here. What he is doing there, I have no idea.

'The leader of the Barkhûshim, that accursed Okhíso, claimed to take him when he drove us all from Kûr Anzar. I thought my precious Eshtali long since dead. I know it is dangerous, ${PLAYER}, but I feel a dagger of hope in my chest.

'You have accomplished much with me here. There is no one I trust more with this mission than you. Please, make your way to Esh-kimâkhi and look for him. You will know him by the crimson robes he always wears. And, ${PLAYER}? If you are to return with my husband, know that you will have given me a gift worth more to me than any victory in this war.''Thank you for that news. I had feared this day would come. I had hoped you would return with fairer news, but I appreciate your candor.

'Hope is a cruel master, and one that has now abandoned me.

'When I was a girl, my sisters and I would make shapes, shadows on the wall. We would make funny animals: ducks, and rabbits, and chickens. Oh, and the stories we would tell! The adventures those rabbits and ducks had! Such stories. My sisters have since passed, taken each by disease or famine or war. Sometimes I still see those shadows though; dancing, laughing, playing. I can still hear their laughter.

'When my husband would come home, I would first see him by the shadow he cast on the wall by our home. So broad and powerful, that shadow was the harbinger of my precious Eshtali coming home to me. Just like my sisters, I sought comfort in that shadow, always steady, strangely solid.

'After he was taken, I am ashamed to say I forgot what his face looked like, once so familiar to me. All I can see now of him is that shadow on the wall, insubstantial like a wraith, endlessly dancing through my memories.'Mizâdi has received word from her spies that her missing husband, Eshtali, has been sighted near the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi. Make your way there and look for clues to his whereabouts.Meet with Razâl, Mizâdi's scout, outside of Esh-kimâkhi. The Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi can be found south-east of Urmâkh.Meet with Razâl outside of Esh-kimâkhiSearch the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi south of Urmâkh for signs of Mizâdi's missing husband, Eshtali. Mizâdi said he would be wearing crimson robes.Continue searching the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi south of Urmâkh for signs of Mizâdi's missing husband, Eshtali.Continue searching around Esh-kimâkhi - Eshtali may be closeExamine the man to determine if he is Eshtali.Examine the man to determine if he is EshtaliSpeak with Razâl at the edge of Esh-kimâkhi.Speak with Razâl at the edge of Esh-kimâkhiGive Mizâdi in Urmâkh news of her husband's death, and what you found of his possessions.Bring Mizâdi in Urmâkh her husband's effects, and news of his death'I have a personal matter with which I would ask your assistance, ${PLAYER}.

'I have received word from my spies of a rumour that my husband, Eshtali, has recently been seen outside the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi to the south of here. What he is doing there, I have no idea.

'The leader of the Barkhûshim, that accursed Okhíso, claimed to take him when he drove us all from Kûr Anzar. I thought my precious Eshtali long since dead. I know it is dangerous, ${PLAYER}, but I feel a dagger of hope in my chest.

'You have accomplished much with me here. There is no one I trust more with this mission than you. Please, make your way to Esh-kimâkhi and look for him. You will know him by the crimson robes he always wears. I have sent Razâl ahead of you to scout the terrain, speak with him when you arrive.

'And, ${PLAYER}? If you are to return with my husband, know that you will have given me a gift worth more to me than any victory in this war.''Thank you for that news, and for his effects. Hope is a cruel master, and one that has now abandoned me.

'I remember when I was a girl, my sisters and I would make shapes, shadows on the wall. We would make funny animals: ducks, and rabbits, and chickens. Oh, and the stories we would tell! The adventures those rabbits and ducks had! Such stories. Those days have long passed, but when I close my eyes I can still see those shadows; dancing, vaulting, gamboling. I still hear their peals of laughter.

'When my husband came home, I would first see him by the shadow he cast on the wall. So broad and powerful, that shadow was the harbinger of my precious Eshtali coming home to me. Just like my sisters, I sought comfort in that shadow, always steady, strangely solid.

'After he was taken, I am ashamed to say I forgot what his face looked like, once so familiar to me. I can no longer see his face. All I see of him now is that shadow on the wall, insubstantial like a wraith, endlessly dancing through my memories.''This is as far as we have been able to advance. The restless dead of Esh-kimâkhi make it impossible for us to scout further.

'You have shown yourself quite capable in a fight. My eyes are keen, but my sword arm is slow. Would you scout further into Esh-kimâkhi and search for signs of Eshtali? I will remain here in case you or Eshtali have need of my aid.''This is the worst fate we could have feared. With the way now cleared, we will recover Eshtali. We will treat him with the utmost respect. You should let Mizâdi know with all due haste, and bring what you found of Eshtali's. This is grim news indeed, but she will want to hear it, and from your lips.'Rothog has requested that you venture into the catacombs, and visit a small encampment beneath the Arena called Hulzidâr. He has asked you to speak to Dabôr the Breaker, a former gladiator from Dahâl Huliz, the leader of the camp, and assist them in any way that you can.Beneath Dahâl Huliz, there is a small settlement in the catacombs that has been established by Rothog.

He requested that you seek out Dabôr the Breaker to see how you might be of some assistance.Talk to Dabôr the Breaker within Hulzidâr, beneath the arena'It is good that you have come. As your prowess and fame has spread throughout the land, I find myself in need of your services. Beneath the arena, in the catacombs, there is a small encampment known as Hulzidâr. The people that live in that encampment are considered under my protection and may require aid.

'Go to Hulzidâr, speak to Dabôr the Breaker, a former gladiator, and see how you might assist these people whom I hold dear.''Ah, ${PLAYER}! The Storm had mentioned that he might be sending an extra set of hands. To be blunt, our position is dire. Between the cultists to the north, the group of gladiators that left the camp after stealing much needed supplies, and the twisted Dead further into the tunnels, I fear we may have a good deal of work for you, if you might be willing.

'Thank you for coming to assist us.'Ashkab requests assistance in collecting materials from the beasts of Ikorbân to clothe and shelter the people of Jirush.Ashkab requires scorpion chitin, jackal hides, and lizard frills to help clothe and shelter the people of Jirush. He suggests the jackals can be found west in the waste-plains, scorpions in the quarry north-west of Jirush, and lizards to south-west of Jirush.Collect jackal hides from within Khûd Zagin (${NUMBER}/8)Collect scorpion chitin from the quarry in Khûd Zagin (${NUMBER}/8)Collect lizard frills from around Khûd Zagin (${NUMBER}/8)You hunted the wildlife of Khûd Zagin for their hide, chitin, and leathery frills. You should deliver the items to Ashkab at his home in Jirush.'Malgat is too kind. Though his time in the wild is over, he finds ways to assist us with our needs. He also maintains our morale, which is more difficult by the day.

'As he said, I outfit the outpost with hides, chitin, and frills. Whether we use them directly or trade them to caravans as they move along the roads, these are the primary goods we have to offer. Recent efforts by the Ordâkhai in the fort overlooking Jirush and their encampment in the south-east gave pause to our hunters. Our supplies dwindle to nearly nothing, and we risk losing what little trade we have.

'If you are willing, hunt the jackals and scorpions in the northern, western, and central areas of Khûd Zagin for their hides and chitin, respectively. Then turn west to hunt the lizards for their frills.''Jackals traverse the waste-plains of Khûd Zagin in packs, though you may find them in dens west of Jirush. The scorpions make the quarry far to the north-west of Jirush their main habitat in Khûd Zagin. Lastly, the lizards are to the south-west of Jirush. Return to me when you have collected that for which I have asked.''You work quickly and well. I shall put all of these items to good use. The people will have shelter, armour, and pouches aplenty. If there were more like you, perhaps our trade with caravans would be more profitable.'Galâmka has asked you to clear out the outposts the Orcs have set up outside of Maurûsh to prevent them from calling for help when the attack begins.Find the Orc outpost to the west of Maurûsh that was discovered by the scouts.Find the western Orc outpostDefeat the Orcs at the western outpost to help Galâmka in their preparations for the battle in Maurûsh.Defeat Orcs in western outpost (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the Orc outpost to the south of Maurûsh that was discovered by the scouts.Find the southern Orc outpostDefeat the Orcs at the southern outpost to help Galâmka in their preparations for the battle in Maurûsh.Defeat Orcs in southern outpost (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the Orc outpost to the east of Maurûsh that was discovered by the scouts.Find the eastern Orc outpostDefeat the Orcs at the eastern outpost to help Galâmka in their preparations for the battle in Maurûsh.Defeat Orcs in eastern outpost (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Galâmka in Ub Nishir to the north of Maurûsh and inform him that the outposts have been cleared out.Return to Galâmka in Ub Nishir'Good, you have arrived. The battle draws near but there is one more task I ask of you.

'My scouts have returned from the spots detailed in the scraps you recovered from the Orcs. They mark the locations of Orc outposts and from what my scouts can gather they are for scouting and calling for help if Maurûsh should come under heavy attack. We must take them out before we can attempt to take the stronghold.'

Galâmka gestures to three locations on his map surrounding Maurûsh.

'These spots to the west, south, and east are where the outposts stand. Go there are slay the Orcs so they can not call for aid during our attack.''Have you dealt with the outposts?'

You tell Galâmka that you have successfully defeated the Orcs in the outposts the scouts had found.

'Wonderous news! Again, I can not thank you enough for all that you have done. Our preparations here are coming to an end and hope grows in the people. I ask that you join us in battle. We are ready to retake our home.

'We are ready to fight for Maurûsh.'You have completed many tasks to support the Dumûri at Sûru.Ningêna has asked you to return to Girhâzi and update her on the situation at Sûru.Talk to Girhâzi in Iridír'${PLAYER}, thank you for aiding our efforts here at Sûru. Please return to Girhâzi and tell her of our progress. Our work goes quite well, owing in no small part to the support you have given us ${PLAYER}.''Thank you for aiding our efforts here at Sûru, ${PLAYER}. Please return to Girhâzi and tell her of our progress.''How goes Sûru, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell her that the Dumûri are holding steady at the crossing and that construction on the fortress continues without issue.

'That is good news! I am grateful for your contributions there. Once we have gathered enough strength, we will push the Ordâkhai out of Eshadûr and Ambarûl will be free. Unfortunately, even that will not be enough. The more difficult task will be ensuring Ambarûl remains free, as there always seems to be a new threat on the horizon.'Slay many foes in Adagím.Slay many foes in Adagím.Complete Bog-slayer of Adagím (Advanced)Complete Crocodile-slayer of Adagím (Advanced)Complete Huorn-bane of Adagím (Advanced)Complete Orc-bane of Adagím (Advanced)Complete Spider-slayer of Adagím (Advanced)Complete Wood-troll Slayer of Adagím (Advanced)Slay many foes in Ambarûl.Slay many foes in Ambarûl.Complete Insect-slayer of Ambarûl (Advanced)Complete Brigand-bane of Ambarûl (Advanced)Complete Ordâkhai-bane of Ambarûl (Advanced)Complete Feral Cat-bane of Ambarûl (Advanced)Complete Boar-slayer of Ambarûl (Advanced)Complete Scorpion-slayer of Ambarûl (Advanced)Slay many foes in An Shêru.Slay many foes in An Shêru.Complete Brigand-bane of An Shêru (Advanced)Complete Dead-slayer of An Shêru (Advanced)Complete Utûgi-bane of An Shêru (Advanced)Complete Grodbog-slayer of An Shêru (Advanced)Complete Ordâkhai-bane of An Shêru (Advanced)Complete Worm-bane of An Shêru (Advanced)Slay many foes in eastern Dil-irmíz.Slay many foes in Dil-irmíz.Complete Smuggler-bane of Dil-irmíz (Advanced)Complete Criminal-bane of Dil-irmíz (Advanced)Slay many foes in Idagâl.Slay many foes in Idagâl.Complete Brigand-bane of Idagâl (Advanced)Complete Cobra-slayer of Idagâl (Advanced)Complete Drake-slayer of Idagâl (Advanced)Complete Utûgi-bane of Idagâl (Advanced)Complete Kergrim-slayer of Idagâl (Advanced)Complete Ordâkhai-bane of Idagâl (Advanced)Slay many foes in Ilmabiri.Slay many foes in Ilmabiri.Complete Forsaken-slayer of Ilmabiri (Advanced)Goblin-slayer of Ilmabiri (Advanced)Crocodile-slayer of Ilmabiri (Advanced)Slay many foes in Imhûlar.Slay many foes in Imhûlar.Complete All-seeing Slayer of Imhûlar (Advanced)Complete Dead-slayer of Imhûlar (Advanced)Complete Diseased-bane of Imhûlar (Advanced)Complete Orc-slayer of Imhûlar (Advanced)Complete Ordâkhai-bane of Imhûlar (Advanced)Complete Scorpion-bane of Imhûlar (Advanced)Slay many foes in Kamrabezûr.Slay many foes in Kamrabezûr.Complete Cultist-slayer of Kamrabezûr (Advanced)Complete Gladiator-slayer of Kamrabezûr (Advanced)Complete Dead-slayer of Kamrabezûr (Advanced)Slay many foes in Khabârkhad.Slay many foes in Khabârkhad.Complete Crypt-raider Slayer of Khabârkhad (Advanced)Complete Spider-bane of Khabârkhad (Advanced)Complete Dead-slayer of Khabârkhad (Advanced)Slay many foes in Khûd Zagin.Slay many foes in Khûd Zagin.Complete Craban-slayer of Khûd Zagin (Advanced)Crocodile-slayer of Khûd Zagin (Advanced)Complete Dead-slayer of Khûd Zagin (Advanced)Complete Jackal-bane of Khûd Zagin (Advanced)Complete Ordâkhai-bane of Khûd Zagin (Advanced)Complete Sand-sifter Slayer of Khûd Zagin (Advanced)Slay many foes in Kighân.Slay many foes in Kighân.Complete Tarsâri-bane of Kighân (Advanced)Complete Bee-slayer of Kighân (Advanced)Complete Brigand-bane of Kighân (Advanced)Complete Goblin-bane of Kighân (Advanced)Complete Ordâkhai-bane of Kighân (Advanced)Complete Spider-slayer of Kighân (Advanced)Slay many foes throughout Mûr Ghala.Slay many foes throughout Mûr Ghala.Complete Slayer of AdagímComplete Slayer of KighânComplete Slayer of An ShêruComplete Slayer of IdagâlSlay many foes in Tâkhdar.Slay many foes in Tâkhdar.Grodbog-slayer of Tâkhdar (Advanced)Complete Smuggler-bane of Tâkhdar (Advanced)Complete Spider-bane of Tâkhdar (Advanced)Slay many foes throughout the Ikorbân Valley.Slay many foes throughout the Ikorbân Valley.Complete Slayer of AmbarûlComplete Slayer of Khûd ZaginComplete Slayer of ImhûlarComplete Slayer of Urash DârSlay many foes in the Umbar-môkh.Slay many foes in the Umbar-môkh.Complete Slayer of KhabârkhadComplete Slayer of IlmabiriComplete Slayer of KamrabezûrComplete Slayer of TâkhdarComplete Slayer of Dil-irmízSlay many foes in Urash Dâr.Slay many foes in Urash Dâr.Complete Brigand-bane of Urash Dâr (Advanced)Complete Jackal-slayer of Urash Dâr (Advanced)Complete Kergrim-slayer of Urash Dâr (Advanced)Complete Orc-bane of Urash Dâr (Advanced)Complete Scorpion-bane of Urash Dâr (Advanced)Complete Spider-slayer of Urash Dâr (Advanced)Usan-kûni, the local name for the huge scorpions that infest Ambarûl, are clustered in Nirikal.You should slay some usan-kûni, the scorpions gathered in Nirikal, the south-western desert of Ambarûl.Defeat usan-kûni (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Deadly usan-kûni scorpions are gathered in Nirikal, the south-western desert of Ambarûl. They are a danger to the local population. You should slay some of the usan-kûni.Khôltekh has asked you to go to Deshûkh, the Blood Market, to rescue a group of kidnapped Umbari nobles.Khôltekh has asked you to go to Deshûkh, the Blood Market, to rescue a group of kidnapped Umbari nobles. First you must go see the Guard Captain Nûru in Mekab-kuphâr, the Temámir guard outpost in Khabârkhad.Talk to the Temámir Guard Captain Nûru in Mekab-kuphâr, in southern KhabârkhadNuru has told you that the Blood Market is located south-west of here, in Dil-irmíz, the Berths.Defeat smugglers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rescue first kidnapped nobleRescue second kidnapped nobleRescue third kidnapped nobleReturn to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja, the Hall of the Kindred.Return to Khôltekh in the Hall of the Kindred'You seem somewhat capable; you may yet survive in Umbar Baharbêl. I must ask your assistance with a quite dangerous task.

'I have heard increasing reports of theft, kidnapping and worse in the Undercity. My dwarves have formed a foothold in the crypts, but villainy spills out in Umbar-môkh more quickly and readily than the waters of the Bay.

'Long have we above ground turned a blind eye toward what happens under our feet. No longer can we afford such luxury. This morning, a party of Umbari nobility were set upon on the road to the Cape. Several escaped, but a small group were dragged away. It is of the utmost importance that we get them back.

'I happen to know from my contacts that there is an encampment of the worst sort of offenders - thieves, murderers, smugglers and cutthroats in Dil-irmíz, the Berths. These smugglers call it Deshûkh - the Blood Market. This is where these nobles are likely to be taken. Go to my guard outpost in Khabârkhad - Nûru will tell you the way to this encampment.

'Please, ${PLAYER}. These Umbari men and women have their lives in your hands. Will you help?''This is most pleasing news. I need to think more on the Umbar-môkh, the land beneath Umbar. For too long has it evaded our gaze. Nonetheless, a hundred thanks for your brave deeds. I am glad you came back with your skin and they with theirs.''Khôltekh sent you? Deshûkh, the Blood Market? Finally someone is doing something about those scoundrels. We don't venture that far south. It's too dangerous - few who reside there are friendly to dwarves.

'The Blood Market is south-west of here, in Dil-irmíz, the Berths. Be careful - outside these environs, you will find few friendly faces.'Defeat many smugglers in Dil-irmíz.Defeat many smugglers in Dil-irmíz.Defeat many smugglers in Dil-irmízDefeat a great many smugglers in Dil-irmíz.Defeat many smugglers in Dil-irmíz.Defeat a great many smugglers in Dil-irmíz.Defeat a great many smugglers in Dil-irmízDefeat many smugglers in Tâkhdar.Defeat many smugglers in Tâkhdar.Defeat many smugglers in TâkhdarDefeat a great many smugglers in Tâkhdar.Defeat many smugglers in Tâkhdar.Defeat a great many smugglers in Tâkhdar.Defeat a great many smugglers in TâkhdarJâbex, a former cultist of the All-Seeing Eye, has asked you to search for a mysterious artifact the cult is using to threaten his peaceful life as a free man.Defeat cultists guarding the mysterious artifact throughout Tâkhdar, the Cellars of Umbar.Defeat cultists in Tâkhdar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Jâbex's artifact lies within the cultists' coffer at their camp somewhere near the centre of Tâkhdar.Search the cultists' coffer in their camp in the centre of TâkhdarJâbex can be found in the cross-roads of Umbar-môkh.

Jâbex will doubtlessly be relieved to have the artifact back in his possession.Return to Jâbex with news of the artifactThe fountain can be found in the cross-roads on the western side of Tâkhdar.

Jâbex has asked you to negate the artifact's power and end its hold on him by submerging it in a fountain inside the cross-roads courtyard.Submerge the artifact in the courtyard fountainDouse the artifact in water, ensuring its curious mechanisms are thoroughly cleansed of all power.The artifact must soak for some timeJâbex is waiting in the south-western side of Tâkhdar, at the cross-roads.

Jâbex will be pleased to learn he is finally free of the artifact's hold.Jâbex is waiting by in the cross-roads of Tâkhdar'I beg you not to look so suspiciously at me; I require your discretion and aid. I have built a life for myself here in Umbar, and I do not wish it disturbed.

'As a foolish youth, I was lured here from Gondor by a cult you might recognize as the cult of the All-Seeing Eye. I have since renounced their ways, but I live in terror they may one day learn I yet live, and use the horrors of a terrible artifact to punish me for my betrayal.

'The members of the cult skulk about Tâkhdar and should not be difficult to encounter, but the artifact must still be hidden in a coffer on the eastern side. I have no right to ask such a favour of you, but please, would you find a way to retrieve the artifact for me so I may rest easy?''Have you encountered difficulties in defeating my former brethren? Many such members of the Cult of the All-Seeing Eye yet remain throughout the cellars -- or in the local dialect, the Tâkhdar.''You return? With my artifact, I assume! ...Might I see it? To be certain you discovered the correct one?

'Yes.... It looks... just as I remember. Did it always radiate such power?'

Jâbex takes ahold of himself and snaps to attention.

'You must destroy it yourself. I cannot be trusted to handle it. I thought at first to submerge it in the fountain in the courtyard here, to negate its corruption, but with you here... would you do me this last kindness?''The artifact still must be drowned to negate its foul powers. The fountain in this courtyard ahead of me would be my choice to submerge it. I would do so myself, but I fear the artifact's hold over me.''You return successful, then? You have done away with it? Just like that? Strange.... My mind feels clearer, but I have a lingering sense of disquiet. Like I am afraid of missing out on some grand design....

'It is naught but old excuses and nightmares of my past, I know. Nothing a hearty bowl of rice cannot cure, as my wife always says. Thank you for your assistance, friend. Now, your reward!'Rukân is concerned about a new spate of dead fish washing up on the nearby shore.Rukân asked you to inspect the dead fish that have washed up on the shore to the south-west.Retrieve dead fish from the shore to the south-west (${NUMBER}/4)Rukân asked you to inspect the dead fish that have washed up on the shore to the south-west.Retrieve dead fish from the shore to the south-west (3/4)Rukân is waiting for you to return from the shore with anything you might have discovered about the dead fish.The fisherman Bôdo in the village of Khûtra may know something about the unpleasant fish-hook you found.Talk to Bôdo in the village of KhûtraBôdo told you he saw a box with similar decorations to the unpleasant fish-hook among the hills to the north-west of Khûtra.Find the box of unpleasant design among the hills to the north-west of KhûtraYou found the box Bôdo described among the hills north-west of Khûtra, and should now search it for some clue to its purpose.Search the box of unpleasant design among the hills north-west of KhûtraGoblins or their Corsair allies must have taken away the contents of the box. You should recover as many of the cruel fish-hooks as you can.Recover stolen fish-hooks from goblins or their Corsair allies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bôdo will be glad to have the fish-hooks out of the hands of the goblins and their corsair allies, even if it means he must now dispose of the unpleasant artifacts.Rukân is east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl.Talk to Rukân east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl'You came back to help me? I did not know if I should wait for you or if you would forget we needed you.

'I spoke to you of the pestilence that lately troubled Khûtra, inflicting famine upon the folk of the Cape. It seemed it must abate, but the fish that remain our livelihood still wash up on the shore... dead! Will you examine some of these recent corpses for me? It may be that you will notice something I have not.

'There are dead fish along the shore to the south-west.''Will you examine some of these dead fish for me? It may be that you will notice something I have not. They are along the shore to the south-west.''It may be that you will notice something I have not. There are dead fish along the shore to the south-west.''Did you find anything to explain why these fish are dying?'

You hand the small metal hook of unpleasant design to Rukân. She eyes the curved metal loops and sharp points with distaste.

'Are these... tentacles?' she asks. She shakes her head.

'Someone fashioned this hook in the style of a terrible creature of the Sea. Let us hope they did not see it with their own eyes, and this design is the product of a... vivid imagination. See how it glistens? I think this metal is coated with some sort of poison; take care not to touch it!

'I think the fish that are snared with hooks such as this are slain by the poison and carried by the waves onto the shore, but no one should eat any fish that are caught in this fashion! Find my neighbour Bôdo on the other side of Khûtra and tell him what we have discovered.''Find my neighbour Bôdo on the other side of Khûtra and tell him what we have discovered.''What brings you back to Khûtra, my friend?'

You show Bôdo the unpleasant hook you found in the mouth of a dead fish on the other side of the village, and he traces a ward against evil in the dirt with the grip of his fishing pole.

'You found another one of those terrible poisoned hooks? I knew they were trouble. We discovered a box of the things up the hill to the north-west. We should have hidden it, or some such work that would have prevented others from stumbling upon it, but we have had so many difficulties of late that it was easier just to put it out of mind.'

He studies it as carefully as he can without touching the glistening metal.

'Yes, this is like the others we found. You should climb up to that evil-looking box and make sure the rest of them are still inside. Then we can dispose of it.''You should climb up to that evil-looking box and make sure the rest of them are still inside. Then we can dispose of it.''You should climb up to that evil-looking box and make sure the rest of them are still inside. Then we can dispose of it.''Goblins and Corsairs might have plundered the contents of that strongbox? That is not good, friend. We must get those poisoned fish-hooks back or they will ruin the fishing all along the Cape!''You tracked down the poisoned fish-hooks stolen by the goblins and their Corsair allies? That is very good, my friend. I will return them to the strongbox in which they were found, and I will do what I should have done before. I will bury it so deep that none will make use of them again. The folk of Khûtra rely upon the bounty of the sea for our livelihood, and if the fish are poisoned then so too are we.

'Return to Rukân beyond the village and tell her we have taken care of the problem. Thank her for sending you back to me as well! You were just the reminder I needed that we should have done something before now!''Return to Rukân beyond the village and tell her we have taken care of the problem. Thank her for sending you back to me as well! You were just the reminder I needed that we should have done something before now!''Bôdo said he will bury the box so no one else will make use of the poisoned fish-hooks within? Let us hope he does, and he buries it deep. Things do not always stay buried on the Cape of Umbar. You have seen the Dead that walk outside the Mâkhda Khorbo, I trust?

'But I thank you and Bôdo for finding the sea-bed of this problem. May the fish of Khûtra remain unspoiled from this day forth!'Edâkhi asks you to investigate behind the waterfall for more signs of Enârshan.Edâkhi has asked you to investigate behind the waterfall for the home of the Idâmi.Investigate the waterfall for an entranceSpeak with the Idâmi in her home behind the waterfall in Ilûritu.Speak with Enârshan, the Idâmi'Ah! You are here! I believe I have unravelled the clues you discovered.

'I have come to believe that the tales which speak of Enârshan and the Falls of Ilûritu, are meant to be read directly.

'My group and I have searched these falls and the surrounding hills for any dwellings or places where the Idâmi may be. But we have not done what the stories say... exactly.

'The stories all say that the Idâmi dwells within the waterfall. Mayhap by within they are saying that there is a dwelling behind the falls themselves? Your discoveries appear to point to this as well, and we had not chanced to venture there as it was too dangerous to climb behind the falls.

'I ask that you go and search for yourself. It should not be a problem for a hardy adventurer such as you! I believe that you will find Enârshan there. But I beg you to be careful if you do.''${CLASS}, you enter my home not by my song, but by your own curiosity.

'I am Enârshan. Idâmi of these falls.

'You are either bold or foolish to have done this, but today luck is with you, for I am in need of assistance.'With news of the assaults led by Bârshud II, Ashnân wants to plant extra crops to ensure they have the supplies needed for their troops.Gather bags of seeds to help Ashnân plant extra crops in Burukíri.Gather seed bags (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Plant the seeds in the locations at which the soil has already been tilled around Burukíri.Plant seeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Ashnân in Burukíri and inform him that you have planted the crop seeds for him.Return to Ashnân in Burukíri'${PLAYER}, you must have heard of the assaults that Bârshud II is leading in Ambarûl. I am not much of a fighter, but I want to do what I can to help the ones who are.

'The fighters will need food, and while we have much here already I know we will need more. If you are willing, would you take these bags of seeds and plant them in the soil nearby, so that I can begin growing extra crops? You should be able to easily spot locations where the soil has been tilled already.''Thank you my friend. I hope these crops will be enough to sustain our fighters, but it is the best I can do for now. Please accept this as a token of my gratitude for your help.'Defeat many spiders in Khabârkhad.Defeat many spiders in Khabârkhad.Defeat many spiders in KhabârkhadDefeat a great many spiders in Khabârkhad.Defeat many spiders in Khabârkhad.Defeat a great many spiders in KhabârkhadDefeat a great many spiders in KhabârkhadDefeat many spiders in Tâkhdar.Defeat many spiders in Tâkhdar.Defeat many spiders in TâkhdarDefeat a great many spiders in Tâkhdar.Defeat many spiders in Tâkhdar.Defeat a great many spiders in Tâkhdar.Defeat a great many spiders in TâkhdarSlay many spiders throughout Mûr Ghala.Slay many spiders throughout Mûr Ghala.Complete Spider-slayer of Adagím (Advanced)Complete Spider-slayer of Kighân (Advanced)Defeat many spiders in Urash Dâr.Defeat many spiders in Urash Dâr.Defeat many spiders in Urash DârDefeat a great many spiders in Urash Dâr.Defeat many spiders in Urash Dâr.Defeat a great many spiders in Urash Dâr.Defeat a great many spiders in Urash DârThe troublesome woman can be found at The Din of Arms in the Tor-gardens, in the western side of Umbar Baharbêl.

A wine-merchant has asked you to speak with a woman who seems to have lost her husband.Find and speak with Hanâth at The Din of Arms in the Tor Gardens.

Shemâya, a wine-merchant of Umbar Baharbêl has come to Dâr Laja to file a complaint against a frequent visitor to the shop. She suggests first meeting with his wife, Hanâth at The Din of Arms in the Tor Gardens.Talk to Hanâth at The Din of ArmsHanâth's husband is somewhere in Tâkhdar, likely in Kheb Hanût.

A frantic woman is looking for her husband, who has gotten himself banned from every wine-house for drunken behaviour. She suspects he is still drinking somewhere in Tâkhdar.Search for Hanâth's husband in TâkhdarHanâth's husband is probably in Tâkhdar in the black market at Kheb Hanût.

Search for someone who seems particularly inebriated in the cellars.Search for a drunken man in Kheb HanûtHanâth's husband is drinking himself blind in Tâkhdar at Kheb Hanût.

You have found Hanâth's husband in the cellars. You should greet him and see if he is sober enough to ascend.Speak with Hanâth's inebriated spouse'I had thought the opening of Dâr Laja would allow all to be heard, but it is difficult enough to hear my own thoughts. I have a wine-shop to run. I cannot wait indefinitely for the Kindred of the Coins to hear my complaints. It is a small enough matter; would you take care of it for me?

'A woman looking for her husband is causing a bit of ruckus in my wine shop in the Tor-gardens, The Din of Arms. I beg you, see what she is on about. She is irritating my patrons.''Have you yet spoken with Hanâth, or whatever her name was? That woman still terrorizes my patrons. Does she not realize her husband will not return there? I have forbidden him entry time and time again! Please find him, if only to cease her nattering.''I would ask if you had seen my husband, but I know he has been forbidden from showing his face at this wine-house, too. That man has caused no end of trouble at every single wine-house and tavern and even friend's home in the entire city!

'I am certain he is still drinking somewhere. Perhaps in Tâkhdar, although I do not know where, and am certain I will not descend to such unsavoury depths. You seem like you journey there often. Look for him next time you are there!''Have you come to a conclusion on my husband's whereabouts? Then what are you doing here? Go fetch him! I am beside myself with worry!''So you found my husband in Tâkhdar after all? My foresight was correct; I know my foolish love too well. But you did not return him to me! Go give him a piece of my mind and bring him home!''And who are... do I know you? You are wavy around the edges... but I like the shape of those waves! You are unknown to me, and it is always good health to drink to a new friendship! Here, share these bottles with me! Not wine, but almost as good.

'I am... Baziphâr. I do not... remember your name. Do not expect me to! Ha ha! Come, let us imbibe together as friends!'The barricades protecting Sûru from Ordâkhai attacks were damaged in recent fighting.Ningêna has asked you to repair the barricades protecting Sûru.Repair barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have repaired the barricades protecting Sûru. You should return to Ningêna.Talk to Ningêna'In last night's fighting, many of our barricades were damaged or destroyed. If you wish to assist us, you could repair them so we will be ready for the next Ordâkhai assault.''If you wish to assist us, you could repair the barricades so we will be ready for the next assault.''The barricades are all repaired? Thank you ${PLAYER}, you have been a great help.'Ilzhâna, a perfectly legitimate trader in Tilmakhím, has asked you to recover some missing parcels and slay the spiders who stole them. She asked you not to look inside.Spiders and their captured prey can be found in Shak Phêlex, on the eastern side of Tâkhdar.

Slay spiders throughout Tilmakhím and collect Ilzhâna's missing probably-not-contraband parcels. The spiders probably dragged them back to their nest in Shak Phêlex.Slay spiders in Tâkhdar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect the trader's misplaced shipment parcels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ilzhâna can be found at Tilmakhím on the western side of Tâkhdar.

Return to Ilzhâna with the parcels.Return to Ilzhâna'You have a good eye for honest business, friend! I assure you, every single one of my legitimate wares has legitimate paperwork from legitimate origins!

'It pains me to say, but you have come to trade at a bad time. I fear some scoundrel has made off with my latest shipment. That spider nest to the north-east causes much trouble for honest traders like myself.

'Recover my shipment and you shall be amply rewarded, friend! Doubly so for your subtlety!''I cannot continue my reputable business and share my incredible deals until those parcels are returned to me and the spiders dealt with, my dear friend and future customer!''You return victorious, my capable and discreet new friend! And you did not... steal a peek inside those unassuming crates, no? Excellent, excellent! I knew you were to be trusted.

'Your reward, for business well conducted!'Turizi has asked you to retrieve the stolen bags of rice from bandits.The bandits that stole the farmers rice can be found north of Ekagar in Ambarûl.Defeat bandits and recover sacks of rice (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have recovered the stolen rice. You should return to Turizi at Ekagar in Ambarûl.'If you are looking for someone in need of help, then you have found one.'

The man flushes with embarrassment.

'It pains me to speak of it, but thieves have stolen some of our rice that was ready to go to market. Normally I would track them down and get it back myself but...'

He looks down at where his now amputated arm once was.

'I have been training... but I am not yet skilled at fighting right-handed.'

His embarrassment quickly shifts to anger.

'I will have you know that I am not helpless. I grow stronger by the day. I am a capable man and can do my own work on the farm. I only ask for your aid because we are in dire need of the income we would get from selling the rice. I am not destitute though, and need no charity. I will pay you to deal with these bandits. You will likely find them to the north of the farm.''The khmêg that stole my rice can be found north of here. I would be grateful if you could get it back from them.''You have done it! Truly, I did not expect you to return. I cannot thank you enough for bringing back our goods. Some coin will have to do.'The patriarch of the Ghôlkhas noble family has asked you to retrieve a set of armour stolen from his family during the days of the Heirs of Castamir.Bandits tend to lurk in north-west Tâkhdar.

Okhtâr Ghôlkhas, head of a prominent family, has asked you to retrieve heirloom armour a group of bandits called the Denjâri stole from the family tomb. He has asked you to retrieve it.Search the bandit camp for the Ghôlkhas patriarch's armourDefeat Denjâri bandits.Defeat Denjâri bandits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Search for clues as to the armour's whereaboutsSearch for clues as to the armour's whereaboutsRashâm can be found in the black market of Kheb Hanût.

A letter from the Denjâri bandits' leader says she has sold the Ghôlkhas's stolen armour to a black market fence named Rashâm.Look for Rashâm in the black market of Kheb HanûtSpeak with Rashâm in Kheb Hanût.Speak with Rashâm in Kheb Hanût'One would think my noble title as patriarch of House Ghôlkhas would grant me speedy audience with the Kindred, but it appears I was mistaken. Would you consider my request instead?

'A suit of my predecessor's ceremonial armour was pilfered from the family mausoleum. My servants have heard tell of a shameless group of brigands known as the Denjâri boasting of such a piece somewhere in Tâkhdar.

'If you investigate these claims, you would have my gratitude and patronage.''My servants have all said the Denjâri bandits, and many others, spend their days in Takhdâr. I do not ask my servants how they know such things, as their history is more interesting as a mystery. It helps me keep my sense of adventure without dirtying my silk clothing!''The Denjâri bandits did not frighten you away, did they? I cannot blame you if they did; I myself would be terrified! Ha! But this is why I will be paying you so well, no? Please return to me with news of my armour!''I hope you are here to buy, stranger. I have more sundry than I care to offload at present.

'Zulkhêma of the Denjâri? Did she sell me a peculiar set of armour, you ask? I might know that name, and I might even know the armour. I have recently come into possession of a great many pieces of treasure. I hardly know what to do with them all; I may have paid more than their worth.'Galâmka has realized that he needs additional help to take back Maurûsh and asked you to go speak with some of his associates and get them to join the fight.Speak with Agazi near the rockslide on the road to Ambarûl to the west.Speak with Agazi near the rockslide to the westDefeat spiny lizards near the rockslide blocking the path to Ambarûl.Defeat spiny lizards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Agazi near the rockslide blocking the path to Ambarûl in the west.Return to AgaziSpeak with Balgiba near the Channel of Bâdizal to the south of Maurûsh.Speak with Balgiba in the Channel of BâdizalBalgiba has asked you to gather tortoise shells for him near the Channel of Bâdizal for the armour he is trying to craft.Collect tortoise shells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bring the tortoise shells back to Balgiba in the Channel of Bâdizal.Return to Galâmka in Maurûsh and update him on Agazi and Balgiba.Return to Galâmka in Ub Nishir'Ah yes, there you are. We are in need of more people who can fight with us. I know of some groups who reside nearby that we may be able to bring into the cause, especially with your help.

'There is Agazi, who last I saw with her band near the rockslide to the west, on the road to Ambarûl. Then Balgiba, he is camped near the Channel of Bâdizal to the south of Maurûsh.

'I ask that you go and speak with them. Convince them to join our cause to retake the stronghold if you can. Groups here have come to an understanding since Utug-bûr opened and we gained a common foe, so them and their cohorts should know to not attack you on sight, though if they do, you need only tell them I sent you.''What brings you here, stranger?'

Agazi looks as you with hesitation, her posture appearing ready for a fight as you explain that you were sent by Galâmka in need of help.

'Ah, Galâmka needs help with his conquest of Maurûsh then? He has helped me many times in the past so I will not refuse his call.

'We here are trying to clear what we can of the rockslide to make safe the path Ambarûl. People are trying to flee this land and the path to the south contains many more dangers. Our task would go quicker if it were not for these lizards.

'Might you help and rid us of them? That would let us complete our work and head for Ub Nishir.''Thank you for your help, ${CLASS}. I see why Galâmka trusts you so.

'With the lizards gone we will hurry to finish what we must here and then make our way to Maurûsh. Truly, my friend, you have not only helped us this day but helped the people of Urash Dâr have safer passage from this land, and these demons who aim to take it from us.''Ah, and who are you? Someone who has lost their way?

'No, no, you must be the one who has been helping Galâmka, and this fight for Maurûsh! He must be wishing for my help and has sent you, or am I mistaken?'

Balgiba appears cheerful but wary of letting you get too close. He stands ready to attack if needed. You tell him that he is correct, and that you were sent by Galâmka to request his help.

'Ha! I knew it! Well, ${CLASS}, I wish to reclaim Maurûsh as well, so our swords will gladly join with his.

'We are working to harden our armours. Would you help us gather some tortoise shells? Their shells here in Urash Dâr are very sturdy, and I am certain we can find some use for them. Once we have enough, my band and I will joyfully join Galâmka.''These are flawless! Thank you my friend! Ha-ha!'

Balgiba laughs as he takes the tortoise shells from you.

'We shall pack up here and make haste to Ub Nishir. We are happy to help retake the stronghold, and reclaim this land, our homes, from these Orcs and these monsters from the demon-pit.''You are back. Have you spoken with Agazi and Balgiba?'

You tell Galâmka of how you helped them and that they both pledged their swords to his cause.

'My friend, this is good news you bring me. I am glad that you could help them, and that they are so eager to retake our homes. We will need that fire in the battle to come.

'I will await their arrival here and get them sorted. There will be more to do when you can spare the time. For now, I thank you again.'Galâmka has asked you to sabotage the supplies the Orcs are using in Maurûsh.Find the supplies the Orcs are using in the northern area of Maurûsh.Find the Orc supplies in the northern part of MaurûshSabotage the Orc supplies you have found in the northern area of Maurûsh.Sabotage Orc supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find the supplies the Orcs are using in the western area of Maurûsh.Find the Orc supplies in the western part of MaurushSabotage the Orc supplies you have found in the western area of Maurûsh.Sabotage Orc supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Galâmka in Ub Nishir and inform him of your success.Speak to Galamka'Ah, ${CLASS}, welcome. We can now make use of the information that was in the report you retrieved from Zukhal.

'Her report has made known where the Orcs are keeping their supplies. If we can sabotage those then we can greatly weaken them.'

Galâmka indicates to locations on the map indicating two locations.

'Zukhal marked these areas, one in the north of Maurûsh, and one to the west. I ask of you to make your way to these locations and do what you can to disrupt their supplies in the stronghold.''I hear reports again of your success in Maurûsh! You amaze me again, my friend. We are unstoppable with you on our side!

'The Orcs have lost much thanks to you. There is still more that we must do to prepare, so I ask that you rest and return when you are ready.'Nangar explains the walls of Jirush need repair and archer windows need concealment. He asks that you collect stone from the quarry in the west, and reeds from the marsh in the north to repair the outpost.Nangar asked you to collect sandstone to repair the walls of Jirush from the quarry west of the outpost and reeds from the marshland far to the north of Jirush to conceal archers' windows.Collect large chunks of sandstone from the quarry north-west of Jirush (${NUMBER}/3)Collect reeds from the marsh in northern Khûd Zagin (${NUMBER}/6)You acquired both the sandstone and reeds. Return to Jirush and patch the walls with the sandstone. Then conceal the archers' windows with the reeds.You completed the patch work and hanging of reeds. You should return to Nangar and let him know the work is complete.'To the north-west of Jírush is an ancient quarry where our number were forced into labour by our Ordâkhai overlords. The very stones we mined built some of the ancient walls surrounding the outpost. I need a few stones from that quarry to patch our walls.

'Then to the north and slightly west, near the spot where the once mighty Ikorbân River roared, there are reeds to be gathered and made into lashings to conceal archers' positions in the city.

'Go to these places and gather what I ask. Then patch the locations along our walls to reinforce them and return to me.''You will find the sandstone I need in the quarry to the west of Jirush. The reeds grow far to the north in the last remaining marshland of Khûd Zagin. When you have all I have asked you to collect, you can repair the walls.''Keeping the walls sturdy and strong is an ongoing effort. The wind does as much damage to the outpost as our enemies. Concealing the archers' windows allows us an element of surprise when we are attacked. Your help in addressing both issues is most welcome.''I saw you return with the stone and reeds. The other elders did as well. They are beginning to understand that you are not here as an enemy. They do not yet believe you are a friend. I, on the other hand, trust you enough.'As you liberate Kûr Anzar, recover supplies stolen from Urmâkh along the way.Grab supplies and packs that belong to the innocent residents of Urmâkh as you move through Kûr Anzar.Grab Urmâkhi supplies in Kûr Anzar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bring the stolen packs back to Numûru in Urmâkh.Bring the stolen packs back to Numûru in Urmâkh'As we move throughout Kûr Anzar, be on the look out for supplies. Many valuables and packs have been stolen from residents of Urmâkh, both in the initial fight for Kûr Anzar that saw us expelled and in the time since in Urmâkh.

'Grab any supplies or packs you see. You'll be harming their war efforts and aiding the everyday people of Renewed Hamât.''This is a wonder. Well done. Every pack not in their possession is food in the bellies and supplies on the shelves of the people of Renewed Hamât. Thank you for this.'Some new recruits have volunteered in Iridír after news of the attacks. Bâdarul has asked that you help supply them with weapons so they can begin their training.Some new recruits have volunteered in Iridír after news of the attacks. Bâdarul has asked that you help supply them with weapons so they can begin their training.

Gather supplies of weapons from crates nearby.Gather crate of swordsGather crate of spearsGather crate of bowsArm the recruits in Iridír with the weapons they desire so that they can begin their training.Arm recruits with swords (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Arm recruits with spears (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Arm recruits with bows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Bâdarul in Iridír and inform him that you have armed the new recruits and they are not ready to begin training.Return to Bâdarul'Greetings ${PLAYER}. In the wake of the assault led by Bârshud II we have many people from the area gathering here to volunteer to fight back.

'This warms my heart to see such bravery. I will be busy training the recruits as they are ready but I know that some are still needing to be armed before they can begin. Take some weapons from the crates nearby and arm the recruits with the weapons they desire to learn.''The recruits have been arriving and telling me that you supplied them all! I will have them in fighting shape in no time.'Girhâzi has suggested you assist the Dumûri defending Iridír near the river.You should talk to the Dumûri captain, Dalagín, on the south side of Iridír, near the river.Talk to Dalagín'If you wish to help us hold Iridír, you should head south, to the river-front. There you will find Dumûri archers protecting the city from the Ordâkhai in Eshadûr. Talk to the captain, Dalagín, and see if she requires anything.''Talk to the captain of the archers on the river-front, Dalagín. See if she requires anything.''Girhâzi sent you? It is strange to have an offer of help from an outsider, but I will trust Girhâzi's judgement.'

She sizes you up momentarily as if deciding how much to tell you.

'We are charged with protecting Iridír from a river approach. For a thousand years, there was a grand bridge here called Zibâla, also known as The Flood-span. It was a part of the Road of Riches, and connected Iridír to the fishing village of Eshadûr, on the other side of the Ikorbân.

'It was collapsed one hundred years ago by our people when the Empire of Ordâkh decided our lands should be theirs. Destroying the bridge slowed their advance, but unfortunately failed to keep them out.

'Currently, Ordâkhai forces occupy Eshadûr and it is our duty to make sure that they stay there and do not rebuild the bridge.'The great Roc threatening the ships of Umbar must be defeated - but its lair sits upon a forbidding jungle island rumoured to have been a den for pirates until they were driven away by strange beasts of enormous stature.Complete 'The Isle of Storms -- Tier 1'Complete 'The Isle of Storms -- Tier 2'Complete 'The Isle of Storms -- Tier 3'Complete 'The Isle of Storms -- Great Beasts'Complete 'The Isle of Storms -- Tier 4'Complete 'The Isle of Storms -- Tier 5'Scather-flies, the marsh-flies that infest Umûn Khab in Ambarûl, are both dangerous and numerous.You should slay some scather-flies in Umûn Khab to diminish their population. Umûn Khab is a marsh on the southern banks of the Ikorbân River.Defeat scather-flies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Scather-flies plague this part of Ambarûl's marshes. Slaying some scather-flies to diminish their population would be beneficial to the people of Ambarûl.Meliri informed you they keep beehives around the orchard to pollinate the trees. They produce enough extra honey that they are able to sell some of it at the market.Meliri has tasked you with visiting each of the five beehives around the orange groves of Burukíri in Ambarûl, from which you are to collect honeycombs.Collect honeycombs from beehives (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have visited each of the five beehives around the orange groves of Burukíri in Ambarûl, from which you collected honeycombs. You bring them to Meliri.'I have another job that needs doing. Not afraid of bees, are you? We keep bees here at the orchard to help pollinate the trees. As a nice little extra, we get enough honey from them that we can sell some of it at the market. There are five beehives around Burukíri. Visit each one, collect some honeycomb, and bring them to me.''If you want to make the coin you must do the work! Say hello to the bees at each hive and collect honeycombs.''Beautiful!

'Not you, lûkal, the honey. I mean no insult, but you do look somewhat strange. Which is fine for a stranger. Anyway, here is your coin.'Enârshan has asked you to sabotage the supplies in Khûn Sagaz with the Idâmi concoction as well as take as many of their weapons as you can.Enârshan has provided you with the Idâmi concoction to use on the supplies in Khûn Sagaz to weaken them. She also instructed you to take from them any weapons you find.Contaminate supplies in Khûn Sagaz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather weapons in Khûn Sagaz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Enârshan in the Falls of Ilûritu and let her know you have used her concoction on the supplies and taken what weapons you could.'Ah, you are here. Good. Everything is now ready.'

Enârshan hands you the concoction she crafted.

'Take this concoction and pour it over their supplies within Khûn Sagaz. I also ask that you take any weapons you can from them.

'This will give us the advantage we need to drive them away at last. My falls will soon be free with your help.''You are back. Were you able to find success in Khûn Sagaz?'

Enârshan smiles slightly as you give her the weapons you took and confirm that you used her concoction on the supplies.

'Wonderful news. I believe we are nearing our goal.

'You have done well.'The denizens of Adagím have many tasks, big and small, for you to accomplish.Complete quests in Adagím in Mûr Ghala.Complete quests in Adagím in Mûr GhalaThe denizens of Ambarûl have many tasks, big and small, for you to accomplish.Complete quests in Ambarûl in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete quests in Ambarûl in the Ikorbân Valley.The denizens of Dil-irmíz have many tasks, big and small, for you to accomplish.Complete quests in Dil-irmíz in the Umbar-môkh.Complete quests in Dil-irmíz in the Umbar-môkhThe denizens of Ilmabiri have many tasks, big and small, for you to accomplish.Complete quests in Ilmabiri in the Umbar-môkh.Complete quests in Ilmabiri in the Umbar-môkhThe denizens of Imhûlar have many tasks, big and small, for you to accomplish.Complete quests in Imhûlar in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete quests in Imhûlar in the Ikorbân Valley.The denizens of Kamrabezûr have many tasks, big and small, for you to accomplish.Complete quests in Kamrabezûr in the Umbar-môkh.Complete quests in Kamrabezûr in the Umbar-môkhThe denizens of Khabârkhad have many tasks, big and small, for you to accomplish.Complete quests in Khabârkhad in the Umbar-môkh.Complete quests in Khabârkhad in the Umbar-môkhThe denizens of Khûd Zagin have many tasks, big and small, for you to accomplish.Complete quests in Khûd Zagin in the Ikorbân Valley.Complete quests in Khûd Zagin in the Ikorbân Valley.The denizens of Tâkhdar have many tasks, big and small, for you to accomplish.Complete quests in Tâkhdar in the Umbar-môkh.Complete quests in Tâkhdar in the Umbar-môkhYou have gone on a long and eventful journey with Mizâdi and seen and done much within Shagâna with her.Help Mizadi restore peace, achieve freedom for the Shagâni and renew Hamât in the Ikorbân Valley.Aid Mizâdi by completing the Crown of Hamât in the Ikorbân ValleyThe peoples of the Ikorbân Valley have many tasks, big and small, for you to help them accomplish.Complete quests in the Ikorbân 