<rgb=#ff0000>All Elven Menders must not falter</rgb>Defeat Daikhag.Defeat DaikhagPress deeper into Thûr Hin.Press deeper into Thûr HinListen to Kormoltur, Lord of Terror.Listen to Kormoltur, Lord of TerrorAttack Kormoltur.Attack KormolturDefeat the Utûgi.Defeat the UtûgiDefeat Kormoltur, Lord of Terror.Defeat Kormoltur, Lord of TerrorRaphûz asked you to collect berries from the banks of a small pond at the top of a waterfall north-east of Iridír. He will collect water in the town.Raphûz asked you to find berries with medicinal qualities at a pond atop a waterfall north-east of the settlement of Iridír.Collect wild berries from the pond above the waterfall (${NUMBER}/15)You collected the berries and felt as though you were being watched. You should return the berries to Raphûz in Iridír.'On my return to Iridír, I visited an apothecary and acquired an herb poultice for the deer's wound. I can manage the collection of water here in the village. I cannot, however, leave my post long enough to get food for the deer.

'I learned that this type of deer enjoys a certain berry that grows along the banks of the river. The berries can be found where the water collects before forming a waterfall east and north of here. Can you gather berries to feed the deer?''The pond where the berries grow is north and east of Iridír atop a waterfall. Please collect the wild berries and deliver them to me here in Iridír.''They smell delicious. I asked the people of Iridír if the berries are edible. They suggested we not eat them. They use the berries only in times of illness and claim there are undesirable effects when used. For the deer, they are part of their diet.

'If you are willing, I have another request.'You encountered a watcher tentacle in the area, Bôgalekh in Jadambor would want to hear more about this.You have defeated a watcher tentacle in Dil-irmíz. Bôgalekh in Jadambor would surely like to hear about this.You defeated a watcher tentacleSpeak with Bôgalekh in Jadambor in Dil-irmíz.Speak with Bôgalekh in JadamborYou encountered a watcher tentacle in the area and were able to defeat it.

Bôgalekh in Jadambor would want to hear more about this as it may be an emerging threat.'${CLASS}, I thank you for bringing this news to me.

'We have had reports from our scouts of sightings related to gatherings of men who claim to be followers of the beast Umshûra that have begun to call themselves the Hakâri. I fear your encounter may be entwined with them.

'We may need to delve deeper into this matter and shed light on this group's activities before it is too late.'Repair supplies collected (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'I am all for freedom fighting, but this is simply unbearable.... What? No, what do you care for Jirush's troubles? These battlements are falling apart, and no one will do anything about it! Half of my carpentry crew has left to join the rebels in the hills, leaving me with a mountain of tasks. I do not even have time to collect the supplies I need!

'If you have enough time to listen to an old carpenter's ravings, perhaps you could track down some good materials for me.''If only half my friends would put in the effort you have just done for me. Thank you, you seem to have an excellent understanding of carpentry. I could not have picked better materials myself -- as if I would have had time! I am most grateful. Now I just need to find out where to put everything... no, do not mind me. I will ask for your help again should I require.'A woman waits outside the Dahâl Huliz to see her favourite Hûlaz.Hasna has asked you to pick leafy vines from trellises. However, you must avoid being spotted by gardeners more than a few times.

The trellises can be found around the eastern side of the Tor-gardens pool.Pick leafy vines from trellises (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})<rgb=#FF0000>You must not be spotted by sharp-eyed gardeners! (${NUMBER}/4)</rgb>You have gathered many leafy vines.

You should bring them back to Hasna at the Dahâl Huliz.Hasna is too nervous to give Phêrida Iron-edge the vine circlet and has asked you to go instead.

Phêrida can be found at the Dahâl Huliz.'Are you here to see the Hûliz too? I never have time to watch the fights nowadays, so I come to at least catch a glimpse of them. My favourite is Phêrida Iron-edge -- I used to go to every one of her matches! The way she fights -- '

She stops, red colouring her cheeks.

'Sorry. I did not mean to ramble.

'I had hoped to weave a vine circlet for Phêrida, but the gardeners have seen me take from the trellises one too many times. You, though... you are a fresh face! If you are willing to aid me, the trellises on the eastern side of the pool always have the best vines.''Phêrida is just over there! Quick, give me the vines and I shall weave as fast as I can!'

The instant you hand her the vines, Hasna's nimble fingers go to work. Within a short amount of time, she holds out an impressive circlet made of vines.

'I -- I cannot give this to her. My nerves are getting the best of me. Please go in my stead.'Before you can utter a single word, the Hûlaz politely holds up a hand to stop you.

'This is from Hasna, is it not? I noticed she stopped coming to watch my fights, but she has always been there for me after. Even if she has been too nervous to approach me.' She chuckles. 'It was very sweet of you to help. Now, I do believe it is time for me to talk to her, so if you will excuse me....'Dagortas, an elder among the Kintai Elves of the Ikorbân Valley welcomed you to Shonith and invited you to meet with her assistants in the dying oasis.Dagortas, an elder among the Kintai Elves asked you to introduce yourself to her assistants Thridarlan and Alidal. Each plays an important role in measuring and rewarding the value of those who aid the Kintai in the Valley of Ikorbân.Speak with the sage Thridarlan in ShonithSpeak with the quartermaster AlidalYou spoke with Thridarlan and Alidal. You should return to the elder Elf, Dagortas. She will be pleased to know you met her assistants in Shonith.Return to and speak with Dagortas in Shonith'We have forgotten more songs than we remember, and soon we shall sing no more. We safe-guarded these lands for a reason long ago, but we cannot recall why or how.

'Our time ends, but we are not without hope. The natural order comes undone all around us, and it is all we can do to sustain what bastions remain.

'We plan for an unclear future; fully aware we will not be part of it. We ask you the impossible. We invite you to support us, though we cannot support you in kind.

'Thridarlan and Alidal will speak more about our requests, should you desire to help.''You are welcome among us so long as you do not bring imbalance to the natural order. Speak with Thridarlan and Alidal to learn how you can aid us in our efforts to maintain our land, and how we can repay your efforts.''Dagortas carries the weight of many losses with her and is slow to believe there is good in the world. I believe there is still good and hope. Your willingness to speak with me shows me this is not untrue.

'Our numbers thin, this is true, but our duty remains. We seek harmony with the natural world and will work to maintain careful balance.

'Your aid in restoring and maintaining all things natural and pure will draw us closer and earn what gifts we can afford to provide.

'Please ensure you speak with Alidal.''Our gifts are not the usual bounty you find from Men. While trappings are necessary to survive in the wild, we tend to use our abilities to co-exist with our surroundings rather than destroy or harvest them for personal purposes or gain.

'We will share our knowledge and gifts with those worthiest of them.

'Ensure that you speak with Thridarlan.''We shall honour your efforts if you honour our place. The world grows darker and we only hope to bring more light before we can no longer see. We will not beg your assistance. We will reward your kindness with our own.

'We are the Adúrhid. In the common tongue, we are called the Oasis Elves or Kintai. A fitting name. Now you know us. Will you help us?'Sigênik suggested he would test your attention to details, and that you should pay attention when meeting the elders. It appears he was truthful. He means to test you.Sigênik wishes to ascertain if you paid attention and learned the identity of the elder who is allied with the Rebels in Khûd Zagin. He does not wish to speak within the outpost and suggests you discuss elsewhere.Complete Instance: Who Is Our Ally?You satisfied Sigênik's concerns and correctly identified the elder allied to the rebellion. After returning to Jírush you should speak with Sigênik to learn what is next.Speak with Sigênik near the north entrance of Jírush'The test is simple. Alas, it is not something we should discuss in the open. When you are prepared, return to me so we may find a place more conducive to discussions such as ours.''Do your best to recall the discussions and how you were greeted by each of the elders. Follow me, and please, sheathe your weapons. You will not need them.''I believe you provided enough insight that we may trust you further. Know there will be eyes ever on you as you venture through Khûd Zagin.'Akhamâl's assistant has not returned with a wine delivery.Akhamâl has told you to check the north-western entrance of the Dahâl Huliz for Belhax.Check the Dahâl Huliz's north-western entranceYou have found a leaking crate at the Dahâl Huliz's north-western entrance. Belhax is nowhere in sight.

You should examine it and the puddle it's leaving.Examine the crateExamine the puddleYou have found Belhax's wine delivery, but not him. A trail of wine droplets leads you further around the Tor-gardens pool.

You should follow it.Follow the wine droplet trailYou have found Belhax's wine delivery, but not him. A trail of wine droplets leads you further around the Tor-gardens pool.

You should follow it.Follow the wine droplet trailYou have found Belhax at the gazebo in the center of the Tor-gardens pool!

You should try to talk to him.Talk to BelhaxYou've found Belhax safe and sound.

You should tell Akhamâl back at the Dahâl Huliz.Talk to Akhamâl at the Dahâl Huliz'Where is that boy...?

'You -- on your way here, did you happen across young man about this tall, carrying a crate? Goes by the name of Belhax? No? He should be here by now! We will not have enough wine for arena-goers at this rate....

'If you would like some extra coin, I will pay you to find him for me. First, you should make sure he is not already at the arena's north-western entrance.'Despite your best efforts to wake him, the assistant seems to have fallen into a deep sleep.

Next to him lies a discarded, empty wine bottle. The glass on its side has cracked; perhaps this was what caused the puddle next to the crate. Rather than let the wine go to waste, Belhax might have run off to drink the rest.

It might be kindest to let him continue sleeping while you report back to Akhamâl.After you relay the story of Belhax and the wine, Akhamâl huffs in amusement.

'I am equal parts disgruntled, amused, and impressed. He managed to drink a good amount of wine before falling asleep.

'Thank you for checking on him, and for giving me a story to tell my friends. For now, however, it is time that I woke him. He has a mess to clean up.'The leader of the Tale-wardens is concerned about a new recruit, Raphûz, and asked you to check on the young man. He is concerned because his first time out of Umbar is going poorly.Make your way to Raphûz in the shadow of Telperiën's Wall and ask the young man why he is sullen.Speak with Raphûz near Telperiën's WallRaphûz confessed to dropping his pack while investigating something he saw in the distance while travelling with the caravan. He asked you to follow the road to the south-west and search for his missing pack.Search the area around the road for Raphûz's packYou found the location Raphûz described where he lost his pack and noticed what looked like a person watching you to the north-west. You should investigate.Investigate the person watching you to the north-westYou saw something to the north-west and went to investigate. When you arrived you did not find a person. You did, however, find a pack.Collect Raphûz's packYou took the pack from the ground and made certain it was Raphûz's. You can find no signs that anyone was standing here a moment ago. Return the pack to Raphûz.Raphûz is grateful to you for returning his pack. He asks you to go to Kizeri and tell her that you helped him as she asked.'If you please, ${PLAYER}, our arrival at Telperiën's Wall seems to have upset one of my few Tale-wardens. I cannot attend to the young man's needs with my workload. Could you enquire why the man grew melancholy with our arrival?

'You will find him near the supplies on the south side of the wall. Ask him what weighs so heavily upon him.''Raphûz is young. It is his first time out of Umbar. I am concerned the travel to the south and the tales of this land is making him nervous. Please speak with him.'The young man seems flustered as you approach.

'How can I assist you?'

You explain the request from Kizeri.

'It appears I have not masked my mood well enough to keep it from notice. This bodes poorly for me. My first steps outside of Umbar, and already I am a failure.

'You see, back along the road to the south-west, I spied a vision in the distance and strayed from the trail. Only for a moment, but long enough to lose pace with the caravan. In my haste and struggle to return, I lost my cataloguing pack.

'Before I could explain, Kizeri set me to organize this cart. I know where I lost my pack, but I cannot leave my post.

'I wonder. Would you look south-west just off the road near a rock outcropping and find my pack? I'll confess my failure to Kizeri and accept whatever fate befalls me.'Raphûz looks excited as you approach.

'You found my pack. I am blessed. If I lost this pack, the dishonour I would bring my father's name would be unbearable.'

His smile fades.

'I have nothing to offer you for this kindness. In truth, I do not know if I am worth your kindness.

'I do not know if I should have joined the Phetekâri or made this journey. Everything moved so quickly when my mother passed. The decision to join the Tale-wardens seemed right. Now, I am unsure.

'Thank you. Please tell Kizeri you helped me. Put her at ease. I will find my bearing.''Please tell Kizeri that you helped me recover my pack. I will speak with her shortly.''He could have told me plainly. We have more packs. We are not expecting to only fill one catalogue in our time here.'Mizâdi asks your help in expelling the cruel Bârshud II. War has come to Imhûlar!Speak with Mizâdi in southern Imhûlar outside Bârshud's camp of Nisigurûm.Speak with Mizâdi in southern Imhûlar outside NisigurûmDefeat Ekhamâti and plant Mizâdi's banner in each area.Defeat Ekhamâti forces on the battlefield (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Place Mizâdi's standard outside the gates of NisigurûmPlace Mizâdi's standard in the first encampment of Bârshud's forcesPlace Mizâdi's standard just within the gates of NisigurûmRegroup near Mizâdi on the battlefield.Regroup near Mizâdi on the battlefieldSpeak with Mizâdi on the battlefield.Speak with Mizâdi on the battlefield'I do not long for war, and yet it seems to keep finding me all the same. I tell myself, my shoulders are broad, my back will not break. This is my burden alone.

'Let us meet him then, on the battlefield. We will march south and drive this false Shâr from Imhûlar.''His forces are numerous, but our soldiers are of a greater quality. I would ask you to cut through his lines of Ordâkhai. Plant our banner outside his gates, in his first camp, and just inside the gates. Our troops will be heartened and flood into Nisigurûm. Be the spear-tip, ${PLAYER}.

'My Subuzûri will follow close behind you.''We have lost many good Subuzûri, but now we must press our advantage. We must move into Nisigurûm and find this Bârshud. This snake of Ekhamât will not long survive without its head, and this bloodshed can be brought to a swift conclusion once he is dead.'Mizâdi asks your help in finding and defeating Bârshud II within Nisigurûm, so that the Ekhamâti forces may crumble and flee with their leader slain.Search for Bârshud II near the red tents to the west in Nisigurûm and challenge him to a duel.Search for Bârshud II near the western tents in NisigurûmContinue searching for Bârshud II near the eastern tents further in Nisigurûm and challenge him to a duel.Continue searching for Bârshud near the eastern tents further in NisigurûmSearch for Bârshud II near the main tent in Nisigurûm and challenge him to a duel.Search for Bârshud II near the main tent in NisigurûmDefeat Antagâl, Bârshud's Umûni!Defeat Antagâl, Bârshud's UmûniAntagâl is wounded. He scuttled behind the main tent in Nisigurûm. Interrogate Antagâl about where Bârshud really is.Interrogate Antagâl about where Bârshud really isFind Mizâdi on the battlefield and give her this grim news.Find Mizâdi on the battlefield and give her this grim news'We must find Bârshud within the camp. Head towards the back, to the Shâr's tent. If you find him, defeat him. Shout out when you see him. I will be close, and if I hear you, I will close the distance and end his threat myself.

'Now go - we must find him quickly. We are outnumbered, and I fear with each passing moment more of my Subuzûri will fall and this day may be lost.''He is not here, you cur! He is too smart for you. He left this small force here to tie up Mizâdi, the pretender. Her army is the largest in Shagâna beside our own. It would have been inconvenient for her to intercept the Shâr as he cuts a glorious path through Khûd Zagin and Ambarûl.

'Ambarûl has grain enough for all of Ekhamât. We never wanted your cursed land. Your soil is fit for nothing but blood and oaths. Your Mizâdi danced right to the tune we played for her.

'I may die, but Ekhamât is forever.'

With those words, Antagâl's body falls back and he is no more.'No! I don't believe it. What a fool I was!'Raphûz is soon to move to Khûd Zagin and asks you to help him get food from the wilds of Ambarûl, near Wrackwade, to provide him with rations for his journey.Raphûz wants to prove that he can live off the land as the Shagâni do. He asks that you head into the wilds and collect nuts, berries, and meat from across Ambarûl to use on his upcoming journey.Collect wild food near Wrackwade in Ambarûl (${NUMBER}/12)You collected food from around Ambarûl. You should deliver what you found and collected to Raphûz at Wrackwade.'I received orders. I am soon to move south into Khûd Zagin. The adventure continues, eh?'

He smirks.

'On the journey south, I want to live as the Shagâni live. I want to use the land and its bounty to survive. Again, however, the eyes of my leader are upon me, and I cannot leave my post.

'Will you go into the wilds and collect nuts, berries, and meat?''There is enough to last a month. You are a true friend. I thank you again for all the assistance. I hope that I shall see you once I cross the bridge into Khûd Zagin.'Entering the city of Zajâna is awe-inspiring. The weight of centuries dwells within her walls, and her people look to build a future free of tyranny. You are sure to become an ally.The leaders of Zajâna are not as welcoming as others may be. Too many times has an open hand quickly turned to a shackle. Valakhâri directed you to introduce yourself to the Alahamâr for further instruction.Speak with Quartermaster Alahamâr at ZajânaYour introduction to the quartermaster is complete. Return to Valakhâri and tell her you are ready to assist the city and her people.Speak with Valakhâri in Zajâna'Another face unknown to me. There are many such now. Not long past, those like you would go west to the cells of Emax Dûl. Civility returns and Zajâna stirs, and the Doorwards seek again the name it bore of old: a city of esteem, and cross-roads of the wise. The City of Keys.

'If you would earn regard of our folk, your deeds shall be weighed, and your worth measured. Speak with the Quartermaster—they will show what task may earn you standing.''To make a name here, you must act in service to Kighân and more, to Zajâna. Our land, like our people, stands at a turning. We seek again the freedom we once knew, and still desire.

'Aid us truly, and your name shall be writ among those of good repute. Cross us, and it shall be stricken, and you marked foe. The choice lies with you.

'Prove your worth, and we shall speak of trade and reward. For now, begone; I have much to address.''Take no offence at our reserve. Zajâna has suffered long, and we have learned to be wary of open hands. Too often have gifts masked chains. We will watch. We will judge. Let your actions speak until your voice has earned its weight.'A worker in the fortress asked if you were interested in betting on the odds of a terrible event befalling a worker under the watchful eyes of one of the foretress' foremen.You were asked if you wanted to participate in a macabre game that the workers of Rakhatâb are playing. You will need to pay the entry fee and then make a choice: Which foreman do you think will have an accident befall a worker under their care?Speak with Othax'I do not need to know who you are. All I know is that you are not holding a rod, and so you are like us: a worker or a mercenary.

'If you are looking to earn a little favour from the workers and people here, we can allow you join our little game.

'The premise is gruesome, but the payout can be good.

'A good day is a day without injury or worse here in Rakhatâb. A bad day, on the other hand, I am sure you can imagine.

'All you need do is tell me what foreman will have tragedy befall their workers. If you choose correctly, you earn a share of the bets. If you lose, it is only a bit of coin. What say you?''If you would like to play, all you need to do next is tell me which foreman you think will have a worker experience an accident.'The Streets of Râhal Bakh cast a darkened vignette on the people of Umbar. Brave the tapestry of corruption set upon you by Khâshap and free the Umbari of his influence and shadow.Complete 'The Streets of Râhal Bakh -- Tier 1'Complete 'The Streets of Râhal Bakh -- Tier 2'Complete 'The Streets of Râhal Bakh -- Tier 3'Complete 'The Streets of Râhal Bakh -- Braver'Complete 'The Streets of Râhal Bakh -- Tier 4'Complete 'The Streets of Râhal Bakh -- Tier 5'The Mâkhda Khorbo, Temple of the All-Seeing, crumbled into ruin at the moment of Sauron's defeat, but remains a place of great interest for those seeking artifacts of evil. When Azagath Sea-shadow fled from the Citadel of Winds in the company of his comrades Belondor and Nakási Wave-reaper, his purpose was not escape alone. What treasure of the Dark Lord's might he have wrested from those buried ruins? Its identity remains unknown, but your pursuit of Azagath played a role in fracturing the bonds between some of these Kindred.The Mâkhda Khorbo, Temple of the All-Seeing, crumbled into ruin at the moment of Sauron's defeat, but remains a place of great interest for those seeking artifacts of evil. When Azagath Sea-shadow fled from the Citadel of Winds in the company of his comrades Belondor and Nakási Wave-reaper, his purpose was not escape alone. What treasure of the Dark Lord's might he have wrested from those buried ruins? Its identity remains unknown, but your pursuit of Azagath played a role in fracturing the bonds between some of these Kindred.The Mâkhda Khorbo, Temple of the All-Seeing, crumbled into ruin at the moment of Sauron's defeat but remains a place of great interest for th