ing the bonds between some of these Kindred.Defeat Azagath's Sea-shadow and his crewDefeat Belondor and his crewDefeat Umshûra the GluttonAfter a battle at the Tower of Winds that crippled their ship, Azagath, Belondor, and Nakási, Reaper of the Waves flee to the cavernous underground beneath Mâkhda Khorbo. The subterranean harbour served as an illicit smuggler's den for the Temple of the All-seeing Eye, and the evil wrought by its inhabitant remains in the stone.Azagath's personal guard, bolstered by a fell-shade of the man, bar the entrance to the smuggler's cover beneath Mâkhda Khorbo. Their orders are to slaughter any interlopers.Defeat Azagath's Sea-shade and his crewDefeat Belondor and his crewDefeat Umshûra the Glutton within the Mâkhda KhorboThe Mâkhda Khorbo, Temple of the All-Seeing, crumbled into ruin at the moment of Sauron's defeat but remains a place of great interest for those seeking artifacts of evil. When Azagath Sea-shadow fled from the Citadel of Winds in the company of his comrades Belondor and Nakási Wave-reaper, his purpose was not escape alone. What treasure of the Dark Lord's might he have wrested from those buried ruins? Its identity remains unknown, but your pursuit of Azagath played a role in fracturing the bonds between some of these Kindred.The Mâkhda Khorbo, Temple of the All-Seeing, crumbled into ruin at the moment of Sauron's defeat but remains a place of great interest for those seeking artifacts of evil. When Azagath Sea-shadow fled from the Citadel of Winds in the company of his comrades Belondor and Nakási Wave-reaper, his purpose was not escape alone. What treasure of the Dark Lord's might he have wrested from those buried ruins? Its identity remains unknown, but your pursuit of Azagath played a role in fracturing the bonds between some of these Kindred.Defeat Azagath's Sea-shadow and his crewDefeat Belondor and his crewDefeat Umshûra the GluttonAfter a battle at the Tower of Winds that crippled their ship, Azagath, Belondor, and Nakási, Reaper of the Waves flee to the cavernous underground beneath Mâkhda Khorbo. The subterranean harbour served as an illicit smuggler's den for the Temple of the All-seeing Eye, and the evil wrought by its inhabitant remains in the stone.Azagath's personal guard, bolstered by a fell-shade of the man, bar the entrance to the smuggler's cover beneath Mâkhda Khorbo. Their orders are to slaughter any interlopers.Defeat Azagath's Sea-shade and his crewDefeat Belondor and his crewDefeat Umshûra the Glutton within the Mâkhda KhorboThe Mâkhda Khorbo, Temple of the All-Seeing, crumbled into ruin at the moment of Sauron's defeat but remains a place of great interest for those seeking artifacts of evil. When Azagath Sea-shadow fled from the Citadel of Winds in the company of his comrades Belondor and Nakási Wave-reaper, his purpose was not escape alone. What treasure of the Dark Lord's might he have wrested from those buried ruins? Its identity remains unknown, but your pursuit of Azagath played a role in fracturing the bonds between some of these Kindred.The Mâkhda Khorbo, Temple of the All-Seeing, crumbled into ruin at the moment of Sauron's defeat but remains a place of great interest for those seeking artifacts of evil. When Azagath Sea-shadow fled from the Citadel of Winds in the company of his comrades Belondor and Nakási Wave-reaper, his purpose was not escape alone. What treasure of the Dark Lord's might he have wrested from those buried ruins? Its identity remains unknown, but your pursuit of Azagath played a role in fracturing the bonds between some of these Kindred.Defeat Azagath's Sea-shadow and his crewDefeat Belondor and his crewDefeat Umshûra the GluttonThe local dog-catcher, Barûl, has asked for your help in acquiring some supplies with which to catch stray dogs in Urmâkh.Barûl has asked for your help in collecting discarded cloth to treat wounds and loose rope for leashes for the stray dogs of Urmâkh. You can find discarded cloth and loose rope around Urmâkh.Gather discarded cloth in Urmâkh for stray dogs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather loose rope in Urmâkh for stray dogs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Barûl in Urmâkh with the cloth and rope you have collected.'I have a matter with which I could use your help, if you are willing. I do what I can to keep stray dogs off the streets of Urmâkh. I collect them, treat their wounds with stray cloth and fashion leashes from loose rope I find. I am running low on supplies. If you're willing, I could use whatever you find around Urmâkh. My work keeps me busy, so I have little time to collect more.''This is wonderful. I can help so many stray dogs with this. Thank you. I appreciate your help, friend.'Urdush, a local resident, claims there are no dogs in Urmâkh. You should investigate more.Speak with Urmâkh villagers to learn more about the vanishing of Urmâkh's dogs.Speak with Agiti about the vanished dogsSpeak with Sûdakh about the vanished dogsSpeak with Ghemûna about the vanished dogsCheck the rumoured dog locations to see if any clues or dogs reside there.Check the southern edge of Urmâkh for signs of dogsCheck the north-eastern corner of Urmâkh for signs of dogsCheck near the blacksmith's forge for signs of dogsReturn to speak with Urdush.Return to speak with Urdush'You've been gathering supplies to catch stray dogs? We used to have many, but they all disappeared recently. There are no dogs here in Urmâkh. No dogs at all. Who did you say you gathered these items for?

'Barûl? I've never heard of a Barûl. He isn't a resident here - I've lived in Urmâkh all my life.

'You can try asking around and talking with other Urmâkh residents, but we don't have a dog-catcher here in Urmâkh. All the dogs disappeared - we don't need one.''It is as I feared. I believe this dog-catcher may have designs on the fate of dogs, and possibly worse. You should speak with Niriga. Her husband is missing - he did not come home. I hope he is merely drunk and will soon stagger home after sleeping it off, but I fear this dog-catcher may wish ill of more than dogs.

'You should speak with her to learn more. She is across the way, over by Nukûsh, the blacksmith.''Dogs? No, no dogs here. We used to have dogs and then they all just... vanished. I haven't heard a dog barking in weeks. It's strange, now that you mention it. We used to have lots of dogs in Urmâkh.''No, no dogs. My dog, Hunter, went outside to relieve himself three weeks ago. That was the last I saw of him. I miss him every day. He used to always relieve himself by Nukûsh's forge. Might check there. Don't tell Nukûsh that though, please.''I don't miss the dogs, but I know many others do. All that howling and yelling at all hours. But yes, that all stopped several weeks ago. It's been eerily quiet at night. I know the dogs used to gather in the north-east and south-east corners of Urmâkh. There might be something there. I always stayed away from the dogs.'Niriga, a resident of Urmâkh, is worried about her husband, Namâkh, who didn't come home last night.Speak with Niriga in Urmâkh to determine the best course of action.Speak with Niriga in UrmâkhSpeak with Sûdakh and Ghemûna in Urmâkh.Speak with Sûdakh in UrmâkhSpeak with Ghemûna in UrmâkhReturn to Niriga in Urmâkh with what you have learned.Speak with Niriga when you are ready to goReturn to Niriga in Urmâkh and tell her what happened in Shakhdag.Return to Niriga in Urmâkh'Have you seen my husband, Namâkh? He never came home last night. I am worried about him. The jackals are getting hungrier and more ferocious with each passing day.

'I love my husband, but he is a fool with drink sloshing in his head. He doesn't know his top from his bottom with a bit of ale in him.

'Would you help me find him?''He's taken him? Barûl's taken my husband? We must find Namâkh. We must find him immediately!''Shakhdag is overrun with wild boar! Why would he take such a risk? Why not simply tell me he needed time alone? This is terrible, he could have been gored! You must go to Shakhdag at once. You must find my husband.''Whenever he drinks he doesn't go anywhere without his co-conspirators. A terrible influence, they are. Best to start with them; Sûdakh and Ghemûna are their names.''He wasn't out with us last night, we could have used him. Had to finish off twice the ale with him gone! I didn't see him. Maybe Ghemûna knows more?''Well he wasn't with me, if that's what you're implying. I know that's what Niriga is implying. She's never been fond of our friendship. But no, he wasn't in my company either.'

Ghemûna pauses. She looks like she is collecting her thoughts. Decision made, she turns to you.

'Look, sometimes Namâkh needs time by himself. He has told me and Sûdakh as much. He goes out to Shakhdag and just thinks. Niriga would never understand. But if Niriga truly is worried about him, Shakhdag to the east is where I'd look for him.'Shakhdag is over-run with wild boar and crumbling ruins. Search amongst both for signs of Niriga's husband, Namâkh.Search among the ruins for signs of Namâkh.Search among the ruins for signs of NamâkhListen to Barûl.Listen to BarûlNiriga is worried her husband has been kidnapped by Barûl, the dog-catcher. Search for clues as to Namâkh's whereabouts.Search Urmâkh for Namâkh's personal effects for clues as to Namâkh's location.Return to Niriga with the items and report the location you found them.Return to Niriga in UrmâkhSpeak with Niriga when you are ready to go.Speak with Niriga when you are ready to goComfort Niriga as best you can.Comfort Niriga'We must do everything we can to find Namâkh! I know he would have left me clues. I believe he and Barûl may still be in Urmâkh. We need to search Urmâkh for anything that could have been on my husband - anything he left behind for us.''He's gone. I can't believe he's gone. And that... thing. I don't know what it was - it called itself The Hungry Storm? I thought it was just a legend? It was so awful. So awful.

'I can't believe he's gone.

'I can't believe he's gone.''Quickly. My husband may be wounded or bound as we speak. We must go!''Where did you say they were? That house all the items were around is abandoned... or at least it was. Quickly, we must go there! I believe Namâkh was there. And I am coming with you. I will do anything I can to help my husband.'You have traced Namâkh and Barûl to this house in Urmâkh. Inside, the smell is musty, infused with the scent of blood. As you enter, you see Namâkh bound in the corner, with Barûl standing over him.Defeat Barûl.Defeat BarûlListen to Barûl and Niriga.Listen to Barûl and NirigaDefeat Barûl.Defeat BarûlListen to Barûl.Listen to BarûlCheck on Namâkh.Check on NamâkhDahâl Huliz has long been home to many spectacular contests, pitting capable gladiators against all forms of opponents. Rothog has summoned you to witness the unveiling of his latest spectacle for the Arena.Rothog has summoned you to witness the unveiling of his latest spectacle for the Arena. Speak to him.Talk to Rothog the Storm in the ArenaWith Ragrekhûl's escape, a Tempestuous Flame has appeared within the arena. Defeat the creature so it does not cause additional damage and loss of life.Defeat the Tempestuous FlameDuring the commotion, members of the cult of the All-Seeing Eye have taken the opportunity to attack the city. With Ragrekhûl circling the Citadel of the Winds, you must now secure the approach to the Citadel of the Winds.Secure the approach to the Citadel of the WindsSecure the courtyard outside of the Citadel of the Winds.Defeat the All-Seeing Eye cultistsRagrekhûl's rampage across Umbar has endangered the Umbari citizens. Defeat Ragrekhûl in the Courtyard of the Citadel of the Winds before more perish.Defeat Ragrekhûl'Welcome to Dahâl Huliz, the grand arena of Umbar Baharbêl! Today on this sacred ground, I will unveil a most fearsome spectacle, Ragrekhûl, the Storm Serpent.

'As you know, Shaidal was sent forth to capture this beast, and to my surprise, he was successful!

'This will be one of my greatest displays and ensure my legacy. I have asked you here to witness the unveiling, and for you to see Shaidal receive his well-deserved reward.

