'Now, to the presentation!'The gladiatorial pits of Umbar Baharbêl serve several important purposes: entertaining the masses, keeping their attention focused, and meting justice upon those who break the laws of the city.Complete 'The Dragon and the Storm -- Tier 5'Mizâdi has asked you to accompany the southern scout Nimasi to search for the missing Hamati scout Surâsh.Speak with Nimasi in southern Imhûlar.Speak with Nimasi in southern ImhûlarExamine the banner Nimasi found.Examine the banner Nimasi foundFollow the bootprints that lead away from the banner south-west and see where they lead.Look for clues to the south-westContinue following the bootprints that lead away from the banner south-west.Look for clues you find and follow where they leadContinue following the bootprints that lead away from the banner north-west.Look for clues you find to determine where they leadSpeak with Nimasi outside of the camp.Speak with Nimasi outside of the camp'Thank you for looking after this situation in the south. I hope Surâsh is merely waylaid, and the situation is not worse.

'Please, hurry back here after you are done. There is much still to do in Kûr Anzar, and we have only just begun.''Hashtal-gûr favoured outsider, and praise to the Shâra, who is indeed benevolent. We must find the source of these disappearances - or I fear for all of our safety.

'This is the site where we were supposed to meet with Surâsh, but she never came. Instead I found the banner I gave you. As you can see, there are many bootprints around this area, and some leading away to the south.

'I believe we can follow them to find the source of these disappearances, and the banners. I have not gone myself for fear of disappearing, but with the liberator of Kûr Anzar, I know we can overcome anything these lûbaras throw at us.''Hurry! Get over here before you're seen!

'Look at all the banners - and the furnishings for that tent. This must be the source of the attacks.

'We need to investigate this camp, I'd wager this is where they are keeping Surâsh. There are so many of them, I wonder from where they all left.'Upset that she has been asked to leave Arwáth, Agalûnu wishes to speak to Shanathar directly.Agalûnu has asked you to take her to meet the warden of Arwáth. You should tell her when you are ready to go.Complete Instance: The Fading of the ForestsYou escorted Agalûnu to meet with Shanthar. He explained why she should not clear-cut trees, especially in Ambarûl. You should talk to Agalûnu and find out what she is thinking.Talk to Agalûnu'This is madness, ${PLAYER}. I am well enough for a little travel. I would like you to take me to this supposed Kinta Elf. I will talk to him and see what, exactly, is so important that he would shoot someone but not speak with them. Tell me when you are ready to leave.''Are you ready to go? I will talk to this ignorant Kinta and make him see reason.''I am a fool ${PLAYER}. I had no idea the whole of Ambarûl was once covered in a lush forest of such extraordinary trees. Worse yet, I am no better than my forebears who destroyed them. Like I did, they doubtless took for granted that it would always be there, no matter what.'

Agalûnu sits in silent thought for several moments before she winces.

'I spoke the truth when I told the Kinta I wanted to help, but I confess that perhaps my wound is not as healed as I thought. I do not think I will be capable of helping him anytime soon.'Raphûz recounts a tale he overheard while travelling to Iridír of a woman searching for her pet deer traded to a man meant to free her mother's spirit from the creature.Raphûz asked you to assist him in saving a deer from being sacrificed to a serval sire in a den north-west of Iridír. He will meet you near the den where the deer is kept.Defeat servals in their den north-west of Iridír (${NUMBER}/8)You fought your way through the servals. Find Raphûz outside of the den and speak with him.Speak with Raphûz outside of the serval sire's denRaphûz is injured and cannot assist with fighting the serval. He asked you to enter the den to defeat the serval and recover the deer.Defeat the serval sire, BuzanbûriThe deer lay before you, injured, but alive. You dealt with the serval. You should lift the fallow deer and deliver it to Raphûz.Rescue the deer and bring it to RaphûzYou brought the deer to Raphûz. He bound his wound and said he would take the deer back to Iridír and secure medicine to heal the deer. He asked you to visit him in Iridír.Speak with Raphûz at Iridír'${PLAYER}, I overheard a remarkable story.

'A merchant delivered his daughter's prized pet to a man here in Ambarûl. The merchant believed the spirit of his deceased wife inhabited the deer and an Ambarûli man pledged he would free the woman's spirit.

'The Ambarûli man lies and instead plans to sacrifice the deer to a serval sire plaguing him. The daughter came to Ambarûl to collect her pet. The descriptions of the woman match the woman we saw near Telperiën's wall.

'I found the serval pride's den. I need help rescuing the deer. The den is north-west of Iridír, east of Telperiën's wall. Will you meet me there and help me rescue the woman's pet?''The deer was taken to a serval den north-west of Iridír. I will meet you there and we can rescue the deer together.''Do not worry about me, ${PLAYER}. My wound is minor. I need to bind it. The serval sire is nearby. Can you slay it? Then, rescue the deer and return it to me.''Do not worry after me. I will bind my wound and be ready to leave this place. Quickly, the beast and deer are up ahead. Defeat the serval and rescue the deer.'The deer stirs and begins to follow you.

Bring the deer to Raphûz.'Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I have earned some coins since arriving in Iridír. I will share them with you. I will also mark an entry in my records for the Phetekâri.'Shubârza has asked that you find the sword once wielded by her brother, Iregâr, who fell in battle nearby in an Ekhamâti assault.Shubârza has asked that you find the sword once wielded by her brother, Iregâr, who fell in battle nearby in an Ekhamâti assault.Reach the battlefield Shubârza describedYou have reached the battle-ground about which Shubârza told you. There are many weapons scattered around. One of these must be the sword once wielded by her brother, Iregâr, who fell in battle nearby in an Ekhamâti assault.Find ZigûliReturn to Shubârza in Amalíbi's camp near Iridír with her brother's sword.Return to Shubârza with Zigûli'${CLASS}, I have a request to ask of you.'

Shubârza sits up slightly and groans from her healing wounds.

'In a recent attack led by the Ekhamâti my brother, Iregâr, fell. We were able to recover the bodies and give them proper funerals, but the ones who brought them back did not recover their weapons.

'My brother wielded a sword known as Zigûli which has been passed down in our family. I wished to wield it to honour him and continue the tradition, but I was recently injured and can not go recover it myself. I fear some brigand or worse, an Ekhamâti soldier, will take it.

'It should be to the north-east at the top of the waterfall and across a wooden bridge where they recovered his body. You can identify it by the gold engravings on the blade.''You... you found it.'

Tears well up in Shubârza eyes as she holds the sword tight.

'I can not thank you enough for this kindness. I miss my brother deeply, but now, thanks to you, I can at least fight on in his honour. Please take this. It is less than you deserve, but it is all I can offer.'For over a hundred years, the Kintai Elves have battled a mysterious blight, seemingly brought on by the Din of Stone. It has already consumed once-beautiful Adagím, and now threatens the rest of the Elven glades. An investigation by the Rangers Faeron and Rhadrog has tracked the source of the blight to The Folly of Nagakhêdi, but what dangers lurk inside the ancient and abandoned wonder?Defeat the threats that lurk within The Folly of Nagakhêdi.Defeat Badharál the GorgerDefeat MaukhornDefeat the Legion of LhaerethDefeat Zamâktar the PutrescentFor over a hundred years, the Kintai Elves have battled a mysterious blight, seemingly brought on by the Din of Stone. It has already consumed once-beautiful Adagím, and now threatens the rest of the Elven glades. An investigation by the Rangers Faeron and Rhadrog has tracked the source of the blight to The Folly of Nagakhêdi, but what dangers lurk inside the ancient and abandoned wonder?Defeat the threats that lurk within The Folly of Nagakhêdi.Defeat Badharál the GorgerDefeat MaukhornDefeat the Legion of LhaerethDefeat Zamâktar the PutrescentFor over a hundred years, the Kintai Elves have battled a mysterious blight, seemingly brought on by the Din of Stone. It has already consumed once-beautiful Adagím, and now threatens the rest of the Elven glades. An investigation by the Rangers Faeron and Rhadrog has tracked the source of the blight to The Folly of Nagakhêdi, but what dangers lurk inside the ancient and abandoned wonder?Defeat the threats that lurk within The Folly of Nagakhêdi.Defeat Badharál the GorgerDefeat MaukhornDefeat the Legion of LhaerethDefeat Zamâktar the PutrescentYour aid is requested in the continued efforts to improve the fortunes of Umbar Baharbêl.The Fortunes of Umbar Baharbêl daily quests are available at the Hunter's Expedition Camp, in Rakhatâb, and in Jax Phanâl.Complete Fortunes of Umbar Baharbêl daily quests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Completed many Fortunes of Umbar Baharbêl daily quests quests, assisting the citizens of Umbar Baharbêl.Completed'We must continue to improve the fortunes of Umbar Baharbêl for all of its citizens!

'If you are willing to lend your efforts several more times, I will be able to reward your accomplishments.'Your efforts have truly assisted those who work to improve the fortunes of Umbar Baharbêl. You will be rewarded for your efforts.Members of the Kindred of the Coins take petitions from nobles throughout Umbar. Rothog has summoned you to his chambers to hear one specific complaint.Speak to Rothog about the audience.Travel with Rothog to the audienceRothog has requested your presence for a petition of one of his nobles.Talk to RothogFollowing the audience, Rothog would like a word regarding the petition.Talk to Rothog in Dâr Laja'It is good to see you again. Your work throughout these lands has spread far and wide. I have a request to make of you. Would you bear witness to a complaint that might involve one of my gladiators?''${PLAYER}, It is good of you to come to me. I may have a bit of a issue with one of my gladiators. I have received a petition from a rather bothersome noble by the name of Zarzíra Dawn-star.

'I fear this may become an issue, and I may need someone of your abilities to assist. Will you come and bear witness to the proceedings?''Are you ready? Let us get this over with.''It was interesting to hear her need of justice in this case. However, it does seem to jog my memory of a conversation with Shaidal and his claims of innocence. Something to think on.'Within the halls of Dahâl Huliz, the gladiators make their home. Rothog has asked that you question Shaidal.Speak to Rothog regarding the petition from Zarzíra Dawn-star.Talk to RothogRothog has asked that you travel to within Dahâl Huliz, inside the the gladiator residences and speak to Shaidal about the situation.Talk to RothogAfter your conversation with Shaidal and the surprising ambush, speak to Rothog regarding the encounter.Talk to Rothog in Dâr Laja'Given the petition that we just heard from Zarzíra Dawn-star, I feel that it might be a good time to speak to Shaidal and hear what he might have to say regarding it. You see, he was in the employ of Zarzíra, when one of her competitors was slain. He was brought here to face justice for the act, but has always proclaimed his innocence. She had advocated for his death, but instead he was sentenced to fight in the sands. She again calls for his head very quickly.

'This makes me think that there may be fire behind the smoke, eh?

'He is in the residences for our formidable fighters within halls of the Dahâl Huliz. Go find him and speak to him, find out what information you can learn, and then report back to me.''${PLAYER}, it is time to travel into the residences of the gladiators in Dahâl Huliz. Please speak to Shaidal, and report your findings.''Time for you to meet Shaidal, yes?''This brazen attack within Dahâl Huliz is most troubling to me. His tale seems to indicate that there might be more to his case.

'I will call him here, keep him within sight, and perhaps you can speak to him and gather more proof of what is really going on.'Shaidal has requested that you seek out Makhil who has fled into Kamrabezûr to escape Zarzíra Dawn-star and her Khadeji.Search Hulzidâr, a small encampment beneath the arena, for Makhil's path.Locate Makhil's passage near HulzidârContinue your search for Makhil's path, west of Hulzidâr.Locate Makhil's passage west of HulzidârContinue your search for Makhil's path, north of the cross-roads, west of Hulzidâr.Locate Makhil's passage north of the cross-roadsContinue your search for Makhil's path, near Kên Taghlim in Kamrabezûr.Locate Makhil's passage near Kên TaghlimSpeak to Makhil's about the information that he recovered from Zarzíra Dawn-star's estate.Talk to Makhil east of Kên Taghlim'As I mentioned, Zarzíra Dawn-star has been attempting to frame me for some of her misdeeds. Several weeks ago, I was able to contact and hire a burglar named Makhil, who promised to recover information needed for my release.

'He mentioned that he would flee to Kamrabezûr in the catacombs. You may wish to start looking in Hulzidâr, a small encampment beneath the arena.

'Can you go into Kamrabezûr, located underneath Dahâl Huliz and look for signs of his passage?''You have at last caught me, unless... are you a friend of Shaidal's? Oh most joyous news.

'I fear that the Khadeji continue to search for me, and the information that I gathered.

'Before you arrived, I hid the information that was recovered elsewhere in a place which might be dangerous to others, but thank you for finding me.'Makhil has requested that you recover a series of evidence parcels hidden throughout Ghâr Mejet, an ancient crypt teeming with Wights in Kamrabezûr.Makhil has requested that you recover a series of evidence parcels hidden throughout Ghâr Mejet, an ancient crypt teeming with Wights in Kamrabezûr.Locate parcels in Ghâr Mejet (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Dâr Laja and speak to Shaidal about the evidence that you recovered.Return to Dâr Laja and speak to Shaidal'So that you are aware, the documents that I recovered on behalf of Shaidal uncovered both correspondence between Rothog's enemies and also a series of ledgers that have suspicious financial information that Shaidal was trying to expose before his capture.

'Unfortunately, with the Khadeji hunting for me, I chose to hide it in a fairly dangerous place.
 
'The parcels of information are hidden within Ghâr Mejet, an ancient crypt infested with Wights. Could you recover these and return them to Shaidal in Dâr Laja?''You are back so soon? I hope you bring good news.

'Thank you for gathering this information, these parcels should prove most useful when The Storm next holds his court. It is frightening to think that this woman goes to such lengths to bring ruin upon me, and betray Rothog as well.

'Thank you, I hope this will be enough to set me free.'Armed with proof of Shaidal's innocence, you approach Rothog the Storm with your findings.Rothog the Storm asks you to approach with your findings.Travel with Rothog to the audience chamberRothog has requested that you present the evidence that you have gathered regarding Shaidal's actions.Talk to RothogFollowing the audience, Rothog would like a word.Talk to Rothog in Dâr Laja'It seems to be time for our conversation regarding Shaidal and Zarzíra's actions. Your work in this matter has been excellent and I am most thankful for your thoroughness in this matter.

'Will you meet me in my audience chamber so we can discuss this delicate matter more quietly?''${PLAYER}, it is good of you to come to me. This petition has been most bothersome, and I seek to discover the heart of the matter.

'Would you be kind enough to find your way to my audience chamber, so I could join you shortly?''Please go ahead, I will join you rather shortly.''You may think me cruel for sending Shaidal on such a difficult journey, but his agents did violate the home of one of my nobles, and I could not simply allow that to happen. That being said, the information gathered allowed me to give him the chance to free himself.

'However, this Zarzíra's treachery does give me pause and require some thought, I may ask you to attend when I kindly suggest that she make a mandatory appearance in my presence.'Rothog the Storm has requested that you travel into the catacombs below Dahâl Huliz and recover a precious shipment that was important to him.Rothog the Storm has requested that travel into the catacombs to Harkhaphâr and do several tasks. He requests that you thin the number of gladiators there, gather their metal chains, and recover food stuffs from the camp.Collect metal chains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat gladiators (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather Rothog's food stuffs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rothog awaits you in the Dâr Laja Meeting Hall.

Return with the stolen objects and inform him of your victory.Rothog awaits you in the Dâr Laja Meeting Hall'${PLAYER}! While I await for Zarzíra to arrive, I have a task that I would welcome your assistance.  You see, your friend Shaidal has gone to fetch something that is precious to me. However, the beast requires certain items that are needed to assist us on the creature's arrival.

'The problem is that there are those who dwell in the catacombs below the arena who wish to do me harm, and they had the audacity to steal my shipment.

'Could you travel to Harkhaphâr, south of Hulzidâr below, and assist me with this problem?'You present the recovered goods to Rothog the Storm.

'I see that my trust in you was not misplaced. My hope was that those who betrayed us may have learned an important lesson. Perhaps they will. Once again your work is exemplary, and your hand in my spectacle will not be forgotten by me.

'Thank you for your help!'Rothog the Storm has requested your aid in travelling to retrieve needed supplies for his next spectacle. Travel to Kheb Hanût and The Dûlkar, speak to Rothog's contacts, and return.Travel to Kheb Hanût and speak to Sâkhariz there to gather reinforced bolts to secure the creature.Speak to Sâkhariz regarding the requested goodsTravel to The Dûlkar and speak to Nadima and retrieve apothecary supplies.Travel to The Dûlkar and speak to NadimaReturn to Rothog and meet him in the Dâr Laja Meeting Hall.Talk to Rothog in Dâr Laja Meeting Hall'Some of my messengers have had most unpleasant difficulties when attempting to gather items that I need quite urgently. These items are rare and can be somewhat sought after.

'Could you find your way to Kheb Hanût and speak to my contact Sâkhariz there? I need you to gather reinforced bolts to secure the creature, and then travel to The Dûlkar and speak to Nadima and retrieve supplies that our apothecaries require most urgently.''I understand that your patron has requested very special goods. Luckily, I was able to obtain them with some great challenges to myself. Please let your benefactor know that these goods should perform to expectations.''While I know the traversal of the catacombs below can be problematic, I appreciate your discretion and willingness to go to that place.

'I hope that these objects will make my grand unveiling something truly to behold.

'Thank you for your work again. I can see why your name has become known within this hall.''Oh, you are here. I believe I have the package that was requested by your patron. I do warn you that the objects inside appear to have been jostled, but I assure you of the quality of the product.

'I wish you all the best of luck with its use.'Now with proof of her treachery, Rothog calls forth Zarzíra Dawn-star for questioning.Speak to Rothog the Storm about the situationTravel with Rothog to the audience chamberRothog has requested your attendance in his questioning of Zarzíra Dawn-star.Talk to RothogFollowing Zarzíra's actions in his chambers, Rothog asks to speak to you.Talk to Rothog in Dâr Laja'It seems that Zarzíra has decided it was time to grace us with her presence. Amongst the difficulties is that I feel that she may have a patron or someone who sought to weaken my position amongst the Kindred. Such an idea is laughable of course.

'Now I would request your presence so that you can see what is done to those who seek to fool me or betray me for no reason. Please remember that this woman had wrongfully imprisoned Shaidal and caused pain to his family.''${PLAYER}, it seems as if it is time to get to the heart of the matter. I believe that we should be able to resolve this peacefully, of course.''It is time to deal with this problem. Please join me.''It would seem that Zarzíra's treachery was deeper rooted that I might have estimated. I appreciate your willingness to combat her and her men on my behalf. I would have stepped forward, but I did not feel they were worth bloodying my blades.

'Oh, I have heard word that Shaidal has managed to capture my prize and has survived the ordeal. Your good work in this has secured his freedom upon the creature's unveiling.'Lukíd has asked you to investigate Zikrum-dûl. He claims there is a hermit in the area that may be in need of your help.Lukíd has asked you to investigate Zikrum-dûl and seek out the mythical hermit.Seek out the hermit of Zikrum-dûlSpeak with the hermit at his camp in Zikrum-dûl.Speak with the hermitReturn to Lukíd in Ub Nishir to the north of Maurûsh and tell him that you found the hermit and what you saw in Zikrum-dûl.Return to Lukíd in Ub Nishir'You must be the ${CLASS} of which Galâmka spoke. He mentioned you might be around, asking people if they are in need of help. I am Lukíd.'

Lukíd shifts slightly with a wince of pain on his face from his injury.

'I know of a place nearby, and someone who might be in need. Over to the east. In Zikrum-dûl.

'Have you heard of the old cloud-shouter? He is a hermit who is said to live there. Well, I fear for his safety and all, what with the Orcs and other beasts roaming the land... and of course the brigands after the treasures said to be in the ruins.'

Lukíd trails off slightly as he mentions the treasure.

'I thought you might you go and see if you can check the area? Then let me know what you find. I'm hoping to hear information such as if it is dangerous for people or not. I would hate for people to go searching for that treasure if it is not safe.'

Lukíd's eyes grow wide.

'Oh! And of course making sure old cloud-shouter is well!''Oh my, a visitor! Who are you? I am Angârmu!'

You explain you were sent to find him and to see how dangerous Zikrum-dûl is.

'I have never known this Lukíd or this Ub Nishir. No. No, I will stay here. In my home.

'This land here though, Zikrum-dûl, is filled will dangers, yes. I have seen Orcs roam the land, and thieves, and beasts. Very dangerous, now that you ask me.'

Angârmu's eyes look to the sky briefly and seem to squint at the sight of the clouds.

'But I stay. I fear not these dangers. I have other, more fearsome dangers for which to watch. Yes much more fearsome. I can not let them find me.

'Thank you for your visit.''Aye, ${CLASS}. Have you been to Zikrum-dûl?'

You explain to Lukíd that you found Angârmu, but he wishes to stay, and that Zikrum-dûl is still very dangerous.

'Hold on a moment though, what do you mean you found the old cloud-shouter? That was just a myt-uh, I meant that is great that you found him! Are you are sure it was him and not just some trader?'

Lukíd has a look of confusion mixed with surprise on his face, he appears to have not expected you to find the hermit. He regains focus and continues.

'And true shame about Zikrum-dûl, especially for those thieves trying to take advantage of all this chaos.'

Lukíd tries not to appear disappointed at the news.

'Thank you for your help. Galâmka was right about you.'The hostile forces of Ekhamât have claimed Dun Shûma, the hidden fortress of Shâr Shûma III, seeking the lost crown of Aragín the Queller.Use the Instance Finder to complete 'Dun Shûma, the King's Fortress' on any difficulty.Complete 'Dun Shûma, the King's Fortress' on any difficultyYou have reclaimed Dun Shûma from the Ekhamâti forces.

You should talk to Mizâdi.Talk to Mizâdi'Bârshud has fled, but our work is not yet finished. The remainder of the Ekhamâti Umûni and their Ordâkhai forces are holed up inside the hidden fortress before us.

'Dun Shûma, built by an ancient Shâr of Nísaka, is said to hold many of our ancestral treasures. I suspect there is one treasure in particular that Bârshud seeks: the lost crown of Aragín the Queller. Holding such a thing would give his claim to the throne of Hamât legitimacy. We must prevent Ekhamât from seizing it, at all costs.''We are victorious. I now hold the Lion-crown of Aragín the Queller, and must make official my claim to the throne of Hamât. This, I fear, is just the beginning of a long campaign.

'That sorcerer has given us a parting gift, a secret he expected us to take to our graves: Ordâkh is manipulating Ekhamât, puppeteering Bârshud to fight their war for them. The new Hul must be eager to regain control of all Shagâna, and will use unwitting vassals to do so. Even if Bârshud’s claim over Hamât is defeated, my people will not be truly safe until the threat of Ordâkh is eliminated for good.

'You have been by my side through all of this, ${PLAYER}. For now, I have little to offer but my sincerest thanks, but once this war is finally won, the Kingdom of Hamât will forever be in your debt.'Enârshan has asked you to investigate Khûn Sagaz nearby and find out more about it.Enârshan has asked you to travel to Khûn Sagaz at the top of the hill nearby to investigate.Reach Khûn SagazInvestigate Khûn Sagaz near the Falls of Ilûritu for Enârshan the Idâmi.Locate where supplies are kept in Khûn SagazLocate where weapons are kept in Khûn SagazDefeat Orcs in Khûn Sagaz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Enârshan in her home behind the waterfall in Ilûritu.Return to Enârshan behind the waterfall in Ilûritu'I see you wish to help then. Perhaps you are indeed bold instead of foolish.

'You undoubtably have seen these Orcs in these lands, these Utûgi, these Sere Ones, I loathe them. I ask for your aid in driving them from my falls. I regret to say that my song holds no power over them so I can not get rid my waters of them myself.

'They have a dwelling nearby. It has been called many names, but the brigands who resided there before the Orcs gave it the name Khûn Sagaz. You must travel there and learn all that you can.

'Of course, I recommend you also slay any Orc that crosses your path.''I see you have returned to my home and I trust you have been to Khûn Sagaz.'

You tell Enârshan that you have found where the Orcs store their supplies and keep their weapons. As well as slain any that you had encountered.

'Good. Then you have not betrayed me, ${CLASS}. I will trust you for the time, but remember, these are my waters. I know how we can deal with this plague upon Ilûritu.

'Return to me when you are prepared to do more.'Shulum in Ub Nishir has asked you to slay Ogarkha to the north-east of Maurûsh, near the Gorge of Woe and bring back a trophy of your conquest.Shulum in Ub Nishir has asked you to slay Ogarkha to the north-east of Maurûsh, near the Gorge of Woe, and bring him a trophy as proof.Defeat Ogarkha and retrieve his golden ringReturn to Shulum in Ub Nishir and give him the trophy you took from Ogarkha.'Ah, hello ${CLASS}. Might I trouble you for your help? I am in dire need of it.

'I wish for you to defeat an Orc by the name of Ogarkha. This monster killed my companions and many more. I was powerless to prevent it. I barely escaped with my life. He must be defeated to spare others from his malice.

'If you seek him out, he has been spotted to the north-east, wandering the lands between Maurûsh and the Gorge of Woe. He can be identified by a golden ring he wears on his hand.

'I beg of you, bring down this monster, and bring me his ring as proof of your victory.''${CLASS}, you have returned!'

You hand Shulum the trophy you collected from Ogarkha.

'And you gathered the proof for which I asked. I thank you. You have saved many lives by ridding the lands of that demon. My sorrow over my companions has eased slightly knowing they have been avenged.

'I shall cherish this trophy in their honour.'Dagâdah, a leader among the people of Shagâna is cautious of your arrival and directs you to meet his assistants in Iridír.Dagâdah, a leader of the Shagâna, known as the Ikorbâni by those from the north, directed you to entreat with his assistants Kildûg and Nêkhur. He also warned against doing anything to harm the people of the valley.Speak with Kildûg, an Ikorbâni Tale-weaverSpeak with the Ikorbâni Quartermaster, NêkhurYou met with both Kildûg and Nêkhur. You can return to Dagâdah and speak with him again.Speak with Dagâdah in the settlement of Iridír'Prove to us you are not here to steal our heritage, our land, or to further injure our people, and we will find a way to reward you.

'We do not have much wealth, but we have much need. All who would assist us are welcome. We are a proud and earnest people.

'If you assist us, we will not forget your effort or let your kindness go unnoticed.

'My assistants Kildûg and Nêkhur will explain more. Return to me when you learn from them.''Kildûg is good with faces, names, and our history. He will remember all you do and weave tales about you. Nêkhur watches over our wealth and will see you rewarded for assisting us.''As Dagâdah explained, we face many struggles here in Shagâna, the occupation by the Ordâkhai is chief among the challenges but only one small portion of our strife.

'The end of the war in the North and fracturing of the Ordâkhai forces in Shagâna provides strength. We choose freedom. We will reclaim our culture and all we lost under Ordâkhai rule. Nature revolted against them and poisoned the land. Our farms, the finest in Shagâna, fell to ruin while our healthy people marched to war. 

'We recall the stories of our past, but the written word is lost. This is a sample of the difficulties we face. Prove yourself honest.''Dagâdah asked me to maintain our collected wealth and trade materials. I am pleased to do this work. I am overjoyed to furnish gifts to those who aid us in restoring our livelihood and culture.

'For too long, the Ordâkhai subjugated our people and put us beneath their heels. We struggle to recall our litanies, and the few who are literate face the arduous task of recovering our history and teaching our written word to future generations.

'It falls to that generation to learn our history, to trust in the nobility of outsiders, and to restore what is lost. If you are such a person, it will bring me joy to gift you a piece of what we still control and make.''You have spoken with Kildûg and Nêkhur?'

You assert that you have.

'Then I offer a request and warning. If you are of noble heart, see to helping our people. If you mean us harm or prove ignoble in your efforts, prepare to suffer our wrath. For we are born anew and will fight any aggressors who mean to suppress our will again.'Defeat all of the great beasts upon the Isle of StormsDefeat all of the great beasts upon the Isle of StormsDefeat KrizhmûlDefeat Urâbaz the MightyDefeat RaghârikThe great Roc threatening the ships of Umbar must be defeated - but its lair sits upon a forbidding jungle island rumoured to have been a den for pirates until they were driven away by strange beasts of enormous stature.Complete 'The Isle of Storms -- Tier 1'The great Roc threatening the ships of Umbar must be defeated - but its lair sits upon a forbidding jungle island rumoured to have been a den for pirates until they were driven away by strange beasts of enormous stature.Complete 'The Isle of Storms -- Tier 2'The great Roc threatening the ships of Umbar must be defeated - but its lair sits upon a forbidding jungle island rumoured to have been a den for pirates until they were driven away by strange beasts of enormous stature.Complete 'The Isle of Storms -- Tier 3'The great Roc threatening the ships of Umbar must be defeated - but its lair sits upon a forbidding jungle island rumoured to have been a den for pirates until they were driven away by strange beasts of enormous stature.Complete 'The Isle of Storms -- Tier 4'The great Roc threatening the ships of Umbar must be defeated - but its lair sits upon a forbidding jungle island rumoured to have been a den for pirates until they were driven away by strange beasts of enormous stature.Complete 'The Isle of Storms -- Tier 5'The great Roc threatening the ships of Umbar must be defeated - but its lair sits upon a forbidding jungle island rumoured to have been a den for pirates until they were driven away by strange beasts of enormous stature.Complete 'The Isle of Storms -- Tier 5'Welcomed by the Kintai of Sul Madásh, your reputation with an alliance in the North endears you to the Elves, and they look to you for assistance in preserving what remains of the Emerald Wood.After speaking with Dithúrim, she directed you to speak with Quartermaster Aralath. He will provide further information in how we can assist the Kintai in Adagím.Speak with Quartermaster Aralath in Sul MadáshQuartermaster Aralath informed you of how you can assist the Kintai and bid you return to Dithúrim for final instruction and a gift.Speak with Dithúrim in Sul Madásh'Well met, ${PLAYER}. Word of your valour in the North has reached us, and you are welcome as a friend of the Kintai.

'In the West, the once-hallowed forest Nisigím lies stricken. Now it is named Adagím, for it is shadowed by blight, and foulness spreads where once light dwelt. Trees and beasts alike wither, and though some persist, most fall silent as the Mother Trees perish. Only Sul Madásh endures, untouched.

'Seek Quartermaster Aralath. They will tell you what aid we can spare—and what we ask in turn.''Welcome, ${PLAYER}. Your honoured name reached us from our groves to the North. Your coming renews our hope that virtue yet walks among us.

'Our stores are thin, as in the North, and what we can grant in exchange for aid is little beside its worth. Yet we will deal in good faith.

'As the blight spreads, still there remain unspoiled roots and seeds in Adagím. We ask this: gather what is pure. Take the seedlings untouched by corruption; bring us the seeds that hold the memory of the Emerald Wood.

'Here, beneath the boughs of Sul Madásh, hope clings still. With your help, the forest may yet be reborn.''If you should find the unsullied seeds of Nisigím, gather them with care. In them lies the memory of what once was and the hope, faint though it be, of what might yet return.

'We offer you tools to claim and harvest, or the means to make them. Choose as you will, and know this: even before your hand turns to aid us, we are already in your debt.'Tharashil is concerned about two members of her oasis. She asks you to visit them to help them accept and move toward their end.Tharashil asked that you find Aítarshun and Filadal and assist them with the tasks they want to accomplish before they can move forward without pain while they fade from the world.Complete the task from FiladalComplete the task from AítarshunYou aided the fading Elves Tharashil asked you to help. You should return to her and tell her of the assistance you provided.Return to Tharashil and inform them of Filadal and Aítarshun's plight'There are two in my care who suffer as they fade. Aítarshun can no longer wield a blade or move freely outside the oasis. The other, Filadal, can no longer leave the spot where she sits. Each looks to me to fulfil a wound or oath to be at peace before they fade.

'I have not the heart to tell them there is nothing I can do.

'I wonder, will you assist them?

'Aítarshun is found in the central island and Fildal can be found on the island closest to the shore.''I did not know the depth of pain that Filadal held or the depth of Aítarshun's oath. Your assistance gives me pause, friend.

'I believe there is something we can do for the men of Khûd Zagin.'Khôltekh has asked you to talk to a merchant friend of his, Rathâni in the Sail-haven, about a missing chest.Khôltekh has asked you to speak with Rathâni about a missing chest. She can be found near the market by the docks in the Sail-haven.Speak with the merchant Rathâni in the Sail-havenSearch for Khôltekh's missing chest in Deshûkh in Dil-irmíz.Search for Khôltekh's missing chest in DeshûkhReturn to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja, Hall of the Kindred, with the missing chest.Return to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with the missing chest'I hope you've met with clear skies and swift sails. I've a task uniquely suited for your gifts. Do well, and I may have a larger ask for you.

'There's a chest with something quite precious to me locked inside. It was supposed to arrive two days ago. Two days have gone by, and only my irritation has arrived. It was supposed to arrive by ship. I suspect foul play and interference from smugglers in the Umbar-môkh.

'Go see the merchant who was supposed to receive the shipment with this chest. Rathâni may have more insight into where this shipment has gone awry.'

Khôltekh leans in close.

'I am trusting you with this. Do not betray my trust, ${PLAYER}.''Clear skies and swift sails to you. Khôltekh? Ah, of course. The chest.

'Yes, it was supposed to arrive two days ago. However the ship it was on was ransacked by Corsairs not far from port. The ship has only just come in, and half her cargo is gone. Namely the expensive half. I am afraid Khôltekh's chest was among the items not found. Khôltekh has always had good taste, and it seems the Corsairs agreed.

'I do not know what is in that chest, but I do have a sense of where it might be. Corsairs and smugglers move freely in the Umbar-môkh. Seeing as how those items were freshly seized, it is most likely they are in Deshûkh, the Blood Market. That's in Dil-irmíz, the Berths. It is an area rife with thieves, smugglers and Corsairs, and it is where I would go if I was looking to offload freshly stolen goods. I would start there.

'Be careful, that is a very dangerous area, and smugglers are not likely to part with their hard-won treasures with just a stern word.''I knew you were up to the task. Come, we have much to discuss.'

Khôltekh takes the chest deftly, quickly handing it off to one of his guards.

'I have a sense for these things. And, as promised, you have a greater role to play in the coming events. Tell me, what do you know of the Umbar-môkh? Wait, not here. You must accompany me to my house here in Umbar.'Khôltekh has taken you into his trust, for now. He's asked you to accompany him to his house to speak more about his plans for Umbar.Khôltekh has taken you into his trust, for now. He's asked you to accompany him to his house to speak more about his plans for Umbar.Speak with Khôltekh when you are ready to go'Only a fool trusts those he doesn't know. But we're good friends now, aren't we? I will trust you, for now. 

'You must come with me to my house here in Umbar. Well, one of them, anyway. I also make residence in Thargushakâl, the Shoreward Stone, but this house has many advantages. Namely, a much shorter walk.'

Khôltekh roars in laughter, amused at his own joke.

'Make ready, we will be off soon.''Ready? Excellent. These layabouts guarding me need some exercise anyway.

'Keep a sharp eye, you might pick up some decorating tips. My house is one of the best furnished in all of Umbar.'Khôltekh has asked you to speak with Nûru in Mekab-kuphâr in Khabârkhad. Nûru has information from an Umbar-môkh contact about Sêkhta.Speak with Nûru in Mekab-kuphâr in southern Khabârkhad about Sêkhta.Speak with Nûru in Mekab-kuphâr about SêkhtaSpeak with Khôltekh's contact Zihârax in the Dûlkar, the Shadow Market in Dil-irmíz. The Dûlkar is located south-east of Mekab-kuphâr.Speak with Khôltekh's contact Zihârax in the Dûlkar in Dil-irmízZihârax has asked you to get his ring back from hoodlum in the market stands to the east.Find the hoodlums that took Zihârax's ringFight off the market cutthroats that have attacked you!Fight off the market cutthroats that have attacked youReturn to Zihârax with the ring.Return to Zihârax with the ring'We must find Sêkhta. A snake with no head perishes quickly. Talk to Nûru, he has information on Sêkhta's whereabouts. One of my Umbar-môkh allies spoke with him recently.

'Nûru can be found in Mekab-kuphâr in Khabârkhad. Go quickly, this Sêkhta is elusive, always one step ahead, like water through my hands.''Aye, I know of this Sêkhta, the Blight. You'll want to speak with Zihârax in Dûlkar, the Shadow Market. It's located south-east of here, in Dil-irmíz.

'I don't like this Zihârax, or many that Khôltekh consorts with. But we don't get to pick our allies down here, and his information has been sound in the past. He spoke with me this morning, told me he had important information, but that he would only tell Khôltekh or his appointed representative. I guess that's you.

'One word of caution: the Dûlkar is not always a friendly place. Stick to the main market. If you go poking your nose in every stall, don't be surprised to find a sword blade pointing back.''I knew you could handle yourself. Sorry they attacked you. Thanks for getting my ring back, I don't feel whole without it.

'All right, I'll tell you what I know.''Lower your voice. That name carries great weight here.

'Of course I know Sêkhta. Everyone here does, don't be a fool. The difference is I have information Khôltekh wants. About Amârbo, Sêkhta's right-hand man.

'Listen, I want to be of service to the Kindred and Khôltekh, but I have a problem. You see, this morning my prized ring was stolen from me by hoodlums. Can you believe that? I was going to ask Khôltekh for coin in exchange for this information, but you look like you can handle yourself in a fight and that ring means more to me than a bag of coins.

'I was jumped to the east of here, right by the eastern market entrance. Get me my ring back, and I'll tell you what I know.'Zihârax, Khôltekh's contact, has told you an associate of Sêkhta's, Amârbo, has been seen in Deshûkh. You should investigate Deshûkh for Amârbo.You should investigate Deshûkh for signs of Amârbo. Deshûkh is located north-west of the Dûlkar.Defeat Deshûkh smugglers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Search for Amârbo in Deshûkh, the Blood Market.Search for Amârbo in DeshûkhAsk Amârbo what he knows of Sêkhta and his whereabouts.Ask Amârbo what he knows of Sêkhta and his whereaboutsReturn to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja, Hall of the Kindred, with this information.Return to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with this information'Here's what I know. Amârbo, Sêkhta's right-hand man, has been seen spending his time in Deshûkh, the Blood Market.

'Amârbo knows what Sêkhta knows. I know Khôltekh has been looking for Sêkhta's base of operations. Amârbo knows all this and more. Find him, and you'll make Khôltekh right pleased with you indeed.

'I'd recommend you head over there now, I happen to know this is a time he likes to frequent Deshûkh. Thanks again for getting my ring back.''I yield! I am no fighter. I will tell you what I know!

'Sêkhta has an outpost not far from here, to the south, from which his influence spreads all throughout Umbar-môkh. You cannot get past the door without a key, however. The way is barred, and the keys are scarce, and quite valuable. That is where you are likely to find him.

'That is all I know.''The way is barred, and the keys are scarce, and quite valuable... I do so love a riddle!

'You've done well, ${PLAYER}. but it seems our work has only just begun.'Khôltekh has asked you to investigate the area Amârbo told you about, where you will hopefully find Dar Sêkhta, and a clue as to Sêkhta's whereabouts.Khôltekh has asked you to look for Dar Sêkhta, and a suspicious lock there that might fit a mysterious key. According to Amârbo, it is located south of Deshûkh in Dil-irmíz.Find Dar Sêkhta in Dil-irmízLook for an alcove or door with an unconventional lock.Look for a door within Dar Sêkhta with a suspicious lockExamine the strange lock for clues as to its key.Examine the strange lock for clues as to its keyReturn to Dâr Laja with your description of the lock. Perhaps Khôltekh has a clue as to its key.Return to Dâr Laja and tell Khôltekh your description of the lockAccompany Khôltekh to his house, so he may think clearly on this key.Speak with Khôltekh when you are ready to go'You should go to Dâr Sêkhta. Even if you cannot gain access, we may yet learn more about this key by examining the lock.

'Amârbo, if he is to be trusted at sword-point, said it was quite close to Deshûkh. South of it, if I recall correctly? That is the place to start.''Ready? Let's be off then. Far too stuffy here. And the chairs aren't as nice. Ho ho!

'The way is barred, and the keys are scarce and quite valuable... Hmmm... Hmmm....''You found some of Sêkhta's men guarding this door? No doubt there is something valuable or important to Sêkhta hidden inside. We must find a way to open it.

'A series of deep, narrow cuts in the stone, you say? Interesting. Interesting.

'I cannot think clearly here. Come, we must go to my house once more. We must figure out how to open this door, and to do that I need to think in peace.'Khôltekh has asked you to find a pristine wight's hand in Khabârkhad. He believes that to be the key that is "scarce" but "quite valuable" that will open the way to Dâr Sêkhta's hidden area.Khôltekh has asked you to go to Sektakhâb in Khabârkhad and find a pristine wight's hand. He believes this is the key to Dâr Sêkhta that will open the way and find Sêkhta or necessary clues about him.Find a pristine crypt-walker's hand by defeating crypt-walkersKhôltekh has asked you to go to Sektakhâb in Khabârkhad and find a pristine wight's hand. He believes this is the key to Dâr Sêkhta that will open the way and find Sêkhta or necessary clues about him.Find a pristine crypt-walker's hand by defeating crypt-walkersGo back to Dâr Sêkhta and insert the pristine wight's hand into the lock.Go back to Dâr Sêkhta and insert the pristine wight's hand into the lockEnter the hidden area of Dâr Sêkhta.Enter the hidden area of Dâr SêkhtaReturn to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with the clues you have found.Return to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with the clues you have found'A wight's hand. All bone. That's the key.

'The five narrow holes are for finger-bones. Luckily there's a great many crypt-walkers in Sektakhâb in Khabârkhad. You need one in exceedingly good condition, nothing broken, so it may take several tries to find one.

'Find a suitable hand, take it to the door and find the whereabouts of this shadow. We need to put an end to the suffering of Umbari citizens at the hands of this villain.''This is most troubling news. Why would a criminal have such scholarly books? And that saying...

'Hmmm. "A candle flickers in the dark, and is extinguished." Another riddle, it seems.'Khôltekh has asked you to go find a bookseller in Tilmakhím. He believes she may have the missing volume to 'A History of Castamir and His Heirs' that you found in Dâr Sêkhta.Find a bookseller named Ephrâti in Tilmakhím, in Tâkhdar. Khôltekh is looking for the missing volume from the set you found in Dâr Sêkhta.Speak with Ephrâti in Tilmakhím in TâkhdarReturn to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with the book.Return to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with the bookAccompany Khôltekh to the Tor-gardens.Speak with Khôltekh when you are ready to goSpeak with Khôltekh outside the Pot and Quill in the Tor-gardens about his revelation.Speak with Khôltekh about his revelation'I know not what "a candle flickers in the dark, and is extinguished" means.

'Still, these clues help a great deal. There was a volume missing from the books you found. I wonder if the missing volume holds any secrets from Sêkhta. Would you go to Tilmakhím in Tâkhdar? There is a bookseller there who may have the missing volume. Ephrâti, I believe her name is.

'We need every clue we can grasp to find this Sêkhta.''Come, we must go to the Tor-gardens to expose this archivist where he lives and works. Sêkhta is there, I'm sure of it!''Just as I thought - each of these books show a fascination bordering on obsession with the Heirs of Castamir.

'These robes - even stained in blood they speak to Umbari nobility. And these books, much more scholarly than one would think for a lowly criminal. And his writing style from the note, so neat, like he was trained or schooled in it....

'I've got it! An archivist! An Umbari historian! It all fits. They are members of Umbari nobility, highly educated, trained in reading and writing. Sêkhta is an archivist!

'Archivists live and work in the Tor-gardens. They are quite few in number. Hmmm... yes.

'I have a plan. Come, we must go to the Tor-gardens at once!''I have the book, but your coin is no good here. If I take it Mâramit, the purveyor of traps across the market, will have my head.'

Ephrâti leans in close.

'She and Khôltekh have an arrangement, if you get my meaning. You understand. Off with you then, I need to devise my next counterattack against these rats.''The Candle! The Candle is a ship! They mean to commandeer the Candle of Umbar!'Khôltekh believes that Sêkhta is stealing the Candle of Umbar, a ship docked in the Sail-haven. Help him apprehend Sêkhta!Speak with Khôltekh to go to the Sail-haven.Speak with Khôltekh when you are ready to goSpeak with Khôltekh in Dâr Laja.Speak with Khôltekh in Dâr Laja'Meet me at the westernmost dock of the Sail-haven – I know that's where Sêkhta went!''Come! We've not a moment to lose!''I wasn't sure about you at first, ${PLAYER}. But you've proven a ready ally and friend to Umbar. And, more importantly, to me. Ho ho!

'You should be very proud. Because of you, many Umbari citizens will sleep easier at night. Thank you.'You roared at the inspiring sight of the Watcher of Urmâkh.Roar at the inspiring sight of the Watcher of Urmâkh.You roared at the inspiring sight of the Watcher of Urmâkh.Your work in the southern part of Ilmabiri, the sewers beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl, appears to be complete.Porókho would like to speak with you privately. Porókho is in Hêbatokh, the clan Morutágya camp in Ilmabiri, beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.Talk to PorókhoAfter helping the grateful Morutágya clan with their requests, you feel that you have been dismissed. You should return to Belondor in Dâr Laja, the Meeting Hall and tell him what you learned.Talk to Belondor in Dâr Laja'Come, ${PLAYER}, I would speak with you privately.''Welcome back, ${PLAYER}. What news do you bring?'

You tell Belondor of the reaction of the Morutágya clan to the confirmation of Tumúldo's death, and the warning that there will be clan infighting for leadership. Belondor nods.

'This sort of thing is not terribly common, but it isn't unheard of either. The Kindred will keep an eye on the situation. I will also learn what I can of this Umisúm person you spoke of. If she does manage to step up, she could become an important player in the politics of the city.

'Thank you for your help, as always ${PLAYER}.'Porókho pulls you aside and speaks to you quietly.

'I want to thank you for humouring us with these tasks. Even Gajóta,' he says with a warm chuckle. 'We really should get him a cat. Unfortunately, dark times lie ahead for us Morutágya. Tumúldo was our leader by right of birth, but he was also a great hero to our people and was well-loved. We would have readily followed Nakási, but she seems to have abandoned us for that khmêg Azagath.

You can see on his face that Nakási's flight weighs heavy upon his heart.

'They have a child, Umisúm, who would now be our leader by right of birth, but she will not go unchallenged. She is in her teen years and has yet to prove herself to our people. I hope for her sake that she is as cunning as her father and as fierce as her mother or she may not make it to adulthood. You know how families are.

'I wanted to thank you for bringing us the letter from that ugly Gondorian. It is better to know than to be left wondering. There are difficult times ahead for all Morutágya, but we have survived worse. Now go. Leave these sewers and visit the baths. You stink.'

He waves you off and you are clearly being dismissed.Bangud, a traveller resting in Western Khanâg, has injured his back and is unable to tend to his tired donkey.Water seems to be the donkey's most immediate need. There is a bucket of water near the north-eastern fountain in Western Khanâg.Bring a bucket of water to the tired donkeyYou have given the donkey some refreshing water. Next, you should find some fresh straw and give him something to eat. There is a stack of donkey feed on the north-west side of Western Khanâg.Bring fresh straw to the tired donkeyYou have watered and fed the tired donkey. Next, you should brush the dust from his coat.Groom the tired donkeyYou have watered, fed, and groomed the tired donkey. Donkeys are social animals. Perhaps you should also talk to him and give him a compliment?Tell the donkey that he is very handsomeYou have done everything you can think of to fulfil the donkey's needs. You should talk to his owner, Bangud, in Western Khanâg.Talk to Bangud'Excuse me stranger, have you a moment to spare? I have thrown out my back and I am unable to care for my donkey. We have just returned from a long journey and the poor animal needs tending to, but I am unable to do it.

'Do you have a moment to help? He needs fresh food, water, and the dust brushed from his coat.''I thank you for your help, stranger. He looks much happier now. Telling him that he is handsome was a good touch.'Zidek's partner, Ubdun, is out herding goats but should have returned by now. The butcher has asked you to ensure the goatherd is all right and thinks he may have gone in the direction of Jirush.Look near Jirush, to the south-east of Western Khanâg, for the missing goatherd.Find the missing goatherdYou have found goats near Jirush. You should look for the goatherd.<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> for the goatherdNear Jirush, you have found goats without a goatherd. Was he harmed by brigands, as Zidek feared? You should find the camp Zidek mentioned.Find the nearby brigand campYou have found the brigand camp, and saw that they are holding a prisoner. You should defeat the brigands and free their prisoner.Defeat Khûdi toughs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Free UbdunYou have defeated the brigands and freed their prisoner, Ubdun the goatherd. You should return to where you saw the goats near Jirush and talk to Ubdun.Talk to UbdunYou have freed Ubdun from being taken prisoner by brigands. He has returned to tend his goats and asked you to talk to Zidek in Western Khanâg.Talk to Zidek in Western Khanâg'Excuse me, could I bother you for a moment? My partner should have been back by now and I am worried about him. I would look for him, but I cannot leave my shop. He took the goats out to graze and has yet to return. I told him not to go too close to Jirush, but I fear he has done it anyway.

'There are some evil folk out that way, I told him, and of course, he says there are evil folk everywhere. He is not wrong, but I have heard some brigands have been camping in that area, and I do not like it. Would you check on him and see that he and the goats are safe? I am finding it difficult to focus on my work.''Thank you for saving me! It was lucky you happened by.'

You tell him it was no accident, and that Zidek had sent you to find him.

'Bless Zidek, I hope he is not too cross with me. There is nowhere in the Khûd that is not dangerous, and the goats must be taken somewhere to graze. This patch of green is as good as any. Give my thanks to Zidek for sending you, and tell him I will return when the goats have had their fill.''Where is Ubdun?'

You recount the tale of what happened, and Zidek looks both relieved and frustrated.

'I am glad he is safe, but curse him, he is probably right that there would be some sort of danger no matter where he took them. I do not know what else there is to be done. Thank you for your help, especially for saving Ubdun.'After travelling with the expedition to the south, you are introduced to the Phetekâri, the Tale-wardens of Umbar, in the shadow of Telperiën's Wall.Kizeri, the leader of the Tale-wardens, asked you to visit and introduce yourself to the other members of her order, Mashêm and Shulêga. Each are located close to Kizeri in the shadow of Telperiën's Wall.Speak with the Tale-warden MashêmSpeak with the Tale-warden ShulêgaReturn to Kizeri, the leader of the Tale-wardens, and tell her you have introduced yourself to her assistants at Telperiën's wall.'Welcome to our encampment, ${PLAYER}.

'Do not be surprised. Captain Rothog told us to look forward to your arrival.'

She smiles genuinely.

'You made an impression on the Kindred of the Coin. An impression good enough that when Captain Rothog signed on to the expedition here, he asked that we, the Phetekâri of Umbar, join them to catalogue the journey.

'We could use assistance if you are willing. We are small in number and have discovered so much already, and we are only at Telperiën's Wall.

'Please speak to my companions, Mashêm, and Shulêga. They will provide more information.''Please introduce yourself and learn from Mashêm and Shulêga. They will assist in tracking and rewarding you for your contributions in cataloguing the history of Shagâna. Both are nearby in this small camp.'He nods.

'Very good. You will want to know why we are here.

'We Phetekâri are an ancient sect of scholars who hid away from the church of the All-seeing Eye. Only recently, with Captain Rothog's gracious involvement, have we emerged from our long secrecy.

'Our purpose is to collect and maintain remnants of the past for posterity and purposes of study and history. In your tongue, we are called Tale-wardens.

'We accompany this excursion to catalogue and collect the mysteries of the past to maintain for future generations. We will ask for permission to excise any materials we find of historical significance and will record the rest with as much accuracy as we can.

'For your part, should you help us, Captain Rothog supplied us with trinkets, clothing, and gifts he believes you may find interesting or beneficial.

'Make certain you speak with Shulêga, if you have not.''It is good you have come to me, ${PLAYER}. I overheard your conversation with Kizeri, and I am pleased to show you the wares that Captain Rothog sent with us to Ikorbân.

'Your assistance with collecting information, relics, and curiosities of the past allows me to offer you access to our small menagerie of treasures.

'We must be cautious not to upset or remove important Ikorbâni relics. We are observers and outsiders here. What little we know of the conflict in this land forces us to use great caution lest we make ourselves an enemy of the Ikorbâni. We are historians and cataloguers. Let us do right here, my friend.

'We will send word to you when your assistance warrants greater reward. After you speak with Mashêm, return to Kizeri.''Your reputation, ${PLAYER}, speaks of a trustworthy and noble spirit. We hope you see the merit in our charge in this land. There are many secrets in these lands. There is history here in the Valley of Ikorbân, suppressed too long beneath a yoke of oppression and a veil of superstition. We seek only to understand the past of this land, our ancestors, and ensure that no harm comes to their memory due to the actions of the Sea-shadow.'Girhâzi has asked for your help in dealing with an Ordâkhai prisoner, the former overseer of Ambarûl, Khûldim Umûn.Girhâzi has asked you to speak to Amâsu about the prisoner.Talk to AmâsuAmâsu has told you that she believes Khûldim Umûn knows the location of the Dubarâkh, a hidden library archiving the history and culture of the Ambarûli people. She has asked you to talk to the prisoner in the cell on the west side of the lodge and see what you can learn.Find where the prisoner is heldAmâsu has told you that she believes Khûldim Umûn knows the location of the Dubarâkh, a hidden library archiving the history and culture of the Ambarûli people. She has asked you to talk to the prisoner in the cell on the west side of the lodge and see what you can learn.Talk to Khûldim UmûnAmâsu has told you that she believes Khûldim Umûn knows the location of the Dubarâkh, a hidden library archiving the history and culture of the Ambarûli people. You have talked to the prisoner and should now return to Girhâzi.Talk to Girhâzi'${PLAYER}, it is good to see you. Tell me, how is Ningêna? I am happy that things are progressing at Sûru.

'I must confess, I have a problem for which I hope to gain your assistance. We have a prisoner by the name of Khûldim. He was once the Umûn, the Lord here, sent by the Empire of Ordâkh to keep the Ambarûli under their evil thumb. He was responsible for much suffering.'

Girhâzi clenches her teeth, visibly still angry about things this man has done.

'The pashâg surrendered to us instead of fighting, and now we are stuck deciding what to do with him. Some want him executed for his crimes. Others think we should ransom him to the Ordâkhai, as surely he comes from a rich family.

'Amâsu thinks he may have a use, though. She believes he may have information for which we have been looking, but so far, we have learned nothing from him. You should talk to Amâsu though, she can explain better than I.''Ah yes, Khûldim Umûn.'

Amâsu spits out his name like just saying it befouls her tongue.

'That man has a corrupted heart and is... was, a steadfast follower of the One Who Sees All. I weep for his mother, who must live knowing that this heartless creature is what her child became. But I am nonetheless glad the Dumûri gave him mercy, as I believe he uncovered a secret during his time as overseer, and I would have him tell it to us.'

The old woman clears her throat and her demeanor shifts into that of a teacher.

'Throughout the majority of Ambarûl's history, we have been ruled over by invaders from foreign lands. Our land is valuable for its fertility, and we are too few to be able to field an army large enough to defend ourselves. The Empire of Ordâkh is only the latest in a long history of tyrants.

'One thing that the Ordâkhai did that the others did not was forbid the teaching of reading and writing to any Ambarûli. With knowledge comes power, and they wanted to deny us that. When we lost our literacy, we lost our history and our culture. The Old Way was forgotten and we have become a people who does not truly know who we are.

'Not all literacy was lost, however. When this was first enacted, a woman swore an oath that she would teach another of a younger generation, in secret, so that all would not be forgotten. This oath has been passed on to me, and I have passed it to Girhâzi. What has also been passed on is the tale of the Dubarâkh, a hidden library where the books telling the stories of our people have been saved. Unfortunately, the location of this library has been lost to time.

'I believe that during his time as overseer, Khûldim learned the location of the Dubarâkh. It is vital to the survival of our culture that it is found. This is the only lead we have. Please, speak to Khûldim and see what you can learn. He is held here in the lodge.''What is this, a visitor? Introduce yourself, stranger. Who are you, and why are you here?'

You give him your name and tell him you came to question him. He leers at you for a moment and then begins to laugh.

'You are a fool, ${PLAYER}, sent on a fools' errand. Why should I tell anyone anything? My secrets are keeping me alive. If I tell you what I know, these people will lose the only reason they have to not execute me. All I have to do is keep my mouth shut and await rescue.'

Khûldim leans closer and sneers at you.

'You know, where I come from a man in my position would be properly tortured. Instead, you torture me with your poor company and mildly unpleasant food. You are all weak and pathetic.'

You inform him that nobody is coming to rescue him and take your leave.'How dare he insult our food!'

She rubs her chin thoughtfully.

'He expects to be tortured, does he? I have an idea.'Dangerous foul creatures fill this forsaken area. Seek out these creatures and destroy them before they can harm others.Dangerous foul creatures fill this forsaken area. Seek out these creatures and destroy them before they can harm others.Defeat Wights near Ghâr Mejet (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Talk to Yâshri and let her know that fewer of these creatures haunt this place.Talk to Yâshri outside of Ghâr Mejet'Within the halls of Ghâr Mejet, dangerous foul creatures fill this forsaken area. These creatures pose a grave danger to anyone who inhabits Umbar-môkh. We have lost several folks who have come too close.

'Can you thin the ranks of the restless Dead throughout this area?''These creatures have taken many lives from those of us who choose to live below. Thank you for thinning the ranks of these foul things.'Khôltekh has asked you to venture into Sektakhâb and cull the rising population of the Dead.Khôltekh has asked you to venture into Sektakhâb and cull the rising population of the Dead. You can find them west of Mekab-kuphâr, the Temámir guard outpost in southern Khabârkhad.Defeat crypt-walkers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat crypt-sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat crypt-bellowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja, the Hall of the Kindred.Return to Khôltekh in the Hall of the Kindred'The more we explore Umbar-môkh, the Undercity, the more danger we uncover.

'My guards have established a foothold in the southern crypts of the Umbar-môkh, My scouts have patrolled outward, mapping Umbar-môkh as best they dare. Recently, several of my patrols were attacked by the dead. Nûru, the Captain of my guard, tells me they are coming from west of Mekab-kuphâr, my guard outpost, and that their attacks have become more frequent, and violent.

'Far to the west of the crypts there is an area my scouts call Sektakhâb, the Silent Sepulcher. There the Dead roam freely.

'I need you to make your way there and cull these dead. The last thing Umbar needs is the Dead preying on innocent Umbari civilians, or my guards.''I am relieved. This issue of the Dead had been weighing on me. Thanks to your brave deeds, Umbari citizens and my guards can sleep much easier tonight.'You have brought the leaders of Ambarûl, Khûd Zagin, and Imhûlar together in Iridír. Mizâdi has much to do before Girhâzi and Amalíbi trust her or her leadership.Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír when you are ready to go.Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír when you are ready to goSpeak with Mizâdi in Iridír.Speak with Mizâdi in Iridír'Now that everyone is here, we must meet to figure out how to fight this Bârshud and oppose his considerable forces.

'I dread this part, ${PLAYER}. I am no good at negotiating, and worse at diplomacy. Yet here we are. We should go inside and join the others.''That went as well as I expected. I wish I chose my words more carefully, but it is something for which I never developed the talent.

'At least we now have a plan for moving against Bârshud. Thank you for your part in aiding us, friend.''Let us go into the hall and have words with the others. The sooner we do so the sooner we can act to counter this Bârshud.'Ningêna has sent a Dumûri to find you and relay her request for you to come talk to her at the Wrackwade.You should travel to the Wrackwade and talk to Ningêna.Talk to Ningêna'Hashtal-gûr, ${PLAYER}. My captain, Ningêna, sent me to seek you out. She would like you to consider helping a man from Khûd Zagin to the south. He is insistent, and I feel she finds him rather irksome. She requests that you come to speak with her at the Wrackwade.''${PLAYER}, there you are. I see my warrior found you. Your willingness to return is appreciated.'You have helped the guards that Belondor sent to the sewers beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.Nashôn has asked you to report to Belondor in Dâr Laja, the Meeting-hall in Umbar Baharbêl with news of the guards' progress in the sewers beneath the Sail-haven.Talk to Belondor'Thank you for your assistance, ${PLAYER}. Without your help, setting up an outpost here would have been much more difficult. And perhaps we would have sent aid supplies to goblins.'

Nashôn's face momentarily flushes red before he clears his throat and resumes speaking.

'Our work here will continue, but I will only ask one more thing of you. Belondor wants a report on how things are proceeding here at Kruha-sûrja. Would you mind speaking to him in Dâr Laja on our behalf? Thank you for all of your help ${PLAYER}.''${PLAYER}, you have returned. How goes the efforts in the sewers?'

You tell Belondor of the efforts taken in the new guard post at Kruha-sûrja, and he nods.

'Thank you for helping them get a head start while they work on setting up the outpost. Assuring the safety of the people of the Sail-haven will go a long way in restoring their confidence in the Kindred of the Coins.'Defeat all of the Jephai Corsairs within The Streets of Râhal Bakh.Defeat the Jephai CorsairsFrom the apothecaries of Carn Dûm to Langstrand all the way to Umbar, Indagir now known as Khâshap has been transporting a draught of the vilest make. We now grasp at his heels as he makes his final attempt to deliver this substance to his master. We will not fail. We cannot. Khâshap must be stopped, now!Khâshap has lured you into the Gut, and has turned the streets against you. Give chase as he makes his way to his master!Pursue Khâshap!Khâshap has fled deeper into the back streets. Continue your pursuit before he delivers the Bile of Ifrinn!Chase Khâshap to the Gate of Sorrow!Khâshap has left you to deal with his most trusted cohort, Utho the Grasper.

