Defeat Utho the Grasper.Defeat Utho the GrasperKhâshap has taken to the Fleetfast. He is running out of places to run. You must corner him at last!Follow Khâshap to the Gate of StormsKhâshap has been cornered at the Gate of Storms. You must defeat him before he can make his final attempt at delivering this Bile of Ifrinn to his master.Defeat Khâshap, Irinn's AbominationThe Streets of Râhal Bakh cast a darkened vignette on the people of Umbar. Brave the tapestry of corruption set upon you by Khâshap and free the Umbari of his influence and shadow.Complete 'The Streets of Râhal Bakh -- Tier 5'Galâmka thinks that you should know more about the situation in Urash Dâr.Speak with Galâmka to learn more about the situation in Urash Dâr.Speak with Galâmka to learn moreSpeak with Thugóch to learn more about the Ordâkhai in Urash Dâr.Speak with Thugóch to learn more about the people hereReturn to Galâmka after learning more about the situation in Urash Dâr.Return to Galâmka'Greetings, ${CLASS}. I am Galâmka, the leader of this here band.

'You appear to be capable. If you truly wish to be of help though, there is much for you to learn of Urash Dâr and our struggles here.''Urash Dâr has been a danger to all who live here for as long as can be remembered. In recent days the danger has grown. There are whispers of the doors of Utug-bûr, the demon-pits, having opened, releasing an evil upon us.

'You may have seen the stronghold of Maurûsh on your travels to our camp. Maurûsh used to be ours, our homes, until these vicious utûgi invaded and it took it from us.

'We managed to escape and have gathered here among refugees from all over the sands. We have put aside out differences to drive back this enemy, these Orcs, and retake our homes.

'I ask of you to speak with Thugóch nearby, he will tell you more of the people here in the camp.''You must be the one of which Galâmka spoke.

'This camp is a sanctuary for refugees in this land and the residents of Maurûsh. They have put their differences aside to escape the demons that emerged from the north.

'You will find people from Ashâgir, Zikrum-dûl, and of course the stronghold of Maurûsh working together in an uneasy alliance, and I am sure that you have noticed by now that my companions and myself are Ordâkhai, and we are considered by many to be hostages of Galâmka, though I myself consider him a close friend.

'We abandoned our campaign as we did not wish to fight under Sauron and came to Maurûsh, only to be captured by Galâmka. After the attack we were asked to help and now we fight by their side so that we can return home ourselves.''Now you know of the people here and how we have all been driven from our homes by our common enemy.

'I am planning to retake our home in Maurûsh, if you can lend your aid it would be welcomed, as it will be a hard road ahead.Angârmu has told you of a mystical talking tortoise he has encountered nearby and asked you to seek it out.Angârmu has asked that you seek out a mystical talking tortoise near Zikrum-dûl to the east along the river.Find the tortoise denYou found a tortoise at the den near Zikrum-dûl. Speak with it to see if it's the one Angârmu told you about.Speak with the tortoise nearbyYou tried speaking to a tortoise at the den near Zikrum-dûl, but it turned out to be a generic tortoise. Speak with another to see if it's the one Angârmu told you about.Try speaking with a different tortoise in the areaYou found a slightly more interesting tortoise at the den near Zikrum-dûl. Try speaking with it to see if it's the one Angârmu told you about.Attempt to speak with the tortoiseReturn to Angârmu in Malgâma near Zikrum-dûl with the tortoise.'Ah, hello! I need your assistance with this, I can not go myself.

'To the east, you will find tortoises. You must go there and bring back my friend.

'He is easy to spot, of course. I do miss our talks. Yes, he will be the one that talks, the others they are not friendly and they do not talk. I wish to talk with my friend though, bring him here for me.''Yes, yes! It is him! My good friend it is good to see you!

Angârmu takes the tortoise from you.

'Thank you, thank you! Now if you will, we have much to speak on.'

Angârmu begins having a quiet one-sided conversation with the tortoise and seemingly forgets you are there.Recently returned to the surface world, the younger members of Jiret-menêsh look to re-establish a means of commerce with those remaining in An Shêru. They request your assistance.After speaking with Tirukêni, he directed you to speak with Quartermaster Semanísi. He will provide further information in how we can assist the Temámir of Jiret-menêsh.Speak with Quartermaster Semanísi in Jiret-menêshQuartermaster Semanísi informed you of how you can assist the Temámir and bid you return to Tirukêni for final instruction.Speak with Tirukêni in Jiret-menêsh'A rare day indeed—and welcome. Few have come, and fewer still returned. Long have we laboured in the deep, far from sun and sky. Now, by craft and council, the gates are unbarred.

'The elder and the cautious remain in the halls of stone. Those who yearned for light and the green earth have returned, and we behold the scars left upon the Mûr.

'Through dark years and bitter days, we held fast in Jiret-menêsh, our beloved hall. We kept it whole, though the world above faltered and threatened to shake her apart. When the time came to look beyond the doors, many refused. We, who rose, heard whispers that the long shadow was lifting, and that light once more touched the land.

'Thus came we forward, to trade anew, and to see if the old pacts may be struck again. To see if Elves and even Men would share their wealth. Now we seek the trader, the wanderer, and the warrior alike; and by your bearing, you may be all three.

'Seek the quartermaster. We have wrought much in the silent years. If you would aid our return to the world above, there is work to be done and reward for those who earn it.''Ho there, traveller. Our return to the surface is met with both marvel and mourning. When last we looked upon these lands, they were green with life and bright with running water. Now dry beds, and pools turned foul.

'Yet the shadow recedes, and so we step forward to trade, to speak, to mend what was broken. Aid us, ${RACE}, and in return, you shall see a share of our wealth and craft.''We are settled now. You know us, and we know you. Aid us as we return to the old ways upon the surface, and together we shall see prosperity grow, stone by stone.'Travel to Jâx Ugikh, explore the grand staircase, and clear out cultists in the area.Travel to Jâx Ugikh and explore the grand stair entranceApproach the entrance to Jâx UgikhSeek out and drive off cultists located near Jâx Ugikh.Defeat cultists near Jâx Ugikh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Travel to Kên Taghlim located north of Jâx Ugikh and inform Azrât that some of the cultists have been driven off.Talk to Azrât in Kên Taghlim'To the north there is a large encampment known as Jâx Ugikh. This encampment is home to a variety of cultists who seem to draw their power from that place. These cultists have been attacking folks from this camp and throughout the catacombs.

'Could you travel to Jâx Ugikh, explore the entrance, and drive cultists from that accursed place?''The foul cultists that inhabit Jâx Ugikh present an ever-growing problem within the catacombs. These cultists have attacked supply lines, captured refugees, and continue their dark work.

'Thank you for your assistance in dispatching them.'Tilmakhím is to the south of Tâkhdar.

Hármelak has asked you to acquire more traps from Mâramit to ensnare more pests in Tâkhdar.Mâramit can be found at Tilmakhím, to the south of Tâkhdar.

Ask Mâramit for more traps to place in order to capture pests. Hármelak will pay her later.Ask Mâramit for more trapsTilmakhím is to the south of Tâkhdar.

Lay the traps in various locations around Tilmakhím.Set traps (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mâramit can be found at Tilmakhím, to the south of Tâkhdar.

Speak with Mâramit and inform her the traps have been laid. She will want you to deliver a message to Hármelak to receive payment for her services.Speak with MâramitHármelak is waiting in Dâr Laja.

Return to Hármelak to convey Mâramit's good wishes, and inform her the traps have been set.Return to Hármelak'Your assistance in discovering those dangerous traps was most welcome, ${PLAYER}. I have been made aware of the true source of these pests, and I require your assistance once more.

'I assume you recall Mâramit, a purveyor of traps in Tilmakhím? Inform her you are my messenger, and that I will pay her well once she has given you more traps to place in these areas I will mark for you. She will not hesitate to comply, I am certain.''Have you spoken with Mâramit? I would not wish to wait long, lest those pests in Tâkhdar learn of our plans to ensnare them. I jest, of course, but the sooner the better to keep my people safe.''Welcome back to my lovely little shop! Did you forget something? Or did you miss me?

'Ah, Hármelak sent you this time. She has kept her word with me before. Yes, I will give you even more of my wares. Come see me again when you are finished setting the traps and we will discuss further, you and I.''Do not forget to speak with me once you have finished setting all your traps! I must trust that you will convey my message to Hármelak regarding my payment.''Has Mâramit asked payment for her services? Bring me the exact amount, and I will be sure to thank her for her discretion most handsomely.''You are finished with your task? Excellent. I will guess Hármelak wishes our exchange to be kept our little secret, no? I am accustomed to such matters in my trade. I just sell the things; what you do with them matters naught to me.

'Tell Hármelak I will not expect payment this once, but I would like my generosity remembered next time any guards might want to poke their noses where they do not belong. Say this nicely, please!''Do not forget to tell Hármelak I appreciate her wisdom! Make sure you mention how reasonable and generous my business is, as well.''You return from Takhdâr. Then you faced no difficulty in setting my traps for those pests? I knew you would not disappoint.

'Mâramit is a most beloved ally of mine. She has naught to fear from me, although I do find her magnanimous gesture touching. I thank you for sharing her kind words with me.

'As before, I appreciate your delicacy and discretion in keeping our city safe. I do not think these pests will trouble us any longer.'Yamin has had work piling up ever since his last apprentice left, and he would like you to help him with some of it.The first door to test is to the north-east of the Grand Market, by the Stable-master in the Upper Ward.Test the lock on the door to the north-east of the Grand Market, by the Stable-masterThe second door to test is to the north-east of the Grand Market, within the walls of an enclosed estate in the Upper Ward.Test the lock on the door to the north-east of the Grand Market, in the yard of an enclosed estateThe third door to test is to the north-east of Dâr Laja, the Meeting-hall, and is the entrance to a palatial manor within the Upper Ward.Test the lock on the door to the palatial manor north-east of Dâr LajaYamin is at the Grand Market in the Upper Ward.Talk to Yamin in the Grand Market of the Upper WardRocks with shiny flakes and crocodiles with sharp teeth can be found near Bâlakhat, outside the city and along the south-eastern shore.Collect rocks with shiny flakes from Bâlakhat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect crocodile teeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Kîflu can be found at the Shoreward Stone, waiting to accept delivery of the items you collected for Yamin.You hear approaching footsteps.You hear approaching footstepsKhôltekh nods to you in greeting, summoning you to speak with him outside the Shoreward Stone.Talk to Khôltekh at the Shoreward StoneYamin is at the Grand Market in the Upper Ward.Talk to Yamin by the Grand Market in the Upper Ward'You have come back, which is more than I might say of my last apprentice! He was frightened of the crocodiles outside the city, and when I told him to just move faster than they do, he left my service on the spot! How ungrateful! But that means the coin I would have given to him can instead be given to whoever fulfills his duties for me, and those have been piling up: coin and duties both!

'One of the services I provide for every lock I fashion is a periodic test to ensure that the lock remains in good condition. This involves trying to open the locked door, and making certain that the lock holds. Will you perform these tests for me? The doors in question are to the north-east of the Grand Market. Test all three of the doors and report back to me with your findings.''One of the services I provide for every lock I fashion is a periodic test to ensure that the lock remains in good condition. This involves trying to open the locked door, and making certain that the lock holds. Will you perform these tests for me? The doors in question are to the north-east of the Grand Market. Test all three of the doors and report back to me with your findings.''One of the services I provide for every lock I fashion is a periodic test to ensure that the lock remains in good condition. This involves trying to open the locked door, and making certain that the lock holds. Will you perform these tests for me? The doors in question are to the north-east of the Grand Market. Test all three of the doors and report back to me with your findings.''One of the services I provide for every lock I fashion is a periodic test to ensure that the lock remains in good condition. This involves trying to open the locked door, and making certain that the lock holds. Will you perform these tests for me? The doors in question are to the north-east of Dâr Laja. Test all three of the doors and report back to me with your findings.''One of the locks is nearly ready to give out? I will need to see that replaced, which means I need to send you with some resources to my supplier, a Temámir dwarf named Kîflu.

'There are rocks with shiny flakes east of the city, at a place called Bâlakhat. Collect some of those rocks and bring them to my supplier outside the Shoreward Stone. We have a deal, he and I, so be sure to also gather some teeth from the crocodiles that lurk at Bâlakhat. He gives my requests a higher priority if they are accompanied by crocodile teeth. He is making a necklace of the things, I believe.

'Aye, Bâlakhat is the area that my former apprentice refused to traverse. Why do you ask?''There are rocks with shiny flakes east of the city, at a place called Bâlakhat. Collect some of those rocks and bring them to my supplier outside the Shoreward Stone. We have a deal, he and I, so be sure to also gather some teeth from the crocodiles that lurk at Bâlakhat. He gives my requests a higher priority if they are accompanied by crocodile teeth. He is making a necklace of the things, I believe.'Bring the rocks and the crocodile teeth to my supplier, a Temámir dwarf named Kîflu outside the Shoreward Stone.'The dwarf sizes you up in silence. When you present the items you have brought, his expression changes completely.

'Our key-making friend has another request? Ah! I see you have some crocodile teeth! I will make certain he gets the supplies that he needs!

'It is good that he continues to honour our deal.'Khôltekh regards you silently.

'It is very important to have a lock on your door, my friend. Does it not warm your heart to know you are safe and secure in your own bed, behind strong walls? It is the pride of the Temámir to aid our local locksmiths and key-makers by supplying the molds with which they fashion all such devices. It is the least we can do.'

You ask Khôltekh if this means the Temámir know how to open all of the locks that are made in the city, and he smiles broadly.

'I like you, friend. You amuse me.''You have made the arrangements with my supplier at the Shoreward Stone? Good, good! It is nice to have a reliable apprentice once again! Are you interested in learning the trade of a locksmith? It is not very difficult, to tell you the truth. I mostly use the molds prepared for me by the Temámir.

'But it is good to know you are not afraid of a few crocodiles! My last apprentice was so frightened of them he swore never to again leave the city, and as far as I know he never has! But here is your payment. Take it with my thanks!'Shanthar of the Kintai is the ever-vigilant protector of Arwáth. It is his sworn duty to protect the trees of the grove.Shanthar has asked you to return to Agalûnu and tell her to leave Arwáth.Talk to AgalûnuYou bow to the stranger and introduce yourself as an Elf-friend.

'It does not interest me that you are a friend of the Eldar. Will you prove a friend of the Kintai? We are not the Elves that you know. Shanthar is my name. Whether you have my friendship will depend greatly on why you have come here. Tell me.'

You tell him of Agalûnu, whom you found injured by an arrow, and ask Shanthar if he was the one who shot her.

'It was. I dislike taking such actions, but this woman is resilient. Most Men do not come here at all. Those who do usually leave once they meet one of the Väiri, one of my departed elders. This woman is unafraid. I tried many times to cause her enough distress that she would leave the wood, but none of my efforts had borne fruit. I could not stand by idle while she felled trees of Arwáth. So yes, I loosed an arrow upon her. But know this Elf-friend, had I wanted to slay her, slain she would be. I only want her to leave.

'I am the warden of this grove, and it is my sworn duty to my elders that the trees of Arwáth be protected from harm. I will ask you to please return to this Agalûnu and ask her to leave me and the trees of Arwáth in peace.''I ask you to please return to Agalûnu and tell her to leave me and the trees of Arwáth in peace.''Hashtal-gûr. Have you any news?'

You tell Agalûnu about Shanthar and his duty to safe-guard the trees of Arwáth.

'Kintai? I had thought those Elves to be only a legend, and long gone had they ever existed at all. This is absurd ${PLAYER}. Are you a woodworker? Have you ever tried to make furniture or chests with the wood of palms? The attempt brings nothing but misery, and the stuff dulls the sharpest of blades almost instantly. It is important to source quality hardwood. The trees of this grove are beautiful and perfect!

'Not to mention, if this supposed Kinta only wanted me to depart, why did he not just talk to me and say so? Why the games, and then shooting me with an arrow of all things!'Khaltâg has asked you to find his wife's necklace. Investigate Sektakhâb, the area of Khabârkhad Khaltâg described.Investigate Sektakhâb for Khaltâg's wife's necklace. Sektakhâb is located west of Mekab-kuphâr in Khabârkhad.Investigate Sektakhâb for Khaltâg's wife's necklaceSearch nearby for any sign of Khaltâg's wife's necklace.Find and pick up Khaltâg's necklaceReturn to Mekab-kuphâr to give Khaltâg his wife's necklace.Return to Mekab-kuphâr to give Khaltâg his wife's necklaceKhaltâg has asked you to inform Pharida, his daughter, that her mother's necklace has been found. She can be found working in the Dûlkar, in Dil-irmíz.Find Khaltâg's daughter Pharida and share the good news'Please, you look capable. I need the aid of someone strong to find my wife's necklace.

'Please, just a moment of your time. Oh, you stopped. Excellent!

'My wife was the most beautiful woman I have ever seen. She was taken from us too soon. I had given her a beautiful ruby necklace just months before she died. On the day we laid her to rest, I dressed her in her finest garb, with the necklace. But moments later, the necklace was gone. Some scoundrel must have made off with it!

'It is the only thing I have to remember her by. Now I hear rumours that a similar-looking necklace has been seen in Sektakhâb, where the Dead walk. I tried to go there myself, but the Dead proved too much for me. I barely escaped with my life. Please, I do not have much, but what little coin I have is yours if you can find the necklace for me.''Oh you found it! I never thought I would see the day. Oh thank you, thank you! Please, can you let my daughter Pharida know the good news?

'This is the first happy day I have had since my wife's passing. So many shadowed days have crossed my face since then, without much light to scare them away. This is truly a joyous occasion!

'You've done so much for me, but I wonder if you would do one more thing - could you tell my daughter, Pharida? She works in the Dûlkar, in Dil-irmíz. It is south-east of here. She needs to share this joy as well!''You found the necklace for Khaltâg? I do not believe it is so much a boon as he thinks.

'My mother was always in poor health. Sickly, frequently bed-ridden, plagued by the Jin-ri, the Black Wind. My father bought that necklace to try to brighten her spirits, and because he was told it had healing properties. But after she wore it, I saw a change in her. She was a warm woman, always giving. But after wearing it, her heart hardened. Her words hardened, and stung as knives. She shut herself off from the world. From us.

'I know not if it was the necklace or the knots of her mind, but my mother soon died after wearing that necklace. My father thinks it an artifact, a physical memory of her. I think it a cursed memory, and one that was better to have stayed lost.'Pharida, Khaltâg's daughter, has asked you to relay her concerns about the necklace to her father. Khaltâg is in Mekab-kuphâr, in Khabârkhad.Return to Khaltâg in Mekab-kuphâr and relay Pharida's message.Return to Khaltâg in Mekab-kuphâr and relay Pharida's messageAsk Muntâkh, the merchant, if he knows where Khaltâg went.Ask Muntâkh if he knows where Khaltâg wentInvestigate Sektakhâb for signs of Khaltâg.Investigate Sektakhâb for signs of KhaltâgAsk Khaltâg why he came to Sektakhâb.Ask Khaltâg why he came to Sektakhâb'You should caution Khaltâg about the necklace. I know it is hard for him to see properly through eyes stained with grief, but holding on to the memory of my mother is causing him more pain than letting her go.

'I do not want to sap his joy, but I do not see any good that can come from hanging on to that cursed past. He should return the necklace to where it was found. Some things are better left lost.''Aye, I saw your man Khaltâg. He was causing quite an uproar a little while ago. Wouldn't stop shouting - Nûru tried to calm him, but he wasn't having it. Kept saying his wife was calling him home. I don't know what that means.

'He ran off to the west. Said something about finding her.

'She's dead? Khmêg. That is ill news, indeed. There are many buried in Sektakhâb, to the west. It's likely he fled there, if he intends to be with her.''I can't stop hearing them! The voices, my wife, she beckons me to join her!'Khaltâg has run into Sektakhâb, claiming his wife is calling him to her. Help him if you can.Speak with Khaltâg.Speak with KhaltâgSpeak with Khaltâg.Speak with KhaltâgProtect Khaltâg and fight off the crypt-walkers that have appeared!Defeat Sektakhâb Dead (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Aid Khaltâg.Aid KhaltâgSpeak with Khaltâg.Speak with KhaltâgPick up the heavy necklace.Pick up the heavy necklaceGo to the Sail-haven. On the western docks past the Harbour-warden's tower there is a wharf jutting into the Bay. The deep waters of the Bay of Belfalas should hide the necklace for an age.Throw the necklace into the Bay from the wharf past the harbour-warden's towerSpeak with Pharida in the Dûlkar in Dil-irmíz about the fate of her father.Speak with Pharida about the fate of her father'Throw this necklace into the bay. It is a curse. It is a curse!''One of the dead wounded me. I can't move. My strength fades.

'Please, throw this necklace into the Bay. It is cursed. It lets you speak with the dead... by becoming one of them. No one should wear it.

'Her voice is strong now, in my ear. She calls to me. My darling, I am coming home.''Khaltâg is dead? Oh no. Oh no...'

She stares off into the distance behind you. Her grief is plain to see.

'I hope he is at peace now. I knew that necklace was a curse! I knew it.

'Thank you for trying to help him, and for throwing that... thing into the Bay. No one else need feel like this.'Mokhlêsh is eager to receive his winnings from a recent wager.Mokhlêsh asked you to collect his winnings from Khâhir the Quick outside the arena.Talk to Khâhir the Quick outside the arenaThe upstart who stole the wager can be found outside the Raven and Albatross in the Upper Ward.Khâhir the Quick is outside the arena.Return the wayward wager to Khâhir the Quick outside the arenaMokhlêsh is at the Baths of Ilmai Iforikh in the Upper Ward.'Ah, you have returned! I am pleased to see it.'

Mokhlêsh looks slyly to the left and to the right, then lowers his voice.

'I was thinking about what we talked about, my friend. You remember that I won a large sum of money on a wager at the Dahâl Huliz? Well, your words planted a seedling in my head: what if the Lady Hármelak thinks to take some portion of my winnings for her own? Such taxes were commonplace when Ordakh ruled, and I fear the Kindred may decide to take more coins of their own to add to their fortunes!

'You are a trustworthy sort, I can tell, but better still you are recognizable... I am not afraid you will disappear on me. Will you speak with Khâhir the Quick and collect my winnings? You will be rewarded for doing this for me, and for keeping news of my success to yourself! Khâhir is outside the Dahâl Huliz, in the Tor-gardens. Give him my name and he will give you a hefty purse full of coin!''You are a trustworthy sort, I can tell, but better still you are recognizable... I am not afraid you will disappear on me. Will you speak with Khâhir the Quick and collect my winnings? You will be rewarded for doing this for me, and for keeping news of my success to yourself! Khâhir is outside the Dahâl Huliz, in the Tor-gardens. Give him my name and he will give you a hefty purse full of coin!''Are you here to collect a winning wager? Well, I must tell you that we may not be able to satisfy that obligation at this time. You are here on behalf of Mokhlêsh? Well, we cannot pay either of you.

'Some upstart Corsairs have taken to stealing records of the wagers made at Dahâl Huliz, hoping to modify the records and claim the winning as their own. Until Mokhlêsh's wager is recovered from the upstarts outside the Raven and Albatross, we of the arena cannot pay anything.''Some upstart Corsairs have taken to stealing records of the wagers made at Dahâl Huliz, hoping to modify the records and claim the winning as their own. Until Mokhlêsh's wager is recovered from the upstarts outside the Raven and Albatross, we of the arena cannot pay anything.''You recovered the wager? Mokhlêsh is fortunate on two counts, then: to have won his wager, and to call you his friend!'

Khâhir takes the wager from you and examines it. He is about to put it back on the table when his eyebrows suddenly knit together. Then he looks up at you.

'I take back what I said. Mokhlêsh may still be fortunate to call you his friend... but he has not won this wager. See here, where he placed his coins upon Othnâm? Well, Othnâm did not win that bout! The winner was Uthmân! It is true that their names are quite similar... but Mokhlêsh did not win this wager at all! There is nothing to pay him!

'I am sorry you put yourself to all this trouble when he did not even win, friend. But there is nothing I can do about it. Tell Mokhlêsh to be more careful when he places a wager!''I am sorry you put yourself to all this trouble when he did not even win, friend. But there is nothing I can do about it. Tell Mokhlêsh to be more careful when he places a wager!''You have returned! Now where are my winnings? Never fear, you will be given your share, my friend!'

You explain the situation to Mokhlêsh and his face falls.

'Wait... did I really place my money upon Othnâm? I meant to put it upon Uthmân, did I not? There should be a rule that no two fighters can be named so similarly!

'This is not the joyous day I thought it was, friend. But at least I do not need to worry that Hármelak will take a large portion of my winnings....

'Ah, I will still see you rewarded for your effort, though it will not be as large a sum as I planned. There is always next time, and I have a good feeling about Uthmân! Or is it Othnâm?'Raphûz bemoans the monotony of his work as a Tale-warden. He shares a rumour he heard about a merchant being captured by the Ordâkhai and asks for your assistance.Raphûz asked for your help in gaining an audience with Ashâmi's father. He believes that rescuing his other daughter's husband from Ordâkhai captivity could be the boon he needs to gain an audience with Ashâmi's father.Defeat Ordâkhai captors at Ar-jirush (${NUMBER}/10)Rescue the captured merchant from Ar-jirushYou succeeded in rescuing Ardub and culled many of the Ordâkhai from Ar-jirush. Return to Raphûz with the news.Return to Jirush and speak with RaphûzMake your way across Jirush to Igbâl. Tell the man you rescued his daughter's husband.Speak with the merchant Igbâl at JirushIgbâl would not speak with you, but his translator drew your attention. You should speak with him.Speak with Igbâl's translator, GalamêGalamê, Igbâl's translator, asked you to inform Raphûz that they want to meet him at his earliest convenience. Return to Raphûz, at his location in Jirush, and share the news.'My friend, my duties weigh upon me and drown me in monotony. Catalogue this, transcribe that. How will I grow if all I do is etch words into a diary? This a madness I did not expect. One my parents would not want for me.

'I apologize. I learned that Ashâmi is the daughter of a merchant here in Jirush and that her sister's husband is a captive of the Ordâkhai. I have been unable to leave my post and seek an audience with Ashâmi's father.

'I wish to earn favour with him, but I cannot leave. Would you help me again?

'Go into the Ordâkhai encampment north of this outpost, rescue the man and defeat his captors. Perhaps such a feat will earn an audience with the merchant.''I do not know you, but your arrival is kismet. Free me, and I will see you paid handsomely. Please do not leave me to the whims of these Ordâkhai dogs and their leader, Jombahok.''I did not doubt you would succeed, ${PLAYER}. It is only proper that you go and visit Igbâl, Ashâmi's father, and speak with him about the rescue. It would not be proper for me to attend. After all, you made the effort, not me.'As you speak, the man looks at you quizzically before blinking slowly and dismissively.'Make your way to Igbâl's home east of this location. You should inform him of your good deed.'You repeat the tale of rescuing the merchant's son-in-law to Galamê.

'It appears Ardub's penchant for exaggeration is another of his bountiful eccentricities. If it was this man, Raphûz, who sent you on the task to free Ardub, we would like to thank him. Inform him to visit us at his earliest convenience.''I am pleased to see you return, friend. Tell me, what did Igbâl share?'

You recount what occurred to Raphûz.

'I admit, I am surprised. No, not by the liar in their midst but the response. They offered you the reward, did they not?

'I find that strange. I wonder if this is another custom of theirs or, as the captive Ardub said, kismet.'To the south, the Nêpharai have made a small encampment known as Harkhaphâr. The Nêpharai broke away from Hulzidâr, killing several inhabitants and pillaging the camp as they fled. Seek out the Nêpharai and weaken their numbers.Seek out the Nêpharai and weaken their numbers before they pose a greater threat to the camp.Defeat Nêpharai gladiators (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Bâkhadir located just north of Harkhaphâr and inform him of your deeds.Talk to Bâkhadir outside of Harkhaphâr'The Nêpharai have begun to build out their settlement in Harkhaphâr. The Nêpharai were perpetrators of a most foul betrayal injuring many of those whom called this camp home. They attempted to destroy this place, and continue to hunt our people. We are left with little choice but to ask for your aid in driving them out.

'Search the camp and thin the Nêpharai numbers in an attempt to push them elsewhere in the catacombs.''I wish this bloodshed could have been avoided, but after attacking many of those who call Hulzidâr home, we had to weaken them so they pose less of a threat to us.'Several refugees have gone missing recently while exploring north of the settlement looking for supplies. Seek out the refugees and see if you can return them to their home.Several ambushed refugees have been lost near Jâx Ugikh.

Please aid them and return them home.Rescue ambushed refugees (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Azrât is an archivist in Kên Taghlim and an aid to our cause. Seek her out and let her know about what is happening in Jâx Ugikh.Talk to Azrât in Kên Taghlim'${PLAYER}, several of our refugees went to go scavenge for supplies. While we have warned them of the dangers of going near Jâx Ugikh, they wished to be of some assistance. One of our scouts saw that they headed north towards Jâx Ugikh and we fear the worst.

'Could you see if you can locate them and return them home safely?''Luckily, the refugees should have made their way to safety. I fear that perhaps the cultists might be gathering them for use in a foul ritual. By returning them home, hopefully they will warn others to not be as careless.

'Thank you not letting these folks fall into the cult's clutches.'Porókho has told you that a group of forsaken Heirsworn and All-seeing Eye believers hiding in Ilmabiri have kidnapped his nephew Khetúku in an attempt to coerce the Morutágya clan into giving them transport out of Umbar. He tells you that if you rescue Khetúku, there will be a handsome reward.Discover where the forsaken Heirsworn and Church of the All-seeing Eye are encamped. Porókho said they are in the southernmost part of Ilmabiri.Find the forsaken campYou have found the location of the camp of forsaken. You should defeat some of them so Khetúku will be able to escape.Defeat fugitives (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Free KhetúkuYou have defeated many of the fugitives and freed Khetúku. You should return to Porókho at his camp in the sewers to bring him the news.Talk to Porókho'I am sorry stranger, but you brought us this news when we were already having a bad day. My nephew Khetúku has been taken captive by wicked Men who are trying to force us to help them. There is a group of Heirsworn and those depraved Church of the All-seeing cowards that stowed themselves away in our sewers. They have been in the southern part of Ilmabiri since the Sea-stone Mutiny, hiding and trying to get someone to ferry them to safety.

'We have no more love for that khmêg than we do for Gondorians. Let them rot, I say! Their time ruling Umbar was not a pleasant one for my people. But now they have captured Khetúku and say they will kill him if we do not help them, and I have no doubt that they will.

'I know you have no reason to help us, but you look hardy and resourceful. If I can persuade you to rescue Khetúku, I will see to it that you are rewarded!''I cannot believe it! You rescued Khetúku! You have lifted such a burden from my shoulders as well as my heart. You are welcome to stay with us as long as you like. Here is your reward, as promised.'Delving deeply into the world, the forces of the enemy are more powerful and vicious.You must place a delving zircon into the fissure in the delving stone. This will unlock the potency trapped within the gemstone and unleash it upon the world.A malice spread from within the gemstone you affixed to the delving stone. You must defeat the enemies and complete the mission to rid the evil from the world.Complete the current mission and find the scoutFailure: Leave the instanceHaving completed the mission with the malice affecting the denizens within, you should now make your way back to the mission giver and tell them of your success.Speak with the mission giverThe stone is inert. There is a clear fissure in the surface where one, with a little effort, could affix a gem of some sort. Perhaps you have such a gem in your possession.The delving zircon fits into the fissure within the delving stone. The zircon cracks and the darkness within creeps out of the stone and moves into the air as a black tendril. A flash of dread fills you but passes.'The enemy grew stronger? Well... that bodes ill. We should be cautious about freeing whatever evil is within these gems.

