'Thank you for this news. It is not what I wished to hear, but at least now I know the truth.'Razâl has a theory that the jázgai will become less aggressive after the leaders of their pack are defeated. He asks you to bait traps to catch the leaders of the jázgai near Dân Shatagan.Defeat oryx near Sâkhazai for their meat. Razâl believes that the jázgai will become less aggressive and retreat further into their hunting grounds if their pack leaders are defeated.Defeat oryx near Sâkhazai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather wood for makeshift traps near Sâkhazai in Kighân. Sâkhazai is located north-west of Ingar-garâsh.Gather wood for makeshift traps near Sâkhazai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Set the first makeshift trap in Dân Shatagan for the jázgai matron.Set the first makeshift trap in Dân ShataganDefeat Zalânda near Dân Shatagan.Defeat Zalânda near Dân ShataganSet the second makeshift trap in Dân Shatagan for the jázgai matron.Set the second makeshift trap in Dân ShataganDefeat Kôda near Dân Shatagan.Defeat Kôda near Dân ShataganSet the third makeshift trap in Dân Shatagan for the jázgai matron.Set the third makeshift trap in Dân ShataganDefeat Zûmri near Dân Shatagan.Defeat Zûmri near Dân ShataganReturn to Razâl in Ingar-garâsh with news of your triumph.'These jázgai, they hunt in packs. I believe if we slay the leader, the pack will fall back in disarray.

