Your Suspicion Level is: <rgb=#00FF00>LOW</rgb>Rahâzi is outside the Ordâkhai camp of Khomar Bóha.Talk to Rahâzi outside the Ordâkhai camp of Khomar Bóha'None saw us arrive, ${PLAYER}. Might we use this to our advantage?

'I doubt not that the bounds of this land are watched by sharp-eyed guards, but the Temámir who drove this waggon is known to them. He has carried us, all unknowing, to a place where it must be assumed every person belongs.

'I hear the sounds of an encampment to the north-west. What if we simply walk among these people and see what we might learn of their purpose here, and how near this secret fleet may be to completion?''Carefully approach the camp to the north-west and we will test this supposition of mine.

'They will have no reason to be suspicious of us, unless we give them one.''Hoy, stranger! You must be new here. All glory to the Hûl!'

You repeat the sentiment, and Onúkho nods pleasantly.

'It warms my heart to hear it! The Orcs claim to share our purpose here, but I do not believe it. If they thought Mordor had the advantage they would turn on us in the span of a breath! And the Corsairs down at Bâkhridar and at Starkhaven mumble their oaths, but they resent the Hûl, I am sure of it. I wish Ordâkh had no need of either, but this great work began before I was even born, and I was not consulted! It has taken great cost in lives to build the Song of Waves and Wind, and now we wait only for the signal to sail!

'You are fortunate to join us today, stranger. Habâti the Dwarf has just arrived, and he brings goods and provisions from far away. He comes back every few weeks and sets up shop. His arrival is always welcome... it helps to break up the monotony of our days, which are spent mostly in waiting. His prices could be lower, though, I admit it.''If you cause no trouble, no trouble will come to you. That is something the Orcs could stand to learn, and the Corsairs would do well to remember!''If you cause no trouble, no trouble will come to you. That is something the Orcs could stand to learn, and the Corsairs would do well to remember!''What do you think you're doing? You should not be lingering in this place!

'Habâti the Dwarf has just arrived, but instead of going to see him you insist upon poking into places where you do not belong? What were you looking at just now?'

You tell Jóla that you were just about to go see Habâti, but you were worrying that you would not be able to afford his unreasonable prices. She stares at you suspiciously.

'Go on, then. Into the main tent with you.''The Temámir has set up his wares inside the main tent! Hurry now, or you will miss him.

'Delay will not lower his prices for you, or for anyone. Go on, then.''Do I know you, stranger? You look familiar to me for some reason.'

You assure Habâti that you and he have never met, but before he can respond the Ordâkhai erupt in a chorus of complaints.

'There is a line,' Habâti says, and you step back before you draw any further attention to yourself.'Hmmm... are you certain we have not met?''How fared you within the enemy encampment, ${PLAYER}?'

You describe to Rahâzi the map you memorized, and she nods agreeably, assigning names to locations in her head.

'I too have learned some things that may be of use to us. The Ordâkhai are not alone in Sûg Nidar, and they are not happy about it.'You and Rahâzi have learned that the various groups working to complete the Song of Waves and Wind are not as unified as they might be.

<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>Rahâzi has suggested that you travel east toward the Orc-encampment of Drushkála so that you might learn more.Travel east in the direction of the Orc-encampment of DrushkálaRahâzi stands west of the Orc-encampment of Drushkála and stares at the ships of the Song moored off the shore.Talk to Rahâzi west of DrushkálaRahâzi asked you to descend the slope and approach the Orc-encampment of Drushkála, remaining alert for anything out of the ordinary.Approach Drushkála and remain alert for anything out of the ordinaryWhat slew this Orc so near to the entrance of Drushkála?Search the Orc for some sign of what killed himYou should slay Orcs at their encampment of Drushkála and look for signs of your potential ally.Defeat Orcs at Drushkála (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Having slain many Orcs at Drushkála, you should return to the entrance of the Orc-encampment and see if you have drawn the attention of your potential ally.Return to the entrance of Drushkála and look for your potential allyRahâzi stands alongside an unexpected friend near the outer palisade of Drushkála.Talk to Rahâzi near the entrance to DrushkálaCorudan stands outside the Orc-encampment of Drushkála, a good distance from where last you saw him.'By listening to the conversation of the Ordâkhai, I have learned something of their associates in the Fearwater. Orcs have established an encampment to the east of here at Drushkála, a fort that was drowned when the lake of Sûg Nidar was formed. During the reign of Barkhûsh, the Orcs and the Ordâkhai were made to work together; now that he is gone, the two groups find it more difficult to coexist, and there has been fighting between the two.

'The map you saw contained markings on the other side of the river for a place called the Haven of Bâkhridar, which seems to be a Corsair encampment. The Ordâkhai need crews to sail the ships, but I am not certain how they convinced these sailors; there is little love between Umbar and Ordâkh these days. Beyond Bâkhridar, the wharfs and jetties of Starkhaven must serve as the primary shipbuilding location for the Song.

'Let us first travel eastward toward Drushkála. After we have seen the Orcs, we will turn our attention to the other side of the river.''We should get a closer look at this encampment of Orcs to the east.''Look there!''So many ships, and they all ready for war! You told me what you learned in Emax Dûl, that the fleet has been in construction for so many years... but it is different entire to see the evidence with my own eyes!

'Let us descend the slope toward Drushkála. Go carefully! Remain alert for anything out of the ordinary.''We should get closer to the Orc encampment. But be cautious, and remain alert for anything out of the ordinary!''Look who I found!''Look who I found: an unexpected friend!

'Corudan tells me that his sister Sigileth and Cúridwan the Golden Maiden are elsewhere in Sûg Nidar; the three of them followed troubling signs to this place, but now that they have laid eyes upon the Song of Waves and Wind, they intend to counter it, if such a thing is possible. Together we will do this!''Look who I found: an unexpected friend! Corudan, his sister Sigileth, and Cúridwan the Golden Maiden are elsewhere in Sûg Nidar. Now that they have laid eyes upon the Song of Waves and Wind, they intend to counter it, if such a thing is possible. Together we will do this!''I did not expect to see you here, my friend, but it is a welcome surprise! We must each share the paths we have trod to arrive in this place, but quickly, for the days are dangerous and time is short! I believe the Kindred of the Coins has allied with Orcs of Mordor and the Empire of Ordâkh to construct this fleet of warships.

'Using this fleet, the Song of Waves and Wind, its masters might threaten all of Middle-earth!'Corudan and Sigileth have come to the Fearwater, bolstering your ability to destroy the Song of Waves and Wind.

<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>You have travelled with Corudan to the opposite shore, very near to the Haven of Bâkhridar, an encampment of Heirsworn within Sûg Nidar.Talk to Corudan outside the Haven of Bâkhridar, in Sûg NidarCorudan asked you to search supply crates within the Haven of Bâkhridar and then meet him and Rahâzi on the other side.Rahâzi and Corudan agreed to meet up with you south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar.Meet with Rahâzi and Corudan south-east of the Haven of BâkhridarRahâzi stands south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar.Talk to Rahâzi south-east of the Haven of BâkhridarCorudan stands south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar.Talk to Corudan south-east of the Haven of Bâkhridar<rgb=#00FF00>When you accept this quest, you will travel with Corudan to the opposite shore.</rgb>

'My sister and I departed Sul Madásh after you left with Inkanûsh and Glorfindel, making once again for Utug-bûr. Sigileth believed we could put the spirit of Silirtas to rest, but alas we found no sign of her. What we found instead set our course: waggon-tracks, ${PLAYER}, waggon-tracks sunk deep into the rocky ground from the weight of the goods they carried. The tracks travelled from west to east, and when I convinced my sister that we must learn from where they came, my deepest fears were realized. The guards at Ashâgir were slain, and the stockpile of Narghâk contained within was gone. Few only knew of the dangerous substance held within Ashâgir, and only one might command such waggons to transport it away. They were waggons of Temámir design, ${PLAYER}.

'Nakási Wave-reaper has taken command of this fleet, and Khôltekh has supplied it with Narghâk, the Hungry Fire. We may not yet know their full purpose... but I can make some guesses. That is the bad news! There are good tidings as well: Sigileth and I encountered Cúridwan as we followed the road towards Sûg Nidar, and with her aid we were able to slip past the border-guards. Let us walk to the other side of the river and we will speak more about what we have learned.''And so the three of us came to the Fearwater, where we have worked to sow dissent among the groups that labour to finish the fleet. As a result, each group is now alert to anything suspicious... I am afraid you will not be able to walk among them without combat any longer, ${PLAYER}!

'I have seen Balakhâd, the son of Balakhôr, from afar; he seems to command the Corsairs of this place. I know not where Nakási may be found, but my sister believes she might have established a command post on the island to the south-east. If Khôltekh is with her, he has remained out of sight. It is also possible he remains in Umbar, and arranged for the delivery of the Narghâk only through his agents.

'We have arrived outside the Haven of Bâkhridar, which seems to be an encampment of Corsairs loyal to the Heirs of Castamir who have now sworn to follow Balakhâd. Let us search the camp and see how well-supplied the Corsairs are, and if they are ready to sail. Then we will meet up on the other side of the Heirsworn camp.''Search the crates within the Heirsworn camp and we may learn how prepared they are to sail. I will meet you on the other side of the camp!''Search the crates within the Heirsworn camp and we may learn how prepared they are to sail. I will meet you on the other side of the camp!''What have you learned of the Heirsworn Corsairs? Are they prepared to sail?'

You tell Rahâzi that the Corsairs spend their time in idleness, but that supply crates within the Haven of Bâkhridar have much of what they would need to set sail on the ships of the Song.

'They will go nowhere until their leaders tell them to depart. If we put an end to Nakási and to Balakhâd, they will be content to remain here. Has not the fleet lingered here, unused, for many years?''These Corsairs are ready to sail for war, if it is commanded of them. We must do something about any who might issue such a command!''My study of this camp has revealed to me some things of interest. The Corsairs support Balakhâd; they believe he has picked up the mantle set down by his father Balakhôr, and they think he will lead them to victory over Gondor and over Ordâkh alike. They are uncertain of Nakási's loyalty, and they hate the Orcs. They believe she is the one forcing them to work alongside the creatures, and they resent her for it. Many hope Balakhâd will break ties with her and seize control of the Song for himself.

'I agree with Rahâzi. If we can kill or capture these leaders, we will have struck a major blow against those who might wield the Song of Waves and Wind against us.'Before you can confront the Song of Waves and Wind, you must rejoin Sigileth and Cúridwan.

<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>Sigileth and Cúridwan intended to set up camp on the island that holds the ruins of Kasukhín, but the bridge leading there lies beyond Starkhaven.Make your way to the island on which stands the ruins of Kasukhín, and find SigilethSigileth is by the camp-fire at Fearwater Notch, on the island of Kasukhín.Talk to Sigileth at Fearwater NotchCúridwan went to perform an investigation north-east of Fearwater Notch, on the shore of Kasukhín.Find Cúridwan north-east of Fearwater Notch, by the shore of KasukhínCúridwan stands by the water's edge north-east of Fearwater Notch.Talk to Cúridwan north-east of Fearwater NotchYou should return to Fearwater Notch with news of Cúridwan's investigation.Return to Fearwater Notch with news of Cúridwan's potential solutionSigileth stands at Fearwater Notch, awaiting news.Talk to Sigileth at Fearwater Notch'But we should not get ahead of ourselves: first we must rejoin my sister and Cúridwan. Sigileth intended to make camp on the island that lies to the south-east of here. High atop that rocky place stands the ruin of Kasukhín, and my sister suggested making camp somewhere in its shadow. Cúridwan says the fort once perched atop a hill that was a meeting-place for travellers, but that was before the floods claimed the valley.

'A single bridge stretches to the island, and it will be a long journey to the south-east along the shore to reach it. Find my sister beneath Kasukhín, but take special care as you pass through Starkhaven; that place is surely crawling with Heirsworn and Ordâkhai alike.''Sigileth intended to make camp on the island to the south-east, in the shadow of the ruined keep. A lone bridge stretches to the island, and it will be a long journey to the south-east along the shore to reach it. Take special care as you pass through Starkhaven; that place is surely crawling with both Heirsworn and Ordâkhai.''Welcome to Sûg Nidar, ${PLAYER}. I have taken this campsite from the soldiers who made it. I have named it Fearwater Notch, and it is now mine. Should they return they will not live long enough to inform anyone of our presence here. These others dislike the Ordâkhai as much as we do, and have offered their services to us. For now they have my trust.

'Did my brother tell you that we encountered Cúridwan on the road to this place? She has gone down to the water north-east of here, intending to perform an investigation of some sort. I pressed her not on the subject, but what I understood from her mumblings and musings was that she hoped to find some means of sinking the Song to the bottom of the lake?

'You should see if the Golden Maiden found success. Such a thing would be very helpful to us!''You have joined us?''You should look for Cúridwan by the water's edge to the north-east.''I see you found your way here. Have you brought the Wizard Inkanûsh with you? He will be most interested to hear what I have learned!'

You tell Cúridwan that, regretfully, Inkanûsh remained behind when you came in search of the Song of Waves and Wind, but you are also interested to hear of her discoveries. Cúridwan motions at the submerged boat.

'After you and Inkanûsh left Sul Madásh, my steps took me to Laivárth, and the Kinta Shadalith spoke to me of her experimentation with the Lâg Dávrit. She told me that you helpfully provided a number of blight samples, ${PLAYER}, but when you added them to water, in time they damaged the integrity of the bucket that held it; the wooden slats of the bucket fell apart, spilling the water onto the ground.

'I have done the same with this row-boat I found moored alongside this island. In a matter of moments, a small sample of the blight has damaged the seals that held together this boat, causing it to take on water and sink. Most curious.

'I am ready to return to Fearwater Notch, if you are. My investigation here is complete, and in it I see a means to destroy the fleet these enemies of the natural order think to wield against the Kintai and the other peoples of Shagâna. Sûg Nidar may yet become a watery grave for the Song of Waves and Wind!''The light of hope shines upon Sûg Nidar! It may yet become a watery grave for the Song of Waves and Wind!''Has Cúridwan found what she sought, ${PLAYER}?'

You briefly relate what you understand of the Golden Maiden's discovery, and its potential use for sinking the warships before they depart the Fearwater.

'A means of utilizing the blight to destroy the Song of Waves and Wind? Let us hope she is right, for our sake and for that of all Middle-earth! But it is not enough to sink the ships. We must also combat the crews here mustered, and the leaders who drive them to war.'In order to prevent the Song of Waves and Wind from threatening Middle-earth, you and your companions must achieve several important objectives.

<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>Your companions at Fearwater Notch on the island of Kasukhín have several objectives you must achieve if you are to prevent the Song of Waves and Wind from endangering Middle-earth.Talk to Corudan at Fearwater Notch and complete 'The Stockpile'Talk to Cúridwan at Fearwater Notch and complete 'Evil's Uses'Talk to Rahâzi at Fearwater Notch and complete 'Even A Single Sword'Sigileth is at Fearwater Notch on the island of Kasukhín.Talk to Sigileth at Fearwater Notch'Together we may yet defeat the schemes of Nakási and Balakhâd, but it will not be easy. Aid each of our companions with the task they choose for themselves, and together we may be able to ensure the Song of Waves and Wind can never leave Sûg Nidar!''Aid the companions with their objectives, and we will end the threat of the Song of Waves and Wind.''We are almost finished now, ${PLAYER}. Only one thing remains to be done: we must put an end to Nakási and Balakhâd.'If you and your companions can defeat Nakási and Balakhâd, you will deprive the Song of Waves and Wind of its leaders and its purpose.

<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>Sigileth is waiting for your signal to confront Nakási and Balakhâd atop the island of Kasukhín.Talk to Sigileth at Fearwater Notch and go with her to confront the leaders of the SongRahâzi is atop the island of Kasukhín.Talk to Rahâzi on the island of Kasukhín'Are you ready to deprive this fleet of its leaders, ${PLAYER}? You have only to give the word and we will search the ruins for Nakási and Balakhâd. They cannot escape the four of us: you, me, my brother, and the Dumûri warrior Rahâzi.

'Meanwhile, Cúridwan will continue to use the blight to damage the seaworthiness of the Song. It will not be long before every vessel lies at the bottom of the lake! We must give her time enough to distribute the blight to every vessel of the fleet.''I am ready if you are. They will not long hide from us.''This is bad, ${PLAYER}! Corudan lies bleeding, and Balakhâd and Nakási escape us! They will sail the surviving ships of the Song of Waves and Wind downriver... to war!'The King has been wounded!

<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>King Elessar lies in the graveyard, wounded. What happened while you were away?Talk to King Elessar in the graveyard and learn how he was woundedAphadaer ran for the docks, intending to join Balakhâd and be rewarded for the death of King Elessar.Pursue Aphadaer to the northern docks of the burning HarlondTatháta is by the northern docks of the burning Harlond, near the flagship of the Song.Talk to Tatháta by the northern docks of the burning Harlond'My King! My King! Who has done this to you?''What treacherous snake has dared harm the King?'King Elessar grimaces with pain, and blood trickles from beneath his chestplate.

'${PLAYER}, my friend... heed my words...

'It was Aphadaer... my groom of horses...

'He stood close by... and whispered in my ear. "For the Heirs of Castamir!" hissed he, and his knife found a gap... in the plates of my armour.

'He must have been... the traitor we suspected...'

Elessar laughs quietly, but the action causes him pain.

'I thought such a one... would be higher in my counsels...''We must end this. Now.''What treacherous snake has dared harm the King? If this worm thinks to join his master, he will make for the Heirsworn ship moored at the docks!''We must end this. Now.'

You ask Tatháta if she has seen Aphadaer, the man you pursued to the docks.

'He is just ahead,' she responds. 'But he is no one. We must put an end to his masters.'You and Tatháta must today end the threat posed by the Song of Waves and Wind, or lose this chance forever.

<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>Tatháta is by the northern docks in the burning Harlond, not far from the flagship of the Song.Talk to Tatháta and go with her to confront Nakási and BalakhâdTatháta stands on Nakási's flagship, Tumuldo-râba, outside the burning Harlond.Talk to Tatháta on the deck of Nakási's flagship, Tumuldo-râba'Nakási and Balakhâd must die, not for the safety of Gondor but for that of Umbar, and her people.

'Are you ready to see this done, ${PLAYER}?'Tatháta's eyes burn fiercely. She need say no more for you to know what is in her mind: vengeance and justice.'She is defeated. Her life nears its end.'You stand on the deck of Nakási's flagship, Tumuldo-râba, and survey the damage done by her pursuit of vengeance.

<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>Tatháta stands on the deck of Nakási's flagship, Tumuldo-râba, outside the burning Harlond.Talk to Tatháta and consider Nakási's final wordsLíniel is in the infirmary of the Harlond, helping those injured during the attack.Talk to Líniel inside the Harlond infirmary'Her eyes dim. Nakási sees us no longer.''It may be our words will still reach her... but that time will not last.

'If you have anything to say to Nakási, say it now.''Let me put your mind at ease, ${PLAYER}: King Elessar's wound is shallow, and we tended to it in time. He will survive the traitor's blade.'The threat posed by the Song of Waves and Wind has been met, and now those wounded during the attack must work to recover their wounds and rebuild their homes.

<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>King Elessar recovers from his wound in the Harlond infirmary.Talk to King Elessar in the Harlond infirmaryQueen Arwen and Ioreth the Healer have come to the Harlond infirmary.Talk to Ioreth in the Harlond infirmaryTalk to Queen Arwen in the Harlond infirmaryKing Elessar recovers from his wound in the Harlond infirmary.Talk to King Elessar in the Harlond infirmaryJajax is in the Harlond infirmary.Talk to Jajax in the Harlond infirmary'He has asked to see you. Disturb him not overlong! But I would not dare to keep you from him, lest I risk either your ire or that of the King!''Do not make the King wait! He wants to speak to you and hear that the battle is ended!'The King smiles at you, and you are reassured to see the return of his strength.

'My friend, I am glad to see you survived the battle! The reports I have heard tell me the threat of the Song is ended.'

You tell King Elessar that Aphadaer has paid for his treachery, and both Nakási and Balakhâd perished during the fighting. He nods.

'Would that we could have dissuaded them from this course, but alas! Only rarely is that possible. I confess to you it never occurred to me that Aphadaer could have been the supporter of the Heirs of Castamir whose presence we suspected in Minas Tirith. The gaze of my suspicion turned always to those who wielded greater power than my groom of horses! And yet the Heirsworn prized his reports, believing he was always only moments away from wielding the blade that would end my life. Surely there were opportunities to be had before today, ${PLAYER}?

'This I believe, for it seems to fit every fact. While the Harlond burned, Aphadaer stood near enough to me to whisper his battle-cry in my ear. "For the Heirs of Castamir!" he said as he slipped his knife beneath my armour, and I all unsuspecting. How then did his blade not pierce a vital organ? How could he inflict this wound with such murderous intent and yet not spill the last of my life's blood?

'I think our tour of King's Gondor planted a seed, ${PLAYER}. When he travelled with us to Anfalas and to Pinnath Gelin, he did so intending to serve the interests of the Heirs of Castamir, but I think our journey caused a sapling to grow within his heart. When today he saw the opportunity to carry out his intention, I believe he was unable to fully wield the blade that could end my life, and his aim went astray, despite his purpose.

'None can say if this be truly so, but that is my belief. I weep not for Aphadaer, but I hail him for my life, even as he sought the taking of it.''I mourn the loss of so much life, but I am grateful for such heroes as you, my friend. Without your aid the cost of this day would have been much worse.'Ioreth sputters madly, for once at a loss for words.

'The Queen asked me to attend her as she came to the Harlond. Is it true that Aphadaer thought to attack the King? Oh me! Oh my!'

You tell Ioreth that the groom attempted to kill the King, but was unsuccessful in the attempt and perished defending Balakhâd, son of Balakhôr. She nods sagely, overcoming her surprise.

'I always suspected he was a villain, ${PLAYER}. Did I not tell you as we journeyed in Outer Gondor that he was up to no good? Let none say Ioreth fails to see things as they are!'Arwen smiles at you warmly.

'I am once again in your debt, dear ${PLAYER}! My husband is ever eager to charge near and far in support of his people. Perhaps this bed will keep him from embarking upon foolish errands for a time!

'A short time only, I suspect. I am told his wound is shallow, and it would take one of more severity to keep him from tending to the needs of his people! But today he will rest, and for that I am grateful.'Ioreth sputters to herself with disbelief.Queen Arwen smiles at you and turns her attention to her injured husband.You can tell the King will not long remain abed. Already he desires to get up and move around, despite the instructions of his healers! You advise that he lay still and not aggravate his injury, and he shakes his head with amusement.

'The battle has ended, but there is something I need you to do, ${PLAYER}.

'Nakási's attack on Gondor must reshape the Kindred of the Coins, for it is my understanding that some of that body supported her in this and others did not. Belondor died in our defence, but Rothog and Tatháta also fought on our behalf, and they survived. What befell those who remained behind in Umbar?

'I ask that you speak to Jajax here in the infirmary and prepare to return with him to his city, ${PLAYER}. We must learn what we can of the situation in Umbar now that the threat posed by the Song of Waves and Wind has been eliminated.''Speak to Jajax and return with him to Umbar. I must know the state of that city, and the position of its ruling Kindred.'<rgb=#00FF00>When you complete this quest, you will sail back to Umbar with Jajax to carry out King Elessar's wishes.</rgb>

'Yes, I understand. When we sailed from Umbar Baharbêl, the city was in turmoil, and my brother was somehow in the middle of it! Let us return to the Sail-haven and learn what happened while we were gone. I will speak with you not far from the Beacon-gate when we have arrived. I have many questions.

'Does the Kindred rule still? Might there be a reward for those of us who fought to protect both Gondor and Umbar from the ravages of the Song? King Elessar is not the only one who wants answers, ${PLAYER}! Let us go at once!'The Song of Waves and Wind must not be permitted to endanger the lands of Middle-earth.<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Fearwater by using the banner at Khanâg Valoyar, in An Shêru.</rgb>

Rahâzi is atop the island of Kasukhín, in the middle of the Fearwater, with an urgent mission for you.Mount your steed and talk to Rahâzi by Kasukhín to undertake the urgent missionKhashig stands at his guard-post east of Umbar Baharbêl.Talk to Khashig at his guard-post east of Umbar Baharbêl'Through our efforts, most of the ships were damaged and cannot sail... but not all! Balakhâd and Nakási will sail the remaining ships of the Song down the River Ikorbân, endangering all the lands through which it flows!

'Mount your steed, ${PLAYER}! The city of Umbar Baharbêl lies at the mouth of the river, and if you bring word of the approaching ships to the rulers of the city, they may be able to close the river gate before the Song of Waves and Wind passes the city! Speak to me if you will do this!''We will follow behind you as we can, ${PLAYER}, but you must ride with as much speed as you can! You must get to Umbar before the Song of Waves and Wind!''If this fleet is as dangerous as you say it is, the city is in grave danger!'The people of Umbar Baharbêl must be warned about the danger that approaches them from the east!You must hurry to the eastern gate of Umbar Baharbêl and warn the guardsmen there of the approaching danger.Ride west to Umbar Baharbêl and give your warning to the guardsmen at the White GateThe guardsman would not listen. You should hurry to the Waterway Market and <rgb=#00FF00>beckon</rgb> for the folk by the pool to heed you.Will they heed you?Will they heed you?The folk near the Waterway Market must be warned of the approaching danger!Talk to Tasâdi the RumourmongerTalk to Ushrin the PurchaserTalk to Mother PhúrsiPhârex stands at attention, worried by the tidings you have brought to his city.Talk to Guardsman Phârex by the fountainDaxamat stands by the fountain, a worried expression upon his face.Talk to Daxamat by the poolDaxamat hurries off to warn the folk of the city about the approaching threat.Daxamat and the others run off to warn the folk of the city!According to his brother, you will find Jajax at the forum of Bith Gabâr.Find Jajax at the forum of Bith Gabâr and warn him of the dangerJajax stands at the forum of Bith Gabâr in the Upper Ward of Umbar Baharbêl.Talk to Jajax and go with him to warn the Kindred of the Coins about the approaching danger<rgb=#00FF00>Daxamat's Refuge is just west of the Waterway Market in Umbar Baharbêl, behind an unassuming door.</rgb>

Itûr has given you a place to shelter until you can learn what happened to your brother and your friend within Dâr Laja.Talk to Itûr within the refuge he has offered you'You must hurry on to Umbar, ${PLAYER}! Bring your warning to the guards at the gate, and I will follow behind you!''You must hurry on to Umbar! Bring your warning to the guards at the gate, and I will follow behind you!''A hostile fleet sails toward us down the River Ikorbân? That is absurd! What proof have you of this?''How foolish! How absurd!''A hostile fleet approaches from the river? Can this be so?

'I will share these tidings throughout the city!''A fleet of ships manned by the Heirsworn approaches from the River Ikorbân? How can this be?''Are we... are we in danger?''I know you for a friend of the city, ${PLAYER}. If you say a hostile fleet approaches Umbar Baharbêl, then it must be so.

'We must arrange for the defence of the city! We must get everyone away from the river!''I will arrange for the defence of the city!''What is this I hear, ${PLAYER}? Tell me what I can do!'

You ask Daxamat to spread the word to the people of the city that a fleet of dangerous ships carrying Orcs and Ordâkhai soldiers approaches from Ikorbân.

'I will! You should find my brother Jajax at the forum of Bith Gabâr... he will know what to do!''What did you say? A secret fleet sails toward the city? And I was not informed?'

You tell Jajax that Nakási Wave-reaper and Balakhâd have taken control of the Song of Waves and Wind and equipped its ships with dangerous Narghâk weapons. If it is not kept from leaving the Ikorbân River, all of Middle-earth will be in danger.

'You need the Kindred of the Coins to close the river gate? You will want my help with this, ${PLAYER}. Let me know when you are ready for us to speak with them.''The Kindred of the Coins will listen to me, you will see. No one can refuse Jajax!''It is not much, Dax, but you can stay here as long as you need. I have lived here ever since Kinsman Belondor ordered my release from the gaol following his return from Ikorbân. Many of my fellows were freed as well. I know not what Belondor saw there, but I am grateful for it!

'You can stay here until you learn what happened to your brother. There has really been no word of him since he and ${PLAYER} went to Dâr Laja?'Until he can learn what happened to his brother and his adventuring friend, it is up to Daxamat to make sense of things!

<rgb=#00FF00>Daxamat's Refuge is just west of the Waterway Market in Umbar Baharbêl, behind an unassuming door.</rgb>Itûr offered you a place in the left storage room of the Refuge. He said to open the southern door and then the storage room would be on the left side of the hall.Leave your belongings in a corner of the left storage roomItûr has followed you into the left storage room. He has a worried expression on his face.Talk to Itûr in the left storage roomItûr told you a Temámir dwarf has come to the refuge asking for you.Return to the entrance of the refuge to speak with the new Temámir arrivalA Temámir dwarf has come in search of you. But why?Talk to Birûk, the newly-arrived Temámir dwarfItûr has returned to the entrance of the refuge, and has some information for you and the Temámir Birûk.Talk to Itûr by the entrance to the refugeItûr told you about a useful feature of the refuge: a cellar beneath a trapdoor at the far end of the south hall.Explore the cellar beyond the southern hallway of the refugeBirûk nods pleasantly at the boat in the water.Talk to Birûk in the cellar of the refugeHave more people come to the refuge? You should return to the entrance and learn who has arrived and for what purpose.Return to the entrance of the refuge and learn the identity of the new arrivalsTwo residents of the city have come to the refuge. But why?Talk to Phêlex in the entrance to the refugeTalk to Khâsha in the entrance to the refugeItûr stands in the entrance to the refuge, assessing the new arrivals.Talk to Itûr in the entrance to the refugeWhat would they do in this situation, if they were here?What would they do if they were here?Itûr stands in the entrance to the refuge, awaiting your answer.Talk to Itûr in the entrance to the refuge'You can leave your belongings in the storage room. Go through the door behind me into the hall; the storage room is the door on the left.''You can leave your belongings in the storage room. Go through the door behind me into the hall; the storage room is the door on the left.''There is someone here for you, Dax... a Temámir dwarf I have never seen before.

'If he is not a friend of yours, I will send him away. If it is true that an enemy fleet approaches the city, we should not draw attention to this place.''If this Temámir is not a friend of yours, I will send him away.''You are Daxamat, the brother of Jajax? I have been looking for you! I have tidings of him you should hear. I spoke to many people hoping to find you, but at last a rumour-monger directed me to this place. Now hear what I have seen!

'I was in Dâr Laja when your brother and my friend  petitioned the Kindred of the Coins to close shut the river gate and prevent the approaching fleet from passing the city. Almost did I leave, but curiosity stayed my feet, and I watched from afar as they were seized by the guards! They were brought to the gaol, and are now captives of Hármelak... even Khôltekh has sided with her! I can think of no just reason for him to do this!

'I fear the Kindred of the Coins has betrayed the city. Even now I hesitate to return to the streets; they may keep watch for any who witnessed their duplicity!  proved a friend to many of us in the city... how can they justify imprisoning her/him after such monumental deeds on behalf of Umbari and Temámir alike?''I fear the Kindred of the Coins has betrayed the city. Even now I hesitate to return to the streets; they may keep watch for any who witnessed their betrayal!''You need a way to pass unseen from this refuge without being seen by spies loyal to the Kindred of the Coins? I would not call this day fortunate... but perhaps in this matter alone I have some good fortune to share.

'Pass through the door behind me and take the stairs down to the cellar. You will see what I mean.''Pass through the door behind me and take the stairs down to the cellar. You will see what I mean.''Ah, I see what your friend has in mind. I know a waterway to Umbar-môkh when I see one. With this I can enter and leave the refuge without detection by spies loyal to Hármelak.'

Birûk shakes his fists in the air.

'I still cannot believe Khôltekh would endanger the city in this way! I have never known  to lie, and she/he was most clear that a hostile fleet sails down the river toward us!

'I may be able to contact someone who can get a message to the prisoners. I will return and let you know if I succeed.''I may be able to contact someone who can get a message to the prisoners. I will return and let you know.''Word spreads through the city that a hostile fleet approaches on the Ikorbân River, and that  has been imprisoned for trying to stop it. Can this be true?

'My wife Khâsha and I name  a friend. Any who seek to harm her/him must answer to us! My deadliest days are behind me, but I have mates enough throughout the Shield Isles and the Cape to make things difficult for the Kindred of the Coins if they truly have betrayed the city, as the whispering suggests.

'If the word of the advance scouts can be trusted, it seems likely: they say you can hear Orkish voices from at least one of the approaching ships.''Rumours spread like wildfire throughout the Lower Ward. Is it true that  has been imprisoned by the Kindred of the Coins? I can think of no reason for her/him to languish in the gaol, especially if she/he sought to warn us about this approaching danger! Why would the Kindred support this attack?

'My husband owes a great deal to Tumúldo Fierce-water, who convinced him not to join Balakhôr during the war... but that was a different Kindred, and people say Tumúldo is slain.

'People also say you and your brother are 's close companions, Daxamat. Tell us what we must do to help, and we will do it!''The people turn to you for guidance, Dax!'

You stammer to Itûr that you don't know what to do. He rests an assuring hand on your shoulder.

'Ask yourself what ${PLAYER} and Jajax would do, if they were here.''Yes! That is exactly right, Dax!

'Today we begin to fight against those who would betray us! For ${PLAYER}, and for Jajax!'With the heroes imprisoned, it falls to Daxamat to take up the struggle!

<rgb=#00FF00>Daxamat's Refuge is just west of the Waterway Market in Umbar Baharbêl, behind an unassuming door.</rgb>If you are to lead a rebellion against traitorous powers, you will need to prepare. The room to the right of the refuge's entrance should serve.If you are to lead a rebellion against traitorous powers, you will need to prepare. The room to the right of the refuge's entrance should serve.Itûr stands in the planning room to the right of the refuge's entrance.Talk to Itûr in the planning roomItûr wonders what has befallen the prisoners.Talk to Itûr in the planning roomNakûr, another recent arrival, sits in the entrance to the refuge.Talk to Nakûr in the entrance to the refuge'None would mistake me for one of the Corsairs of legend; my prowess is not in combat or swordplay. I spent many weeks in the gaol when the nobleman I thought to rob of his purse proved more vigilant than I expected, so I would not recommend you assign me tasks of thievery!'

Itûr laughs suddenly.

'There is one thing I can help you steal, Dax. Together we will steal the hearts of the people, right from under the noses of the Kindred! Folk have already come here searching for someone to lead them, and more are sure to come. We are going to need a place where we can make our plans.

'Maybe we should set up the room on the right so we can accommodate our growing numbers.''Folk have already come here searching for someone to lead them, and more are sure to come. We are going to need a place where we can make our plans. Maybe we should set up the room on the right so we can accommodate our growing numbers.''This is a start, but there is more to be done. The Kindred of the Coins has two places where their leadership can feel safe: within the Meeting-hall of Dâr Laja, and within the strong walls of the Citadel of the Winds. As our numbers grow, we will need to find some way of threatening these bastions, making the Kindred question its safety and the sources of its power.

'There is something else, too.''Hármelak and Khôltekh have imprisoned two of our most significant figures, Dax. The city will not forgive this outrage, and as word of it spreads, the dominion of the Kindred must begin to weaken. Did they underestimate how beloved ${PLAYER} has become to the people of Umbar Baharbêl? Did they underestimate the popularity of your brother Jajax?

'I think these were mistakes, Dax. But now we must ask ourselves an important question. For how long will the Kindred keep Jajax and ${PLAYER} in captivity? Are they still alive, and if they are, for how long will they remain so?''Messages arrive from all throughout the city, Daxamat.

'The Song of Waves and Wind passing so near to the city has caused our numbers to grow. The people cannot disbelieve the evidence of their own eyes: that the Kindred allowed these ships to sink an Umbari galley. They have allied with Orcs, and by so doing are no better than those vile creatures!

'The fleet has sailed into the Bay and left us behind, but the Kindred will still come to rue its passage.'With the heroes imprisoned, it falls to Daxamat to take up the struggle!

<rgb=#00FF00>Daxamat's Refuge is just west of the Waterway Market in Umbar Baharbêl, behind an unassuming door.</rgb>The last time Nakûr checked there were no messages, but perhaps now there will be. If so, the shopkeeper Sekét will have slipped them under the door at the top of the stairs on the left side of the entrance to the refuge.Check if there are any messages atop the stairs on the left side of the entrance to the refugeNakûr will be pleased to see the arrival of these new messages.Talk to Nakûr in the entrance to the refugeYou should spread out the papers on the table in the planning room to the right of the entrance to the refuge.Shêsha and her cat Rûmina study the papers in the planning room.Talk to Shêsha in the planning roomBirûk was due to arrive sometime soon. You should go down to the cellar and see if the Temámir has returned.Go down to the cellar and see if Birûk has returnedSomething has happened by the entrance to the refuge. You hear the sound of voices raised in anger!Return to the entrance of the refuge and learn what has happenedTwo leaders of the Kindred of the Coins stand ready to fight!Can bloodshed be avoided?Rothog the Storm stares at you carefully.Talk to Rothog in the entrance to the refugeKinsman Belondor appraises you.Talk to Belondor in the entrance to the refuge'Messages are coming from every Ward of the city; I have been running hither and yon all morning! Let me rest, I beg you, only for a moment! Once I have caught my breath I will return to the work!'

You tell Nakûr he should rest, for he will be of little use to Ilma-ghôli, the rising tide of rebellion, if he falls down from exhaustion. He smiles gratefully.

'I only need a moment, Daxamat, really! But if you climb the stairs and check to see if Sekét has slipped any more messages under his door, my rest should cost us very little. There were none when last I checked, but that was a few minutes ago.''I only need a moment, Daxamat, really! But if you climb the stairs and check to see if Sekét has slipped any more messages under his door, my rest should cost us very little. There were none when last I checked, but that was a few minutes ago.''Already there are more messages from elsewhere in the city? Events are moving quickly, Daxamat! You should spread out those papers on the planning table. More folk wait for their orders!''You should spread out those papers on the planning table. More folk wait for their orders!''Rûmina and I can move unnoticed through the Lower Ward with great speed... until the moment we want to be seen, and to be heard. I am confident we can spread the news of Hármelak's betrayal of the city, and that Khôltekh may be aiding her. It will not be difficult: few of the Umbari failed to see the enemy ships as they passed the city, and it was apparent to all that their Corsair crews had joined hands with soldiers of Ordâkh and Orcs of Mordor. It is an outrage and a mockery!

'I understand there is a plan in motion to free your brother and ${PLAYER} from captivity? Has there yet been any word?''One more thing! I understand there is a plan in motion to free your brother and ${PLAYER} from captivity? Has there yet been any word?''I bring good news from Umbar-môkh, Daxamat.

'My contact has spoken with . She/He and Jajax are being held within the Fleetfast gaol, and the Terâsi girl is willing to show us a secret way inside. She seemed very insistent that if she performs this task for us, we will see that the enemy fleet is destroyed. I know not if that is within our power... but I told her we would consider it.

'We need  and Jajax freed. We can consider nothing until that happens, am I right?''Something has happened upstairs! Are we discovered?''For now I relent. If you give me a reason to fight, I will not again lower my khopeshes until the battle is done!

'Belondor and I were away from the city, visiting the arid hills of Damarzâg and looking for evidence of the Thardúth. We found none, but when we returned to Umbar Baharbêl the shouting of its people could be mistaken by no one. Someone had allowed a fleet of Mordor and Ordâkh to pass by the city, and as it sailed into the Bay it turned its cannons upon Umbari ships! Even now the wreck of an Umbari galley smoulders with the blue flames of the Hungry Fire!

'Some members of my Kindred seem to have allied with this fleet, but only one arranged for me and Belondor to be away from the city when it arrived. This was the work of Hármelak! She knew this fleet was on its way, and she wanted to ensure Rothog did not stop it!''You are Daxamat, yes? The brother of Jajax? These men follow your command?'

Belondor looks you up and down, and releases his hand from the hilt of his sword.

'I should have known something was amiss, Daxamat. Hármelak's sudden interest in the Thardúth should have raised my suspicion, for always has she dismissed the servants of Morgoth we faced in Urash Dâr as less of a threat to Umbar than others. To ask Rothog and I to travel to Damarzâg, to learn if they have any presence there... it seems an obvious ruse, now, a means of keeping two members of the Kindred from interfering with her plans. When we departed I thought only that at last she was taking seriously the danger.

'But now we have returned, and we must decide what can be done. Where is ? We should ask her/him for her/his thoughts.'With the heroes imprisoned, it falls to Daxamat to take up the struggle!

<rgb=#00FF00>Daxamat's Refuge is just west of the Waterway Market in Umbar Baharbêl, behind an unassuming door.</rgb>The time has come for you to use the table and address the gathering in the planning room to the right of the entrance.Use the table in the planning room to address the gatheringYour gathered allies await their orders in the planning room to the right of the entrance to the refuge.Your gathered allies await their orders in the planning room to the right of the entrance to the refuge.Talk to Belondor and go with him to rescue the prisonersBelondor awaits the word to begin the rescue mission.Talk to Belondor and stay behind while he goes to rescue the prisoners<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>

You have arrived at the Harlond in time of war, the port-city wreathed in flames.Talk to Tatháta while the Harlond burns'Imprisoned? We will need to do something about that.

'Something else troubles me. Some of the people with whom I spoke claim that Nakási commands the fleet, and she has joined hands with Balakhâd, the son of Balakhôr; their ships are crewed with Heirsworn Corsairs, Orcs of Mordor, and Ordâkhai soldiers alike. If this is true, fully half of the Kindred of the Coins have changed their loyalties: Nakási, Hármelak, and Khôltekh can no longer be trusted to lead.

'Where is Tatháta in all this? She has always been more solitary than the rest, but if she sides with the betrayers it will be difficult for Rothog and I to convince the city that our position is just. That way is certain to lead to bloodshed. I do not fear it! I would prefer not to slay my fellows if it might be avoided, but we need to remove the blight from the Kindred of the Coins in order to cleanse it, one way or another. 

'But you are the leader of this band of fighters, Daxamat. Consider all that must be done, and give your people their commands. The uprising in Umbar begins now!''But you are the leader of this band of fighters, Daxamat. Consider all that must be done, and give your people their commands. The uprising in Umbar begins now!''Rûmina and I have many contacts within the Sail-haven and the Lower Ward. We will spread the news of Hármelak's betrayal, and rally the Umbari to march upon Dâr Laja. Corsairs and mariners, vendors and caravan drivers, even the troublemakers and brigands of the Gut... all these folk have reason to overthrow the rulers who think to sell us to Mordor or to Ordâkh!

'Even the Corsair Jeduth may join us in this. He has retired from the privateering trade, but he will see the rightness of Ilma-ghôli's cause!''I know of a place where many weapons are stored, Dax: beneath the Dahâl Huliz, in Kamrabezûr, are racks and racks of weapons for use in the arena. But that is not all we can take from there. The gladiators revere Rothog as both a great warrior and a leader of the city. If they are shown he sides with us to overthrow the villains who betray Umbar Baharbêl, we will have obtained not just weapons, but fighters to wield them as well.

'We must not underestimate the reputation of Rothog the Storm! The prospect of facing him in single combat was enough to keep me safely and content in the gaol. I knew not that Kinsman Belondor would free me from captivity without fighting only days later, but I did know not to face Rothog on the blood-sands for my freedom!

'But today I will fight for freedom from the traitors who pretend to speak for Umbar... but I fight beside the Storm, and not against him!''There is no need to draw stones, as is the custom among my people in Khabârkhad; I know what duty is set before me.

'First I will go to Mekab-kuphâr with this unpleasant news: Khôltekh has jeopardized the lives, safety, and wealth of the Temámir people. I will bring those of my fellows who agree with this position to the Shoreward Stone, where we will seek an audience with Inîk Jewel-brow, the Hall-father. One way or another, Khôltekh will be removed from power for his part in this calamity.

'While I do this, someone else must make use of the secret entrance into the Fleetfast gaol in order to free your brother and ${PLAYER}.''You have given these folk their orders, Daxamat. What now is your role to play?'

You tell Belondor that you are ready to free your brother Jajax and the hero ${PLAYER} from the Fleetfast gaol, but before you can say anything else, he shakes his head.

'I think not, Daxamat. That is a dangerous undertaking. I cannot say how it has happened, but you have somehow become the leader of this rising tide, this Ilma-ghôli. Without you to focus these varied and disparate fighters, I think this uprising is snuffed out like a torch doused in sea-water. You must remain here at this refuge in order to coordinate the efforts of Ilma-ghôli.

'The rescue of ${PLAYER} and your brother must be left to others.''Rothog and I will lead this rescue mission. ${PLAYER} and Jajax are imprisoned by those we counted allies, even friends. The two of us must set this right.

'I will speak with the Temámir about this secret entrance he has discovered. Were it not now of use, I would rue its very existence! But it seems such a way into the gaol will now help us bring our friends to freedom, and about that I will not complain.

'Regret not that you do not accompany us! There will be danger enough for you here, Daxamat. All of the city will soon come alive with anger, and you must be ready to guide its furious voice!''The Harlond burns. We have arrived too late.'You have sailed in haste to Gondor, but the Song arrived before you, and the Harlond is in flames.

<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>You should make your way north-west past the reeds in search of Gondorian defenders.Make your way north-west in search of Gondorian defendersA soldier of Gondor greets you by the southern side of the burning Harlond, desperate hope written on his face.Talk to the soldier of Gondor by the south-western edge of the HarlondDefenders of Gondor fought bravely against the assault of the Song, but were pushed back to a slope north-west of the Harlond, beyond the graveyard.Find more defenders north-west of the Harlond, past the graveyardBorndir stands on the slope north-west of the burning Harlond, past the graveyard.Talk to Borndir on the slope north-west of the graveyard outside the HarlondBorndir told you that King Elessar has gathered a number of soldiers on the overlook at the top of the sloping path north-west of the burning Harlond, and prepares to make a counter-attack against the invaders.Find King Elessar at the overlook atop the sloping path north-west of the graveyard outside the burning HarlondKing Elessar prepares for the counter-attack from the overlook north-west of the burning Harlond.Talk to King Elessar at the overlook north-west of the burning Harlond'Gondor cannot be without defenders! Where are its knights? Where are its fighters? The King of Gondor would not permit an incursion so near to the White City to remain unmet... unless he had no choice.

'We must press forward to the north-west in search of any who might stand against Nakási.''Press forward and search for Gondor's defenders! Follow the sound of fighting to the north-west!

'Gondor would not willingly abandon this port-city to the ravages of the Song.''Over here!''Press forward and search for Gondor's defenders! Follow the sound of fighting to the north-west!

'Gondor would not willingly abandon this port-city to the ravages of the Song.''Is that you, ${PLAYER}? We are hard-pressed here, and have lost many men in an attempt to learn what villain bedevils us! I thought the Corsairs tasted bitter defeat during the war, and their fleet destroyed!'

You tell the soldier that the Song of Waves and Wind had been kept secret from most of Umbar, but a number of their captains schemed to use it against Gondor.

'We sallied forth from Minas Tirith when we first received word of enemy ships sailing toward the Harlond. King Elessar led the charge, but we could not get near enough for fear of the terrible blue flames fired from their weapons! Is it true they have wrought new quantities of the Umbari Fire?

'The King was pushed away from the river... find his men to the north-west, past the graveyard!''Look for Borndir at the base of the slope to the north! He guards the path to the King's encampment!''${PLAYER}!''Do my eyes deceive me? No! You have returned to stand with us against the Corsairs of Umbar, ${PLAYER}? I only hope you have not arrived too late!

'When we travelled with King Elessar to Outer Gondor that he might hear the concerns of his people and help them rebuild from the war, I did not think we would so soon be thrust once again into such horrors as have come to the Harlond this day!

'It was my duty, and Lornion's, to safeguard the King. But how can we protect him against a fleet that wields such terrible weapons, and is crewed by every enemy that ever vowed to destroy Gondor: Corsairs, Haradrim, and Orcs, all united in hatred against us?

'King Elessar has established a camp on the overlook atop this sloping path, ${PLAYER}. Go to him and learn what can be done against these invaders, if there be anything!''You will find King Elessar at the top of this path! Go to him with haste!'King Elessar stands here.King Elessar turns to face you, his expression brightening as he recognizes your return from distant lands.

'You return to Gondor in its time of need, my friend; I deem that is no coincidence. Tell me everything you know of this fleet and the villains who captain it!'Gondor has suffered a defeat, but now it is time for the counter-attack to begin.

<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>King Elessar has asked you to speak to his attendants on the overlook north-west of the burning Harlond to learn what must be done for the counter-attack to begin.Talk to Aphadaer on the overlookTalk to Lornion on the overlookTalk to Glindor on the overlookGondorian swords were dropped on the sloping path when the soldiers retreated to the overlook north-west of the burning Harlond.Retrieve Gondorian swords dropped on the path to the overlook during the retreat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You were told to leave the swords you retrieved in a barrel by the graveyard outside the burning Harlond, rescue frightened horses that fled in the direction of the main street, and defeat Orcs and Ordâkhai that threaten the port.Find the horse Agladal along the main street and send him to safetyFind the horse Gaeranor along the main street and send him to safetyDefeat Orcs throughout the burning Harlond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ordâkhai soldiers throughout the burning Harlond (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})With the tasks given to you by King Elessar's attendants now completed, you should return to the graveyard outside the burning Harlond and prepare to push back the invaders.Return to the graveyard outside the burning HarlondAphadaer has called you to him at the graveyard outside the burning Harlond.Talk to Aphadaer at the graveyardKing Elessar is at the graveyard outside the burning Harlond, preparing to strike back against the invaders.Talk to King Elessar at the graveyardBelondor is at the graveyard outside the burning Harlond.Talk to Belondor at the graveyardElessar sighs when you finish your account, and you can tell the events of the day have taken their toll.

'The death of Nakási's husband Tumúldo at the hands of the Heirsworn was an injustice, but it cannot warrant such an attack as this. Had she remained in Umbar, nursing her hatred of Gondor, that would be a sorrow, and I would share her grief. But for her to seize command of this fleet and these weapons and bring them to bear against my people... that cannot be forgiven.

'Five ships have come to the Harlond wielding the Hungry Fire I thought was gone. Nakási captains the largest of these. Two others are crewed by Haradrim soldiers, and one has Orcs aboard. I could not see who commands the crew of the last ship, but from your account I deem it must be Balakhâd, son of Balakhôr the Scourge. The Heirs of Castamir remain to trouble us, it seems.

'It has been a losing struggle to this point, ${PLAYER}, but perhaps your arrival will help to turn the tide. Speak to my attendants here on the overlook and we will begin to fight back against these invaders!''Speak to my attendants and learn how we can fight back against Nakási and Balakhâd!''It has only been a matter of weeks since I travelled with you in Anfalas, ${PLAYER}, but so much has happened! Is it true that the son of Balakhôr the Scourge captains one of these ships against us? Are the Heirs of Castamir behind this attack?'

You tell Aphadaer that Balakhâd supplied Corsair crews for some of Nakási's fleet, but most of those ships were damaged before they could sail to Gondor. You ask him what you can do to help fight against the five ships that made the journey.

'There was much chaos as we retreated to this overlook, ${PLAYER}, and we were pursued by our enemies. As the King's groom, it is my job to see to the horses, and I did as best I could, but two of them slipped from my tending and fled toward the main street that runs through the centre of the Harlond. They were crazed by the flames, you see. Who among us was not? If you find Agladal and Gaeranor, send them back to me, if they still live!''The ships sailed into the Harlond with no warning, ${PLAYER}. Their crews of Orcs and Haradrim set the port ablaze in the span of a single hour. They came ashore and we met them with sword and spear, but we were unprepared for such ferocity in time of peace. Our counter attack will come, and it must come soon!

'Face any of those who now pillage the Harlond, and you will help us regain the advantage!''King Elessar rode bravely from the White City and led a sortie against the invaders, but we were pushed back to this hill. During the retreat, some of our soldiers dropped their weapons on the slope. Retrieve these weapons as you descend from the overlook, and leave them in the weapons barrel that has been placed by the graveyard. They will be used again!''Can you pick up the weapons we dropped on the path as we climbed to this overlook? After you have them, leave them in a barrel by the graveyard for other soldiers to wield in defence of Gondor!''Leave the swords you collected in a barrel by the graveyard for other soldiers to wield in defence of Gondor!''The horses bolted from the unnatural blue flames. Search for them along the main street of the Harlond, to the east!''We must prove to the Orcs and Haradrim that Gondor is not without courage!'Aphadaer stands here.'Did you see the son of Balakhôr? I heard shouting above the tumult, and voices cried that the Heirs of Castamir have designs upon the White City! Could it be true?'

You assure Aphadaer that the Heirsworn will not have victory, despite their initial success, and that the counter attack will begin at Elessar's command.

'Of course, of course. Heed not my jumbled thoughts!''How have the Heirs of Castamir come to wield these blue flames? Is the son of Balakhôr an enchanter?'The King's expression is already greatly-changed from when you first encountered him today. His weariness has been replaced with determination.

'This is the hour in which we fight back against the invaders,' he says.

'Belondor tells me that Nakási has broken with his Kindred, and is an enemy too of Umbar. I believe him. He counts himself no longer a man of Gondor, but today we will fight side by side to prevent Nakási and her allies from endangering our lands and our homes, though they be not shared.'The King motions to the man standing nearby, a man once of Gondor but now of Umbar.

'Belondor tells me Nakási has broken with the Kindred of the Coins, and I believe him.''We have to do something about the Narghâk weapons Nakási has mounted upon the Song, ${PLAYER}.'As long as the Song possesses its Narghâk weapons, every shore in Middle-earth remains at risk.

<rgb=#00FF00>You can return to the Harlond in Flames by using the banner east of the Beacon-gate, in Umbar Baharbêl.</rgb>Jajax is on the eastern side of the port-city, preparing to storm the docks.Find Jajax on the eastern side of the burning Harlond, preparing to storm the docksJajax is on the eastern side of the port-city, preparing to storm the docks.Talk to Jajax and go with him to sabotage the Narghâk weapons of the SongThe day is not yet won. You must return to the graveyard outside the burning Harlond and learn what next can be done.Return to the graveyard and talk to King ElessarTalk to Borndir at the graveyard and learn what happened to the King.Talk to Borndir at the graveyard'Nakási inflicted great damage upon the Harlond with her initial attack, but her forces are limited to those who made the crossing. The soldiers of Minas Tirith greatly outnumber the warriors at Nakási's disposal; when King Elessar mounts his counter attack, they should be able to overwhelm the crews of the Song. The Narghâk weapons remain the real danger, for they greatly make up for her disadvantage in numbers. We have to disable those weapons, ${PLAYER}.

'I will go with Rothog to destroy the Narghâk weapons aboard the Orc ship. You should find Jajax on the eastern side of the port-city, near the docks, and go with him to destroy the Narghâk weapons aboard one of the Ordâkhai vessels! Then we will have levelled the playing-field somewhat, and given King Elessar an opportunity to mount the counter attack. This is what Sirgon wanted, ${PLAYER}: peace between Gondor and Umbar. I will not allow Nakási to shatter the chance for good relations between our peoples!''Find Jajax and work with him to disable the Narghâk weapons on one of the ships! Rothog and I will do the same for another!

'This is what Sirgon wanted: peace between Gondor and Umbar. I will not allow Nakási to shatter the chance for good relations between our peoples!'Jajax stands here.'Belondor and Rothog will disable the Narghâk weapons on another of the ships? Then let it be a competition, ${PLAYER}! With your good fortune and my incredible skill we will accomplish our own mission before they succeed!''I don't... I don't know what happened!''I don't... I don't know what happened! One moment the King was issuing commands to his knights, and the next he was upon the ground!

'I think he has been stabbed by a secret knife, ${PLAYER}!'Ordâkhai have captured many Beltáni with the intention to force them into servitude. They need to be rescued before they can be taken to Esh Mêkag.Kûrmi fears that the Ordâkhai have captured some of the Beltáni and taken them to Wither-watch.

You should travel to Wither-watch and free any captured Beltáni you find.Free captured Beltáni (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have freed many captured Beltáni from the Ordâkhai at Wither-watch.

You should return to Ahâba and talk to Kûrmi.Talk to Kûrmi'For years, the Ordâkhai have attempted to recruit us to their cause. Those who refuse are kidnapped in raids and sent to Esh Mêkag to work.

'Many of our people have gone missing since their last raid, and we fear the worst. If you travel to the Ordâkhai camp at Okhatohól, Wither-watch, look for our people, and free them if you can.''The Beltáni you freed have returned! Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You have proven yourself a friend to our people in my eyes.'Rahâzi trusts in Cúridwan's plan, but she worries that the Corsairs and Ordâkhai might be a threat even without the Song of Waves and Wind.Rahâzi wants you to deprive the Corsairs and Ordâkhai of Sûg Nidar of their weapons.Defeat Heirsworn of Sûg Nidar and take their weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ordâkhai of Sûg Nidar and take their weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rahâzi asked to meet with you to the north-east of Fearwater Notch to dispose of the Heirsworn and Ordâkh weapons.Talk to Rahâzi at the shore north-east of Fearwater NotchRahâzi asked you to dispose of the weapons at the shore north-east of Fearwater Notch.Dispose of the weapons at the shore north-east of Fearwater NotchRahâzi asked you to dispose of the weapons at the shore north-east of Fearwater Notch.Dispose of more weapons at the shore north-east of Fearwater NotchRahâzi asked you to dispose of the weapons at the shore north-east of Fearwater Notch.Dispose of the rest of the weapons at the shore north-east of Fearwater Notch<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> farewell to the weapons that can no longer be used by your enemies.<rgb=#00FF00>Wave</rgb> farewell to the weapons that can no longer be used by your enemiesRahâzi is at the shore north-east of Fearwater Notch, where you disposed of the weapons you gathered from your enemies.Talk to Rahâzi at the shore north-east of Fearwater Notch'Starkhaven swarms with Heirsworn Corsairs and soldiers of Ordâkh, but at Nakási's command they will board the ships and sail to war. I trust in Cúridwan's plan, but even if the fleets of the Song are made unable to sail, these enemies will remain to threaten the Ikorbân valley and my home of Ambarûl!

'Even a single sword can inflict great injury, ${PLAYER}. Let us defeat these foes and wrest from them their blades. Then we will dump them in the water on the north-eastern shore of this island and ensure they cannot be wielded against the peaceful residents along the river, should the Golden Maiden's plan prove unsuccessful.''We must deprive the Corsairs and the Ordâkhai of their weapons! Let us defeat these foes and wrest from them their blades. Then we will dump them in the water on the north-eastern shore of this island and ensure they cannot be wielded against the peaceful residents along the river, should the Golden Maiden's plan prove unsuccessful.''This is a good spot. Dispose of the swords you gathered, and the water will erode the sharpness of the blades, rendering them unusable by our foes.''The former owners of those blades will not think to look for them here!''The former owners of those blades will not think to look for them here!''The former owners of those blades will not think to look for them here!''Bid farewell to your weapons, enemies of Ambarûl!''Ha! You amuse me, ${PLAYER}.

'Now the Heirsworn Corsairs and the soldiers of Ordâkh will find it more difficult to threaten the peaceful lands downriver, should Cúridwan's plan not succeed. I hope it will, but we must plan for anything; that is a lesson of my mother Girhâzi, and of the great hero Shurug-nîn!'Cúridwan needs as much of the blight as she can find if she is to use it to damage the Song of Waves and Wind.Cúridwan has identified some locations outside Starkhaven where the blight has crept into Sûg Nidar, along with some creatures from Adagím.Collect useful samples of the blight outside Starkhaven (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat creatures from Adagím that have slipped into Sûg Nidar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Cúridwan is outside the blighted vale located outside the eastern entrance to Starkhaven, in Sûg Nidar.'I never expected to use the blight for a good purpose, but this is truly a day for surprises.

'Some of the mysteries that plagued Imhûlar and Adagím have been made clear to me now that I see what has transpired within the Fearwater. For many years I believed the floods cascading into Adagím from the north were caused when spring rains overfed the Ikorbân River, but it was not so. The Ordâkhai dredged an old tributary channel, carving a path south from Sûg Nidar. Now the floods that might have destroyed their wharves were instead spilled upon Adagím, already suffering from the blight. Was the extent of the Lâg Dávrit worsened by these annual floods and the noisome bog to which they contributed? It must have been.

'But now I have need of the blight to counter this Ordâkhai fleet, and its pervasive reach will be of use to us! Pods of the blight push into Sûg Nidar from Adagím, and they have taken root within a narrow vale just outside the eastern entrance to Starkhaven, not far from the long bridge that leads to this island. Take this sack and trowel and collect samples of blighted pods for me while you combat some of the creatures that even now push into Sûg Nidar. I will meet you outside that blighted place once you have done this.''I need you to collect samples of the blight I can use to disable the fleet. Pods of the blight push into Sûg Nidar from Adagím, and they have taken root within a narrow vale just outside the eastern entrance to Starkhaven, not far from the long bridge that leads to this island. Take this sack and trowel and collect samples of blighted pods for me while you combat some of the creatures that even now push into Sûg Nidar. I will meet you outside that blighted place once you have done this.''The trowel I gave to you will enable you to collect samples of the blight I can use to disable the fleet.''Have you done as I asked? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. When handled with care, such samples as these may prove that even evil has its uses... for if the Song of Waves and Wind can be made unseaworthy then even the Lâg Dávrit may save some lives.

'I will continue my work applying the blight to the water by the ships of the Song. In time no vessel will remain afloat, and the designs of Ordâkh and Mordor will be ruined. Sigileth is right that the leaders must be captured or slain to truly end this threat... but sinking the Song is an important step on that road. Thank you again for your efforts.'You have agreed to help Isamó and Engéru escape from Starkhaven before the Song sails to war.The sloping path that leads out of Starkhaven is to the south. You should travel ahead of Isamó and ensure the way is clear for her to follow.Travel ahead of Isamó to the sloping path that leads out of StarkhavenA path out of Starkhaven climbs to the north-west. Isamó asked that you clear the way to that gate for her.Climb north-west to the gate out of StarkhavenIsamó has arrived at one of the paths that leads out of Starkhaven.Talk to Isamó by the gateShe wipes her eyes.

'There is a sloping path that leads to a gate in the south-west reaches of Starkhaven. The gate is usually closed, but Engéru arranged that it would be left open for us on this day.

'Go ahead of me, to this south-western gate, and clear the way of enemies. If you will be my eyes, I will do the best I can to carry out my husband's wishes, though it pains me.'Isamó has resolved to be courageous, but her eyes are still full of tears.

'Go ahead of me, to this south-western gate, and clear the way of enemies. If you will be my eyes, I will do the best I can to carry out my husband's wishes, though it pains me.'Isamó stares at the open gate as if part of her wished it remained closed.

'My feet are heavy, stranger, but for Engéru I will let them carry me from Starkhaven. I thank you for showing me the way safely here, and I have only one thing more to ask of you.

'Think not ill of me or of my husband. Each of us were born into our families' work, and the construction of the fleet was all we ever knew. Of course ships are made for war! But when such a fleet sits idle for so many years, is it so strange to believe it might always remain unused? So it was for our families, and for Engéru, and for myself.

'Farewell, stranger. If you might somehow prevail against the Song, know that Engéru and Isamó celebrate with you.'Shepherd Nahíd in Ahâba needs help finding his lost sheep.Nahíd has requested help gathering his sheep.

You should start by collecting the nearby hay bale.Collect hay baleSeveral sheep have wandered off and become lost in and near Ahâba.

You should find and <rgb=#00FFFF>whistle</rgb> at the lost sheep to send them home.<rgb=#00FFFF>Whistle</rgb> at lost sheep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have found all of Nahíd's lost sheep.

You should return to Nahíd.Talk to Nahíd'Welcome to Ahâba, stranger. I am Nahíd, a humble shepherd. If you are here to help, I would appreciate it. My hands are full enough as it is!

'Several of my sheep have wandered off. They should still be nearby, but I fear if I go looking for them, these two in the pen will wander off as well! Would you be willing to find them and bring them back?

'Here, take some of this hay. They cannot resist it! Whistle with it in your hand, and they should come.''They have all returned! Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Now, we just need to get them into their pen....'Shepherd Nahíd's sheep have returned, but they now need to herded back into their pen.Nahíd's sheep have returned, but need to be herded into their pen.

You should <rgb=#00FFFF>whistle</rgb> at Líshu to let her know it is time to work.<rgb=#00FFFF>Whistle</rgb> at LíshuLíshu is ready to herd the sheep into their pen.

You should <rgb=#00FFFF>point</rgb> at the sheep near the pen to instruct Líshu to herd them.

If Líshu is missing, you can use Líshu's Horn, on the fence near Nahíd, to recall her.<rgb=#00FFFF>Point</rgb> out sheep for Líshu to herd (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The sheep have all been returned to their pen.

You should let Líshu know she has done a good job!

If Líshu is missing, you can use Líshu's Horn, on the fence near Nahíd, to recall her.Talk to LíshuLíshu's job is finished.

You should talk to Nahíd.Talk to Nahíd'The sheep have returned, but now they need to be rounded up. This is the perfect job for Líshu! Would you like to try commanding her? Just point at the sheep you want her to herd, and she will see it done.''I knew Líshu would finish this task in no time! And thanks to you, my friend, for helping. Unfortunately, it won't be long until they wander off again. A shepherd's work is never done!'You let Líshu know she has done a good job, and offer a pat on the head.

'Rowf!'

She offers a single bark and a wagging tail in return.Gredbyg have infested an an area near the Dawn-warden and now threaten the Aradûni.The gredbyg have infested an area to the north of the Dawn-warden called Gnasher's Delf.

You should defeat gredbyg and destroy the grodbog hives with the provided explosives at Gnasher's Delf.Destroy grodbog hives (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat gredbyg in Gnasher's Delf (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have reduced the grodbog numbers at Gnasher's Delf.

You should return to Ashâb at the Dawn-warden.Talk to Ashâb'Are you here to help our war effort, friend? I have work for someone that can hold their own in combat.

'To the north, a grodbog infestation is growing out of control. If you are willing to reduce their numbers for us, I have a small stipend with which to reward you.

'I trust you will have no trouble slaying the insects, but those hives are tough. Take these small explosives. They are meant for clearing rocks for construction, but they should take care of their combs with no trouble!''Have you reduced the gredbyg's numbers? Good work. That is one fewer threat to our incoming soldiers to worry about.'The ship-yard at Sûg Nidar has constructed dozens of ships, with even more still in progress. You should explore the vast ship-yard at Starkhaven.Standing by a banner on the north-western side of Starkhaven, you decide to explore the ship-yard and learn what you can of its workings.Examine the banner at the ship-yard of StarkhavenThe ship-yard at Starkhaven sprawls along the shore at Sûg Nidar, birth-place of a mighty fleet.Explore north-west frame constructionExplore western timber assemblyExplore western central scaffoldingExplore the central keep of StarkhavenExplore eastern central scaffoldingExplore the south-east forgesExplore south-east frame constructionExplore eastern timber assemblyYou have explored the inner workings of the ship-yard at Starkhaven, and learned much of how such a mighty fleet could be constructed.CompletedStanding by a banner on the north-western side of Starkhaven, you reflect upon the construction of such a fleet as the Song. It must have required a tremendous effort from thousands of workers for many years, and such work is revealed by the sprawling vastness of the ship-yard.

You decide to explore Starkhaven and see what you can learn of the construction effort.Your exploration of the ship-yard at Starkhaven has revealed something troubling: despite the hive of activity it must have been over the years, construction has now slowed tremendously. Many ships remain unfinished, and skeletal hulls stand where they were begun.

The Song of Waves and Wind has no need of further ships. The fleet is large enough already, and the threat it poses is very real. You and your friends must do something, or all of coastal Middle-earth is in danger.Together, you and Rahâzi have snuck aboard a waggon carrying supplies and must remain hidden from the Temámir who drives it.Rahâzi is hidden inside the waggon.Talk to Rahâzi inside the waggonYou should stand near the back of the waggon and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for anyone to approach too near.Do not move, and make no noise!Try not to move or make any noiseRahâzi is hidden inside the waggon.Talk to Rahâzi inside the waggonIt will be some time before the waggon arrives. Now you can only wait.Pass the time while the waggon rumbles to its destinationRahâzi is hidden inside the waggon.Talk to Rahâzi inside the waggonYou should stand near the back of the waggon and <rgb=#00FF00>listen</rgb> for anyone to approach too near.If the driver moves away, it should be safe to depart the waggon.Wait for the driver to leave before departing the waggon'Look at the cargo this waggon transports, ${PLAYER}: these are not the ropes and timbers I expected necessary to finish construction of a fleet of ships. Much of these supplies are wealthy goods and valuables.

'For what purpose does the Temámir waggon-driver bring these items to Sûg Nidar?''Now we wait. You might as well make yourself comfortable.''Was Shurug-nîn's own adventure like this, ${PLAYER}? The songs and tales record only her deeds of daring and of courage. Much was made of her contests of strength against the dragons, but little is said of the days and weeks between such battles, though they must have existed.

'Will our own song speak of this waggon-ride? I suppose that depends upon what awaits us at the end of it: triumphant victory or crushing defeat.'Sigileth has tracked Balakhâd and Nakási to the island of Kasukhín, in the middle of the Fearwater.Sigileth is eager to end the threat posed by Balakhâd and Nakási.Talk to Sigileth on the island of KasukhínBalakhâd has expressed a desire to speak with you instead of fighting.Talk to Balakhâd on the island of KasukhínBalakhâd has attempted to convince you of the rightness of his position.Stand your ground against BalakhâdWords will not appease Balakhâd. Only combat will suffice!Defeat Balakhâd on the island of KasukhínNakási has discovered your attempt to destroy the Song of Waves and Wind!Delay Nakási long enough for Cúridwan to finish her missionCorudan has been grievously injured by Nakási's deadly blade.Examine Corudan's wound'Balakhâd and Nakási must be somewhere within the ruins of Kasukhín that sit atop the island; from that high place they can survey the fleet. It will not be long until they begin to see the effects of Cúridwan's interference. We must hurry.

'They will have defenders posted on the bridge that leads to the ruins, ${PLAYER}. Prepare for a fight!''My childhood was one of tumult, ${PLAYER}. My mother and my father spoke often to me of Castamir, instructing me that it was our duty to follow his example. Often I wondered if they were right. Was it true that Elves would always seek to keep our people underfoot, subject to their laws and their shadowy rule?

'Could my parents have been wrong? From time to time I saw Elves of the Oasis, the Kintai, in the markets of Umbar Baharbêl, and they seemed otherworldly to me but never sinister. In truth, much of the evil I saw came at the hands of Men! Did not the Kindred of the Coins hold me captive and chase my mother into hiding at the conclusion of their uprising? Was I not threatened with torture by Azagath Sea-shadow and Nakási Wave-reaper?

'But then I beheld the terrible battle where the waterfalls ran red, and I saw the monstrous Orcs that emerged from Utug-bûr. I heard the battle-cries of the ferocious Utûgi, and I saw the corpses piled at their feet. I perceived the name of their masters, ${PLAYER}, and they were called the Thardúth. From afar I heard the Wizard Inkanûsh speak of them as he strove against their powers, and I knew them for what they were.

'They are Elves, ${PLAYER}. A terrible evil of the ancient world has awoken to endanger the lands of Men, and it is in form and nature precisely what my father believed it would be. Castamir was right, and my parents were right, and in their names I have gathered those who would fight to save our world from Elf-kind. Nakási and I have set aside our quarrel. With her ships and my loyal Heirsworn, we will free all of Middle-earth from the grasp of the Elves, and those who aid them.

'If you will stand with me, I would welcome your prowess. You know how dangerous the Thardúth can be.''${PLAYER}... don't worry about me...

'You have to stop them...'Nakási Wave-reaper sails upon the waters of memory, unknown to all but her.One of the guards within the Citadel of Winds thinks to bar your passage to the chamber where meet the Kindred of the Coins.Talk to the guard within the Citadel of WindsYour husband Tumúldo meets with the other members of the Kindred of the Coins within the Citadel of Winds.Enter the chamber where your husband Tumúldo meets with the other members of the KindredThe Kindred of the Coins debate your presence within the Citadel of Winds.Stand beside Tumúldo while the Kindred of the Coins discusses your presenceYou must <rgb=#00FF00>think</rgb> upon this question: did the Kindred of the Coins live up to its intention?<rgb=#00FF00>Think</rgb> upon this question: did the Kindred of the Coins live up to its intentions?The other members of the Kindred leave their meeting, but you and Tumúldo stay behind.Stay with Tumúldo as the rest of the Kindred departsAzagath desires to speak with you and Tumúldo about a secret matter.Talk to Azagath about a secret matterEver was Tumúldo your stable rock, even when the days were frightening and the nights long and terrible.Remain with Tumúldo for as long as you canThere was something you wanted to tell your husband, but now you cannot remember what it could have been.Take his hand and face whatever comesYour fear, your anger, and your loneliness dissolves away into the darkness.Your fear, your anger, and your loneliness are gone at lastWhatever Nakási may have experienced during her final moments, you hope she is now at peace.Nakási Wave-reaper is goneTatháta stands upon the deck of Tumuldo-râba, Nakási's flagship.Talk to Tatháta on the deck of Tumuldo-râba'I am sorry, Captain. The Kindred of the Coins meets within.

'I cannot let you pass.''You know I have eyes everywhere. Sometimes they see things of interest to me... and to those of my friends I can trust.

'Know you of the vast lake at the head of the Ikorbân? I thought not, for it appears on few maps, and none in Umbar. Any who stray too near this lake, Sûg Nidar, the Fearwater, are slain before they can report of its existence. What deserves such secrecy? I have learned the answer, my friends, and I ask that you hear me out complete before you disregard my words.

'Decades ago, following the destruction of Umbar and the burning of its fleet at the hands of the hated Thorongil, the Dark Lord of Mordor commanded the creation of a new fleet to replace the one that was lost. Barkhûsh ordered the creation of this new armada at Sûg Nidar, far from the prying eyes of Dúnadan and Gondorian spies. "The Song of Waves and Wind" it was named by its builders, and in number it would far exceed even the most grand of the Corsair fleets of history. The work continued for many years, but for reasons unknown to me Barkhûsh began his war without waiting for the Song to be ready; only now does it near completion.

'Let me forestall your objection, my friends! This Kindred exists to oppose the Church of Barkhûsh, and allies with none who worship that Dark Lord, though he be gone. But the Song of Waves and Wind is not of itself evil. It is a tool, a weapon to be used, and just because Barkhûsh set it down does not mean others might not pick it up and use it for their own defence, and for their own aims. This fleet could be a gift to Umbar, and to those who must now lead it through dangerous days.''She is gone, ${PLAYER}.

'With its leaders dispatched and the Narghâk weapons damaged, the Song of Waves and Wind has reached the end of its campaign against Gondor. Already the fighting turns against them.

'The battle will soon be over. Now the healing must begin.'Esh Mêkag, the Silent Mouth, grinds Men to dust year after year. Now, when we few have finally found the strength to escape, they threaten to execute the rest. This will not stand... not while I draw breath!You have travelled to the prison of Esh Mêkag with Ebuzâm.

You should talk to Ebuzâm.Talk to EbuzâmThe door deeper into the prison is locked and guarded.

You should talk to the Ordâkhai guard and convince him to let you pass.Talk to the Ordâkhai guardYou have made it past the first gate.

You should discreetly collect any Ordâkhai weapons you find.Collect Ordâkhai weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected enough weapons to arm the prisoners and stage a riot.

You should free and arm any imprisoned thralls you find.Arm imprisoned thralls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ebuzâm wants to enter the torture chamber to free anyone inside.

You should enter the torture chamber.Enter the torture chamberYou have found several prisoners being tortured in the torture chamber.

You should defeat the torturers and arm any imprisoned thralls you find.Defeat Esh Mêkag torturers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Arm imprisoned thralls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have cleared the torture chamber.

You should continue to the next cell block.Enter the next cell blockYou have cleared the torture chamber, but have yet to find Ratúlko the Bloody.

You should continue forward and arm any imprisoned thralls you find.Arm imprisoned thralls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})There is one chamber left.

You should enter the execution chamber.Enter the execution chamberRatúlko the Bloody is busy having a conversation with Góramul Sai.

You should quietly free and arm the prisoners in the execution chamber while they are talking.Break binding chains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Arm imprisoned thralls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ratúlko the Bloody is having a conversation with Góramul Sai.

You should listen to their conversation. What they say might be valuable information to Mizâdi's cause.Eavesdrop on the conversationRatúlko the Bloody has noticed you.

You should talk to Ratúlko the Bloody and try to convince him you are just a guard.Talk to Ratúlko the BloodyRatúlko the Bloody has discovered your true identity!

You should fight for your life!Survive Ratúlko's attack'We have done it! Ratúlko the Bloody has fled with his tail between his legs! Now these dogs of Ordâkh will pay!

'Let's get out of here for now and regroup at the ruins.''They still believe you are a guard. That should allow us to remain undetected. If anyone asks, you have captured me and are taking me to directly to Ratúlko for punishment.

'Once we're past the first gate, we need to find some weapons. We arm every prisoner we come across, and then we attack! This will only work if we can get everyone armed and ready quietly, and catch the Ordâkhai off-guard. Let's go.'You explain to the guard that you have captured Ebuzâm and are taking him to Ratúlko the Bloody personally. He smirks.

'Good! This one has been a thorn in our side for quite some time. Did you really think you could get away, Ebuzâm? I hope the warden finally puts you in the dirt where you belong.''You there, state your name! Wait. I know you....

'You are the one who attacked us outside Ahâba! Did that traitor Mizâdi send you here to kill me?'Together, you and Tatháta the Beast have determined to defeat the leadership of the Song of Waves and Wind and prevent the fleet from being used further against Gondor or anywhere else.Tatháta is beside the Heirsworn ship Phazanêg.Talk to Tatháta on the dockAphadaer has sought the protection of Balakhâd for the death of King Elessar.Confront Aphadaer and BalakhâdAphadaer claims he has taken the life of King Elessar. Tell him <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>, for the King will survive his wound.Tell them <rgb=#00FF00>no</rgb>, the King will liveRemain alert for any treachery on the part of the Heirsworn.Remain alert for any Heirsworn treacheryAphadaer has decided to prove his loyalty to Balakhâd and the Heirs of Castamir by facing you in battle.Prepare for battle and speak to AphadaerRemain on your guard against those who command the Song of Waves and Wind.Remain on your guard as you confront the leadership of the SongNakási Wave-reaper has accomplished her mission, and she stares at you with contentment.Prepare for battle and talk to Nakási Wave-reaperThe battle is over.Defeat Nakási Wave-reaper'The Heirsworn ship moored alongside the dock here is called Phazanêg, "The Last Heir."

'You must see that this name comes true, and put an end to he who rallies the Heirsworn! My business is with Nakási.''Always have I been loyal to the Heirs of Castamir, ${PLAYER}! I gave them whatever tidings I could of Elessar's plans, and the woman Ioreth proved a font of information! Indeed... it was most challenging to determine what news could be of use amidst all of her ramblings!

'I lost contact with Maethon shortly before the King departed for Outer Gondor, and received no further word from the other supporters of the Heirs; I had to decide what actions to take on my own. That stayed my hand for a time, but always I sought for some means of separating the King from his defenders while we ventured in Anfalas and Pinnath Gelin.

'But now that Balakhâd has assumed his rightful mantle, I can die knowing I have done what I could to support his rise! If I must die, then I will die for him! Praise the memory of Castamir, and all his heirs!''You cannot defeat me, ${PLAYER}, not even with Rothog and Tatháta by your side. My victory is already complete, for I have avenged Tumúldo and satisfied my quest. Gondor burns, as I knew it must. My enemies, all of my enemies, have suffered for the hurts they caused me. Now I am beyond all hurt.

'You have already lost, no matter the outcome of this battle.'Much depends upon your haste! You must reach Umbar Baharbêl!Race to Umbar Baharbêl before it is too late!Race westward along the road to Umbar BaharbêlRace to Umbar Baharbêl before it is too late!Race westward along the road to Umbar BaharbêlKhashig has called for you to stop and explain your haste.Warn Khashig of the approaching danger'Stop! What drives you toward Umbar Baharbêl with such reckless speed?

'${PLAYER}? Is that you?'Desperate for tidings from above, captives wrestle with their helplessness in the face of the evil that threatens Umbar and Gondor.Jajax rests on a cot by the entrance of the cage.Talk to JajaxIt is difficult to measure the passing of time in the cage.Pass the time in your cageIt is difficult to measure the passing of time in the cage.Listen to the words of your visitorJajax rests on a cot by the entrance of the cage.Talk to JajaxYour captor stands outside the cage for some purpose of her own.Listen to the words of your captorYour captor stands outside the cage for some purpose of her own.Talk to your captor through the bars of your cageIt is difficult to measure the passing of time in the cage.Pass the time in your cagePerhaps if you <rgb=#00FF00>beckon</rgb> the girl she will speak to you.<rgb=#00FF00>Beckon</rgb> the girl to speakThe girl eyes you warily.Wait for the girl to speakThe girl eyes you warily.Talk to the mysterious girlThe girl eyes you warily.Talk to the mysterious girlTephísa waits for your response.Give Tephísa your answerYou have given your answer, and must now wait to see her response.Wait to see what she will doThere is nothing more you can do but wait.See what Jajax thinks'You might as well settle down. We're not going anywhere, ${PLAYER}.'You tell Jajax that Hármelak is lying.

'Aye,' he agrees. 'She lied before, and she lies again.''It will not be as you say. The people of the city will know why I could not close the river gate. If the Song of Waves and Wind could not leave the River Ikorbân, Nakási would have turned the Narghâk cannons upon Umbar Baharbêl! Should we have sacrificed our own city for the sake of Gondor?'

You ask Hármelak if she truly believes that Nakási or Balakhâd would have destroyed their own city, and she waves a dismissive hand.

'You believe the people of the city share your uncertainty, ${PLAYER}.''I have a message for you from one of the Temámir. He says "The work continues. We need many hands to mine the Abâshal, and will forge new medallions from it. Remain alert for its shine, and stay safe: the mine is treacherous, but there will be a light in the darkness.'

The girl turns to go, but she hesitates. She faces you again, and you try to remember where you have before heard this voice.

'We watched as the ships passed the city. One galley tried to block the way to open water, and it was sunk. The terrible smoke of the cannons smelled foul. We saw Orcs on the deck of one of the ships. They cheered as the ship of Umbar burned; the water could not quench the blue flames.'You never saw her face before now, but it was in Umbar-môkh that you spoke to Tephísa. She is one of the Terâsi, the forgotten children who make their way through hidden paths beneath the city. It must have been the Temámir Birûk who gave her this message to bring to you and Jajax.

Tephísa studies your face closely.

'I watched the flames destroy my home once, stranger. They were orange and red then, the embers lit by servants of Barkhûsh, but a fire is a fire. Those ships will set ablaze the homes of Gondor, but they will return, and when they return the conflagration will spread to the homes of Umbar.

'I can help you escape, but I have a price.'Jajax sleeps on, oblivious to everything.You have infiltrated the city of Emax Dûl in the guise of a performer with Têrkar's Travellers.Ulishár stands with you in the back-stage chambers of the performance hall in Emax Dûl.Talk to Ulishár in the back-stage chambersSatagêra stands by the doorway leading to the stage.Talk to Satagêra by the rear entrance to the stageSatagêra has told you to wait for your moment to run onto the stage.Wait for your cue to arrive, and then run up the stairs on the right sideYour big moment has arrived! Run up the stairs on the right side of the stage and stand by the door to the west hallway.Run up the stairs and deliver your lineNow you must wait for your second cue. Once Mashkânu says 'Well?' you must faint... but not before!Wait for your next cue<rgb=#00FF00>Faint</rgb> at the sight of the impressive Mûmak.<rgb=#00FF00>Faint</rgb> at the sight of the impressive MûmakNow is your chance! Slip inside the hallway while the audience is distracted.Slip inside the west hallway while the audience is distractedUlishár has joined you in the hallway west of the stage, in the belly of Emax Dûl.Talk to Ulishár in the hallway west of the stageThe papers in the Lord's Study may provide the information you seek. Search them and learn what you can!Read the papers in the Lord's StudyThe papers in the Lord's Study may provide the information you seek. Search them and learn what you can!Read more of the papers in the Lord's StudyUlishár has found an unsent letter in the Lord's Study.Listen to Ulishár read the unsent letter he has foundUlishár wishes to speak with you in the Lord's Study.Talk to Ulishár in the Lord's StudyThe play is almost over, and you should join the other performers on the stage.Join the other performers on the stage as the play comes to an endTake your <rgb=#00FF00>bow</rgb> with the other performers.You learned what you came for, and should now return to the rooms backstage to wait for the rest of Têrkar's Travellers.Return to the rooms backstage and wait for the rest of Têrkar's Travellers'The first part of our mission has gone smoothly, ${PLAYER}: we have infiltrated the very belly of Emax Dûl without raising the suspicion of the lords and ladies of the keep. So far they seem entertained by Satagêra's words and the performances of Asharmûl, Zimêlkha, and Mashkânu... to say nothing of Jêsamin, who always obtains the most laughter and the greatest applause!

'But our role in the performance approaches. Let us join Satagêra by the door to the stage, and await our cue.''The lords and ladies of Emax Dûl seem enraptured by the play to this point... let us hope that continues!

'Remember, ${PLAYER}. Mashkânu will say "Some heroes of Gondor still remain," and then Asharmûl will ask "Who?" At that moment you are to run up the stairs directly opposite us and stand by the entrance to the hallway. I will tell you the precise moment when it happens.

'Then, you will wait until the mûmak makes its appearance, and when Mashkânu asks you "Well?" you are to dramatically faint. Afterwards, while the audience is distracted, you and Ulishár will slip into the hallway and search the Lord's Study for the information Inkanûsh desires.''We have made it, and I believe the audience suspects nothing!

'Follow me, ${PLAYER}. Let us keep our voices down as we make for the Lord's Study.''I have had my attendants gather the notes we possess about the Song of Waves and Wind and I am studying them for good news. I need something with which I can prove my worth to the frightful ones who came from Damudûr. My mind is my own... for now... for now. If the fleet being built at Starkhaven in Sûg Nidar can restore Ordâkh to glory, Thothril may see my value.

'I will write more later. I will double my efforts, and study once more the record of the Song's construction. -GS''Khóbagach was in poetic mood when he named Barkhûsh's fleet "The Song of Waves and Wind," believing it would be the greatest accomplishment he would oversee as Hûl. The wide, dark mere was new and appeared on no map, overlooked only by the skeletal gaze of the ruins of Kasukhín, and it was large enough to hold a vast number of warships. The River Ikorbân remained navigable all the way to the sea, and with sharp-eyed archers and spearmen stationed upon the bounds, the lake and its accompanying shipyard could remain a secret for as long as it proved necessary.

'Nisigím lay nearby, but its trees were blighted and it rapidly became a ghost-forest; few of its timbers were suitable for firewood, let alone for shipbuilding. Timbers for the fleet and stone for the ship-yard and its wharves had to be carted by mûmakil from the Mûr. Waggons departed from Khanâg Valoyar and elsewhere every few days, the Temámir accepting payments of silver and gold and asking few questions.

'Khóbagach Hûl died of the gout long before the Song was completed, but Mordor and Ordâkh worked together to finish the weapon that could destroy their shared enemy. The arrival of the Song of Waves and Wind on the shores of Gondor would signal the beginning of the war, but for some unknown reason Barkhûsh launched the attack before the fleet was ready. It stood idle at Sûg Nidar, the Fearwater, for the duration of the war. It stands there still, even as a new king rules in Gondor and all believe Ordâkh to be defeated. - Prepared for Góramul Sai by Laghíl of Emax Dûl, Scribe of Ordâkh''We have learned something of great import, ${PLAYER}: a secret fleet of warships has been in construction for many years at the head of the River Ikorbân, and even now it nears completion! This must be enough for Inkanûsh; we have been away for too long!'Our pursuit of Bârshud has led us to Idagâl, a scorched land of scavengers and cruelty. Here we will stand defiant and push the empire of Ordâkh out of the region for good. But first, we need allies.Mizâdi is ready to meet with her allies and plan her strategy for Idagâl.

You should speak to Mizâdi to begin the meeting.Talk to MizâdiMizâdi is speaking with her advisors about the situation in Idagâl.

You should listen to the conversation.Listen to the conversation'That is the plan. We gather more allies... and then we strike.''Good. We are convened. Let us learn the weaknesses of our enemies.'Together with Belondor and Rothog, you and Jajax are determined to destroy the Narghâk weapons on two of the ships of the Song.You have come with Jajax, Rothog, and Belondor to destroy the Narghâk weapons used by the Song.Talk to Jajax on the dockIf you tamper with the Narghâk weapons aboard the Ordâkhai ship Kosagháti, you should be able to prevent their further use.You have successfully disabled the Narghâk weapons aboard the Ordâkhai ship Kosagháti.Stand by Jajax and decide your next courseSomething has happened to the Orc-ship Grishúlvosh. Jajax demands your attention.Talk to Jajax on the KosaghátiRothog grieves beside his fallen comrade.Talk to Rothog beside the burning wreck of the Orc-ship Grishúlvosh'I have overheard the speech of our enemies, ${PLAYER}, and learned the names of their ships. The Ordâkhai ship Kosagháti is moored nearby. The Orc-ship Grishúlvosh lies at the end of this dock.

'You need not commit those names to your memory, for they will not long matter! We will teach their captains the lesson of the flames: that he who sets a fire may be the one who burns!''That explosion came from the direction of Grishúlvosh!''I was too late, ${PLAYER}... too late to save him.'

Rothog looks up from his fallen comrade, the half-troll's own body singed and crackling in the heat.

'I battled the captain of this ship in combat while Belondor went to disable the Narghâk weapons. Something went wrong... the Hungry Fire...

'The Orcs knew our purpose here, and set a trap for us. They damaged the mechanism of the Narghâk weapons, and when Belondor...'

Rothog bares his fangs at you.

'After the explosion, I ran into the flames and carried Belondor out of the inferno... but it was too late. He completed his mission, but he has left us.'The haste of your errand permits no delay: the Kindred of the Coins must be warned of the approaching danger!Jajax has come with you to Dâr Laja to warn the Kindred of the Coins about the approaching danger.Talk to Jajax in Dâr LajaHármelak stands upon the dais in Dâr Laja.Talk to Hármelak in Dâr LajaHármelak stares at you in disbelief, waiting for you to answer her question with a <rgb=#00FF00>yes</rgb>.Assure Hármelak that <rgb=#00FF00>yes</rgb>, you have seen itOnly the Kindred of the Coins can command the river gate be closed. You and Jajax must convince Hármelak to issue the order.Convince Hármelak that the river gate must be closedYou and Jajax stand alone against the guardsmen in Dâr Laja.Talk to Jajax in Dâr LajaKhôltekh has stepped through the line of Temámir archers to address you.Talk to Khôltekh in Dâr LajaYou and Jajax have done what you could. Now it must be up to others.Talk to Jajax in Dâr Laja'If by our warning we save the city, the Kindred will surely seek to reward us for our actions today, ${PLAYER}. Let us hurry!''A hostile fleet approaches? My business with the Kindred can wait!

'There is coin to be made, ${PLAYER}!''${PLAYER}! I have not seen you since your steps brought you to Umbar-môkh. I have come aboveground to ask Khôltekh... but my errand can wait. Something troubles you?'

You quickly tell Birûk that Nakási Wave-reaper sails a hostile fleet toward the city, and the banks of the Ikorbân River are not safe.

'I will delay you no longer! Tell the Kindred of the Coins what you have told me!''Your face is lined with worry, ${PLAYER}. What brings you with such urgency to Dâr Laja?'

You tell Hármelak that Nakási Wave-reaper sails a secret fleet armed with Narghâk cannons and crewed by Orcs of Mordor and soldiers of Ordâkh down the Ikorbân River. She frowns uncertainly.'So it is a fight, then. Fine! There are not enough of them to best both Jajax and ${PLAYER}!''You know there is little to be gained by dying here, ${PLAYER}.'

Khôltekh lowers his voice so only you can hear him.

'Hármelak might have pretended she first heard the name "The Song of Waves and Wind" from you, when you visited her in her manor, but she is not as clever as she thinks herself to be. Wealth cannot buy wisdom; only experience can do that.

'When Azagath told us of the Song's existence, neither of us believed in it. If the Dark Lord of Mordor could not rely upon such a fleet, of what use could it be to us? But it seems Nakási has done the impossible. The Narghâk I sent her from Ashâgir will prove the difference, I think.

'When Gondor burns, the folk of Umbar Baharbêl will rejoice.''Looks like this is it, ${PLAYER}.

'We have to put our faith in Daxamat now.'Tidings from the city outside are cut off from the prisoners in the Fleetfast gaol. What is happening in Umbar Baharbêl?Jajax is in one of the cages of the Fleetfast gaol.Talk to JajaxThere is a commotion outside the cage in the Fleetfast gaol.Remain alertBelondor and Rothog have come to free you from the Fleetfast gaol.Talk to Belondor in the Fleetfast gaolJajax is in the Fleetfast gaol.Talk to JajaxJajax has suggested that you search the bodies of the slain guards to see if either of them have the keys to the gaol.Search the bodies of the slain guards for the keys to the gaolJajax has suggested that you search the bodies of the slain guards to see if either of them have the keys to the gaol.Search the bodies of the slain guards for the keys to the gaolBelondor and Rothog entered the gaol from a hatch downstairs that leads to Umbar-môkh. Now you should find your way downstairs to escape!Make your way downstairs to the hatch leading to Umbar-môkhTatháta stands by the hatch leading to Umbar-môkh.Talk to Tatháta in the Fleetfast gaolBelondor stands by the hatch leading to Umbar-môkh.Talk to Belondor in the Fleetfast gaolTatháta stands by the hatch leading to Umbar-môkh.Talk to Tatháta in the Fleetfast gaolThe path of your escape leads into Umbar-môkh.Descend into Umbar-môkhYou and Jajax have escaped from the gaol, but there are foes between you and the hidden harbour.Talk to Jajax in Umbar-môkhYour foes now defeated, the way to the hidden harbour is open to you.Make your way to the hidden harbourYou should board Tatháta's ship so you may pursue the Song.Board Tatháta's ship and go belowdecksYour allies stand ready to pursue the Song.Talk to Jajax in the ship SotókaTalk to Belondor in the ship SotókaTalk to Rothog in the ship SotókaYour allies stand ready to pursue the Song.Talk to Tatháta in her ship SotókaYour pursuit of the Song begins.Pursue the Song to Gondor'I wonder if Gondor has already been defeated, ${PLAYER}? It is difficult to tell the passage of time from down here, but if the weapons of the Song are as dangerous as you say, it will not take long for Nakási to complete her mission.''It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}, but we have not the time to catch up! Rothog and I will stay and guard the rear while you and Jajax make your escape; the way out is downstairs.

'Daxamat leads the rebellion against Hármelak and Khôltekh. With every passing moment, more and more of the people join Ilma-ghôli, the rising tide.

'I am sorry this has happened, my friend. I thought the sickness in the Kindred ended with Azagath, but it was not so. Hármelak and Khôltekh have betrayed the city, and I must make it right.''Did he say DAXAMAT leads the uprising against the Kindred? My brother Daxamat? There has not been some misunderstanding? My brother is one who follows, not one who leads! I am the one who leads!

'I know I said we should put our faith in Dax, ${PLAYER}, but I did not expect something like this! We had better go. I have to see it before I will believe it!''The Kindred of the Coins is dead, ${PLAYER}. It was created to protect the people of the city, not to burn them alive as did the Church of Barkhûsh. If the Umbari do not slay Hármelak and Khôltekh for their betrayal, I will do it myself.

'Below the city I witnessed Belondor and Rothog travelling with great speed, and pursued them. Had they supported Hármelak's treachery they would be dead already, but it seems these two have not abandoned their wits.

'We are to bring you by paths beneath the city to the hideout where the uprising began. Are you ready?'

You hesitate. Images of thatched Gondorian cottages wreathed by blue flame flash before your eyes, followed by homes in the Umbari style suffering the same fate. You remember a small voice asking you to destroy the ships and their masters.'What is the cause for this delay, ${PLAYER}? The city above is a tinder-box ready to catch fire at the slightest spark, and Ilma-ghôli cannot now be stopped.'

You tell Belondor that you fear for the people of Gondor, unaware of the deadly danger that sails toward them, and for the people of Umbar. He nods.

'It had occurred to me that Nakási will not give up this fleet when her business in Gondor is completed,' he replies.

'She will return with it to Umbar Baharbêl, and any passing whim will be enforced by cannon and with Hungry Fire.''My ship Sotóka is moored in a hidden harbour not far from here, ${PLAYER}, and none can match her speed when her sails are full.'

You ask Tatháta if she would be willing to pursue the Song of Waves and Wind to Gondor, despite the danger, and she stares at you seriously.

'On my last voyage with Nakási, we sailed around the coast of Outer Gondor. Our purpose was to prove to the new King of Gondor that despite the defeat of Umbar in the war, the Kindred of the Coins was not without strength. Umbar would not be subservient; Umbar must be treated as a powerful neighbour, worthy of respect.

'But then Tumúldo was slain, and the light in Nakási's eyes changed. Hatred drove her. We encountered the grove of a tree-tender on the cape of Anfalas. Later I learned from Nestinanessornë that his name, at least in the tongue used by Elves and Men, was Leafshade. Nakási threatened to burn his grove as a message to Gondor, and I told her I wanted no part of it... but had Nestinanessornë not surrendered to her I know she would have burned that grove with fire and torches, and all of Gondor beside.

'Now she possesses the ability to do just that, ${PLAYER}. If my ship Sotóka can stop her, I cannot remain idly by and claim to have not aided her. For Leafshade, if not for any others, my ship is yours. Agents of Khôltekh and the Heirsworn stand between you and the hidden harbour. I hope you are ready.''The hidden harbour is just ahead. We must cut through these foes if we are to reach Tatháta's ship!''Ah, this is more like it. I have always been more at home aboard a ship, even if that ship carries me to dangerous battle in defence of Gondor, of all places! At least the legend of Jajax will continue to grow!

'We will leave the uprising against Hármelak and Khôltekh in Daxamat's capable hands. Ha! Capable? There is a first time for everything, I suppose.

'I hope we are not making a grave mistake, ${PLAYER}!''Sirgon has been upon my mind these last few hours, ${PLAYER}. What would he say to know that now I sail to his home of Gondor in a desperate bid to defend it from destruction?

'Ah, I know the answer. He would smile and clap me upon the back, and say he would do the same for my own home. What do Gondor and Umbar have in common? Sons and daughters who would die for them, against any threatening danger.''I am sad, ${PLAYER}.'

You ask Rothog why he is sad, and he grumbles something you cannot hear. When you ask him to repeat it, he heaves a heavy sigh.

'I did not think to bring Húrshauk with me when we came to rescue you from the gaol, and Tatháta says there is no time for me to go get him. Now he must stay behind in the city instead of joining the battle in Gondor.

'He will miss all of the fighting! Perhaps one of the members of Ilma-ghôli will bring him to Dâr Laja to slay Hármelak or Khôltekh? He would like that. Oh, I hope they do!''Sotóka is a fast ship, but the Song departed many hours before us. We may be too late to prevent Nakási from completing her mission.

'She is driven by vengeance, ${PLAYER}: not just for the death of Tumúldo, but for every injury and injustice she has suffered during her years of life. Each of these wounds has fed her hatred, and now she has been blinded by her desire for vengeance.'

Tatháta smiles grimly, a most rare sight indeed.

'That is the meaning of "Sotóka," ${PLAYER}: Vengeance. Is it chance or plan that speeds us in pursuit of Nakási aboard a ship of vengeance? I cannot say. The world is a curious place.'Arâniz believes the only way to rescue the captured soldiers is to convince the escaped thralls to help you infiltrate Esh Mêkag.Arâniz believes you will need the escaped thralls' help to get into Esh Mêkag.

You should talk to Ishûri and mention the name 'Ebuzâm'.Talk to IshûriIshûri has agreed to show you the secret way into Esh Mêkag.

You should talk to Ishûri when you are ready to enter Esh Mêkag.Talk to Ishûri to enter Esh MêkagYou have entered Esh Mêkag via the escapees' secret route.

You should talk to Ishûri in Esh Mêkag.

If you need to re-enter Esh Mêkag, talk to Ishûri in Dur Nâgu.Talk to IshûriYou should find Ebuzâm somewhere in the Esh Mêkag pit-mine.

If you need to re-enter Esh Mêkag, talk to Ishûri in Dur Nâgu.Find EbuzâmYou must help some prisoners escape Esh Mêkag before Ebuzâm will leave.

You should rescue Ebuzâm's children, Enûtu and Shakûl, as well as the Aradûni soldiers and the kidnapped Beltáni.

If you need to re-enter Esh Mêkag, talk to Ishûri in Dur Nâgu.Free EnûtuFree ShakûlFree the kidnapped BeltániFree the captive AradûniYou have rescued who you can.

You should return to Dur Nâgu using the secret tunnel.Use the tunnel to return to Dur NâguYou have successfully rescued many prisoners from Esh Mêkag.

You should report your success to Arâniz in Dur Nâgu.Talk to Arâniz'The situation here is desperate. My men and many others are trapped inside, subject to unspeakable horrors. They force whoever they can capture to work, and those that will not work are tortured inside the keep until they will. I hear the prison's warden, Ratúlko the Bloody, is particularly sadistic in his approach....

'The only path forward that I can see is careful infiltration. The escaped thralls must know of a secret way inside, but they are reluctant to tell me. They believe anyone who makes it inside will surely be caught and killed, or worse.

'I have heard them mention someone called Ebuzâm with great respect. I think he helped them escape and is still inside. Talk to Ishûri, and see if you can convince her that if we can get you inside, you can help get their friend out.'You ask Ishûri if she will show you the secret way into Esh Mêkag to rescue those inside. She recoils in horror.

'You want to go INSIDE? No! No, you must not! Only a few of us have ever made it out alive... and those left behind are punished! They will torture you to death if they catch you! I can't in good conscience let you go in there!'

You say you can rescue Ebuzâm if she shows you the way inside. She seems shocked that you know the name.

'Ebuzâm? I... we owe him our lives. If you say you will free him, I must trust that you will.''I will show you the way. Please, you must find Ebuzâm!''I will show you the way. Please, you must find Ebuzâm!''This is the pit-mine inside Esh Mêkag. This section is usually less-guarded than the others, but... something is wrong. There are fewer guards and working thralls than I would have expected at this time of day....

'Here, keep this on. This Ordâkhai uniform allowed my escape. It should allow you to walk around unbothered. Find Ebuzâm, but don't draw too much attention! He will know what to do.''I will show you the way. Please, you must find Ebuzâm!''You... you are not one of the Ordâkhai. What is the meaning of this?'

He appears to have been badly beaten, and left tied up in the muck as a form of punishment. You explain that you are here with Ishûri to rescue who you can from the prison.

'Ishûri? She came back? That fool girl. If you say you are here to help, I will take your word for it, as I have little to lose. They plan on executing me tomorrow, either way. But I will not leave without my children. There are also two groups of newcomers that you should free, before the Ordâkhai can torture them to death.

'Find them. I will wait with Ishûri.''I will show you the way. Please, you must find Ebuzâm!''Quickly, Ebuzâm needs medical attention. The others have gone ahead. Go through the tunnel, and we will return to our camp in the ruins.''You have done it! I thought I would never see them again... not alive....

'Ishûri told me there were many prisoners missing from the mine. I fear the worst for them. Ebuzâm should know more. He will want to speak to you.'The soldiers at the Dawn-warden are being harried by an unseen force.You will need Hidâti's help to banish Ishími, the Anguished Wind.

You should talk to Hidâti.Talk to HidâtiHidâti has a plan to banish Ishími, the Anguished Wind from the Dawn-warden.

You should place Kâparai wards and heal the spirits of frightened Aradûni with Hidâti.Place Kâparai wards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Heal frightened Aradûni (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ishími has become enraged by your attempts to banish it.

You should talk to Hidâti.Talk to HidâtiIshími has begun manifesting near the statue of Izighûz Menûndari.

You should find the cyclone of wind near the statue.Find the cyclone of windYou must defeat the coalesced form of Ishími, the Anguished Wind to banish it from the Dawn-warden!

You must place the final Kâparai ward near the cyclone to confront Ishími.Banish Ishími, the Anguished Wind(Optional) Place the final Kâparai wardIshími has successfully been banished.

You should talk to Hidâti.Talk to HidâtiIshími has successfully been banished.

You should talk to Captain Hanâbu.Talk to Captain Hanâbu'I am Captain Hanâbu of the Aradûni, the Servants. Like Hamât Renewed, we have risen to reclaim our ancestral lands from Ordâkh. What was once Nísaka will be Aradûn, by will of our leader, Damakhêra Ardu.

'I have led this group of soldiers ahead to scout Idagâl, in preparation for our larger force to arrive. We mean to make war on the Ordâkhai, starting with their fortress at Emax Dûl. I thought it fitting to make our first camp under the Dawn-warden, the hero-king Izighûz Menûndari himself, but perhaps he does not look favourably upon us!

'Something haunts this place: a foul, torturing wind. It keeps us from Emax Dûl! We cannot even think straight, let alone plan our invasion!''It is good I came with you. I will banish Ishími from this place, and you will assist me.

'Take these wards. We will place them around the camp, and tend to the Aradûni's broken spirits. This will enrage Ishími, and he will manifest to stop us. We will be ready.''It is as I thought. Ishími is enraged by our attempts to banish it. Look, it manifests on the ridge near the statue of Izighûz Menûndari! It gathers for a final attack! Ready yourself!

'We must place a ward near that whirlwind, forcing it to coalesce itself into something we can fight.''It is done. Ishími is banished, and should no longer trouble the Aradûni.

'You must understand, however, that it is not banished for good, it has just been forced to move. I may be the elder Kâparai, but even I am not powerful enough to permanently banish a spirit of such malevolence. I fear Ishími may haunt Shagâna forever, lest we discover what it really is, and what unleashed it.''The howling wind had abated! You have truly done it! You have truly proven yourself friends of the Aradûni.

'I will speak with Mizâdi on behalf of Damakhêra Ardu. I believe an alliance would benefit both Hamât and Aradûn. Together, we will attack Emax Dûl and push the Ordâkhai from these lands!'The ancient Tombs of Khâb Ishil have been despoiled by kergrim and need to be cleared out.Tombs of Khâb Ishil have been overrun with kergrim and need to be cleared out.

You should defeat the kergrim and their leader, Lamâmut, the Corpse-chewer, at the Tombs of Khâb Ishil.Defeat kergrim at the Tombs of Khâb Ishil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Lamâmut, the Corpse-chewerYou have cleared the kergrim from the Tombs of Khâb Ishil.

You should return to Malêrti at the Dawn-warden.Talk to Malêrti'If you are ready to face some danger, ${CLASS}, I have a job for you.

'Nearby, the Tombs of Khâb Ishil house the remains of the honoured heroes of ancient Nísaka. The tombs are considered sacred to our people and were sealed long go. In recent times, it seems they have begun to collapse, likely caused by the Din of Stone. One of our scouts looked inside after we arrived and found the area overrun with kergrim. They despoil the dead and dishonour our heritage. Please, do what you can to clear them out!''Have you defeated the kergrim? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. You have done both the Aradûni and the spirits of our ancient heroes a great service.'The robbers in Kidu-bâla have stolen many valuables from the Beltáni and other travellers. They should be reclaimed and returned to their rightful owners.Kûrmi has asked you to retrieve the items stolen from the Beltáni.

You should travel to the robber camp, Kidu-bâla, and retrieve the stolen valuables.Collect stolen valuables (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have reclaimed many items stolen by the robbers.

You should return to Kûrmi in Ahâba with the items.Talk to Kûrmi'If you are here to help, stranger, we could surely use it.

'There is a camp of robbers in the cliffs to the north called Kidu-bâla. They have stolen much from the Beltáni, and anyone travelling alone along the Great Road. If you go to Kidu-bâla, please retrieve our valuables, and return them to Ahâba.''Thank you, ${PLAYER}. I will ensure these items are all returned to their true owners.

'Perhaps you really are a friend to the Beltáni.'Râsabur will not return to his station at the Dawn-warden until the drakes at Ushumût are culled.The wild-drakes nest at Ushumût, the ancient bones of dragons. The drakes present a danger to everyone nearby.

You should defeat drakes and destroy wild-drake eggs at Ushumût.Defeat drakes in Ushumût (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy wild-drake eggs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have done much to clear the drakes from Ushumût.

You should return to Râsabur.Talk to Râsabur'You there! Come closer, quickly, before they fly down and snatch you!

'I am Râsabur, soldier of Aradûn. I became separated from the rest of my unit when we were attacked by these wild-drakes. I saw them carry many of us away, but some escaped, I am sure! I am afraid if I try to make a run for it, I too will be taken, fed to their hungry young or worse! Will you help me cull this nest, before more Aradûni are preyed upon?

'I will... stay here... for now.... Thank you....''I saw you defeat those drakes from here! You truly are an inspiration, ${CLASS}. 

'There is only one thing left to do, and because of you, I have worked up the courage to attempt it....'Batâla has asked for you help gathering fruit from the plants in Ahâba.Batâla has asked you to gather fruit from the trees and bushes in Ahâba.

You should collect dates, mulberries, and citrus fruits around the oasis.Collect Ahâba dates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect oasis mulberries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect citrus fruits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected fruit from the plants near the oasis.

You should return to Batâla.Talk to Batâla'Greetings, ${CLASS}. I am Batâla. I handle much of the cooking for the village. Unusâli has asked you to help out around Ahâba, and I am not one to turn away idle hands.

'Look around, friend. Our oasis provides for us. Gather fruit from the trees and bushes, and bring it to me.'You show Batâla the fruits you have collected.

'Good, this is enough for the next meal. Now, I have one more task for you.'Orcs who dwell at Drushkála have been invited to join the crew of a ship named Grishúlvosh, but first they must slay the existing crew.Zaumoz the Black Wind, captain of the ship Grishúlvosh, has invited Orcs of Drushkála to join his crew.Examine the parchments strewn upon the barrel near the entrance of DrushkálaYou should search for slain Orcs in Drushkála to see what you can learn of the Grishúlvosh's crew.The Grishúlvosh must now have at least four new crew members.CompletedParchments left atop a barrel within the encampment of Drushkála draw your attention:

"Hear now the words of ZAUMOZ THE BLACK WIND!

'I desire only the very best warriors to crew my ship Grishúlvosh. Do you believe you can stand with ZAUMOZ?

'Many of my crew live and work here in Drushkála. Free up your own spot on my deck by killing these weaklings. Only the strongest deserve to sail with me!'"It would appear that at least four new Orcs have joined the crew of the Grishúlvosh, and these are perhaps more bloodthirsty than the sailors they replaced.

You quietly give thanks that your own crew of the Wave-hunter was not selected in this Orc-fashion. You also wonder how Zaumoz the Black Wind can retain his own position as captain in such an environment.Brigands have set up camp among the cliffs north of Ahâba, called Kidu-bâla. They should be dealt with before more harm can come to the Beltáni people.Brigands make camp in Kidu-bâla, north of Ahâba.

You should defeat the brigands and their leader, Nagísu the Keen-eyed, in Kidu-bâla.Defeat brigands in Kidu-bâla (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Nagísu the Keen-eyedYou have defeated the brigands and their leader in Kidu-bâla.

You should return to Kûrmi in Ahâba.Talk to Kûrmi'To the north, robbers and brigands are holed up in the cliff-side, in a camp we call Kidu-bâla. They have long been a thorn in our side here in Ahâba, attacking any who venture too far from the oasis alone. Recently, their numbers have swelled with Ordâkhai deserters, making them even more dangerous.

'If you truly want to help the Beltáni, you will rid us of those brigands, and their leader, the one called Nagísu, once and for all.''You have defeated the robbers? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Our hunters and shepherds will be relieved to know there is one fewer enemy lurking in the shadows.'To make contact with the Aradûni, you and Mizâdi's envoys must travel west, and cross the perilous dry lake-bed.Unusâli and Sorkamâl will be travelling to the Dawn-warden with you to meet with the Aradûni.

You should talk to Unusâli.Talk to UnusâliUnusâli, Sorkamâl, and Hidâti have gone ahead.

You should meet them near Ushumût, the Grave of Serpents.Find Unusâli, Sorkamâl, and HidâtiYou are being attacked by fell mirages, seemingly caused by Ishími, the Anguished Wind.

You should defeat the mirages!Defeat the miragesUnusâli, Sorkamâl, and Hidâti have gone ahead to the Dawn-warden.

You should continue west and find the Dawn-warden.Continue to the Dawn-wardenIt seems that Ishími, the Anguished Wind haunts the Dawn-warden.

You should find the Aradûni officer in charge of the camp.Talk to Captain Hanâbu'We have secured Ahâba and the aid of the Beltáni, but now an even greater diplomatic challenge must be tackled. To the west, the soldiers of Aradûn gather. It is time for my new envoy to prove her worth!

'Unusâli has volunteered to travel with you and Sorkamâl and provide an introduction with the Aradûni stationed at the Dawn-warden. I trust her to keep you safe while you cross the scorched lake-bed. Numûru and I will stay here and organize our soldiers as they arrive.''I have met with the Aradûni before. It only makes sense that I go with you. They are yet another people who seek justice against Ordâkh. I trust my people will be good hosts to Mizâdi and her soldiers while I am gone.

'To quickly reach the Aradûni at the Dawn-warden while avoiding the Ordâkhai, we must cross the dry lake-bed. It is a treacherous journey, full of venomous reptiles, wild drakes, not to mention the oppressive heat. In recent months, it has become even more dangerous. There is something... unnatural out there, harrying any who cross. Because of this, we must also travel with Hidâti, our elder Kâparai mystic. She will keep us safe.

'The three of us will go ahead and meet you out there. Look for the dragon bones.''There you are, ${PLAYER}! Unusâli says we are about half-way through our journey. It cannot end soon enough, I say! I did not anticipate tromping through dangerous drake-infested wasteland when I volunteered to serve as Mizâdi's diplomat....

'Wait... do you hear that? Is that the... wind?''There you are, ${PLAYER}! Unusâli says we are about half-way through our journey. It cannot end soon enough, I say! I did not anticipate tromping through dangerous drake-infested wasteland when I volunteered to serve as Mizâdi's diplomat....

'Wait... do you hear that? Is that the... wind?''I was not expecting visitors... but you do not look like Ordâkhai. Who are you, stranger?'

You explain that you and your fellows are envoys representing Shâra Mizâdi and Renewed Hamât.

'You are with Shâra Mizâdi? Word of her valour has reached us even in Aradûn! Please, make yourself at home in our camp! Though, even we do not find it comfortable. Not with that accursed howling wind!'The Ordâkhai have taken over the town of Okhatohól, or Witcher-watch, and now use it as a base of operations to launch raids on Ahâba.The Ordâkhai have taken over the town of Wither-watch and now use it as a base of operations.

You should defeat the Ordâkhai and their leader, Ulóngha Bóro, in Wither-watch.Defeat Ordâkhai in Wither-watch (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ulóngha BóroYou have defeated the Ordâkhai at Wither-watch.

You should return to Ahâba and talk to Kûrmi.Talk to Kûrmi'The Ordâkhai recently took over the town of Okhatohól, the Wither-watch. We know not what happened to those living there, but we suspect they were taken to Esh Mêkag. They now use the town as a base to launch their raids on Ahâba.

'If the Ordâkhai are your enemy, as you say, I ask you to defeat them and their leader, before they raid us yet again!''You have defeated the Ordâkhai at Okhatohól? Good. I celebrate the defeat of our mutual enemy!'The morale of the allied soldiers fighting in the streets of Emax Dûl needs improvement.Allied soldiers are still fighting at the four footholds of control in the city.

You should find and use 'Aradûni Battle-horn' on allied soldiers in Emax Dûl to lift their spirits.Use 'Aradûni Battle-horn' on allied soldiers in Emax Dûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect Aradûni Battle-hornYou have rallied the soldiers still fighting in Emax Dûl.

You should return to Hanâbu in Nashûbu.Talk to Hanâbu'Our soldiers are still up there fighting bravely in the streets. There must be something we can do to lift their spirits!

'Find my Aradûni above, and use their war-horns to rally our soldiers. They all look upon you with respect, ${PLAYER}, and their spirits will be lifted by your leadership!''You have returned! Did the sound of the battle-horn lift their spirits? There is nothing special about the horns themselves, you know. What was special was the person sounding it: you!'You have learned that Ghómbok Bóro, a commander of Ordâkh, possesses a dangerous authority.Parchments spread upon a table outside the central keep of Starkhaven describe the dangerous authority of Ghómbok Bóro.Examine the parchments outside the central keep of StarkhavenYou should find the Weirway Gate behind the central keep of Starkhaven and <rgb=#00FF00>appraise</rgb> the danger if it is opened.You have appraised the danger posed by the opening of the Weirway Gate, and found it to be substantial.CompletedThe man possessing Ghómbok Bóro's command lives to the south-east of the Weirway Gate, not far from the courtyard displaying an impressive lion statue.The command to open the Weirway Gate is too dangerous. You should burn it in a nearby brazier.You have saved the residents of Adagím from Ghómbok Bóro's command... at least for now.CompletedParchments spread upon a table outside the central keep of Starkhaven paint a disturbing picture:

"You tell Khâtiph I am not one to be intimidated. I know the one he follows is just one man, and Heirs of Castamir have been slain before; who is to say the son of Balakhôr could escape that fate? If they think to oppose me, remind them of this: I possess the authority to open the Weirway Gate.

'You may be too young to remember the last time it was opened. Count yourself fortunate! It stands behind the central keep of Starkhaven, and is accessed by a wooden walkway. The Weirway Gate holds back the flood, and when it is opened it allows water from Sûg Nidar to spill through the channel, flooding all of forested Adagím to the south. My predecessor used it to control the water level of the lake when the season of the rains seemed to have no end.

'If they move against me, I will open the gate. I have already given the command to one of my trusted men who lives by the plaza of the lion. If anything happens to me he will deliver the parchment with that command, and the Weirway Gate will open. None will shut it ever again, and Sûg Nidar will move to the south, leaving their ships stranded and the Kintai forest underwater!

'Know these are the words of Ghómbok Bóro, and he means every one!'Judging from the location of the Weirway Gate, you determine that the words of Ghómbok Bóro are no bluff: Adagím lies to the south, and if the gate is opened the waters of Sûg Nidar will flow through the channel into the forest in a dangerous torrent. It seems clear to you that it was the previous opening of the Weirway Gate that caused so much of Adagím to become the treacherous swamp-land it is today.

Ghómbok Bóro entrusted a parchment containing the command to open the Weirway Gate to a trusted man living at "the plaza of the lion." He must live somewhere nearby, perhaps to the south-east. It is time to knock on some doors!You have saved the residents of Adagím from the devastation that could have been caused by the opening of the Weirway Gate, at least for now. You will need to find some way to oppose the Song without endangering the peaceful Kintai of Sul Madásh, or any others who live in the lands through which Sûg Nidar would flood at Ghómbok Bóro's command.Heirsworn Corsairs loyal to Balakhâd dwell at the Haven of Bâkhridar, eager to sail to war.Standing by the entrance to the Haven of Bâkhridar, you consider what can be done to oppose the threat of those who dwell here.Examine the banner by the entrance to the Haven of BâkhridarYou should explore the various corners of the Haven of Bâkhridar and learn the mood of those who dwell here.Explore the Heirsworn tents in the north-west corner of the HavenExplore the Heirsworn tents in the south-west corner of the HavenExplore the Heirsworn tents on the central rise of the HavenThe longer the Heirsworn Corsairs remain at the Haven of Bâkhridar, the more their complaints grow.CompletedStanding by the entrance to the Haven of Bâkhridar, you consider what can be done to oppose the threat of those who dwell here. You should explore the Corsair encampment and stay alert for anything you can learn of their plans.It is clear to you that the alliance of your foes assembled in Sûg Nidar is not without its weaknesses: the Heirsworn and the Orcs dislike working so closely with each other, and trust between each group is lacking. If you can make use of these rifts you might benefit from it.Mizâdi Shâra-ingari has come to Idagâl with a small force, seeking to confront her rival, Bârshud, and to find a way to push the Ordâkhai from their stronghold in Mûr Ghala.Mizâdi is ready to meet with her allies and plan her strategy for Idagâl.

You should speak to Mizâdi at her camp near the border of An Shêru to begin the meeting.Complete 'Instance: The Lay of the Dry Land'Mizâdi is ready to put her plan into motion.

You should speak to Mizâdi at her camp near the border of An Shêru to begin the meeting.Talk to Mizâdi'Welcome, friend. We come to this arid place for one reason: to make a stand against Ordâkh. We know that Bârshud has come this way, likely to regroup with his Ordâkhai masters. Their stronghold must be here, and I aim to find a way to take it from them.

'Our group is small for now, only my most trusted allies. The rest of my army will follow when we are ready. Now, we must discuss what the scouts have found in Idagâl, and prepare our strategy.'

You ask about the newcomer in the left tent. She appears to be a scholar from Zajâna. Mizâdi stifles a sigh.

'Ah, yes. Meet Sorkamâl, my new diplomat. Numûru has convinced me we need one after that... misunderstanding in Zajâna. I am sure she will prove herself a valuable member of our cause.

'Now, let us gather the others.''There is much to consider, and much to do. The path forward will not be easy. I hope I can count on you to walk it with me, friend.''Are you ready to hear the report of our scouts?'A mighty light-house stands guard outside Starkhaven, providing a good view of the surrounding lands and aiding the passage of the ships that sail at Sûg Nidar.Standing outside the entrance to Starkhaven, your eye is drawn by the great light-house to the east.Examine the banner outside StarkhavenFrom atop the steps that lead to the light-house you might obtain a good view of the ship-yard of Starkhaven.Climb the steps leading to the light-houseIf you walk to the south-eastern side of the light-house you will have a better place from which to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the ship-yard.A man with a furtive air watches you from the shadows.Talk to the man with the furtive airEngéru asked you to find his wife Isamó somewhere among the chimneys on the western side of Starkhaven and to give her his message.Find Isamó somewhere near the chimneys on the western side of StarkhavenIsamó stands in an alley between buildings on the western side of Starkhaven.Talk to Isamó in the alleyStanding outside the entrance to Starkhaven, your eye is drawn by the great light-house across the bridge to the east. Climbing the steps in front of the light could lead to a good vantage point from which you could observe the mighty fleet and the ship-yard at which it was constructed.The man has a furtive air as he looks you up and down.

'This is not your place, stranger. I have lived here for all the years of my life, as did my father before me. I am Engéru. Mine is a family of ship-builders; we have known nothing else. But you have climbed to this height with ruin in your eye. You wish to see the Song destroyed.

'No, do not deny it! I said I was a ship-builder, and that is true. But I am not a soldier. For decades we worked here in Starkhaven, and every new ship that was added to the fleet seemed a trophy for my family. I did not believe they would ever sail, but now a man of Umbar has come to Sûg Nidar, and he commands hundreds of Corsairs. The woman Nakási orders that new weapons be mounted upon the ships, weapons that breathe terrible blue fire. The Orcs have always been here, but they used to keep to themselves across the lake; now we are expected to work alongside them?

'My wife Isamó and I decided to leave Starkhaven, but I am being watched. I will be pressed into service upon one of the war galleys once I descend from this light. Will you meet with my wife and tell her I cannot join her? She must carry out our plan without me. I have eyes only for Isamó; my heart goes with her, even as we must part.

'See you the chimneys to the east and south of here? That is where we intended to meet. Go now and guide my wife from this place, I beg of you. I will decide how to descend from this light: swiftly, on my own terms, or slowly, pressed into service aboard the weapons I helped create. Either way, I want to know my Isamó was given a chance to escape. Thank you, my friend.'The woman watches you carefully.Engéru gazes out over the vast fleet before speaking again.

'Look for Isamó among the buildings with the chimneys to the east and south of here, friend. Please go.'The woman watches you silently, but when you give her Engéru's message she cries out.

'We must return and save him from the soldiers! He will not try to fight them, but you can!'

You shake your head and tell Isamó that it was her husband's only wish that she escape Starkhaven, and that she is to carry out the plan they devised. There will be little time before the soldiers find her, unless she leaves now.

'I cannot do this by myself,' she says, and you cannot tell if she refers to the escape plan or to the unknown days ahead, without Engéru.People from across Shagâna have been captured by the Ordâkhai and sent to work in Esh Mêkag, the Silent Mouth. If freed, these people may be willing to join Mizâdi's cause.Captain Hanâbu has asked for your getting his soldiers out of Esh Mêkag, the Silent Mouth.

You should talk to your allies before you depart.Talk to UnusâliTalk to Sorkamâl the ForbearingTalk to HidâtiCaptain Hanâbu has sent you to find his scout, Arâniz.

You should find him hidden somewhere outside the prison, Esh Mêkag.Find Arâniz outside Esh Mêkag'There is much to discuss with your diplomat, and there is much to do to prepare the camp before our host arrives, but I have a request for you in the mean time, ${PLAYER}.

'Some of my men were taken by the Ordâkhai. We believe they are being held in Esh Mêkag, the Silent Mouth. I know little about it, save its reputation: a prison where Men are taken to have their spirits and bodies broken. I sent a scout, Arâniz, to find the prison and to see if he can get our soldiers out, but he has yet to report back. Find him, and see what you can do to help.''Another woman seeking to overthrow the Ordâkhai, eh? I expect us all to become fast friends!

'Hanâbu hides it well, but I can tell from the way he speaks of her that this Damakhêra Ardu is more than just his superior. I do not think she will be arriving with the host he expects, based on his sullen demeanor. 

'I have a feeling we will be meeting her sooner than later to fight this war together. I look forward to hunting the Ordâkhai down with yet another powerful woman with a grudge! Haha!''Captain Hanâbu seems grateful for our aid. A promising start, but Damakhêra Ardu is not an easy woman to impress. At least, not from what I have heard. From all accounts she is both fearless and ferocious!

'While you are assisting with the situation in Esh Mêkag, I will be negotiating on behalf of our Shâra. Once the Aradûni arrive, we will lead them to our gathering point: Ahâba. Bring anyone you can free from the prison with you when you return. We will need as large a force as we can possibly muster to face the fortress Emax Dûl.''Worry not! I will help the Aradûni cross the desert when they arrive. Now go, for you are needed elsewhere! There are many Beltáni captive in Esh Mêkag, as well. You can tell me of your success when we next meet.''Who- who goes there? Captain Hanâbu sent you? Oh, thank Ardu! I did not expect to see a friendly face out here.'

You tell Arâniz you were sent to help rescue the Aradûni soldiers from Esh Mêkag.

'Our captured soldiers are inside the prison or the nearby pit-mine somewhere, I am sure of it, but they are not the only ones. The Ordâkhai have sent captured people from all over Shagâna here to work themselves to death. A few of these thralls have managed to escape. I found them first, and they showed me this place. It is not much of a camp, but it is safe.'Corudan is concerned about the development of Narghâk weapons that might be used by the Song of Waves and Wind.Corudan wants to search for the Narghâk workshop he believes to be located somewhere among the buildings on the western shore of the Fearwater, in Starkhaven.Find the Narghâk workshop in Starkhaven, on the western shore of the FearwaterYou should examine one of the unusual-looking weapons at the Narghâk workshop on the western shore of the Fearwater, in Starkhaven.Examine one of the unusual-looking weapons at the Narghâk workshopPlans nearby may describe the construction process for designing such Narghâk weapons as those located at the Starkhaven workshop. You should examine the plans and defeat any who try to stop you.What did the engineer think to retrieve from the marked barrel by the Narghâk workshop?Examine the marked barrel by the Narghâk workshopWhat did the engineer think to retrieve from the marked barrel by the Narghâk workshop?Examine another marked barrel by the Narghâk workshopCorudan has come to the Narghâk workshop at Starkhaven.Talk to Corudan at the Narghâk workshop in StarkhavenCorudan has learned that Heirsworn Corsairs throughout Sûg Nidar may carry small glass bottles containing quantities of Narghâk.Deprive Corsairs in Sûg Nidar of Narghâk bottles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Corudan waits for word of your success at the Narghâk workshop on the western shore of the Fearwater, in Starkhaven.'The Song of Waves and Wind would be dangerous enough by itself, but Nakási has armed it with terrifying weapons. I know not for how long Khôltekh has been working in secret with her, but he had his eye upon the stockpile of Hungry Fire from the moment we discovered it within Ashâgir. Did he wait until you travelled into Mûr Ghala with Inkanûsh and Glorfindel to give the command to his underlings to transport the Narghâk to Sûg Nidar?

'The timing no longer matters. What matters to us now is that we prevent the Song from being equipped with weapons capable of using the Hungry Fire against its enemies. There must be a workshop of some kind within Starkhaven where such weapons can be assembled. Let us search for it among the buildings of Starkhaven on the western shore of the Fearwater. If we can destroy the Narghâk stockpile these weapons will stand empty and unused.''The workshop for constructing the Narghâk weapons must be located among the buildings of Starkhaven on the western shore of the Fearwater. If we can destroy the Narghâk stockpile these weapons will stand empty and unused.''I have made an unpleasant discovery, friend. While I searched for the Narghâk stockpile, I was surprised by a number of Heirsworn Corsairs and it came to fighting. But they were not content to engage in combat with their blades alone, and they threw glass jars containing a small quantity of an oily substance at me.

'I evaded this attack with little difficulty; am I not an Elf of Lórien? But when the jar shattered upon the ground it exploded with blue flame.

'Some of Balakhâd's Corsairs have been given jars of Narghâk to use in battle, ${PLAYER}. We must retrieve these jars from them. Afterwards let us meet back here.''Even a small quantity of Narghâk can inflict grievous harm! We must retrieve as many bottles of this deadly substance from the Heirsworn as we can.''Did you separate the bottles of Narghâk from their bearers? Good, for I have done the same. I also found a stack of parchment within an encampment of the Ordâkhai. I think the soldiers knew not what to make of these papers. They are yellowed with age, and when we have finished here I will take some time to study them.

'We found not the stockpile we sought, but I think we discovered the reason for that: the Hungry Fire has already been loaded onto the ships of the Song, and any excess considered unnecessary for their siphons and cannons have been given to the Heirsworn.

'It is more necessary than ever that we prevent the Song from setting sail. May Cúridwan have the time she needs to distribute the blight among the vessels of the fleet, and may we capture or kill the ones who might give the command to sail! But for now we have done what we can.'The Heirsworn Corsairs that follow Balakhâd are eager for a fight.The Heirsworn Corsairs that follow Balakhâd grow tired of waiting at the Haven of Bâkhridar for the command to sail to war. They want to fight!Defeat Heirsworn Corsairs at the Haven of Bâkhridar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have given some of the Heirsworn what they wanted: an excuse to fight!CompletedThe Heirsworn Corsairs at the Haven of Bâkhridar are eager for a fight. You should give it to them!You have faced a number of Heirsworn Corsairs at the Haven of Bâkhridar, but many still remain to crew the ships of the Song. You will need to find some other means of preventing the fleet from sailing out of Sûg Nidar.Mizâdi has decided to first visit Ahâba, the oasis settlement of the Beltáni people, to offer aid and try to form an alliance with their leader.Mizâdi is going ahead with Numûru and Sorkamâl.

You should meet her outside of Ahâba, north-west of her small camp.Meet Mizâdi on the road to AhâbaSomeone is chasing the Beltáni shepherds in your direction!

You should aid the shepherds.Defeat the Ordâkhai ambushThe Beltáni shepherds you rescued asked you to enter Ahâba and speak to their chieftain.

You should enter Ahâba and speak to Unusâli.Find Unusâli in Ahâba'We will meet you outside Ahâba. I will go ahead with Sorkamâl and Numûru, because he will insist I not go without any of my Subuzûri, but leave the rest of my guards behind for now. I do not want to startle these 'meek shepherds'.

'We will continue along this road toward the main path into the Oasis, to the North. We will not go ahead without you.''There you are. The main path into Ahâba should be this way. I would rather we not accidentally sneak up on them, if they are as timid as Numûru says.

'Wait. I hear something. Someone approaches.''There you are. The main path into Ahâba should be this way. I would rather we not accidentally sneak up on them, if they are as timid as Numûru says.

'Wait. I hear something. Someone approaches.''Here you are, the retinue of Shâra Mizâdi, who my people say saved them from Ordâkhai slavers.

'It seems we have mutual enemies. That does not yet make us friends.'Mizâdi Shâra-ingari has asked for your aid in her campaign in Idagâl.Mizâdi is preparing to launch a campaign in Idagâl and asked for your aid.

You should speak to Mizâdi at her camp near the border of An Shêru.Meet Mizâdi at her forward camp in Idagâl'Hail, ${PLAYER}! I bring word from Mizâdi Shâra-ingari!

'She has personally requested your aid with her campaign in Idagâl. She brings the fight to the Ordâkhai in their fortress! Should your accept her request, seek her out at her forward camp, just past the border of An Shêru.''${PLAYER}! I am glad you could join us! Come, we have much to discuss.'The Tombs of Khâb Ishil contain historic treasures from the kingdom of Nísaka. The Aradûni wish to save these items to preserve their cultural heritage.The Tombs of Khâb Ishil house many historical treasures from the kingdom of Nísaka.

You should collect ancient treasures at the Tombs of Khâb Ishil.Collect ancient treasures (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected many treasures from the Tombs of Khâb Ishil.

You should return to Malêrti at the Dawn-warden.Talk to Malêrti'The Tombs of Khâb Ishil are sacred to my people. Many heroes of our past are buried there, along with many treasures of historical value. If you are headed there, please retrieve what you can before they are corrupted by the kergrim!'Malêrti's eyes gleam as you show her the treasures you have collected.

'Imagine what these treasures have seen! They must all have been important to be buried among the heroes of Nísaka. I will ensure these are properly cared for from now on!'Orcs seeking to join the crew of the Grishúlvosh have been commanded to steal weapons from Drushkála for Zaumoz the Black Wind.An empty weapon rack stands within Drushkála.Examine the empty weapon rack in DrushkálaYou might learn more about the Grishúlvosh if you find more weapon racks to the east in Drushkála.Find another weapon rack to the east in DrushkálaAnother weapon rack stands to the south-east in Drushkála. Does this one still bear weapons?Many of the weapons in Drushkála have been brought to the ship Grishúlvosh.CompletedA small parchment is stuck to the empty weapon rack with a knife:

"You seek to join the crew of the Grishúlvosh? Then bring as many weapons as you can carry from Drushkála! Make yourself more valuable to ZAUMOZ, and he will reward you!"Many of the weapons in Drushkála have been brought to the ship Grishúlvosh, strengthening the fighting power of Zaumoz and his crew.

It is more important than ever that you find some means of hindering the Song of Waves and Wind, preventing ships such as Grishúlvosh from leaving Sûg Nidar.After rescuing them from the gaol, several storytellers wish to honour you with the only reward they can muster; tales of their homeland. They rest in the relative safety of Ahâba.Phardâli invited you to speak with others freed from the gaol-break. They wish to reward you with tales of Mûr Ghala, as they have nothing more to offer your for your noble act.Listen to Malgâras's tale: <rgb=#00ff00>Complete Celebration of Life - Glory</rgb>Listen to Vilgerâ's tale: <rgb=#00ff00>Complete Celebration of Life - Grace</rgb>Listen to Dabâr's tale: <rgb=#00ff00>Complete Celebration of Life - Folly</rgb>Having heard the tales and shared a night with those saved from an ignoble fate within the dungeons of Emax Dûl, you have questions for Dabâr and his tale of the blight. Speak with him at Ahâba.Ask Phardâli Ink-fingers about the Fool King'I had hoped you would find me. There are many here in your debt. Were it not for your action, our lives would be at an end. There is no recompense we can provide, as destitution is the plight of our moment, but we would invite you to entreat with us, those you saved, for a modest gift of storytelling.

'Across this bridge to the north you will find Dabâr. Beyond him, beneath the canopy and near the sheep pen, Vilgêra, and beneath the canopy nearest the stable-master you will find Malgâras. Each has a story to share.

'Will you meet with them, and then return to me?''The King and the Pale Blight? A tale passed down through countless generations. Yet the memory of Men is fleeting and few recall with true clarity.

'Like others, I weave the tale with embellishments to soothe eager ears. But mark this, friend; no maps speak of the Citadel of the King of Folly. No written lore survives to hint at its bearing. So great was the horror the king wrought, his reign was erased from history, passed only in oral tradition, as a warning.

'Yet… among the Temámir dwarves, there may be maps of those peaks they dared not scale. Dwarves, unlike Men, can recall the ancient history of stone; they will know of the place they would not delve.'Mizâdi asks that you and Razâl create a distraction, while she, Rahâzi, and a handful of Subuzûri sneak to Bârshud's fortress in the rear of Imizíla. She asks you to join her once you are done.Arrive at the entrance to the secret passage into Imizíla. The secret passage can be found on the western side of Imizíla. Imizíla can be found south of Ingarûma.Arrive at the entrance to the secret passage into ImizílaMove through the secret passage past the gate into Imizíla.Move through the secret passage past the gate into ImizílaSpeak with Razâl beyond the secret passage gate into Imizíla.Speak with Razâl within ImizílaSet alight hot tar and kegs of black powder within Imizíla to create a distraction so Mizâdi and Rahâzi can slip into the city near Bârshud's fortress.Defeat Ordâkhai within Imizíla (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Set alight kegs of black powder (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Set alight batches of hot tar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Move to and speak with Mizâdi outside Bârshud's fortress in Imizíla.Speak with Mizâdi outside Bârshud's fortress in Imizíla'Now that we have the key, we can move into Imizíla from the secret entrance.

'Work with Razâl to distract the Ordâkhai - draw them away from Bârshud's fortress. Then, meet with us when you can.''Not a moment too soon. Get inside, quickly, quickly, before they see us.''We need to create a distraction so Mizâdi and Rahâzi can move without fear toward Bârshud's fortress at the rear of Imizíla. Luckily there is still much armament here in Imizíla with which to create such a distraction.

'I will head to the west. You should head to the east. Set alight hot tar pots and kegs of black powder. That should give the Ordâkhai guards enough to worry about to allow Mizâdi to slip through unnoticed.'Bârshud is no more, but the work is not yet complete. His forces need to be scattered to the winds, and Imizíla taken.Speak with Mizâdi outside Bârshud's fortress in Imizíla when you are ready.Speak with Mizâdi outside Bârshud's fortress in ImizílaSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located south of Hanamíku, high on a hilltop overlooking Imizíla.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma'Bârshud is no more - but our work is not yet complete. We still have much to do before Imizíla can be rid of the presence of the Ordâkhai.''I cannot thank you enough. Bârshud is no more, although the cost for our victory was great. Much more than I ever wished to pay.''There is much that needs doing this day - Imizíla must be taken, and the remaining Ordâkhai scattered.'A new warden has emerged to claim control of Esh Mêkag prison.A new warden has taken control of Esh Mêkag and is threatening to execute the thralls remaining inside.

You should rescue the imprisoned thralls, and defeat the Ordâkhai inside Esh Mêkag prison.Rescue imprisoned thralls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ordâkhai inside Esh Mêkag prison (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Warden KhusókuThe remaining thralls have been rescued and the new warden defeated.

You should return to Ebuzâm.Talk to Ebuzâm'My people should be able to take control of the pit-mine now that their leadership is in disarray, but the Ordâkhai have taken control of the prison itself.

'Overseer Khusóku has named herself the new warden, and announced the execution of every thrall left under their control. They have reinforced the prison, and will kill any who come near.

'You have done much for us already, ${PLAYER}, but I must ask for your aid one last time. Gather who you can, storm the prison, and put an end to this!''It is done. My people are free and the new warden lies dead! Thank you, ${PLAYER}. We will never forget your heroism.'Mizâdi tells you that several Subuzûri reported seeing Bârshud or his aide, Sudûgul, on their flight from Emax Dûl. She asks you to gather their reports.Speak with each of the Subuzûri witnesses Shâra Mizâdi mentioned in Hanamíku.Speak with Gíshu in HanamíkuSpeak with Zâgsha in HanamíkuSpeak with Nushâba in HanamíkuCollect each of the items for which Gíshu, Zâgsha, and Nushâba asked. Each can likely be found somewhere in or near Hanamíku in Pahar Hatokáli.Gather some skins of fresh water for Gishu (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather new bandages for ZâgshaFind whetstones for Nushâba (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak once more with the Subuzûri warriors Gíshu, Zâgsha, and Nushâba in Hanamíku.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku. Hanamíku can be found in Pahar Hatokáli, within Mûr Ghala.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku'It is you! It is so good to see you again! I have a powerful need for familiar faces in this foreign land.

'Several of my warriors saw Bârshud or his new Ordâkhai ally, Sudûgul, on their flight from the Emax Dûl.

'In the chaos, I have not had the time to gather their reports. We know Bârshud came down here, to the Hatokáli Fells. We know not his purpose or location here, however.

'Would you speak with each of the Subuzûri who saw him? Gíshu, Zâgsha, and Nushâba are their names - they will be with the other Subuzûri here in Hanamíku. Let them know I sent you. Thank you, ${PLAYER} - just seeing you here again is like a great weight has been lifted from my shoulders.''Interesting. I do not know where the dead lie here in Pahar Hatokáli.

'A tomb? I will have Razâl scout for such a place. Thank you, my friend. This has been a great help. In the meanwhile, there is another task I would ask of you, if you are willing.''Bârshud? Yes, I saw the man - when he was in the Palace in Emax Dûl. He was looking for something. I am sorry - my mouth is dry, my throat quite parched.

'Could you gather me some water? I am happy to tell you what I know, but I feel quite light-headed, and it's hard to speak.''Yes, I saw Bârshud. When he was fleeing Emax Dûl. He was fleeing at great speed - he made no attempt at helping children or civilians either, saving only himself, with that frightening servant of his.

'There was something in his hand, ah! My shoulder! It is burning in pain - I cannot think properly. Please, get me a large shoulder bandage - once this is wrapped properly, I will tell you what I know.''I'm not bothering anyone here, am I?

'Bârshud? I did not see him, but I saw his servant, Sudûgul, in the confusion around Emax Dûl. Damn this blade! It could not cut the hair on my head, let alone slice through a servant of Ordâkh here in the fells.

'Would you gather me a whetstone or two? I cannot concentrate - a dull blade brings about a dull mind.''Yes, Bârshud.

'There was so much chaos and confusion, but I did see him - he was looking for a staff. He was yelling at his second, Sudûgul. Something about the Dead. I believe they thought this staff could command them - command the Dead. I know not if he found it, just that he was looking in the Palace for it. I wish I could be more helpful to the Shâra.''Ah, yes. Dry and well-stitched. That will do nicely.

'Yes, Bârshud, of course. He was yelling at his Ordâkhai guards to move faster in his flight. Then he said something about a tomb in Hatokáli. I believe that was where he was headed. I know not what tomb, I am from Imhûlar, this area is quite foreign to me. Maybe the Shâra knows of this tomb.''These will do the job. Never have a dull sword or a dull mind, I say. But if you have to have one, make it the dull mind - ha!

'Bârshud, right. I saw him - a staff? He did not have a staff, but his sorcerer did - I think they call that one Sudûgul. It was a long staff, it looked to be made of bone or something unnaturally white, with the end carved in the shape of a dragon's skull. I know not its import, but Bârshud did possess it through this Sudûgul.'Mizâdi, Shâra of Hamât Renewed, requests your presence in Pahar Hatokáli. She calls for your aid in finishing her hunt of the pretender Shâr Bârshud, who fled Emax Dûl into the wild scrubland of Pahar Hatokáli.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku. Hanamíku can be found in Pahar Hatokáli, which is south of Idagâl, within Mûr Ghala.Speak with Mizâdi in Hanamíku'I am still shaken by what I witnessed here in Emax Dûl, but my resolve is still firm to finish our mission, and bring Bârshud to justice.

'My scouts saw his flight take him south, through a town called Hanamíku, in Pahar Hatokáli, what locals call the Hatokáli Fells. That is where we must next go. Meet me in Hanamíku, friend, when you are able.''It is you! It is so good to see you again, ${PLAYER}! I have great need of your skills this day.'Mizâdi requests your aid in gathering Numûru's armour and sword, scattered across the battlefield, in order to build a memorial for him.Speak with Razâl in Ingarûma about finding Numûru's effects.Speak with Razâl in IngarûmaRetrieve large, smooth stones and Numûru's sword from the area outside of Imizíla.Gather memorial stones for Numûru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and recover Numûru's sword from outside ImizílaRecover Numûru's armour. Razâl believes the armour was taken by the Orcs of Roz Káskrauz. Roz Káskrauz is located in the hills east of Ingarûma.Recover Numûru's armour from Roz KáskrauzSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located south of Hanamíku, high on a hill-top overlooking Imizíla.'I feel a great duty to remember Numûru properly. Will you help me construct a memorial for him?

'His sword and armour have been lost. I believe they should be found on the battlefield outside Imizíla. Speak with Razâl first, though - he may have greater knowledge of the whereabouts of Numûru's effects.

'It would also be a kindness to bring back some large, smooth stones with which to form his memorial. We will build a great cairn by which to remember him.''Thank you. His sword and his armour - yes, this will make for a fine memorial.''Yes, I have seen his sword. It is still outside the main gate of Imizíla. I would ride quickly out there, before it is taken by looters or brigands.

'His armour is a different matter altogether. One of my scouts reported seeing the Orcs of Roz Káskrauz gathering armour as trophies and returning with them to their camp. I'd wager that's where you'll find Numûru's armour.'Valukhâri reviews your map and sends you to the library of Zajâna to look at the Doorward's map for comparison.Valukhâri sent you to the library to find the Doorward's map of Mûr Ghala. You should go there and compare the map provided by Bêtam.After comparing the maps, it is clear the map the Doorwards crafted is missing a section to the far south-east of Adagím. You should return to Valukhâri and ask her about this.You show Bêtam's map to Valukhâri.

'This is a map of all Mûr Ghala. You will find a matching map within the library, here in Zajâna. Feel free to study any other maps you wish to while you are here.'As you compare the maps, you see a distinct difference in the south-eastern corner of Adagím's border. On the map provided by Bêtam, there is an annotation citing the location where they would not go. When compared to the map of Mûr Ghala drafted by the scholars of Zajâna, the section of the mountain range is missing.'Strange indeed. Our maps are renowned for precision and care. It may be that the cartographer who crafted yours has, perhaps, erred in their reckoning.'Kagûlu the Armsman believes he may have the solution for Kishâtal's weapon problem.Kagûlu the Armsman has suggested you bring an axe and a spear to Kishâtal so he can try them and see which one he likes best.Pick up the axe Kagûlu suggestedPick up the spear Kagûlu suggestedKishâtal is down the slope to the south-east of the forges in the war camp of Ingarûma.Kishâtal is excited to test out each of the new weapons, and has encouraged you to fight alongside him by the zizanu nests at Ukh-bâra to the south-east and on the skirmish fields along the road to the east of the war camp.Defeat zizani alongside Kishâtal at Ukh-bâra (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Ordâkhai alongside Kishâtal at the skirmish fields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Kishâtal has returned to the war camp of Ingarûma.Talk to Kishâtal at the war camp of Ingarûma'See you the strain placed on the blade here, and here, right by these cracks? I believe the arc of Kishâtal's swing is placing an undue burden upon the swords he uses. He may have greater success with a different style of weapon.

'I suggest that he try using this axe, or perhaps this spear. Send him into battle with each of these and report back to me his results with these different armaments.''Send Kishâtal into battle with each of these new weapons and report back to me his results.''Send Kishâtal into battle with each of these new weapons and report back to me his results.''I do not know, ${PLAYER}. I have used swords for all my fighting life. Can I really expect to have success with an axe, or with a spear?

'Well, if Kagûlu believes this will help I will not refuse the suggestion. Let the two of us do battle against the zizani of Ukh-bâra and the Ordâkhai on the skirmish fields. I will wield the axe against one foe, and the spear against the other, and we will see if I can break either! Then perhaps Kagûlu will admit it is not Kishâtal who is to blame, but the quality of the arms Kagûlu fashions for us!''Let the two of us do battle against the zizani of Ukh-bâra and the Ordâkhai on the skirmish fields. I will wield the axe against one foe, and the spear against the other, and we will see if I can break either! Then perhaps Kagûlu will admit it is not Kishâtal who is to blame, but the quality of the arms Kagûlu fashions for us!''Thank you for fighting alongside me while I tested each of Kagûlu's suggested armaments. The good tidings are these: neither of them broke while I used them!

'These are the ill tidings: I did not care for either of them. I prefer the swords, though I break them with such rapidity!'Mizâdi is incensed at the treatment of lions in the hands of Ordâkhai and asks you to put a stop to the Ordâkhai operation.Speak with Razâl in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located on a large hill south of Hanamíku in Pahar Hatokáli.Speak with Razâl in IngarûmaEnter Nakársong and free the captive lions and defeat their Ordâkhai trainers. Nakársong can be found south-west of Ingarûma in Pahar Hatokáli.Enter Nakársong in the hills south-west of IngarûmaGo to Nakársong and free the captive lions and defeat their Ordâkhai trainers. Nakársong can be found south-west of Ingarûma in Pahar Hatokáli.Defeat Ordâkhai trainers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Ordâkhai lion cages (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Open lion paddock gates (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located south of Hanamíku, high on a hill-top overlooking Imizíla.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma'Razâl brings me reports of lions being tortured and trained to be Ordâkhai killers in the hills not far from here. I will not allow it.

'Speak with Razâl and then work with him to ensure no more harm comes to these majestic creatures. This is a matter I care about greatly, ${PLAYER}. I know that in your capable hands these lions will receive the aid they need, and the Ordâkhai the justice they require.''These lions deserve far better lives than the Ordâkhai gave them. Thank you for your part in freeing them, my friend.''Yes, my scouts bring reports of lions being tortured and trained to act as killers for the Ordâkhai. The Ordâkhai have a camp not far from here, locals call it Nakársong. This is where the Ordâkhai trap and train these lions to kill.'Lakhêpi the Far-faring is interested in challenging some of her other senses, and wishes to travel further south into Pahar Hatokáli.Lakhêpi asked you to gather snake and kalorkhûn meat from creatures in the wild for her to sample.Collect snake meat in Pahar Hatokáli (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect kalorkhûn meat in Pahar Hatokáli (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lakhêpi the Far-faring agreed to meet you a safe distance outside the brigand camp of Aptíku to the south.Lakhêpi asked you to find the wallowing spot of alap-nâri to the west, a place called Bûlkharar. She also wanted you to bring her some alap-nâri meat, so she can compare its taste to the other meats you gathered for her.Find Bûlkharar, the wallowing spot of the alap-nâri, and note its smellCollect alap-nâri meat from the creatures at Bûlkharar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lakhêpi the Far-faring is waiting outside Aptíku for you to return.You should pick up her satchel and go in search of Lakhêpi. She could be in danger!Pick up Lakhêpi's satchel and go in search of herLakhêpi has returned to the village of Hanamíku.Talk to Lakhêpi in the village of Hanamíku'You have helped me obtain the details of sight and sound, but more senses remain! I speak, of course, of taste, and of smell! As we make our way south toward the Hatokáli River, can you hunt some of the creatures that prowl among the hills? I have not tasted the meat of the snakes or the kalorkhûn that dwell in Pahar Hatokáli in some time, but in my memory they are surprisingly delicious.

'I will meet you nearer to the river once you have attained these foodstuffs, friend helper! There is a brigand camp down there, but we will give it a wide enough berth that they will not trouble us.''As we make our way south toward the Hatokáli River, can you hunt some of the creatures that prowl among the hills? I have not tasted the meat of the snakes or the kalorkhûn that dwell in Pahar Hatokáli in some time, but in my memory they are surprisingly delicious. I will meet you nearer to the river once you have attained these foodstuffs, friend helper!

'There is a brigand camp down there, but we will give it a wide enough berth that they will not trouble us.''You have brought the snake and kalorkhûn meat for which I asked? Good, thank you! I have been watching the brigands that dwell alongside the Hatokáli River, and they...'

Lakhêpi falls silent.

'You know, I overheard them talking about a herd of alap-nâri in the wetlands to the west. Alap-nâri are water oxen... and I suspect their meat would provide a delicious counterpoint to the steaks you have already brought me. We cannot discount the importance of taste as a sensation! Will you find this herd to the west and bring me some alap-nâri steaks to cook? Keep your nose at the ready as well, for I will not leave out the very important sensation of smell as I prepare my next story!

'I will meet you here when you return, friend helper.''Will you find this herd to the west and bring me some alap-nâri steaks to cook? Keep your nose at the ready as well, for I will not leave out the very important sensation of smell as I prepare my next story!

'I will meet you here when you return, friend helper.'Lakhêpi would not have left her satchel unattended unless she had no choice. Has she fallen prey to some danger?You pick up Lakhêpi's satchel and prepare to go to the story-teller's rescue. You hope only that you are not too late already!'I appreciate your assistance back in Aptíku, although I think I was in very little real danger. His fellows would likely not have harmed a friend of Mashdagâl, despite our parting of ways. When last I saw him, he gave me the kernel of an idea for a new story: something about terrible creatures that invade your mind, and drive you to madness.'

You tell Lakhêpi that you wouldn't want to spread such stories as that for fear of frightening the people of Pahar Hatokáli, and she cocks her head to one side.

'But folk love frightening stories, so long as they are not real! But I will not use that one for now... not yet! If you give me some other ideas I will not need to make use of Mashdagâl's inventive foes! I never knew him to be scared before, but the merest thought of such things drove him nearly to distraction, and he left my company.

'Adventure in Pahar Hatokáli and bring me the kernels of other story ideas, friend helper! You will prove yourself a much better assistant to me than did Mashdagâl, who abandoned me when I still had need of him!'Arimûl, a soldier in Mizâdi's army, was wounded during the fighting and cannot make it back to the war camp without help.Chief Provisioner Dunaïl stands by his tent in the war camp of Ingarûma.Talk to Chief Provisioner Dunaïl in the war camp of IngarûmaChief Provisioner Dunaïl gave you a wooden stave and bandages to bring to Arimûl, injured by a cross-road to the west of the war camp of Ingarûma.'Stranger, wait a moment if you would. Are you with Mizâdi's army? Can you help me?'

You assure the man that if you can aid him, you will do so.

'I have had something of a run of ill fortune and was injured during the fighting; now I cannot walk without help. Could I ask you to bring me a crutch of some kind from the war camp so I can make it safely there? One of the provisioners must have something I can use.''I was injured during the fighting, and now I cannot walk without help. Could I ask you to bring me a crutch of some kind from the war camp so I can make it safely there? One of the provisioners must have something I can use.''You encountered an injured soldier beside the road, and he cannot walk without help? Yes, I have just the thing. Take this bandage and this wooden stave. With these items he should be able to make it back here to the war camp.''Thank you, my friend. I should be able to make it to the camp now.

'But... there is one more thing...'Collect honeycomb from the beehivePick up the beeswaxComplete Instance: A Tale of the Second AgeTalk to CelonorThe Quartermaster has requested your assistance in the continued efforts to aid the people of Mûr Ghala in completing dangerous challenges.<rgb=#FF0000>Complete dangerous Instances in the Mûr Ghala Cluster for the Quartermaster. Use the Instance Finder to enter Mûr Ghala Instances.</rgb>Complete the Treasure Caves of Hurum Kâna (Tier 3)Complete Kôth Rau, the Wailing Hold (Tier 3)Complete Ekal-nêbi, the Fallen Palace (Tier 3)Speak with a Mûr Ghala Quartermaster in Adagím or Zajâna to accept your reward.Speak with a Mûr Ghala Quartermaster for your reward'We must assist the people of Mûr Ghala!

'I ask for your help to aid in our efforts. There are many challenges still to overcome in Mûr Ghala, and much evil still to be met in equal combat and defeated.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Complete dangerous Instances in the Mûr Ghala Instance Cluster for the Quartermaster. Use the Instance Finder to enter Mûr Ghala Instances.</rgb>'We must assist the people of Mûr Ghala!

'I ask for your help to aid in our efforts. There are many challenges still to overcome in Mûr Ghala, and much evil still to be met in equal combat and defeated.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Complete Instances in the Mûr Ghala Instance Cluster for the Quartermaster. Use the Instance Finder to enter Mûr Ghala Instances.</rgb>'Your efforts to end these dangerous threats have aided those who work to forge a new path for the people of Mûr Ghala.

'You will be rewarded for your brave and noble accomplishments.'The Quartermaster has requested your aid in the continued efforts to explore dangers and conquer evils within the Folly of Nagakhêdi.<rgb=#FF0000>Defeat each boss in the Folly of Nagakhêdi raid on Tier 3 for the Quartermaster. Use the Instance Finder to enter the Folly of Nagakhêdi raid instance.</rgb>Defeat Badharál the Gorger on Tier 3Defeat Maukhorn on Tier 3Defeat the Legion of Lhaereth on Tier 3Defeat Zamâktar the Putrescent on Tier 3Speak with a Mûr Ghala Quartermaster in Adagím or Zajâna to accept your reward.Speak with a Mûr Ghala Quartermaster for your reward'I ask for your aid in exploring the depths of the Folly of Nagakhêdi. We believe there are dangerous forces down in the depths of Nagakhêdi, hideous and unnatural foes that pose a great threat not just to Adagím but all of Mûr Ghala.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Complete dangerous instances of the Folly of Nagakhêdi raid for the Quartermaster. Use the Instance Finder to enter the Folly of Nagakhêdi raid instance.</rgb>'I ask for your aid in exploring the depths of the Folly of Nagakhêdi. We believe there are dangerous forces down in the depths of Nagakhêdi, hideous and unnatural foes that pose a great threat not just to Adagím but all of Mûr Ghala.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Complete dangerous instances of the Folly of Nagakhêdi raid for the Quartermaster. Use the Instance Finder to enter the Folly of Nagakhêdi raid instance.</rgb>'You have brought light to the darkness and slayed many dangerous and foul beasts within the inky depths of the Folly of Nagakhêdi.

'You will be rewarded for your brave and noble accomplishments.'Track down and defeat every formidable enemy in Adagím.Track down and defeat every formidable enemy in Adagím.Defeat ShálithDefeat Strákhal the StranglerDefeat ThagáraDefeat Sóthadar the TricksterDefeat Âkhtal the DespoilerDefeat HórushDefeat Lhálach the StrickenDefeat CaelgethDefeat Agáthar the BereftTalk to Bhôd-buri-Mêj at Khel WêroNumûru is worried that a rogue band of Orcs far above Imizíla could use the upcoming battle as an opportunity to attack Hamâti forces from the rear. He asks that you defeat their leader to put the Orkish forces in disarray.Defeat Orcs within Roz Káskrauz. Roz Káskrauz is located in the hills east of Ingarûma.Defeat Hatokáli intimidators (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Hatokáli trackers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Hatokáli skulkers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Rogtúrz Night-eye within Roz Káskrauz. Roz Káskrauz is located east of Ingarûma.Defeat Rogtúrz Night-eye in Roz KáskrauzSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located south of Hanamíku, high on a hill-top overlooking Imizíla.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma'There is one other matter we must attend to before we can strike at Bârshud.

'Razâl brings news that a band of Orcs has made their camp high above Imizíla, in a place called Roz Káskrauz.

'If we attack Bârshud at Imizíla, they could use that opportunity to strike us when we are at our most vulnerable.

'However, if we remove the chieftain of the Orcs, their remaining forces will be plunged into disarray. Defeat this chieftain, so that we may have our opportunity to take Imizíla without fear of counter-attack.''The Orcs are in disarray? This is fortuitous news indeed. Numûru is right. I would scarcely want our Subuzûri looking over their shoulders when we strike at Imizíla.'Razâl has a plan, and a 'trader' who wants to sell Razâl a key to the secret sluice gate that Mizâdi can use to enter Imizíla surreptitiously.Speak with Razâl in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located on a large hill south of Hanamíku in Pahar Hatokáli.Speak with Razâl in IngarûmaSpeak with Razâl near the secret passage outside Imizíla. The secret passage can be found on the western side of Imizíla. Imizíla can be found south of Ingarûma.Speak with Razâl near the secret passage outside ImizílaMeet with the trader Katâl by the secret gate into Imizíla.Meet with the trader Katâl near ImizílaFlee deeper into the secret channel beneath Imizíla.Flee deeper into the secret channel beneath ImizílaPick up the key shining in the dirt in the channel.Pick up the key shining in the dirtSpeak with Razâl near Imizíla.Speak with Razâl near ImizílaSpeak with Razâl near Imizíla.Speak with Razâl near ImizílaSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located south of Hanamíku, high on a hill-top overlooking Imizíla.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma'Razâl believes he found another way into Imizíla. Work with him to find a way inside.''Fortune seems to favour you, but I will gladly take any boon given this day.

'Our plan now seems set. We know what we must do.''I have been scouting Imizíla. I noticed a trader, Katâl, who moved into the secret gate each night. He possesses a key which allows him access to the city. I believe he trades food and supplies within Imizíla in exchange for coin.

'My scouts have approached this trader. He has agreed to give us the key in exchange for a large sum of coin. I do not know if he is to be believed, but bartering with him is our best strategy right now. We are meeting him soon - would you accompany us? I know you can handle yourself if a fight breaks out.

'Keep your wits about you. I trust this 'trader' as far as I can throw him.''Over here! Our friend arrived a few minutes ago. Nervous sort. He seems to be alone.

'Speak with him - I will come in with the Subuzûri if necessary.''It seems we did not come all this way for naught.

'We should return with the key and this knowledge back to the Shâra in Ingarûma.'The Rangers Rhadrog and Faeron have decided to soon depart Gadim-ûn. They want to escort the prisoners you freed from Kôth Rau to Zajâna where they can get proper medical care for their wounds.Before departing for Zajâna, Rhadrog asks you to deal with Ombátha, who will continue to pose a threat to An Shêru. Whether you choose to do so alone or with allies, you should enter the interior of Kôth Rau and battle Ombátha and whatever other threats you discover within.You have defeated the leadership of the Ordâkhai and the Utûgi at Kôth Rau. You should report your success to Nabatínu at Gadim-ûn.Talk to Nabatínu'Faeron and I have already stayed here overlong and must soon return to Adagím. I admit that I'm interested to see what Viznak was able to accomplish in our absence!

'We also cannot leave the people we rescued from Kôth Rau here at Gadim-ûn. They need proper medicine, and they place a strain on the Jatsakóri's already thin resources. We will escort them to Zajâna and then be on our way to Adagím.

'I beg of you, though, to do something about the evil at Kôth Rau. Ombátha and her Utûgi allies cannot be allowed to continue their activities. We have freed some captives, but they will only take more unless they are stopped. Whether or not her defeat would free the remaining Jatsakóri from their thralldom, she will need to be dealt with.

'You may need to gather more allies for this. I leave it up to you.''The entrance to inner Kôth Rau is at the highest point of the slope on the mountainside. I can show you the way, if you like, but make sure you are prepared for battle before we go.''I cannot believe it. My friend, you have done what I thought impossible! Ombátha is defeated, and as I suspected, her spell upon the Jatsakóri weakened, allowing the remaining Jatsakóri to free their minds! The rest of us helped them escape their shackles with the training given to us by the Rangers.

'Kugâna and I are together again because of you! You are truly a hero, and I am proud to call you my friend. We will allow the newly freed Jatsakóri time to regain their strength, and then make our way to Kighân to start our lives anew. Thank you, ${PLAYER}, you will forever be in our hearts.'The Emax Dûl guard barracks may still hold a store of valuable weapons.Numûru has asked you to assist him with investigating the city guard barracks.

You should talk to Numûru and complete 'Instance: Barging into the Barracks'.Complete 'Instance: Barging into the Barracks'You have safely returned to Nashûbu.

You should talk to Numûru.Talk to Numûru'We have located the city guards' barracks on the western side of Emax Dûl. Our scouts tell me it has become unusually quiet; the guards no longer seem to be coming and going. They have also spotted an Utûgi group in the area. We are unsure why, as they have mostly seemed stay near their stronghold on the other side of the city.

'I would like to investigate the barracks, as we believe it is also the location of the city's armoury, but I sense something is amiss. The two of us will go alone, so as not to put anyone else at risk in the event that this is a trap. We will investigate the barracks, and return with any weapons we can find. We can surely use them to arm our growing rebellion!''Are you ready to go to the barracks? This may be a trap, so ensure you are well prepared.''Despite it being a trap, our mission was a great success! I will ensure all of the weapons in the armoury are... 'reallocated' to further our cause. Excellent work, ${PLAYER}.'The final preparations must be made before the battle for Mûr Ghala can begin.Speak with the blacksmith Tebíra in Mizâdi's camp at Ingarûma. Ingarûma can be found south of Hanamíku.Speak with the blacksmith Tebíra in IngarûmaGather ore in the area north of Ingarûma for the blacksmith Tebíra.Gather blacksmithing ore north of Ingarûma (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Help the blacksmith Tebíra repair divots in Subuzûri shields in Ingarûma.Repair Subuzûri shields (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with the blacksmith Tebíra in Ingarûma.Speak with the blacksmith Tebíra in IngarûmaHelp the Subuzûri in Ingarûma construct siege weapons to besiege Imizíla.Help the Subuzûri construct siege weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Help the Subuzûri in Ingarûma construct siege ladders to besiege Imizíla.Help the Subuzûri construct siege ladders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located south of Hanamíku, high on a hill-top overlooking Imizíla.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma'The best way to ensure victory is to prepare for it.

'There is still much to do before we can besiege Imizíla. Please, work with Tebíra, our blacksmith here in Ingarûma. The armour of the Subuzûri is still scarred from previous battles, and will not last another. She will be able to tell you more about what she needs.''Patience is not one of my virtues, my friend. It has been difficult waiting to attack. But all these preparations will be worth it.

'Hamât is going to war!''You have come to help? Will wonders not cease? Another pair of hands to aid in this shield repair.

'I have a great need for more ore. The armour the Subuzûri have given me is more air than iron, and I have a powerful need for more metals to repair these divots. There should be some in the hills surrounding Ingarûma. This work has left me tied to the anvil, otherwise I would go myself.''Yes, this armour is looking much better. I appreciate the help. The Subuzûri could use a pair of hands in constructing their siege weapons and ladders.

'Numûru has told me that is the last thing we must do before we can besiege Imizíla.'Mizâdi asks you to fight alongside the Subuzûri as you take on Bârshud's forces outside of Imizíla.Enter the valley below Ingarûma, near Imizíla.Enter the valley below Ingarûma, near ImizílaContinue moving south, defeating Ordâkhai and aiding wounded Subuzûri as you find them in the valley between Imizíla and Ingarûma.Defeat Ordâkhai (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Aid wounded Subuzûri south of Ingarûma (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Dhókhur Bóro in the valley below Imizíla.Defeat Dhókhur Bóro in the valleyPlace Mizâdi's banner in the valley below Imizíla to claim it in the name of Hamât Renewed.Place Mizâdi's banner to claim the valley for Hamât RenewedSpeak with Mizâdi outside the fort of Imizíla.Speak with Mizâdi outside the fort of Imizíla'Fight! Fight for your brothers and sisters in arms! For Hamât Renewed!''We are so close, my friend. I can taste victory from where I stand.'Defeat many bees throughout Kighân.Defeat many bees throughout Kighân.Defeat many bees throughout KighânDefeat a multitude of bees throughout Kighân.Defeat many bees throughout Kighân.Defeat a great many bees in Kighân.Defeat a great many bees in KighânHaving gathered a secret key and information about Bârshud's aims, Mizadi asks you to accompany her into the tombs of Mut-hûru in pursuit of Bârshud.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku when you are ready.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku when you are readySpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku'There is not a moment to lose, friend. Now that we have the key, we must venture into the tombs of Mut-hûru. Will you accompany us into the tombs?''He was so close. He was so close and now he is into the wind, gone once more.''We must move like the desert wind if we hope to catch Bârshud before he disappears once more.'Mizâdi's forces have pushed back Bârshud and the Ordâkhai to Imizíla. However, Numûru and Mizâdi now disagree on how to proceed in the attack.Speak with Mizâdi near Imizíla when you are ready.Speak with Mizâdi near Imizíla when you are readySpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located south of Hanamíku, high on a hilltop overlooking Imizíla.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma'We are nearly there! We must press the assault.''I - we - I can scarcely believe it. Were I not there, I would not. Numûru...''We shall have our victory this day.'Málacál has asked that you travel to the east of Sul Madásh and help her and her hunters thin the number of blighted spiders that can be found.Málacál has asked that you travel to the east of Sul Madásh and help her and her hunters thin the number of blighted spiders that can be found.Defeat blighted spiders east of Sul Madásh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Málacál near Sul Madásh and report your success of defeating spiders in eastern Adagím.Return to Málacál'The spiders here are quite the challenge for the hunt. They are cunning and hide in their shadows and webs.

'If you can, thin their numbers in the east and make the guild proud. You may need to gather some allies for the task.''You return. I trust your hunt for spiders has been a success?

'We know they will return and their numbers will replenish, but that only keeps the hunt going! Your efforts made us proud, friend.'Mizâdi is done speaking. She is determined to kill Bârshud, no matter the cost.Speak with Mizâdi outside Bârshud's fortress in Imizíla when you are ready.Speak with Mizâdi outside Bârshud's fortress in ImizílaSpeak with Mizâdi outside Bârshud's fortress in Imizíla.Speak with Mizâdi outside Bârshud's fortress in Imizíla'I know Bârshud is here. Move quietly and quickly - before his guards can alert him to our presence.''It is done. At long last - it is done.''Let's go - quickly and quietly, like a blade at midnight.'Defeat many bog-lurkers in the fallow marshes of Adagím.Defeat many bog-lurkers in Adagím.Defeat many bog-lurkers in AdagímDefeat a great many bog-lurkers in the fallow marshes of Adagím.Defeat many bog-lurkers in Adagím.Defeat a great many bog-lurkers in Adagím.Defeat a great many bog-lurkers in AdagímA wanted poster requests the hide of the formidable sûlok called Biret-kôda by the Temámir of Jiret-menêsh.Biret-kôda is said to often be found in Uhumêlu, south-east of the Beast-fields. You should defeat Biret-kôda and collect his hide.Collect the hide of Biret-kôdaYou have defeated Biret-kôda and collected his hide. You should take it to Jiret-menêsh to get your reward.Wanted:

The Armourers' Guild of Jiret-menêsh requests the hide of Biret-kôda, a sûlok reputed to have a thick skin of particular interest to the Guild. Biret-kôda is said to often be found in Uhumêlu, south-east of the Beast-fields. Whosoever brings the beast down should deliver the hide to Mísikir to receive a reward.'Oho, that looks like it must be the hide of Biret-kôda! Well done, ${PLAYER}, the Armourers' Guild will be very pleased. I will see to it that this gets to them. Thank you, and enjoy your reward!'A wanted poster for the defeat of Enudâri, an infamous wight.Enudâri is known to haunt the Mashâli Barrens north of the Crypts of Khâb Daku.Defeat EnudâriYou have defeated Enudâri. You should return to Khanâg Gur to collect your reward.Talk to Halshûm in Khanâg GurA challenge issued to all who consider themselves fearless and skilled with weapons!

Do you have what it takes to fight death, face-to-face?

A reward will be paid to the party that defeats the infamous wight called Enudâri, known to haunt the Mashâli Barrens north of the Crypts of Khâb Daku.'You have defeated Enudâri? Truly? Many braggarts said they would do this thing, but none have managed it... until now! Good work, ${PLAYER}, here is your reward.'A bounty offered for the defeat of Fer-nefâsi, an especially menacing roc.Fer-nefâsi hunts her prey in the Hills of Haramûl, located in north central An Shêru.Defeat Fer-nefâsiYou have defeated the roc Fer-nefâsi. You should return to Jiret-menêsh to collect your reward.Talk to Mísikir in Jiret-menêshReward!

A reward is offered to whoever defeats the roc known as Fer-nefâsi. This savage creature has been witnessed on several occasions harrying dwarves attempting to travel through the Hills of Haramûl. It is only a matter of time before someone is killed!'Did you rid us of that miserable bird Fer-nefâsi? What a relief! I am not sure we, the guard, could have taken her down ourselves without casualties. I did not look forward to it, but you have saved me the trouble! Here is your reward.'The malevolent spider Jûkhtar has been growing her brood and attacking Zajâni citizens near her burrow in Jâr Obadal. You are to defeat her and collect a sample of her venom.The malevolent spider Jûkhtar has been growing her brood and attacking Zajâni citizens near her burrow in Jâr Obadal. You are to defeat her and collect a sample of her venom. Bring it to Nazâkh in Zajâna, that she may give it to those who would prepare a salve to heal citizens poisoned by her children.Defeat Jûkhtar and collect her venomBring Jûkhtar's venom to Nazâkh in Zajâna to collect your reward.The bounty notice reads:

On behalf of the Doorwards of Zajâna, hallowed protectors of commerce and the Great Road, you are empowered to seek out and defeat the great spider Jûkhtar. Many innocents have been attacked and poisoned by her and her children. We ask that you collect a sample of her venom, that the scholars of Zajâna may study it and compose a healing salve for those poisoned by bites from her children.

After her defeat, bring a sample of her venom to Zajâna. Present it to Nazâkh, Huntswoman to the Doorwards, outside the council chambers in Zajâna for a proper reward.'This will save more than you know. I will give this to the Pohâni right away. They will set to work right away creating a salve to heal those afflicted by Jûkhtar and her children. Please accept this reward, with our thanks.'The dread goblin Korutásh has slain many innocent people in Sen Chatâk with his raiding parties. You are to defeat him and return to Nazâkh with his bejewelled dagger.The dread goblin Korutásh has slain many innocent people in Sen Chatâk with his raiding parties. You are to defeat him and return to Nazâkh with his bejewelled dagger. Korutásh can be found north-east of Sen Chatâk, in the hills of Glúkroz.Defeat Korutásh and collect his jewelled daggerBring Korutásh's jewelled dagger to Nazâkh in Zajâna to collect your reward.The bounty notice reads:

On behalf of the Doorwards of Zajâna, hallowed protectors of commerce and the Great Road, you are empowered to seek out and defeat the infamous goblin Korutásh the Cruel. Long have his raiding parties harried and attacked the people of Sen Chatâk and travellers along the Great Road. He can be found in the hills of Glúkroz, north-east of Sen Chatâk.

Proof of his demise shall be Korutásh's infamous bejewelled dagger. Present it to Nazâkh, Huntswoman to the Doorwards, outside the council chambers in Zajâna for a proper reward.'Saráz záro-dan. It was past time for Korutásh's reign of terror to end. Let me see it. Yes, it is a fine blade - good craftmanship, well-balanced. I will give it to one of the Bandázan, protectors of Zajâna. We will see it used for a more valorous purpose in the future.'A reward has been offered for the defeat of a grodbog called Manyêki.Manyêki can usually be found south of Jiret-menêsh in the Hills of Haramûl. You should go there and defeat it.Defeat ManyêkiYou have defeated the grodbog Manyêki. You should return to Jiret-menêsh to collect your reward.Talk to Mísikir in Jiret-menêshNotice:

A reward is offered for the slaying of Manyêki, a grodbog as ferocious as it is repulsive. Do not be fooled by its size! Manyêki is small but mighty.

This detestable creature can usually be found south of Jiret-menêsh in the Hills of Haramûl.'So, Manyêki is defeated? Very good! The road south is safer now!

'Perhaps we should offer a bounty for all of the Ordâkhai soldiers so we can finally be free of them, too!'

The dwarf laughs at the preposterous notion of putting a bounty on hundreds of people as he gives you the promised reward.You are to defeat Nâralarg, the Blighted Root before he can spread noxious disease throughout Kighân. Return to Nazâkh in Zajâna with a sample of his blighted roots to show proof of his demise.You are to defeat Nâralarg, the Blighted Root before he can spread noxious disease throughout Kighân. Return to Nazâkh in Zajâna with a sample of his blighted roots to show proof of his demise. He can be found in the blighted grove of Shádhag, near Adagím.Defeat Nâralarg and collect his blighted rootBring Nâralarg's root to Nazâkh in Zajâna to collect your reward.The bounty notice reads:

On behalf of the Doorwards of Zajâna, hallowed protectors of commerce and the Great Road, you are empowered to seek out and defeat the dread restless tree Nâralarg, the Blighted Root. He has been seen harrying the citizens of Sormedân and spreading blight and disease from Adagím into our unblemished farmlands. He can be found in the blighted grove of Shádhag, near Adagím.

Proof of his demise shall be a piece of Nâralarg's blighted root. Present it to Nazâkh, Huntswoman to the Doorwards, outside the council chambers in Zajâna for a proper reward.'Drógai! I don't believe it. That accursed tree has finally been slain. There is much that is foul in Adagím, and I think it best that those unnatural trees stay there. You have done much to prevent disease and blight from spreading into Sormedân and beyond, and for that, my friend, you have my thanks.'Shahâk, pup of the dread jázga Bloodtooth, has been harassing travellers on the Great Road north of Zajâna. Defeat her and return to Nazâkh in Zajâna with one of her fangs as proof of her demise.Shahâk, pup of the dread jázga Bloodtooth, has been harassing travellers on the Great Road north of Zajâna. Defeat her and return to Nazâkh in Zajâna with one of her fangs as proof of her demise. She is said to haunt the lands near Dân Shatagan, north-east of Zajâna.Defeat Shahâk and collect her mighty fangBring Shahâk's fang to Nazâkh in Zajâna to collect your reward.The bounty notice reads:

On behalf of the Doorwards of Zajâna, hallowed protectors of commerce and the Great Road, you are asked to seek out and defeat the dread jázga Shahâk, pup of Bloodtooth. Long have travellers of the Great Road feared Shahâk and her sharp fangs, as she has slain many. She is said to haunt the lands near Dân Shatagan, north-east of Zajâna.

The proof of her death shall be one of her bloody fangs. Present it to Nazâkh, Huntswoman to the Doorwards, outside the council chambers in Zajâna for a proper reward.'You've no idea how many travellers she and her pack have savaged. Many families will sleep safer tonight because of what you've done. You have my gratitude for your fearless deeds.'A bounty notice asks you to defeat a monstrous sicklefly called Shálith that has been spotted in Saig Hathíl in Adagím, and collect a trophy as proof.A bounty notice asks you to defeat a monstrous sicklefly called Shálith that has been spotted in Saig Hathíl in Adagím, and collect a trophy as proof.Defeat ShálithYou defeated Shálith and obtained a trophy as proof. Return to Sálunath in Sul Madásh to collect the bounty.The bounty notice reads:

'A monstrous sicklefly called Shálith has been spotted in Saig Hathíl to the north-west. The scouts in the area have requested help in defeating it.

'Bring proof to Sálunath in Sul Madásh if you complete this request.''Saig Hathíl with be safer for travellers without Shálith.

'Please take this reward for your efforts, my friend.'A bounty notice asks you to defeat a cunning bog-lurker known as Sóthadar who roams Lhámuth in Adagím, and collect a trophy as proof.A bounty notice asks you to defeat a cunning bog-lurker known as Sóthadar who roams Lhámuth in Adagím, and collect a trophy as proof.Defeat Sóthadar the TricksterYou defeated Sóthadar the Trickster and obtained a trophy as proof. Return to Sálunath in Sul Madásh to collect the bounty.The bounty notice reads:

'There is a bog-lurker known as Sóthadar who has been known to roam in Lhámuth to the north-west. This beast is especially cunning and has earned the title of the trickster as it hides itself well to attack any travelling through its waters. Slay this beast to make the marsh safer for the scouts.

'Bring proof to Sálunath in Sul Madásh if you complete this request.''We are all safer for the end of Sóthadar in Lhámuth.

'They were a tricky beast and a danger to many. Take this as payment.'A bounty notice asks you to defeat a vicious Orc named Strákhal in Fushaum Sûlm in southern Adagím, and collect a trophy as proof.A bounty notice asks you to defeat a vicious Orc named Strákhal in Fushaum Sûlm in southern Adagím, and collect a trophy as proof.Defeat Strákhal the StranglerYou defeated Strákhal the Strangler and obtained a trophy as proof. Return to Sálunath in Sul Madásh to collect the bounty.The bounty notice reads:

'A vicious and deadly Orc named Strákhal, known as The Strangler to locals, has been spotted in Fushaum Sûlm to the south-west. We can not allow these Orcs to prey on our people.

'Bring proof to Sálunath in Sul Madásh if you complete this request.''I am glad to hear that you have brought an end to Strákhal, ${CLASS}.

'He was a dangerous threat to our people. Please accept this as a reward.'A wanted poster for the defeat of one 'Têzdab the Butcher'.Têzdab the Butcher is reported as having been last seen in the vicinity of Khanâg Gur in An Shêru.Defeat Têzdab the ButcherYou have defeated Têzdab the Butcher. You should return to Khanâg Gur to collect your reward.Talk to Halshûm in Khanâg GurWanted: Têzdab 'the Butcher'

For the slaying of innocents in An Shêru. Experienced bounty hunters only!
Last seen in the vicinity of Khanâg Gur, he is ill-tempered and should be approached with caution.'Têzdab has finally been defeated, has he? A remarkable feat! Well done. Here is your reward.'A bounty notice asks you to defeat a deadly crocodile named Thagára, who roams the Lair of the Shadlúgai in Adagím, and collect a trophy as proof.A bounty notice asks you to defeat a deadly crocodile named Thagára, who roams the Lair of the Shadlúgai in Adagím, and collect a trophy as proof.Defeat ThagáraYou defeated Thagára and obtained a trophy as proof. Return to Sálunath in Sul Madásh to collect the bounty.The bounty notice reads:

'A crocodile called Thagára who roams the Lair of the Shadlúgai to the west has been a threat to travellers for too long. We ask that someone put an end to this terror.

'Bring proof to Sálunath in Sul Madásh if you complete this request.''The marsh is safer with Thagára's defeat.

'Thank you, ${CLASS}, the chieftain's reward is yours.'A wanted poster for the defeat of Újumai the Earth-stirrer, a particularly dangerous runaway war mûmak.Újumai the Earth-stirrer roams the highlands of Padugâsha in An Shêru, north-east of the Spent-lodes.Defeat Újumai the Earth-stirrerYou have defeated Újumai the Earth-stirrer. You should return to Khanâg Gur to collect your reward.Talk to Halshûm in Khanâg GurWanted: The Defeat of Újumai the Earth-stirrer

Upon the highlands of Padugâsha in An Shêru there can be found a runaway war mûmak, Újumai the Earth-stirrer. Approach this beast at your own peril!

Should any warrior be able to take the animal down, a reward will be given for the deed.'You have rid us of Újumai the Earth-stirrer? This is excellent news! That beast was as murderous as any war mûmak I have ever seen, and with no Gânda to control it, the animal was a danger to all. Thank you!'Defeat many brigands throughout An Shêru.Defeat many brigands throughout An Shêru.Defeat many brigands throughout An ShêruDefeat a great many brigands throughout An Shêru.Defeat many brigands throughout An Shêru.Defeat a great many brigands in An Shêru.Defeat a great many brigands in An ShêruDefeat many brigands skulking in Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many brigands skulking in Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many brigands in Pahar HatokáliDefeat a great many brigands skulking in Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many brigands skulking in Hatokáli Fells.Defeat a great many brigands skulking in Hatokáli Fells.Defeat a great many brigands in Hatokáli FellsDefeat many thieves throughout Idagâl.Defeat many thieves throughout Idagâl.Defeat many thieves in IdagâlDefeat a great many thieves throughout Idagâl.Defeat many thieves throughout Idagâl.Defeat a great many thieves in Idagâl.Defeat a great many thieves in IdagâlDefeat many brigands along Dûsherim, the Road of Riches, and throughout Kighân.Defeat many brigands throughout Kighân.Defeat many brigands throughout KighânDefeat a great many brigands along Dûsherim, the Road of Riches, and throughout Kighân.Defeat many brigands throughout Kighân.Defeat a great many brigands in Kighân.Defeat a great many brigands in KighânOrdâkhai overseers have come to attempt to regain control of the Esh Mêkag pit-mine.The Ordâkhai overseers have arrived to attempt to regain control of the Esh Mêkag pit-mine.

You should defeat Overseer Basóra, Overseer Purjóro, and Overseer Jóha.Defeat Overseer BasóraDefeat Overseer PurjóroDefeat Overseer JóhaYou have done much to aid the thralls revolting in Esh Mêkag.

You should return to Ebuzâm.Talk to Ebuzâm'The overseers have come from the prison to attempt to regain control of the pit-mine. They are known to us: Basóra, Purjóro, and Jóha. They are monstrous, even among the Ordâkhai, finding glee in destroying the minds and bodies of those that toil under them. Find them, and end them, for all those who have suffered here.''They are dead, then? Good riddance. May the souls of their victims find rest.'The Ordâkhai disturbed the operation of Ebnûr's farm, Kirzâmur, as they passed through Pahar Hatokáli, and now there is much to be done.Ebnûr has given you a number of tasks that will help his farm recover from the damage done to it by the Ordâkhai.Weed the dense patches of burned crops at Kirzâmur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Pick up Ebnûr's rakePick up Ebnûr's hoeClean up half of the spilled grainClean up half of the spilled grainTalk to Ebnûr's son Namtâru and tell him not to despairEbnûr is waiting at his farm for you to complete the tasks he gave to you.Namtâru has emerged from his despair and has something to say to you at his father's farm of Kirzâmur.Talk to Namtâru at his father's farm of Kirzâmur'The Ordâkhai passed through my fields as they hurried south, pursued by the forces of Shâra Mizâdi. They were not so hastened they could not cause my farm a great deal of damage, and this they did, burning crops, spilling my grain, and scattering my tools.

'Can you help me put these things right? I also ask that you speak encouraging words to my son Namtâru. He is so dispirited that he refuses to work, and that is unacceptable!''Can you help me put my farm of Kirzâmur right? I also ask that you speak encouraging words to my son Namtâru. He is so dispirited that he refuses to work, and that is unacceptable!''How can we hope to carry on? The Ordâkhai would have left our farm alone if they were not being pursued by another army! They only left Kirzâmur in ruin because they did not want Shâra Mizâdi's forces to make use of it!

'My father is too soft-hearted. He should rage against these villains, each and every one, but instead he simply accepts whatever ill fortune comes to him. I cannot believe it!''Thank you, friend. All things considered, I would say Kirzâmur will recover. We will rebuild the farm, and in mere weeks it will be as if the Ordâkhai were never here.''Ah, here is my son now.''Yes, yes, we will rebuild and the farm will be better than ever. These are just words, father!

'We cannot rebuild until the Ordâkhai have returned what they stole from us.'Phardâli bid you find Dabâr in Ahâba. Like others freed from Esh Mekag, he wishes to reward you with a tale that kept the prisoners alive while trapped in the gaol.Dabâr warns that his tale is one of caution and offers it as reward for rescuing him, and the other from the gaol. Speak with him near the bridge in the north of Ahâba.Speak with Dabâr at AhâbaDabâr paused. You should ask him to continue his tale.

You can find him near the bridge on the northern side of Ahâba.Speak with Dabâr in AhâbaDabâr paused again, conscious of the eyes upon him. He beckoned you closer to finish his tale.

You should speak with him near the bridge on the north side of Ahâba.Speak with Dabâr to hear the remainder of his story'You have come from Phardâli? Great is the debt I owe, and little in my keeping can repay such valour. I have naught of worth but a tale - and even that lies heavy upon the heart.

'It is not as gracious as the weave of Vilgêra, nor the bold song of glory spoken by Malgâras. Nay, mine is a darker telling - a warning drawn from the dust of sorrow and ruin.

'Yet such as it is, I offer it as recompense, for it is all I have, and you have saved my life.

'Will you stay a while, and hear it spoken?'There is a shift in his voice, 'The people, at last, rose against their oppressor.

'The cries of revolt thundered through the streets, demanding the cessation of the cursed construction and the sealing of the mountain's heart!

'The crowd roared in approval, a shared recognition of the power of the people's will to defy tyranny.

'Thus it was that the surviving workers, their strength spent, withdrew from the mountain.

'They sealed the entrance and put an end to the blight that had threatened them all.''We come to a tale of folly - a tale of ambition unbridled. The story of a king, whose hunger for greatness far outstripped his wisdom.

'A king whose pride cost his people a generation of artisans and labourers.'

He weaves the tale of a king who dreamed beyond measure - a dream of a citadel to surpass the grandeur of Emax Dûl itself. His vision was to carve a bastion from the very bones of the mountains themselves - mountains that even the Temámir dared not tread.

Dabâr's voice darkens, painting a grim picture as he recounts the folly of that decision: the king's heedless command to pierce the mountains, to cut into the stone where nature herself forbade it.

The workers, labouring under the king's ambition, soon began to fall ill, struck by a mysterious wasting disease that sapped their strength and life.

Dabâr speaks of bodies carried back to the hall of the king—pale and shrunken, their faces etched with a terrible sheen.

He recounts, with vivid detail, the horrors of those fifteen long years—of men and women toiling under the weight of a king's dream, even as their bodies withered and their lives dwindled.

He stops for a brief moment.'The king's folly was not his ambition; that was a fire that could have led to glory.

'No, his folly was in his refusal to listen - to heed the counsel of advisors, or to listen to those who laboured beneath his command.'

Dabâr bows his head, and you begin to ponder the sorrow, wasted lives, and lost opportunity beneath the triumph of the people. Then he breaks the silence.

'Thank you for hearing me. Heed well this tale.'Phardâli bid you find Malgâras in Ahâba. Like others freed from Esh Mekag, he wishes to reward you with a tale that kept the prisoners alive while trapped in the gaol.Malgâras bids you stay and listen to him. Speak with him beneath the canopy east of the stable-master in Ahâba.Speak with Malgâras at AhâbaMalgâras appears finished, a smile spreading on his face. Speak with him again beneath the canopy near the stable-master in Ahâba.Speak with Malgâras'Glad am I to see your face, though strange in these lands, it is welcome. You delivered us from a shadow long endured, and for that, no thanks shall suffice.

'Phardâli wisely guided you to me, though I possess little to properly reward your deeds, I wonder, will an old tale - whispered in the gloaming of my youth, recalled again in the gloom of the prison, suffice?

'Perhaps the glory it echoes will inspire you, as it did us, though the lore is strange to those in the North, and may you remember the name as one of a doom-bringer, or harbinger.

'Will you grant me patience awhile, and hear the tale?''Hearken, my people, hearken well. Hear now the tale of glory - of the Menundâri, Izighûz the Worthy, the Eternal, who led our folk from the shadow of oppression. He who raised the mighty walls of Emax Dûl. He, who watches over us still, as the Dawn-warden. He, who shall return!

'A great cheer rose from the crowd, swelling with fervour, I raised my hands, bidding them to stillness. The clamor ebbing, I continued weaving the tale of the the rise of Izighûz in glorious tapestry: a rebel leader, who struck against the North, casting down their yoke and reclaiming the land for his people; his wisdom, his strength, and his boundless life extolled with reverence.

'I invoked the statue of the Dawn-warden, shining bright as the sun's first light, and the citadel of Emax Dûl, standing firm against the ages, praising both in fervent voice.

'And - as my tale of the Eternal One reaches its zenith...'

He motions for you to step back.'If the stories of the Eternal One be true, then surely his return is at hand!'

He pauses, and offers a wry smile.

'A wave of cheers erupted - some voices loud, others hesitant, but all drawn in by the power of the tale. Yet, amidst the joyous roar, a few remain silent, their eyes darkened with doubt.

'For, not all hearts believe in the legend, and the tale, perhaps, has spun too far beyond the threads of truth to grasp. Yet, it remains a great tale of glory these lands once knew.

'Thank you, for listening, traveller. I hope this tale is reward enough for your rescue.'Phardâli bid you find Vilgêra in Ahâba. Like others freed from Esh Mekag, he wishes to reward you with a tale that kept the prisoners alive while trapped in the gaol.Vilgêra wishes to share a tale as a reward for helping to release him. Speak with him beneath the canopy near the sheep pen in Ahâba.Speak with Vilgêra at AhâbaVilgêras stops, his voice growing hoarse. He asked you to step closer to hear the remainder of the tale. He awaits you near the sheep pen in Ahâba.Speak with Vilgêras in Ahâba'I know your face, but not your name. I saw the courage in your eyes, and your well-forged strength - the kind fostered not from pride nor the lure of gold, but from a steadfast heart for a cause both just and unknown. Phardâli said he would suggest you come, and I am glad you have.

'I offer a gift - not of silver nor of blade, but of memory: a tale long kept in the halls of the wise, of our people and of the city that stands at the jewel of Kighân. Grace dwells there, and always has, and always will.

'Will you hear it?''It is the tale of how the pride of Kighân - The City of Keys - Zajâna, came into being.'

He weaves a tale of ancient wealth and boundless riches, of travellers wise and seasoned, who, long ago, carved a waystop between Shagâna and the distant lands of desert and jungle to the south.

From this humble beginning, the city blossomed, its streets laden with the promise of knowledge and the riches of the world.

The story unfurls, recounting the many triumphs of the City of Keys—its foundations built on wisdom and the exchange of lore.

Its gates opened to scholars, its halls shone with learning. From these fertile grounds, wealth and knowledge poured in, like waters flowing from an unbroken stream.

But the tale darkens then, shifting with the winds of time. A great sorrow befell the city.

Vilgera shakes his head, to ask for a moment while he mourns.'Now, Zajâna stands as a beacon of liberty and wisdom, a citadel for reason, its halls hallowed by the pursuit of truth.

'The City of Keys remains steadfast, the enduring home of scholars and keepers of lore.'

His voice softens in reverence.

'And though battered and broken, Zajâna shall endure. It shall safe-guard the wisdom, the history, and the truths of our land and our people, tended in reverence by those who seek knowledge in the City of Keys.'

He bows his head, in solemn grace.

'Thank you for listening.'The Quartermaster has requested your assistance in the continued efforts to aid the people of Mûr Ghala.<rgb=#FF0000>Complete Instances in the Mûr Ghala Cluster for the Quartermaster. Use the Instance Finder to enter Mûr Ghala Instances.</rgb>Complete Mûr Ghala instances (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with a Mûr Ghala Quartermaster in Adagím or Zajâna to accept your reward.Speak with a Mûr Ghala Quartermaster for your reward'We must assist the people of Mûr Ghala!

'I ask for your help to aid in our efforts. There are many challenges still to overcome in Mûr Ghala, and much evil still to be met in equal combat and defeated.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Complete Instances in the Mûr Ghala Instance Cluster for the Quartermaster. Use the Instance Finder to enter Mûr Ghala Instances.</rgb>'We must assist the people of Mûr Ghala!

'I ask for your help to aid in our efforts. There are many challenges still to overcome in Mûr Ghala, and much evil still to be met in equal combat and defeated.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Complete Instances in the Mûr Ghala Instance Cluster for the Quartermaster. Use the Instance Finder to enter Mûr Ghala Instances.</rgb>'Your efforts have truly assisted those who work to forge a new path for the people of Mûr Ghala.

'You will be rewarded for your brave and noble accomplishments.'The Quartermaster has requested your aid in the continued efforts to explore dangers and conquer evils within the Folly of Nagakhêdi.<rgb=#FF0000>Defeat each boss in the Folly of Nagakhêdi raid for the Quartermaster. Use the Instance Finder to enter the Folly of Nagakhêdi raid instance.</rgb>Defeat Badharál the Gorger on any tierDefeat Maukhorn on any tierDefeat the Legion of Lhaereth on any tierDefeat Zamâktar the Putrescent on any tierSpeak with a Mûr Ghala Quartermaster in Adagím or Zajâna to accept your reward.Speak with a Mûr Ghala Quartermaster for your reward'I ask for your aid in exploring the depths of the Folly of Nagakhêdi. We believe there are dangerous forces down in the depths of Nagakhêdi, hideous and unnatural foes that pose a great threat not just to Adagím but all of Mûr Ghala.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Complete instances of the Folly of Nagakhêdi raid for the Quartermaster. Use the Instance Finder to enter the Folly of Nagakhêdi raid instance.</rgb>'I ask for your aid in exploring the depths of the Folly of Nagakhêdi. We believe there are dangerous forces down in the depths of Nagakhêdi, hideous and unnatural foes that pose a great threat not just to Adagím but all of Mûr Ghala.'

<rgb=#FF0000>Complete instances of the Folly of Nagakhêdi raid for the Quartermaster. Use the Instance Finder to enter the Folly of Nagakhêdi raid instance.</rgb>'You have brought light to the darkness and slayed many foul beasts within the inky depths of the Folly of Nagakhêdi.

'You will be rewarded for your brave and noble accomplishments.'Orthonn, Ranger of the Grey Company, has requested that you spend a moment in conversation with him concerning a message he lately received.<rgb=#00FF00>It is recommended, but not required, that you complete 'The Song of Waves and Wind' before you begin this new quest.</rgb>

'${PLAYER}, my friend! You are just the person I was hoping to see. I have received a message from my kinsman Faeron, and I desired to speak with you concerning its contents.'

Orthonn pauses as a peal of thunder rumbles in the distance.

'We spent time enough in the wilderness to learn how quickly rain-clouds can spoil a pleasant day, have we not? Dagoras and I intended to meet in one of the taverns to discuss Faeron's message. We should take advantage of its roof before the rain arrives!''Summer thunderstorms may be short-lived, but they can arrive swiftly and with great ferocity! Together let us hurry to the Splintered Shield. There we can discuss the message sent to me by Faeron as he adventured in Harad, and decide what can be done about the tidings he shares.''I believe this connexion betwixt Gorgoroth and these lands was not traversable until recently, ${PLAYER}. The creation of this narrow pass began with the great shaking of Mordor following the fall of Sauron, and has only recently settled enough to grant us passage.

'I am not ashamed to say it: despite the unknown dangers that lie ahead of us, I am happy indeed to leave the swamps of Agarnaith! Even within this ravine the air feels fresher than that of the bog behind us!'You have descended from the Plateau of Gorgoroth into Heledhris with your companions, bravely preparing to face the unknown.You must pass through the Horror-cut, the ravine that lies between Gorgoroth and Heledhris, and meet up with your companions on its eastern side.Pass through the Horror-cut and meet up with your companions to the eastHarthalín and Thrymm Red-beard study the wild lands that lie east of the Horror-cut.Talk to Harthalín east of the Horror-cutTalk to Thrymm Red-beard east of the Horror-cutThrymm and Harthalín agree that you should defeat the wild-eyed and threatening fighters of Heledhris and also collect some of the bats that swarm nearby. Studying these creatures for sign of Lhaereth's tampering may tell Harthalín if the bats came here from Agarnaith.Harthalín is east of the Horror-cut that connects Gorgoroth to Heledhris. You have collected a number of the bats that swarm in Heledhris and should bring them to Harthalín for study.Ranger Orthonn stands east of the Horror-cut in Heledhris.Talk to Orthonn east of the Horror-cut'Has my excitement betrayed itself? I confess to it!

'You already know of my interest in cartography, ${PLAYER}, and here we have an opportunity to expand the borders of our known map! We must remain alert to any threats as we travel eastward, of course... but I will also remain alert to any notable geologic features we encounter, and when we stop to rest I will add them to the map I intend to prepare.

'Onward, then, with haste and with awareness of every footfall!''We must remain alert to any threats as we travel eastward, of course... but I will also remain alert to any notable geologic features we encounter, and when we stop to rest I will add them to the map I intend to prepare. Onward, with haste and with awareness of every footfall!''The crevice through which we came here from Gorgoroth seems of recent creation. Mordor has always been a land of tumult, but during the years of Sauron's return, Mount Doom regularly erupted with violence. With the eye of my mind I can see towering cliffsides sheared away, their rocky burdens cascading from the heights into the valleys below. Is it any wonder we overlooked this passage until now?

'We are dependent upon this rocky pass, but those with wings are not! Agarnaith is much nearer for them than it seems to us, and if the bats I see around us came from that swamp, we should study them for any sign of experimentation by Lhaereth or her servants. They may tell us if the Lady of Blight came this way from Seregost before we arrived.''The wind whips across these hills, picking up tiny shards of stone and casting them in our faces! Already have I been stung by this grit, and made unwelcome!'

Thrymm tips his head to one side, listening.

'But the wind carries something else upon it, ${PLAYER}. Hear you the sounds of battle, and the harsh cries of warriors? There are fighters not far from here, and their guttural cries remind me of the Orcs I have slain. They are denizens of Mordor, and if they desire battle Thrymm Red-beard will give it to them, and gladly!''We are dependent upon this rocky pass, but those with wings are not! Agarnaith is much nearer for them than it seems to us, and if the bats I see around us came from that swamp, we should study them for any sign of experimentation by Lhaereth or her servants. They may tell us if the Lady of Blight came this way from Seregost before we arrived.''There are fighters not far from here, and their guttural cries remind me of the Orcs I have slain. They are denizens of Mordor, and if they desire battle Thrymm Red-beard will give it to them, and gladly!''I hope the creatures gave you little trouble, ${PLAYER}, and that you were not bitten or scratched by them. We will soon know if Lhaereth used these bats for experimentation with her plague, but if she did...'

Harthalín falls silent as she takes the bodies from you and studies them closely. After a moment she looks at you with a relieved expression.

'If these bats flew from Agarnaith above the Mithram Spur and came thus to Heledhris, they overcame whatever illness they might once have suffered; I see in them no sign of Lhaereth's contagion. We should not lower our guard overmuch, but I do not think the Lady of Blight has come to this place.''We should not lower our guard overmuch, but I do not think the Lady of Blight has come to this place.''Lhaereth may not have come to this land, but it remains part of Mordor and may therefore conceal any number of hidden threats. The ferocious fighters against whom Thrymm is eager to test his blade tells me that, if nothing else will this day!'Orthonn has always been interested in geography and the making of maps, and he is eager to chart the unexplored lands east of Gorgoroth.Thrymm is curious about the wild-eyed men he saw filling bags with stones at Balthlún to the south-west.Collect filled pouches from Khûrz-hai at Balthlún (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Someone has called out to you near Balthlún in Heledhris.You feel eyes upon you'There are few detailed maps of Mordor in the White City. Those I have seen were prepared by the soldiers of the Conquest and they were interested mainly in the defensive fortifications throughout Gorgoroth.

'But I remember the general shape of the land east of the plateau, and believe our course will take us to the banks of a swift-flowing river, the Aegdin, or Glittertine. We will not know if it can be easily-crossed until we get there.''Our course will take us eastward to the banks of a swift-flowing river, the Aegdin, or Glittertine. We will not know if it can be easily-crossed until we get there.''There are more of those rage-filled warriors to the south-west, but unlike the others these seem to have been given a strange task. They carry satchels with them, bulging pouches they fill with stones. Do their leaders put some value upon these rocks?

'Orthonn and I were just praising the construction of this bridge for keeping us out of the river, but if we are to investigate this curious business to the south-west we will need to get wet after all. Ha! That is no matter for a man of Rohan, if it is no problem for you, ${PLAYER}!''If we are to investigate this curious business to the south-west we will need to get wet after all. Ha! That is no matter for a man of Rohan, if it is no problem for you, ${PLAYER}!''You fight Khûrz-hai? Very brave stranger to dare face anger of Khûrz-hai at Balthlún!'

This stout woman is similar in build and appearance to the Woses you have elsewhere encountered, in the Drúadan Forest and at Bhol Rûdh in nearby Agarnaith, but to your eye she belongs to neither of those family lines.

'Never see Khemozêl before today?' she asks. 'We live long in hills, but shaking of earth greatly change face of land. Once we were hidden. Less hidden now.'You have met Kâl-maka-Hôi, a Drúadan woman of the Mithram Hills.Kâl-maka-Hôi has suggested that you help her complete some of the tasks with which she was charged when she departed her village, and that such service will earn you a welcome at Dhol Têg.Defeat ashen bark wood-trolls in Heledhris (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect goltur steaks in Heledhris (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect lizard meat in Heledhris (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Talk to Kâl-maka-Hôi outside Dhol TêgA Khemozêl man has overheard some of Kâl-maka-Hôi's words and approaches you outside the village of Dhol Têg.'I am named Kâl-maka-Hôi. What name is yours?'

You introduce yourself and say you have travelled far from your home to oppose the dangers that stalk this valley and threaten to spill from it. The stout woman laughs.

'Evil for you is like jug of water? Spill it and let disappear? Ha! Khemozêl not believe that.

'Others like you nearby? Kâl-maka-Hôi meet them?''Others like you nearby? Kâl-maka-Hôi meet them?''Friends different as stripes in stone!''I did not expect to see one of the Woses in this place! Her people must be estranged from her kin in the Drúadan Forest, for that is many miles from here and surely they cannot have maintained contact over that span without the Men of the West knowing of it.

'It was only through the guidance of the Wild Men that my people reached Minas Tirith in time during the War of the Ring, and for that alone she has my friendship and the use of my sword-arm!''There is a settlement of Drúedain at Bhol Rûdh in Agarnaith. When I searched that swamp for the presence of Lhaereth and her servants, I befriended the Red Sky Clan and they were of great help to me. They must have become separated from others of their people over the years, though record of their lost kin survived.

'We should assist Kâl-maka-Hôi as much as we can, for her familiarity with this land could be invaluable to us.'Orthonn stares at the Khemozêl woman with astonishment.

'I was never able to meet any of the Drúedain of the Drúadan Forest, ${PLAYER}, for I was aboard one of the Black Ships when King Théoden and the Rohirrim encountered them. I am filled with delight at this meeting!

'Think you that Kâl-maka-Hôi will introduce us to others of her people? They are certain to know if Sauron's influence extended into this valley, and if it remains a danger.''For the actions of her distant Wose kin, she has my friendship and the use of my sword-arm!''We should assist Kâl-maka-Hôi as much as we can, for her familiarity with this land could be invaluable to us.''Think you that Kâl-maka-Hôi will introduce us to others of her people?''Here is place.''This village of Dhol Têg, where Khemozêl live.

'One thing to ask: say not where you met Kâl-maka-Hôi. She not permitted to go so near to Balthlún. Others not understand why she go there.

'Tell others not? You agree?'Kâl-maka-Hôi has frozen in place, a guilty expression upon her face.'Strangers come to Dhol Têg, invited by Kâl-maka-Hôi? I not take away invitation! Prêkh-weni-Pâsh know when foes be near, and he name you ally, if not yet friend. Even so: I not shame Kâl-maka-Hôi for bringing you here!

'But this place kept safe by Khemozêl. Cause trouble and know death.'You have been introduced to the Khemozêl of Dhol Têg, and should learn what you can of their wants and their needs.Prêkh-weni-Pâsh has suggested that you visit several of the Khemozêl and <rgb=#00FF00>bow</rgb> to them by way of introduction.One of the Khemozêl standing nearby sees you studying the wooden carving and begins to speak in a low, sonorous tone. She tells you that this carving represents many of her people that have been slain by the were-wolves in the woods of Nan Ogol to the north. It was the habit of the crafter who fashioned this reminder of the fallen to etch additional wounds onto it for each new victim of the beasts... but after the passage of several years there was no more space on the carving for this practice to continue.The Khemozêl woman follows your gaze to this second carving and relates the story of a once-respected warrior of her people who slew his rival in a fit of passion and fled from the village, never again to be seen by any who live in Dhol Têg.

She tells you the carving represents the victim, Bhêg-buri-Chât, and that the name of the murderer is no longer spoken aloud for fear of calling him near.'Prêkh-weni-Pâsh sent you here? He use sad stories as excuse not to fight.

'I hear these stories and learn something else. I learn Dhol Têg in danger. I learn Khemozêl cannot hide forever.

'Some of my people go to Nan Ogol. Even grand-daughter of the chief go! They intend to fight. Kâl-maka-Hôi want to join them... but still deciding. Not easy choice.''Kâl-maka-Hôi want to join them... but still deciding. Not easy choice.''You listen to stories? Then you know Khemozêl very brave, but elders and youth disagree on best course of action.

'I not afraid to fight! But youth not understand history of our people. Youth hear tales of past and think storytellers stretch truth. But it not so.

'This land once belong to Khemozêl, but no longer. Now were-wolves have dominion.'Prêkh-weni-Pâsh wants to enlist your aid and that of your companions on behalf of the Khemozêl against the foes arrayed against them.Collect salamander hides in Heledhris (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect therapsid claws in Heledhris (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Prêkh-weni-Pâsh not wish to speak of them, but he must. If you walk these paths were-wolves will find you, soon or late; and you not have tricks of Khemozêl. Beware wolf-kind, in all its forms! They are cunning hunters, with no shortage of evil scheme at hand.''Beware wolf-kind, in all its forms! They are cunning hunters, with no shortage of evil scheme at hand.''I am confused, friend. Prêkh-weni-Pâsh speaks of these were-wolves as if they possess the thoughts of men. Are they not beasts?'

Thrymm's eyebrows knit together as his forehead creases with thought. A sudden realization lightens his features.

'Or perhaps they are skin-changers, like old Grimbeorn? Do they take on the form of a wolf as he takes on the form of a bear? Have I solved this mystery?''Or perhaps they are skin-changers, like old Grimbeorn?''No, Red-Bearded One. Were-wolves not change from one shape to another. But different types of wolf, different types of were-wolf. Different in power, different in evil!

'Prêkh-weni-Pâsh explain.''Listen to Prêkh-weni-Pâsh. He share wisdom of our foe.'Prêkh-weni-Pâsh speaks first of the Gaurhoth, mightiest of the were-wolves that served Sauron. Bred by the Dark Lord long ago and imbued with powerful fell-spirits, they grew to tremendous size and became the largest and most intelligent of his wolf-kind, sires of a cruel and vindictive bloodline. Steeped in twisted sorcery, the Gaurhoth possess the power of speech and use it to cow lesser beings, though the Khemozêl proudly tells you that his people are resistant to such intimidation and choose death over servitude. The Gaurhoth form the leadership of the were-wolf power structure in north-eastern Mordor, and they gave to this land the name Draugardh: the Wolven-lands.

Prêkh-weni-Pâsh further tells you that unlike the wargs and wolves with which you may be familiar, Gaurhoth bites are venomous and can inflict a terrible madness in their victims.

'If survive bite,' he says meaningfully.'Listen to Prêkh-weni-Pâsh. He share wisdom of our foe.'Prêkh-weni-Pâsh speaks to you of another creature of wolf-kind created by the Gaurhoth and made to serve their fell purposes: the Draugrim, lesser in power and size than their masters but rivalling them in malice. These lesser were-wolves can stand upright, but fall to all fours to run at great speed after their prey.

The people of Dhol Têg feel a great loathing for the Draugrim, for in the melding of man-like and beast-like features they see a cruel mockery of the Khemozêl.

'Draugrim found in greater numbers than their masters,' Prêkh-weni-Pâsh continues. 'But Gaurhoth quick to punish servants, even with death. Draugrim not dare to disobey.''Listen to Prêkh-weni-Pâsh. He share wisdom of our foe.'Prêkh-weni-Pâsh tells you not to underestimate any of the were-wolves you encounter, whether they be powerful Gaurhoth or fierce Draugrim.

'One more foe,' he continues. 'This one not were-wolf. This one Man.'

The Khemozêl describes a clan of nomadic warriors, the Khashkhilar, who came out of the East and devoted their lives to the worship of the Gaurhoth. They live now on the rocky grassland of Parth Rhavas and revere the were-wolves even as they are slain by them.

With a noise that sounds to your ear quite rude, Prêkh-weni-Pâsh makes it clear what he thinks of the Khashkhilar.'I am grateful to Prêkh-weni-Pâsh for describing the villains arrayed before us, ${PLAYER}, but his explanation has raised further questions in my mind.

'Where were the were-wolves during the War of the Ring? Wolves and wargs fought alongside the armies of Sauron, but I have heard no report of such evils as the Gaurhoth or their bipedal Draugrim servants engaging in battle at the Black Gate or on the Plateau of Gorgoroth. Why would the Dark Lord not make use of every servant at his disposal, unless he possessed some reason unknown to us? It is a mystery to me.

'You know of the Masters of Mordor who fought among themselves following the fall of Sauron, ${PLAYER}; there were no were-wolves among their ranks. Judging from the words of Prêkh-weni-Pâsh, I would have expected one or more of the Gaurhoth to covet power in Mordor. If the pass to Draugardh was clear, why did they not emerge to challenge the others for dominance? There is more going on here than we yet understand.''There is more going on here than we yet understand.''You bring hides and claws? Prêkh-weni-Pâsh pleased at this, but heart not full of gladness! You keep secret from him.'Prêkh-weni-Pâsh has told you of the dangers posed by the dread-sheen flakes collected by Kâl-maka-Hôi, and wants your help to dispose of them.Prêkh-weni-Pâsh has requested your help to dispose of the dread-sheen flakes collected by Kâl-maka-Hôi, but your other companions have their own objectives to complete.Harthalín and Orthonn have departed on their own objectives.Wait for Harthalín and Orthonn to depart'You not say you meet Kâl-maka-Hôi outside mine called Balthlún. She know place not for Khemozêl! Dread-sheen found there, corrupting stone prized by were-wolves. Sickly green crystal found deep in earth. Dread-sheen turn darker as hatred grows.

'Prêkh-weni-Pâsh knew something not right. He learn Kâl-maka-Hôi go to Balthlún to collect dread-sheen... she admit it to him! She think crystal bestow courage, but it not true. She give flakes of dread-sheen she found to Prêkh-weni-Pâsh to dispose.

'You help get rid of dread-sheen? Prêkh-weni-Pâsh understand if companions have other business, but Khemozêl welcome help if offered.''You help get rid of dread-sheen? Prêkh-weni-Pâsh understand if companions have other business, but Khemozêl welcome help if offered.''I encourage you to aid the Khemozêl with this task, ${PLAYER}, but I am still concerned that we know so little about the ruling power in this corner of Mordor. If you will allow it, I would like to scout the lands further to the east and see what I might learn of the were-wolves of Draugardh and their subjects.

'I will find you once I have learned more of this place, my friend. You have my word upon it.''Elves and Rangers relish the opportunity to go scouting in the wilderness, it seems! As for this Man of Rohan, I will help you and our new friend with his task. This evil material he describes, this dread-sheen, is not found in Rohan. I believe him when he says we should dispose of it!''This evil material he describes, this dread-sheen, is not found in Rohan. I believe him when he says we should dispose of it!''Prêkh-weni-Pâsh heard horn-calls from tower. Not first time, but not common. Something wrong? One of your companions in trouble?'The horn-blasts you heard sounded from the direction of Ost Morthil, the tower located in southern Heledhris. Has something happened?Orthonn has joined you at the location from which he spied upon Ost Morthil.The men who once guarded this entrance to Ost Morthil have been slain.Examine the body of the slain guard at the side entrance to Ost MorthilOrthonn is at the unguarded side entrance to Ost Morthil.Talk to Orthonn at the unguarded side entrance to Ost Morthil'Fifty years past, enemies of Khemozêl carve tower from black stone. Use horn-calls to send messages, but Prêkh-weni-Pâsh not hear blasts like this for long time. Something happen at Tower of Black Thorn.''Prêkh-weni-Pâsh not hear horn-blasts like this for long time. Something happen at Tower of Black Thorn.''I am here!''Let us get closer to the tower, but remain on your guard.

'Something is not right.''Let us get closer to the tower, but remain on your guard.

'Something is not right.''Who... or what... has slain these guards?''These guards were slain by wolves or by were-wolves?

'What is happening in this land, ${PLAYER}?'Orthonn insists that you must take advantage of this opportunity to learn what your foes are up to in Draugardh by making use of the unguarded side entrance, no matter the danger.Orthonn is at the unguarded side entrance to Ost Morthil, waiting to delve within in search of useful information.Make use of the unguarded side entrance to infiltrate Ost MorthilOrthonn waits to speak with you at Dhol Têg to discuss what you learned within Ost Morthil.Talk to Orthonn at Dhol Têg'It may be dangerous, but we cannot let this opportunity to learn what transpired within pass us by. We should make use of this side entrance to enter Ost Morthil.

'Something slew these guards and desired to pass within. I want to know for what purpose this unseen aggressor sought to pass inside!''We should make use of this side entrance to enter Ost Morthil. Only then might we learn who slew these guards, and for what purpose they sought to gain admittance to the tower.''I do not regret that our steps carried us into Ost Morthil, ${PLAYER}, but my mind is now more awhirl with confusion than it was before!

'What will this power struggle between the Gúrzyul Nûlbanath and Narchraw the Flesh-render mean for the Khemozêl of this land? What will it mean for us?

'And where is the former ruler of Ost Morthil, Mûlazar Dark-star?'Having learned of the situation in Draugardh from your infiltration of Ost Morthil, you must now let that information guide your steps as you progress further into the wild lands.Kâl-maka-Hôi has overheard your words with Orthonn and wants to tell you what she knows of Mûlazar Dark-star.Talk to Kâl-maka-Hôi in Dhol TêgPrêkh-weni-Pâsh is in Dhol Têg and has opinions to share.Talk to Prêkh-weni-Pâsh in Dhol TêgKâl-maka-Hôi has run to retrieve her weapon.Wait for Kâl-maka-Hôi to departPrêkh-weni-Pâsh is in Dhol Têg.Talk to Prêkh-weni-Pâsh in Dhol TêgPrêkh-weni-Pâsh asked you to collect pygmy drake wings and craban meat in Heledhris you can deliver as an offering to the sentries of Khel Wêro.Collect pygmy drake wings in Heledhris (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect craban meat in Heledhris (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'I judge he and Nûlbanath must belong to the ranks of the Gúrzyul, like those others who sought to dominate Mordor following the defeat of Sauron. Did Mûlazar extend his reach too far and run afoul of his ambition, as did others of that kind in Gorgoroth? I cannot say for certain, but it seems likely.

'At least for now, his consort Nûlbanath is equally in the dark as we are.''Did Mûlazar extend his reach too far and run afoul of his ambition, as did others of the Gúrzyul? I cannot say for certain, but it seems likely. At least for now, his consort Nûlbanath is equally in the dark as we are.''Cruelty of Mûlazar known to us. He hunt Khemozêl for sport over many years. In time he abandon such game, for we learn to disappear when he looses his hunters. Now he the one to vanish? This land better for it.

'Dark Lord give rule over were-wolves to him, but they never love him. Once he rule from Nan Ogol, but he come to live in tower of Black Thorn years ago. Surround himself with Men and Orcs, not with wolves.

'If you adventure eastward, bring Kâl-maka-Hôi? She know when big deeds await, and will be help to you who not know this land.''If you adventure eastward, bring Kâl-maka-Hôi? She know when big deeds await, and will be help to you who not know this land.''Prêkh-weni-Pâsh not old for his people, but he old enough to remember many evils of Mûlazar. That one kill for Dark Lord, but not only when commanded. Khemozêl know he kill for little reason, or none at all.

'He fly in air on winged beast between tower of Black Thorn and old stronghold in Nan Ogol. Ancestors of Khemozêl say Mûlazar stalk this land even then, and no different. He not die as others do.

'Prêkh-weni-Pâsh go with you. Khemozêl not leave this duty to strangers.''I think our wose friend is mistaken about something, ${PLAYER}. Cyneberg would not be satisfied with this outcome, and I think Kâl-maka-Hôi will not either.''You bring these on behalf of Khemozêl of Dhol Têg? Then welcome. But why come here?'

You briefly relate that you are seeking to ensure that these lands are not home to some new evil that might threaten Gondor, and that you seek to learn what might have befallen the missing Gúrzyul Mûlazar. The sentry stares at you for a long moment, and then gurgles with laughter.

'New evil? Evils here very old, stranger. Older than tree, older than stone!'Khel Wêro is the last Khemozêl Drúedain outpost before the wide grasslands of Parth Rhavas, where your investigation must continue.Ranger Orthonn stands within Khel Wêro, waiting to speak with you.Talk to Orthonn inside Khel WêroPrêkh-weni-Pâsh has arrived at Khel Wêro, and he is not alone.Talk to Prêkh-weni-Pâsh inside Khel WêroKâl-maka-Hôi has come to Khel Wêro.Talk to Kâl-maka-Hôi inside Khel WêroThrymm Red-beard stands within Khel Wêro, an amused smile on his face.Talk to Thrymm Red-beard inside Khel WêroPrêkh-weni-Pâsh stands within Khel Wêro, but he is already preparing to leave it.Talk to Prêkh-weni-Pâsh inside Khel WêroThrymm observed a number of enemies on the plains that he desires to test against his strength, and yours, as you descend into Parth Rhavas.Defeat nightgangs in Parth Rhavas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat grims in Parth Rhavas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})'Khemozêl live in hidden vale many years, hidden from enemies. But earth shake when Dark Lord build tower in Gorgoroth. Great crack appear in Greywall Hills where once none. Now eastern way to wide lands, like open door.

'We make Khel Wêro to watch way through Greywall. Friends welcome here... if oppose were-wolves and their allies. We not see Mûlazar in some time. If he dead, Khemozêl rejoice.''We make Khel Wêro to watch way through Greywall. Friends welcome here... if oppose were-wolves and their allies. We not see Mûlazar in some time. If he dead, Khemozêl rejoice.''It would appear that Prêkh-weni-Pâsh's plan has hit a snag, ${PLAYER}.''It would appear that Prêkh-weni-Pâsh's plan has hit a snag.''Kâl-maka-Hôi refuse to stay behind. If she give me her weapon, it as if she here, but without danger! But she not convinced.

'If Kâl-maka-Hôi die, I not weep. She young and foolish! She know danger, and ignore wisdom of all elders.  No one blame Prêkh-weni-Pâsh if young Khemozêl not return unharmed to Dhol Têg.''Kâl-maka-Hôi young and foolish! She know danger, and ignore wisdom of all elders.  No one blame Prêkh-weni-Pâsh if young Khemozêl not return unharmed to Dhol Têg.''Prêkh-weni-Pâsh say he wield my weapons in battle, and it as if I there too? I tell him I follow anyway, but then Kâl-maka-Hôi have no weapons. Much more dangerous, and then Prêkh-weni-Pâsh to blame if she die.

'Kâl-maka-Hôi big help to you. Only fool like Prêkh-weni-Pâsh not see it.''Kâl-maka-Hôi big help to you. Only fool like Prêkh-weni-Pâsh not see it.'Thrymm wears an amused expression. After a moment, he speaks.

'Kâl-maka-Hôi reminds me of my own Cyneberg, ${PLAYER}. Had she not been needed in Wildermore following Núrzum's trail of devastation there, no words could have kept her from following me to war in the Wold and then to Gondor!

'These Khemozêl are hardy folk, and are not wanting in courage!''These Khemozêl are hardy folk, and are not wanting in courage!''I am sorry to disturb you, stranger, but your presence in this land speaks loudly.

'May I ask if you are a friend of one named Harthalín?'You are following in the footsteps of Harthalín, who came to Parth Rhavas some time before you in search of answers.You have found Harthalín at the Wraith's Leap.Talk to Harthalín at the Wraith's LeapHarthalín has asked you to learn what you can about the Order of the Eye cultists who attacked her.Examine one of the Order of the Eye corpses created by HarthalínThe Ranger Orthonn is at the Wraith's Leap in Parth Rhavas.Talk to Orthonn at the Wraith's LeapThrymm Red-beard is at the Wraith's Leap.Talk to Thrymm Red-beard at the Wraith's LeapThrymm asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> out over the great drop at the Wraith's Leap.The Ranger Orthonn is at the Wraith's Leap in Parth Rhavas.Talk to Orthonn at the Wraith's LeapHarthalín is at the Wraith's Leap, in Parth Rhavas.Talk to Harthalín at the Wraith's LeapHarthalín believes she has encountered the wolf-wraith Narchraw in a different Age, when it wore a different name.Harthalín is at the Wraith's Leap in Parth Rhavas.Talk to Harthalín and hear what she has to say about the mighty wolf that terrorized the Great Alliance at the end of the Second AgeHarthalín is at the Wraith's Leap in Parth Rhavas.Talk to Harthalín at the Wraith's LeapHarthalín promised to aid Khálya the Têtikir with some of the problems faced by her people in Parth Rhavas.Defeat Khashkilar throughout Parth Rhavas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect goltur haunches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Pick pungent flowers near Sûlok herds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Several different Easterling tribes have come to Parth Rhavas, and each of them struggles to coexist with the others.Vermâkha stares at you with barely-concealed rage.Remain on your guardThe village of Kol Sákla is in an uproar!Talk to Núrzalat at the entrance to Kol SáklaThe Têtikir residents of Kôl Sakla speak of a terrifying raid that recently devastated their town.Khálya is just inside the entrance of Kôl Sakla.Talk to Khálya at the entrance of Kôl SaklaKhálya has asked you to find out what befell the people of Kôl Sakla during the recent raid.Khálya has asked you to find out what befell the people of Kôl Sakla during the recent raid.The Têtikir Tarásh may have seen where the attackers went following their raid on Kol Sákla.Talk to Thrymm Red-beard in Kôl SaklaYour companions have joined you in Kôl Sakla following the raid upon its people.Talk to Prêkh-weni-Pâsh in Kôl SaklaTalk to Kâl-maka-Hôi in Kôl SaklaTalk to Orthonn in Kôl SaklaTalk to Harthalín in Kôl SaklaTalk to Khálya in Kol SáklaSomething disturbed the stark-crows at Ata-gabar.Defeat Stark-crows at Ata-gabar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Harthalín has joined you at Ata-gabar.Talk to Harthalín at Ata-gabarThe raiders from Bâr Guruthos remain ahead of you, but they and their captives are not yet out of your reach.Harthalín refuses to allow the raiders to escape back to Bâr Guruthos without confrontation.Talk to Harthalín and continue your pursuit of the raidersThe raiders from BG have been slain, but their Têtikir captives escaped into the wild forest of Nan Ogol. You should rescue them before they run afoul of the dangers within the fell vale.Travel to the entrance of Kûs ChelaTalk to Stôr-weni-Kûl in Kûs ChelaTalk to Kâl-maka-Hôi in Kûs ChelaThe Drúedain have asked you to defeat Draugrim and Khashkilar throughout Nan Ogol while you search for the Têtikir who fled from Narchraw.Defeat Draugrim in Nan Ogol (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Khashkilar in Nan Ogol (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have found one of the escaped Têtikir, but he is dead.Examine the body of the slain TêtikirOrthonn says you cannot give up on your pursuit of the remaining Têtikir.Search the cave for the Têtikir escapeeThe Drúedain of Nan Ogol must have used this cave as an outpost, but they should not mind if you take advantage of its comforts for a time.Thrymm Red-beard sees no reason you should not make use of this cave to rest and recover your strength.Talk to Thrymm Red-beard and recover your strengthThe cave's master has returned.Ghôl-buri-Prân, the master of Koi-mêdh-twar, has returned to his home.Prêkh-weni-Pâsh is at the cave of Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Prêkh-weni-Pâsh at Koi-mêdh-twarGhôl-buri-Prân is at the cave of Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Ghôl-buri-Prân at Koi-mêdh-twarYour companions have intruded upon the home of Ghôl-buri-Prân and now seek his forgiveness.Talk to Thrymm Red-beard at Koi-mêdh-twarTalk to Harthalín at Koi-mêdh-twarTalk to Kâl-maka-Hôi at Koi-mêdh-twarTalk to Maurán at Koi-mêdh-twarGhôl-buri-Prân is at the cave of Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Ghôl-buri-Prân at Koi-mêdh-twarCollect kindling for Ghôl-buri-Prân (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Ghôl-buri-Prân is at the cave of Koi-mêdh-twar.Ghôl-buri-Prân has explained the Drúadan concept of Khem-khai to you, but he wants you to demonstrate that you understand its meaning.Ghôl-buri-Prân waits for you at his cave of Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Ghôl-buri-Prân at his cave of Koi-mêdh-twarGhôl-buri-Prân was impressed by the deeds of Kâl-maka-Hôi, and has decided to share with you a secret.Ghôl-buri-Prân is at the cave of Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Ghôl-buri-Prân at Koi-mêdh-twar and become privy to his secretGhôl-buri-Prân is in Mur Rámtor.Talk to Ghôl-buri-Prân in Mur RámtorGhôl-buri-Prân is unwilling to leave Mûlazar unguarded, but there are tasks undone that must be completed.Ghôl-buri-Prân has asked you to select one of your companions to remain on guard duty within Mur Rámtor.Mûlazar Dark-star is now interested to speak with you in Mur Rámtor.Talk to Mûlazar Dark-star in Mur RámtorIt is now your turn to guard the prisoner.Mûlazar has promised to behave while you remain on guard duty in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Mûlazar and take your turn guarding the prisoner in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twarMûlazar is in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Mûlazar in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twarSomeone descends into Mur Rámtor.Wait for the one who approaches to arriveOrthonn has come to Mur Rámtor, and he looks unhappy about something.Talk to Orthonn in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twarOrthonn and Harthalín have returned to Mur Rámtor with terrible news: one of your companions has been seized by the enemy that dwells within Bâr Guruthos.Harthalín has returned to Mur Rámtor following her ordeal in Nan Ogol.Talk to Harthalín in Mur RámtorMûlazar remains a captive within Mur Rámtor, but his demeanour has changed.Talk to Mûlazar in Mur RámtorGhôl-buri-Prân is filled with rage at the prospect that you might free Mûlazar.Talk to Ghôl-buri-Prân in Mur RámtorGhôl-buri-Prân requires you to do something before you even consider negotiating with the prisoner, and he will not relent.Ghôl-buri-Prân is in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Ghôl-buri-Prân in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twarRanger Orthonn is in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Orthonn in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twarMûlazar is willing to tell you what he knows... for a price.Mûlazar may be willing to tell you what you want to know... but not without cost.Talk to Mûlazar in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twarMûlazar Dark-star has a number of demands you must satisfy before he will tell you anything.Complete 'Mûlazar: His Hated Foes'Complete 'Mûlazar: His Resentful Spirit'Complete 'Mûlazar: His Loyal Steed'Complete 'Mûlazar: His Waiting Consort'Mûlazar is in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Wait for Mûlazar's responseMûlazar is in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Mûlazar in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twarMûlazar's condition has worsened. Will he give you the information you need before he succumbs to the venom that courses through his veins?Harthalín is in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Harthalín in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twarMûlazar is in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Despite his deteriorating condition, Mûlazar has refused to drink the water you brought him.Wait for Mûlazar to recoverMûlazar is in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Mûlazar in Mur RámtorOrthonn is in Mur Rámtor.Talk to Orthonn in Mur RámtorThyrsings outside Cebir Ruith may have carried off the contents of the lost saddle-bag.Collect assorted trinkets from the Thyrsings near Cebir Ruith (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Mûlazar is in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Mûlazar has told you of a secret way into Bâr Guruthos with which you might rescue your captured companion.Ghôl-buri-Prân is in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Ghôl-buri-Prân in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twarHarthalín is unsettled by the sight of flames deep in the forest as you return from Bâr Guruthos.The footsteps lead toward the cave of Koi-mêdh-twar.Return to Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twarGhôl-buri-Prân has been grievously wounded within Mur Rámtor.Talk to Ghôl-buri-Prân in Mur RámtorYou achieved the success you sought, but not without cost.All is quiet within Mur Rámtor.Stand beside Ghôl-buri-Prân during his final momentsGhôl-buri-Prân asked you to remove the necklace of delothlin he wore.Remove Ghôl-buri-Prân's delothlin necklace as he requestedThrymm Red-beard stands in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Thrymm Red-beard in Mur RámtorPrêkh-weni-Pâsh and Kâl-maka-Hôi stand in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Prêkh-weni-Pâsh in Mur RámtorTalk to Kâl-maka-Hôi in Mur RámtorYou should go upstairs to meet with Harthalín and Orthonn outside the cave of Koi-mêdh-twar.Climb upstairs and look for Harthalín and Orthonn outside the cave of Koi-mêdh-twar.You have returned to Minas Tirith with both the companions you departed with and some you befriended during the journey.Orthonn knows of a place where you should be able to speak with your companions in peace.Talk to Orthonn and go with him to a place where you can speak in peaceThe Ordâkhai still fight for control of Emax Dûl.Many Ordâkhai still fight in the streets for control of Emax Dûl.

