You should talk to Captain Hanâbu outside Jolakhúro.Talk to Captain HanâbuMizâdi has gone ahead with her Subuzûri to claim the bridge to Emax Dûl.

You should meet Mizâdi just up the road from Jolakhúro.Meet Mizâdi at the bridge to Emax Dûl'Even if we cannot be sure that Kotráka Saiya's help will turn the tide of the coming battle in our favour, the time to act is now. Góramul Sai knows we are here, and will attack Ahâba again unless we can push him into a defensive position in his fortress. You will begin that push.

'There is an Ordâkhai camp between here and Emax Dûl called Jolakhúro. I want you and Captain Hanâbu to attack it. This will both force them to retreat behind their walls, and clear the road for the rest of our troops to get into position to siege the city.

'The Captain has already left with enough Aradûni to attack the camp. Meet him there. I will learn what I can from Kotráka Saiya, and our strategy will be set in motion.''Ah, the hero of Esh Mêkag has arrived! I look forward to fighting by your side! Scout Arâniz told me everything. There is no need to be modest, you did a great good freeing all those prisoners from that horrible place!

'Now, let us turn to the battle at hand. We must dismantle this camp and clear the road for our forces.''The Ordâkhai are in disarray! Excellent work. Our forces should be able to mop up the rest as they march toward the gates of Emax Dûl.

'Shâra Mizâdi came through with her Subuzûri while you were at the camp. They intend to take control of this side of the bridge to Emax Dûl. You should go ahead and see if she needs your help. It should be just up this road.''They were no match for the Subuzûri. We now hold this side of the bridge, but we do not want the Ordâkhai to know this quite yet. Our plan depends on it.'The Ordâkhai forward camp needs to be cleared before Mizâdi's forces can move into position outside Emax Dûl.The Ordâkhai camp, Jolakhúro, must be cleared in preparation for the arrival of Mizâdi's allied forces.

You should help the Aradûni soldiers defeat the Ordâkhai and their leader, Orihóta Bóro.Defeat Ordâkhai in Jolakhúro (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Orihóta BóroThe Ordâkhai in Jolakhúro have been defeated.

You should return to Captain Hanâbu.Talk to Captain Hanâbu'This Ordâkhai camp is quite defensible, but they seem to have let their guard down. They were unprepared for my soldier's assault, and their leader has retreated into the collapsed mine in the camp's rear. Enter the camp, and help us clear it out.''Excellent work, ${PLAYER}. My soldiers can take care of any stragglers.'The Ordâkhai have placed barricades along the road to Emax Dûl to slow the advance of an enemy army.The Ordâkhai have placed barricades along the road to Emax Dûl to slow an advancing army.

