'Can I count on you to fulfil this mission?'You have completed many delvings and done much to aid the peoples of Middle-earth!Defeat many drakes throughout Idagâl.Defeat many drakes throughout Idagâl.Defeat many drakes in IdagâlDefeat a great many drakes throughout Idagâl.Defeat many drakes throughout Idagâl.Defeat a great many drakes in Idagâl.Defeat a great many drakes in IdagâlThe Draugardh Scouts have posted a task to collect blood-coated axes. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire blood-coated axes for the Draugardh Scouts.Wanted: blood-coated axes from Draugardh. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: blood-coated axes from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Draugardh Scouts have posted a task to collect blood-soaked claws. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire blood-soaked claws for the Draugardh Scouts.Wanted: blood-soaked claws from Draugardh. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: blood-soaked claws from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Draugardh Scouts have posted a task to collect blood-stained hides. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire blood-stained hides for the Draugardh Scouts.Wanted: blood-stained hides from Draugardh. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: blood-stained hides from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Draugardh Scouts have posted a task to collect bloody goo. This can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire bloody goo for the Draugardh Scouts.Wanted: bloody goo from Draugardh. Gather it to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: bloody goo from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Draugardh Scouts have posted a task to collect deformed ears. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire deformed ears for the Draugardh Scouts.Wanted: deformed ears from Draugardh. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: deformed ears from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Draugardh Scouts have posted a task to collect wind-cracked sword sheaths. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire wind-cracked sword sheaths for the Draugardh Scouts.Wanted: wind-cracked sword sheaths from Draugardh. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: wind-cracked sword sheaths from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Talk to Bhôd-buri-MêjCollect dry branches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Talk to Bhôd-buri-MêjYou have volunteered to aid Mizâdi's provisioner Dunaïl with the tasks he must complete on a typical day.Chief Provisioner Dunaïl asked you to consult soldiers throughout the war camp of Ingarûma to learn of their needs.Chief Provisioner Dunaïl stands by his tent in the war camp of Ingarûma.Talk to Chief Provisioner Dunaïl in the war camp of IngarûmaChief Provisioner Dunaïl told you where to find what you will need to satisfy each of the requests that were made of you.Collect wrapped rations for the soldiers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect water jar for a soldierCollect a bandage for a soldierTalk to Aradír the Overseer on behalf of the soldier ShimûzHaving obtained what you need for the soldiers with whom you spoke, you should return to them and see if they are satisfied.Chief Provisioner Dunaïl stands by his tent in the war camp of Ingarûma.Talk to Chief Provisioner Dunaïl in the war camp of Ingarûma'It is good to see you again, my friend! We are a long way from Kighân, are we not? But my heart tells me that Shâra Mizâdi nears the end of her conquest, for Bârshud has nowhere else to run!

'It is still my duty to cure the soldiers of anything that might hinder their ability to fight for the Shâra. Are you interested in seeing what my average day is like, ${PLAYER}? If so, speak with the soldiers you see around the war camp here and learn what it is they need. Then return to me and we will see what we can do to solve their problems. That is the role of the Chief Provisioner, and that is what I am!''I asked you to speak with the soldiers you see around the war camp and learn what it is they need. Then return to me and we will see what we can do to solve their problems. That is the role of the Chief Provisioner, and that is what I am!''All right, my friend, what have you learned?

'Hunger should be easily taken care of with the bags of food to my right. Thirst is similarly cured with a jar of water from the counter to the south-east. Injuries call for a bandage, and you can find that on the baskets nearby.

'Shimûz fought all night? He must be given time to rest, or he will not return from battle! Bring word of this to Aradír the Overseer at the camp-fire down the slope, and then distribute all of the items you gathered to the soldiers who asked for them.''Do you remember what I told you?

'Hunger should be easily taken care of with the bags of food to my right. Thirst is similarly cured with a jar of water from the counter to the south-east. Injuries call for a bandage, and you can find that on the baskets nearby.

'Shimûz fought all night? He must be given time to rest, or he will not return from battle! Bring word of this to Aradír the Overseer at the camp-fire down the slope, and then distribute all of the items you gathered to the soldiers who asked for them.''Shimûz needs rest? I am not surprised. He pushes himself too hard on behalf of Shâra Mizâdi. Tell him that he has permission to sleep... and indeed, it is the command of Aradír the Overseer!''Tell Shimûz that he has permission to sleep... and indeed, it is the command of Aradír the Overseer!''Now you come to the hard part: remembering where you left each of the soldiers you agreed to help!''Thank you for bringing me this food. It is just what I need to recover my fighting strength!''This food is just for me? You are a light in the darkness, friend!''This food will get me back to fighting condition in no time! Thank you, friend!''You have brought me a jar of water. Thank you, for I was so parched I could not concentrate on my duties!''Ah, Dunaïl always knows just what we need. This bandage will help me heal my injury much more quickly. Thank you, my friend.''Aradír says I can rest? Thank you, friend!

'I will not sleep long... just enough to... recover my strength....''Well done, my friend. You have now experienced what life is like in my boots for a day. It is a lot of hard work, but I know that without me the work of the soldiers who follow Shâra Mizâdi would be made more difficult, and that keeps me moving forward!

'I know it cannot compare to your adventures, ${PLAYER}, and I do not ask to trade! You face far more monstrous foes than I, and I envy you not for that!'With the supplies you brought him Arimûl will now be able to return to the war camp, but he doesn't want to leave his duties for Mizâdi undone.The nearest entrance to the kergrim caves of Mut-hûru is located north of the road that runs east of Arimûl's position.Search for Ordâkhai outside the nearest entrance to the kergrim caves of Mut-hûruThe nearest entrance to the kergrim caves of Mut-hûru is located north of the road that runs east of Arimûl's position. The body of an Ordâkhai soldier lies here!Search the body of the slain Ordâkhai outside the kergrim cavesKergrim inside the cave of Mut-hûru may have scavenged belongings from the Ordâkhai they killed.Collect Ordâkhai trinkets from kergrim inside Mut-hûru (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Arimûl agreed to meet with you outside the main tent at the war camp of Ingarûma.Meet with Arimûl outside the main tent of the war camp of IngarûmaShenzâmin stands by the side of the main tent of the war camp of Ingarûma.Chief Provisioner Dunaïl stands by his tent in the war camp of Ingarûma.Talk to Chief Provisioner Dunaïl in the war camp of IngarûmaKagûlu the Armsman is by the forges in the war camp of Ingarûma.Talk to Kagûlu the Armsman in the war camp of IngarûmaKishâtal is down the slope to the south-east of the forges in the war camp of Ingarûma.Talk to Kishâtal in the war camp of IngarûmaShenzâmin stands by the side of the main tent of the war camp of Ingarûma.Talk to Shenzâmin beside the main tent of the war camp of Ingarûma'I still have duties I was supposed to perform for Mizâdi, and I should not leave them undone. I cannot complete them now, not with this injury, but perhaps you could see them done on my behalf?

'I was to pursue some men of Ordâkh that intended to raid the kergrim-infested caves of Mut-hûru, and to bring back any of their possessions that might be of value. If you can slay those men and retrieve such trinkets, I would appreciate it! Will you meet with me at the war camp when you have finished? Mizâdi will be most pleased that my injury will not prevent this important duty from being carried out!''I was to pursue some men of Ordâkh that intended to raid the kergrim-infested caves of Mut-hûru, and to bring back any of their possessions that might be of value. If you can slay those men and retrieve such trinkets, I would appreciate it! Will you meet with me at the war camp when you have finished? Mizâdi will be most pleased that my injury will not prevent this important duty from being carried out!'Shenzâmin smiles broadly at you.

'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}! Kishâtal and I completed our mission on behalf of Shâra Mizâdi in An Shêru. Now we accompany her to put an end to Bârshud and his forces here in Pahar Hatokáli. He has nowhere left to run!'

You ask Shenzâmin if he has seen an injured Hamâti soldier wielding a wooden crutch nearby, and he shakes his head.

'I cannot say I have. Perhaps he went to thank Dunaïl for the use of it?''I have not seen such a man. Perhaps he went to thank Dunaïl for the use of the stave and the bandage you brought him?''The soldier with the injured leg? No, he has not yet returned the wooden stave I gave you. I have not seen him. Do you think he ran into further trouble on the road?'

You tell Dunaïl that Arimûl told you he had experienced a run of ill fortune before he was injured.

'It may be nothing to worry about. Perhaps Kagûlu the Armsman has seen him?''It may be nothing to worry about. Perhaps Kagûlu the Armsman has seen him?''A soldier named Arimûl? The name is familiar, but I cannot say why. What did this man look like?'

You describe what you can remember of Arimûl's appearance, and Kagûlu shakes his head.

'Your description rings no forge-hammers for me, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps one of the other soldiers will recognize this man.''Perhaps one of the other soldiers will recognize this man.''You look puzzled, ${PLAYER}.'

You describe the mystery of your missing man to Kishâtal, and when you mention the name Arimûl he looks at you with astonishment.

'But Arimûl is dead. He fell during one of our initial skirmishes with Bârshud's forces when we first came to Pahar Hatokáli. Did the man you meet have a bushy black beard?'

You answer that he did not, and Kishâtal nods with satisfaction.

'You met an imposter, ${PLAYER}. Whoever he is, he is not the Arimûl I knew. You had better tell Shenzâmin.''You met an imposter, ${PLAYER}. Whoever he is, he is not the Arimûl I knew. You had better tell Shenzâmin.''Did you find your missing man, ${PLAYER}?'

You tell Shenzâmin what Kishâtal had to say about the imposter pretending to be the soldier Arimûl.

'You are saying no one knows this man? But for what purpose would he lie to you?'The palace of Ekal-nêbi is the crown jewel of Emax Dûl, an opulent home to rulers from the kingdom of Nêshak, Nísaka... and now from Ordâkh. Hidden in the background of palace life, Thothril the Entangler, Thardúth of Damudûr, quietly began working her enchantments upon the minds of its inhabitants. Now with soldiers of Mizâdi's alliance at the palace doorstep, she asserts final control over the palace.Defeat Ordâkhai within Ekal-nêbi, the Fallen PalaceDefeat Ordâkhai within Ekal-nêbi, the Fallen PalaceThe palace of Ekal-nêbi is the crown jewel of Emax Dûl, an opulent home to rulers from the kingdom of Nêshak, Nísaka... and now from Ordâkh. Hidden in the background of palace life, Thothril the Entangler, Thardúth of Damudûr, quietly began working her enchantments upon the minds of its inhabitants. Now with soldiers of Mizâdi's alliance at the palace doorstep, she asserts final control over the palace.The palace has fallen under the control of the Thardúth, Thothril the Entangler.

