 mother before returning to Irsinith at the Mother Tree.Hear Dáthlil's response to your storyYou learned some more about the blight from Ildimár and Dáthlil, return to Irsinith at the Mother Tree in Adagím and see what she learned from her communion with the ancient tree.Return to Irsinith at the Mother Tree and see what she learnedAfter your explanation and description of the enemies setting upon you on the return to him, Viznak looks off into the distance before speaking.

'Morvul, troll, Orcs, all pawns for Blight Lady. Not spiders, though. Not that I ever see. My bodyguards are smart to send you. We should tell the sad Elf-lady about Blight Lady. Her name is Irsinith. She is a very sad Elf-lady. This news will not cheer her up, but maybe give her a new purpose. You go and talk to her and see if she can teach you more.'Irsinith listens to the tale of the King's Folly with great interest. As you explain the variance in maps from the Temámír and Men, she nods in assent. When you finish, she pauses and looks to the Mother Tree.

'The Temámír map speaks true. In elder days, we held pacts with the dwarves; the defence of Nisigím was a charge borne by all. There were peaks even they dared not climb.

'The Kinta stood firm in that age, though it lies beyond my remembering. My father and mother may recall what I cannot.

'Take your tale to them at Sul Madásh. I shall seek Amûma's counsel—if her grief permits, she may yet speak.'Ildimár and Dáthlil listen to the retelling of the King's Folly, and all you have learned since. They share a glance, and Ildimár speaks.

'Men tell this story in a manner different from what we recall. Ages have passed, the king's bones have long been dust, but a persistent memory endures.

'Bitter woe came to Nisigím, and many reaches of the great wood went unwatched after. Our people fought not only the cruelty of Men, but also the endless creep of Sívigush, the blight that rises now to consume all. In truth, we have always striven against Sívigush. It is as old as the stars.''When the blight returned, it was as in the old tale of the forgotten king: a thin, devouring veil that left naught but ruin behind.

'If the tale holds true, the place of its binding was sealed. But Ordâkh came with sorcery, broke the land's back, and the blight was loosed again.

'If dark things now stir in the North, seeking its source, they must be stayed 'ere all falls. Go to our daughter, Irsinith, upon the Hill of the Mother, and hear what Amûma has revealed to her.''Amûma remains silent; her pain is too great. We should heed my parents' words. Viznak's insight may prove invaluable.'The recent upheavals scarred the city, but now it begins to heal, as do some of the companions who fought by your side.The Apothecary of Dâr Tabib is located in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl.Enter the Apothecary of Dâr Tabib in the Tor-gardens of Umbar BaharbêlCorudan lies in one of the beds of Dâr Tabib.Talk to Corudan in Dâr TabibSigileth watches over her brother in Dâr Tabib.Talk to Sigileth in Dâr TabibSigileth is in Dâr Tabib.Talk to Sigileth in Dâr Tabib and hear her account of their return to the citySigileth is in Dâr Tabib.Talk to Sigileth in Dâr TabibCaebar is in Dâr Tabib.Talk to Caebar in Dâr TabibSigileth is in Dâr Tabib.Talk to Sigileth in Dâr TabibCorudan's possessions can be found in the satchel at the foot of his bed.Retrieve Corudan's notes about the Fearwater from the satchel at the foot of his bedCaebar is in Dâr Tabib.Caebar waits for you in the Tor-gardens outside Dâr Tabib.Talk to Caebar in the Tor-gardens outside Dâr TabibCaebar thinks for a moment about what you have shown him.Wait for Caebar to speak againCaebar stands in the Tor-gardens outside Dâr Tabib.Talk to Caebar in the Tor-gardens outside Dâr Tabib'They returned to the city a few days ago and now recover in Dâr Tabib. You can find this apothecary in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl.''You should visit them at Dâr Tabib, in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl. I know Corudan and Sigileth will be pleased to see you!''${PLAYER}, my friend... my wound is well on its way to healing... but to see you return with victory... eases the pain. I understand Umbar has been saved from... Nakási and Balakhâd? Has Gondor too... escaped from their wrath?'

You tell Corudan that King Elessar and his soldiers fought bravely against the Song, and Gondor survived. He smiles weakly.

'Then the last of Sauron's schemes... has been frustrated, ${PLAYER}. I am glad for my part in it...'

You insist that Corudan rest, and you will speak with him when he is more fully healed.'Our return to the city... was not uneventful. My sister... will speak of it to you.''I understand Nakási is slain and the Song of Waves and Wind defeated, ${PLAYER}. May there now be peace for a time!

'I heard tell that five ships of the Song survived the passage to Gondor, and waged war upon the Harlond? More might have joined them, had the rapids of the Ikorbân not proved too perilous; we saw the ruin of many smaller ships dashed upon the rocks as we travelled this way from Sûg Nidar. The builders of the fleet likely intended that to be a one-way voyage, but they had not counted upon Cúridwan's damaging solution, or your great haste in opposing those who escaped it.

'The raft-bridge of the Wrackwade did not last long against the Narghâk cannons. When we rejoined Rahâzi at Iridír she said her mother intended to see it rebuilt. It would not surprise me to learn she has already done so! But I have gotten ahead of myself. There is more to tell.

'While you pursued the Song toward Umbar, my brother and I and Cúridwan made our own way westward. Our return journey... was not uneventful.''Yes, I will tell you what transpired after you left us.''I cannot say with certainty that the spirit was Silirtas, or that she heard my words. But I believe it was, and she did. I will not hurry to join her, but when at last I come to that place, I hope she and I will reside in comfort and in peace, beyond the loneliness and fear that so troubled Silirtas when she contemplated the unknown days ahead.

'That is my desire, ${PLAYER}. I cannot know if it will come to pass, but if hope leads us ever onward, the pleasant dream of it will live in my heart until the last of my days arrives.''Caebar has visited every day, and kept us informed of events in the city.'Caebar flushes.

'Oh! I am sorry to interrupt, ${PLAYER}! I did not know you had returned! I have visited our friends every day while Corudan recovers, and they have spoken to me of your adventure in the Fearwater.

'Please, finish your visit! I will speak with you afterward.''That reminds me. My brother collected some papers from the Ordâkhai while we adventured in the Fearwater. He intended to give them to Caebar, but the matter has slipped our minds until now. Look for them among Corudan's belongings, and give them to Caebar.''Look for these papers among Corudan's belongings, and give them to Caebar.''Give Caebar the papers my brother collected during our time in the Fearwater.'Caebar accepts the papers and briefly studies them.

'Wait... you say that Corudan found these in an Ordâkh encampment in the Fearwater? I do not want to pester him with questions, ${PLAYER}, so let us speak of this outside.'You find Caebar excitedly studying the papers Corudan retrieved from the Ordâkhai of Sûg Nidar.

'The soldiers would not have understood the meaning of this parchment, ${PLAYER}, but I do. They must have found it among the ruins of Kasukhín while searching for treasure; thinking it unimportant, they kept it unguarded among their belongings, where it went overlooked until it was picked up by Corudan.

'These are the words of Vinyarion, twenty-fourth King of Gondor, who bore the title of Hyarmendacil II: "the South-victor." Set down by a trusted retainer in his old age, only days before his death, these words claim that he repented of his long campaign in Harad, and wept at the bones of Shâraban, a city he destroyed in the days of his youth. On the return journey of his tenth pilgrimage to the lands he once conquered, he rested at the hilltop fort of Kasukhín and died there, peacefully, in his sleep. Sigileth tells me the land around that fort is now changed, and what was once a hill is now an island; might Vinyarion's bones lie there to this day, kept isolated from discovery by the creation of the Fearwater?

'His story raises complicated emotions in my heart, ${PLAYER}; he is considered very differently in Shagâna than he is in Gondor, and it is difficult to reconcile those two perspectives. I am put in mind of the relationship the Umbari must now have with the Kindred of the Coins that preceded the Ghad Imghêda, the Kindred Redeemed.''The Kindred of the Coins was neither entirely evil nor entirely good, ${PLAYER}. Like Hyarmendacil II, they achieved both lasting good and enduring harm. Does one erase the other? Wiser scholars than I may be able to weigh the value of each... but I cannot. Must we forget the instrumental roles played by Azagath and Nakási in the freeing of Umbar from the Heirs of Castamir and the cultists of Sauron? Must we forget Khôltekh's deeds during the Dagor Carlanthir, or Hármelak's advice that Dâr Laja be opened to the needs of her people? Must their later crimes strike from the record their earlier heroics and wise governance?'

Caebar studies the ground intently.

'Must my mother's refusal to see me erase the happy years I spent as a child in Ethring, ${PLAYER}? I think it cannot. So we celebrate the good and we work to remedy the bad, and by so doing we mend what wounds we can, and seek to avoid inflicting further harm. That is healing, of a kind, is it not?'

The Gondorian scribe heaves a sigh and looks up at you again, forcing a smile.

'From conversation with the Umbari I have sketched the members of the original Kindred of the Coins, ${PLAYER}. Umbar will remember both their fine qualities and their faults, neither excusing the other, and with these drawings I hoped to capture that balance. Choose one of your liking and it is yours; the others I will give to the city of Umbar Baharbêl, that it may remember its history and not forget it.'The Ghad Imghêda seeks to uncover answers to some of the pressing questions asked during the past few weeks.Tatháta is at Dâr Rapha, outside the city.Talk to Tatháta at Dâr Rapha and consider her wordsTatháta is at Dâr Rapha, outside the city.Talk to Tatháta at Dâr RaphaDaxamat is at Dâr Rapha, outside the city.Talk to Daxamat at Dâr Rapha'Hármelak and Khôltekh are missing. None have seen them since the uprising began.

'The people of the city who chose us to form the Ghad Imghêda expect us to redeem the Kindred of the Coins, to live up to its goals and not succumb to the rot that festered within it from its early founding. I hope it will be so, but that will be made more difficult if we cannot learn what befell Hármelak and Khôltekh during the uprising.''They may have perished during the uprising. What do you think happened to them when the people arose?''I wonder...?

'It is most likely they were caught and killed by the people they betrayed, but if that is so, where are the bodies? None have come forth to confirm either of their fates, so every suggestion is a supposition only. We can only guess at it.

'I do not like guessing, ${PLAYER}. I like knowing for certain.''The Ghad Imghêda will remain alert for the reappearance of Hármelak or Khôltekh... just in case.''Oh! I had almost forgotten, ${PLAYER}! I have news for you of your friends Corudan and Sigileth!'Your return to Umbar Baharbêl has revealed a change in the political situation of the city.Someone at the Northern Ship-yard around the corner to the east may have further information for you concerning the political situation in Umbar Baharbêl.Find someone at the Northern Ship-yard who will tell you the situation in the cityJínen was on her way to the Gate of Songs north of the city.Talk to Jínen outside the Gate of SongsDâr Rapha is up the hill to the east of the Gate of Songs, outside the city.Meet the Ghad Imghêda at Dâr Rapha, up the hill to the eastJajax has come to Dâr Rapha, outside the city.Talk to Jajax at Dâr RaphaThe leaders of the Ghad Imghêda are at Dâr Rapha.The leaders of the Ghad Imghêda are at Dâr Rapha.The leaders of the Ghad Imghêda are at Dâr Rapha.The leaders of the Ghad Imghêda are at Dâr Rapha.'Our return voyage was not as eventful as the first that brought you to these shores, ${PLAYER}!

'Umbar Baharbêl seemed on the very precipice of the cliff's edge when we departed, but all is now as it was. Let us ask some of the people nearby what transpired while we were away.

'You go to the east and find someone willing to talk near the Northern Ship-yard. The workers there are always willing to spend the day in idle chatter, and the tidings we seek are the furthest thing from trivial!''Someone will tell us what transpired while we were away. Umbar Baharbêl seemed on the very precipice of the cliff's edge when we departed, but all is now as it was! Find someone at the Northern Ship-yard. east of here, who is willing to talk.''How could you not have heard? The Kindred of the Coins was overthrown, and a new Kindred raised in its place: the Ghad Imghêda, the Kindred Redeemed!

'Hármelak Golden-hand and Khôltekh the Temámir were in league with Ordâkh, allying even with Orcs of Mordor! They thought to sell this city to its oppressors, but they counted not on us: the common men and women of Umbar, the ship-builders and the sailors, the merchants and the scholars, the fishermen and the labourers.

'The people of Umbar Baharbêl rose up against them, and with one voice we spoke to them: "It will not be so!" we shouted. The uprising lasted for the better part of the day, and into the night. There was bloodshed, for not every soldier at Hármelak's command threw down his weapons, but many saw the rightness of our cause and joined the just throng.

'Another group opposed us during the uprising: the Heirsworn, who have long troubled the peace of the harbour. One of my workers fought against them on the night of the uprising, and can tell you more. Her name is Jínen, and she was on her way to the Gate of Songs north of the city just moments ago. If you hurry you may find her there.

'But that is in the past. May the new Kindred better serve the interests of the Umbari people, free of the influences of Ordâkh!''May the new Kindred better serve the interests of the Umbari people, free of the influences of Ordâkh!''Yes, I fought against the Heirsworn during the uprising; I am not afraid to speak of it.

'They have always been the weakened side of the ship's hull, still long at sea, and I am not surprised that it eventually burst! The passage by the city of the Ordâkhai ships was a hammer-blow to that imperfection, and the Heirsworn believed their time had come at last to fully seize control once again. What made them so bold? I cannot say for certain, but whispers tell that many of their number had been secretly leaving the city for a number of weeks, rallied somewhere by the son of Balakhôr himself.

'The uprising was short but effective, and a new Kindred has been formed to lead Umbar Baharbêl in the days to come: the Ghad Imghêda! They assemble even now at Dâr Rapha, up the hill to the east. That is where I am going, for I wish to get a look at them. On these wise counsellors we put our hopes!''The Ghad Imghêda meets even now at Dâr Rapha, east of the city. That is where I am going, for I wish to get a look at them. On these wise counsellors we put our hopes!''My brother Dax stands with this new Kindred as if he were one of them! That is an oversight, surely?''How might things have transpired if Dax was locked away, and I was left to manage the uprising? Now that would result in a truly impressive Ghad Imghêda!''One thing followed another, ${PLAYER}. I am not sure what happened. But I am glad to see you safe and alive!

'At first I was just trying to carry out your will, telling the people what you told me... but as more and more folk learned that Hármelak and Khôltekh had imprisoned you and my brother, they became angrier and angrier. You helped many Umbari and Temámir alike when you came to these shores, ${PLAYER}, and it seems you have made more friends than you know!

'What began in confusion became a rebellion, Ilma-ghôli, the rising tide, and then there was no stopping it! Try as I might, I could not convince those who flocked to us that I was not cut out to lead them... and now they have made me part of the Ghad Imghêda. I don't understand how this happened, and yet every step of the way has led me to this moment.

'Is this how you feel every day, ${PLAYER}? I cannot get used to this!''Each member of the Ghad Imghêda is impressive. Until they learn I am not, I will stand beside them and do the best I can!''I wear these burns proudly in memory of Belondor, ${PLAYER}. I believe he sails now in the company of his friend Sirgon, and they are not bound by the oceans of the world.

'I sought not to join the Ghad Imghêda, but the people of the city demanded it. I could not refuse them. They ask for strength, and I possess it. It would be impolite to abandon them.'

Rothog grins, a frightful sight.

'Besides,' he says, 'all of my things are here.''Despite the land where he was born, my husband was a man of Umbar. The wife of such a man must be prepared for the voyage on which he might not return, and I was.'

Mêshka smiles sadly.

'That makes it little easier, ${PLAYER}, but one thing has lightened my sorrow. The people of the city loved my husband, and they grieve with me. The burden is shared across every Ward of Umbar Baharbêl, and so made less.

'They asked me to join the Ghad Imghêda and to rule in Belondor's stead. I agreed, and so honour my husband's memory and the love he held for this city and its people.'Rothog smiles at you, and his grin seems more ferocious than ever.'The people of the city loved my husband. I will rule as part of the Ghad Imghêda in his memory, and on their behalf.''The people called for me to join the Ghad Imghêda; as harbour-warden I could not refuse. I sought not to elevate my position, but with so many of the Heirsworn gone from the city, it would seem my days must be less eventful. This will fill them up.

'To the Umbari who called for me to join this august body, I made this pledge: to remain vigilant, not only of our enemies but also of our friends, and our chosen leaders. It appears to this old sailor that much of the trouble began when Tumúldo sailed to Gondor, and that done at Azagath's command. The old Kindred should have sniffed out the Sea-shadow's evil before he could use it to deprive the city of such a hero as Tumúldo, who might have opposed him.

'Others might be deceived, but not I, and not now the Ghad Imghêda!''The Temámir and the Umbari people must work together, and not at cross-purposes. For that reason, I was chosen to join the Ghad Imghêda.

'I feel I must apologize for the actions taken by Khôltekh during the past few weeks, ${PLAYER}. I have explained to the Umbari and to my own people that I consider it a failing of my own that I did not determine his true allegiances in time to prevent the tragedies that befell the city. I need not tell you that he acted alone and for his own interests, and it was not with the authority of the Shoreward Stone that he fell in with Ordâkh or with the Orcs of Mordor that were seen upon one of the vessels as it passed the city. I am grateful for the assemblage of Temámir who came to Thargushakâl and informed me of his treachery during the early hours of the uprising. They will be rewarded!

'The actions of Khôltekh shame his people. The Umbari can rest more easily now that I have joined the Ghad Imghêda.''The Heirsworn will no longer pose a threat to us. I will see to that.''The actions of Khôltekh shame his people and his city. The Umbari can rest more easily now that I have joined the Ghad Imghêda.''One mystery remains to be solved.'You have proven yourself by conquering what lies within the blight-scarred depths of the Folly of Nagakhêdi.Complete 'The Folly of Nagakhêdi' at Tier 1.Defeat Badharál the Gorger on Tier 1Defeat Maukhorn on Tier 1Defeat the Legion of Lhaereth on Tier 1Defeat Zamâktar the Putrescent on Tier 1You have proven yourself by conquering what lies within the blight-scarred depths of the Folly of Nagakhêdi.Complete 'The Folly of Nagakhêdi' at Tier 2.Defeat Badharál the Gorger on Tier 2Defeat Maukhorn on Tier 2Defeat the Legion of Lhaereth on Tier 2Defeat Zamâktar the Putrescent on Tier 2You have proven yourself by conquering what lies within the blight-scarred depths of the Folly of Nagakhêdi.Complete 'The Folly of Nagakhêdi' at Tier 3.Defeat Badharál the Gorger on Tier 3Defeat Maukhorn on Tier 3Defeat the Legion of Lhaereth on Tier 3Defeat Zamâktar the Putrescent on Tier 3Thoroughly explore every settlement, cave, camp, lair, and point of interest in An Shêru in Mûr Ghala.Explore An Shêru in Mûr Ghala.Complete New Threats in An ShêruComplete Reclaiming An ShêruComplete Treasure-seeker of An ShêruThoroughly explore every settlement, cave, camp, lair, and point of interest in Pahar Hatokáli in Mûr Ghala.Thoroughly explore every settlement, cave, camp, lair, and point of interest in Pahar Hatokáli in Mûr Ghala.Complete Dangers in Hatokáli FellsComplete Scouting Hatokáli FellsComplete Treasure-seeker of Hatokáli FellsThoroughly explore every settlement, cave, camp, lair, and point of interest in Idagâl in Mûr Ghala.Explore Idagâl in Mûr Ghala.Complete New Threats in IdagâlComplete Reclaiming IdagâlComplete Treasure-seeker of IdagâlThoroughly explore every settlement, cave, camp, lair, and point of interest in Kighân in Mûr Ghala.Explore Kighân in Mûr Ghala.Complete Dangers in KighânComplete Rejuvenating KighânComplete Treasure-seeker of KighânThoroughly explore every settlement, canyon, cave, camp, marsh, lair, and point of interest in Mûr Ghala.Thoroughly explore every settlement, canyon, cave, camp, marsh, lair, and point of interest in Mûr Ghala.Complete Explorer of AdagímComplete Explorer of KighânComplete Explorer of An ShêruComplete Explorer of IdagâlThoroughly explore every settlement, cave, camp, lair, and point of interest in Adagím in Mûr Ghala.Explore Adagím in Mûr Ghala.Complete New Threats in AdagímComplete Scouting AdagímComplete Treasure-seeker of AdagímTakhsûl has asked you to scout Imizíla and defeat Ordâkhai you find within its bounds.Ordâkhai can be found throughout Imizíla, as can places of interest to Mizâdi's soldiers.Scout the entrance to the palace in south-east ImizílaScout the overlook in southern ImizílaScout the entrance courtyard in northern ImizílaDefeat Ordâkhai within Imizíla (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Takhsûl is waiting outside Imizíla for your report.Talk to Takhsûl outside Imizíla'The Ordâkhai have fortified Imizíla as much as they can, but they have nowhere else to run and it will prove a futile effort. On this day we will seize victory for Shâra Mizâdi, but for that we will need information.

'Will you scout the city for me and defeat their forces? I will combine your report with my own and bring it to Zalûd so he can inform the Shâra.''Will you scout the city for me and defeat the Ordâkhai forces? I will combine your report with my own and bring it to Zalûd so he can inform the Shâra.''This report will be invaluable for making further plans of battle. Imizíla will not long stand against the forces of Shâra Mizâdi!

'Know you the meaning of "Imizíla" in the Shagâni language, ${PLAYER}? It is "last torch," and we will soon see it snuffed out!'The difference in the maps provided by the scholars of Zajâna and the Temámir are pronounced. The Doorward leader believes that the map provided by Bêtam may be a fraud, or errant. You should consult with your allies from the north, Rhadrog and Faeron.Valukhâri is dismissive that the tale is nothing more than a child's fable spun for a new crowd and age. Something does not sit right with you. Take the map to your allies Rhadrog and Faeron, recently arrived here in Zajâna and gather their opinions.Speak with Rhadrog near the south-west gate in ZajânaRhadrog believes the tale may have merit and wants you to share the story and map with Faeron at the fountain square in Zajâna.Share the story with Faeron at the fountain square ZajânaFaeron and Rhadrog agree there is a reason to investigate further. Faeron suggested you ask Rhadrog how to proceed.Ask Rhadrog how to proceed at the south-west gate in Zajâna'I fear I have nothing more to offer. The map you hold is likely flawed. The tale of the Fool King's Folly is little more than a children's fable, meant to frighten them from the night or keep folk from venturing into Adagím. It has served its purpose. No expedition has ever sought the fabled citadel's location.'You show the map to Rhadrog and recount the tale of the Fool King.

'You were wise to bring this here, ${PLAYER}. The dwarves are long-lived and masters of stone, unless, of course, they are driven by greed and seek to hoard a treasure. Ask Faeron what his counsel may be.''Had the Temámir not believed in what their map suggests, they would have long ago established an outpost. But they are wary. Men, however, are prideful and secretive, prone to hiding uncomfortable truths. I side with Rhadrog—tell him I believe we must inform Viznak and compel him to learn more.''Viznak's insight—or his paranoia—may yet serve us. At the very least, you can tell him the tale of the King's Folly and see if he can establish the connexion between the blight we face and that which claimed a generation.'Rashlût believes with your help he can protect his village.Rashlût gave you some stones with which you can finish the cairn he began constructing north of the village of Hanamíku.Rashlût waits for you in the centre of the village of Hanamíku.Talk to Rashlût in the centre of the village of HanamíkuRashlût gave you some stones with which you can finish the cairn he began constructing south of the village of Hanamíku.Rashlût waits for you in the centre of the village of Hanamíku.Talk to Rashlût in the centre of the village of Hanamíku'You have a look that is familiar to me, friend: the look of a wayfarer! I know it because I possess this same look, the same appearance of one who lives upon the road and travels to distant lands, and never minds the danger!

'I have returned of late from just such a journey, and I am exhausted. Perhaps you can help me finish the task I have begun? It will help protect my village from any who threaten it!

'Take these stones I collected on my latest pilgrimage, and use them to complete the cairn I began by the road just north of Hanamíku. Once you have applied the finishing touches to my incomplete cairn, the enchantment will almost be ready.''Use the stones I gave you to complete the cairn I began by the road just north of Hanamíku. Once you have applied the finishing touches to my incomplete cairn, the enchantment will almost be ready.''You have done as I asked? I delight to hear it! May the spirit of the Menûndari protect Hanamíku from its enemies!'

You ask why Rashlût believes these cairns will have this effect, and he smiles.

'It is because the distant place from which I have now returned is the mighty statue of the Dawn-warden, far to the north, and the stones with which we complete these cairns are from that sacred ground!

'Here, take these last few stones and complete the cairn I began by the road south of the village. Then the blessing of the Eternal Ruler will keep Hanamíku safe!''Use those stones I gave you to complete the cairn I began by the road south of the village. Then the blessing of the Eternal Ruler will keep Hanamíku safe!''Both of the cairns now stand completed? Did you hear the voice of the Eternal Ruler, agreeing to protect these lands and their peoples?'

You tell Rashlût you did not, and to your surprise he nods agreeably.

'Perhaps it will take some time. Just knowing that the cairns are there makes me feel more assured of our protection by the Menûndari, my friend. You and I have done very well this day, and I thank you for your assistance. May we meet again upon the road some day!'Málacál has asked that you travel to east of Sul Madásh, along the ridges, and scout the area for threats.Málacál has asked that you travel to east of Sul Madásh, along the ridges, and scout the area for threats.Scout north-east AdagímScout eastern AdagímScout south-east AdagímReturn to Málacál near Sul Madásh and report your findings after scouting eastern Adagím.Return to Málacál'Greetings, friend.

'The hunter's guild of Mûr Ghala is looking for someone to scout the area to the east here in Adagím.

'We aim to identify suitable targets for our hunts and we would be grateful if you are in the area to make notes of the monsters you see.''Hello again, ${CLASS}. What news do you bring?'

You inform Málacál of the various hunting targets you identified during your scouting efforts.

'This information is most useful and now we can continue to plan our hunts here in Adagím.'Collect pinecones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect berries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect leafy greens (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect dried sap from damaged trees (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Talk to Bhôd-buri-Mêj at Khel WêroComplete Instance: Forming a FriendshipEbuzâm will not give up until he frees everyone he can from Esh Mêkag.Ebuzâm is ready to go back into Esh Mêkag to rescue as many thralls as he can.

You should speak with Ebuzâm and complete 'Instance: Gaol-break'.Complete 'Instance: Gaol-break'You have succeeded in causing a riot in Esh Mêkag and freeing many thralls.

You should talk to Ebuzâm.Talk to Ebuzâm'I am injured, but alive, thanks to you. You have bought me the time to do what needs to be done.

'Ishûri noticed that the pit-mine was much emptier than usual, and she was right. The warden, Ratúlko the Bloody, may he get what he deserves, has taken most of the thralls into the prison for torture and execution. I was to be first, as punishment for helping the others escape.

'I will not allow this injustice to happen. Not while I draw breath! I will go to Esh Mêkag and take down as many of those monsters as I can to stop this, even if I die trying. I would ask for your help, but I know you have a greater battle to win....

'I owe you my life, stranger, but I will not abandon the others. Are you with me?''Back into the jaws of the Silent Mouth....''We have done well, ${PLAYER}. I know I would have died had you not come with me. My body is begging for rest, but I know that I cannot. This will not be finished until the Ordâkhai are gone, and no living souls remain locked in that fortress. 

'With the warden's retreat, the prison has descended into chaos, and those still inside have a fighting chance. There are still more to free inside, but now we have something we long have missed: hope.'Defeat many goblins in Glúkroz and throughout Kighân.Defeat many goblins throughout Kighân.Defeat many goblins throughout KighânDefeat a great many goblins in Glúkroz and throughout Kighân.Defeat many goblins throughout Kighân.Defeat a great many goblins in Kighân.Defeat a great many goblins in KighânDefeat many gredbyg throughout An Shêru.Defeat many gredbyg in An Shêru.Defeat many gredbyg in An ShêruDefeat a great many gredbyg throughout An Shêru.Defeat many gredbyg throughout An Shêru.Defeat a great many gredbyg in An Shêru.Defeat a great many gredbyg in An ShêruYou have chosen Harthalín to remain and guard the prisoner while the rest of your companions see to their assorted tasks in Nan Ogol.Harthalín has agreed to guard the prisoner. Now you should go upstairs to Koi-mêdh-twar and leave her to her duty.Go upstairs to Koi-mêdh-twarGhôl-buri-Prân is at the cave of Koi-mêdh-twar, waiting for you to defend your choice of sentry to guard Mûlazar.Talk to Ghôl-buri-Prân at Koi-mêdh-twarRanger Orthonn is at Koi-mêdh-twar, ready to describe the tasks that need doing throughout Nan Ogol.Talk to Orthonn at Koi-mêdh-twarReturn to Kôl Sakla with the Têtikir and meet with KhályaYou have accomplished the many tasks you desired to complete, and should now return to check on Harthalín in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Harthalín in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twarYou have chosen Ranger Orthonn to remain and guard the prisoner while the rest of your companions see to their assorted tasks in Nan Ogol.Orthonn has agreed to guard the prisoner. Now you should go upstairs to Koi-mêdh-twar and leave him to his duty.Go upstairs to Koi-mêdh-twarGhôl-buri-Prân is at the cave of Koi-mêdh-twar, waiting for you to defend your choice of sentry to guard Mûlazar.Talk to Ghôl-buri-Prân at Koi-mêdh-twarHarthalín is at Koi-mêdh-twar, ready to describe the tasks that need doing throughout Nan Ogol.Talk to Harthalín at Koi-mêdh-twarReturn to Kôl Sakla with the Têtikir and meet with KhályaYou have accomplished the many tasks you desired to complete, and should now return to check on Orthonn in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Orthonn in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twarYou have chosen Prêkh-weni-Pâsh and Kâl-maka-Hôi to remain and guard the prisoner while the rest of your companions see to their assorted tasks in Nan Ogol.The Khemozêl have agreed to guard the prisoner. Now you should go upstairs to Koi-mêdh-twar and leave them to their duty.Go upstairs to Koi-mêdh-twarGhôl-buri-Prân is at the cave of Koi-mêdh-twar, waiting for you to defend your choice of sentries to guard Mûlazar.Talk to Ghôl-buri-Prân at Koi-mêdh-twarHarthalín is at Koi-mêdh-twar, ready to describe the tasks that need doing throughout Nan Ogol.Talk to Harthalín at Koi-mêdh-twarReturn to Kôl Sakla with the Têtikir and meet with KhályaYou have accomplished the many tasks you desired to complete, and should now return to check on Prêkh-weni-Pâsh and Kâl-maka-Hôi in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Prêkh-weni-Pâsh in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twarYou have chosen Thrymm Red-beard to remain and guard the prisoner while the rest of your companions see to their assorted tasks in Nan Ogol.Thrymm has agreed to guard the prisoner. Now you should go upstairs to Koi-mêdh-twar and leave him to his duty.Go upstairs to Koi-mêdh-twarGhôl-buri-Prân is at the cave of Koi-mêdh-twar, waiting for you to defend your choice of sentry to guard Mûlazar.Talk to Ghôl-buri-Prân at Koi-mêdh-twarHarthalín is at Koi-mêdh-twar, ready to describe the tasks that need doing throughout Nan Ogol.Talk to Harthalín at Koi-mêdh-twarReturn to Kôl Sakla with the Têtikir and meet with KhályaYou have accomplished the many tasks you desired to complete, and should now return to check on Thrymm in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twar.Talk to Thrymm Red-beard in Mur Rámtor beneath Koi-mêdh-twarMálacál has asked that you travel east of Sul Madásh and gather any Pale Blight samples you can from the beasts there for the scholars to study.Málacál has asked that you travel east of Sul Madásh and gather any Pale Blight samples you can from the beasts there for the scholars to study.Collect blight samples east of Sul Madásh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Málacál near Sul Madásh and give them the samples of the Pale Blight gathered for the scholars.'${CLASS}, the Hunter's Guild of Mûr Ghala could use the help of someone with your skills.

'The scholars in Sul Madásh have asked for capable hands to gather samples of the Pale Blight from the monsters to the east where the pestilence rages the most.

'We are not used to gathering such materials. Your aid would be appreciated in this task, and you may want to gather allies to assist.''Welcome back. How have you fared in gathering samples of the Pale Blight?'

You give the samples to Málacál.

'You have done well, friend. This is not the usual task of the hunter's guild, but we are glad to be of help to the scholars of this blighted land.

'As always, your efforts are appreciated.'As an instrumental part of Kusâg's efforts to ensure that Mizâdi's rise is undeterred by the Ordâkhai, you are recognized by the master scout for your efforts.Complete Hatokáli Missions: Retaking the Shipments - Day 1Complete Hatokáli Mission: Retaking the Shipments - Day 2Complete Hatokáli Mission: Retaking the Shipments - Day 3Complete Hatokáli Mission: A New Distraction? - Day 4Complete Hatokáli Mission: A New Distraction? - Day 5Complete Hatokáli Mission: Emissaries and Adversaries - Day 6Complete Hatokáli Mission: Emissaries and Adversaries - Day 7Complete Hatokáli Mission: The Engines of War - Day 8Complete Hatokáli Mission: The Engines of War - Day 9Complete Hatokáli Mission: The Engines of War - Day 10You have stalked, tracked down, and defeated every formidable enemy in all of Mûr Ghala.Track down and defeat every formidable enemy in all of Mûr Ghala.Complete Adversaries of AdagímComplete Combatants of KighânComplete Enemies of An ShêruComplete Invaders of IdagâlExamine the statueFind and cut down many Huorns within the foetid swamps of Adagím.Defeat many Huorns in Adagím.Defeat many Huorns in AdagímFind and cut down a great many Huorns within the foetid swamps of Adagím.Defeat many Huorns in Adagím.Defeat a great many Huorns in Adagím.Defeat a great many Huorns in AdagímFilled with a righteous fury, Bâdukhur came to Bolo Thúki to recover his stolen grain... but then wisdom prevailed.The Ordâkhai keep some of the grain they stole from Hanamíku in their camp of Bolo Thúki.Recover stolen grain from within Bolo Thúki (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Bâdukhur should be waiting for his stolen grain back in the village of Hanamíku.'The Ordâkhai had no right to steal our grain, but steal it they did, right out from under our noses! I marched right up here to give them a piece of my mind and take it back... but now that I am here...

'This may be a better job for you, adventurer. I fear my anger might have exceeded my sense in this one instance. Will you recover the stolen sacks of grain from inside Bolo Thúki?

'Look not for me here! I will be back in Hanamíku!''This may be a better job for you, adventurer. I fear my anger might have exceeded my sense in this one instance. Will you recover the stolen sacks of grain from inside Bolo Thúki?

'Look not for me here! I will be back in Hanamíku!''You recovered my stolen grain, and likely prevented me from throwing my life away after it! For that you have my eternal thanks, adventurer, and those of my family!'Talk to MeldirThe Thardúth have gifted the Ordâkhai and Utûgi implements of power to sway them to their side.The Utûgi have brought mysterious gifts from the Thardúth into the city of Emax Dûl.

You should collect Thardúth implements from the east side of Emax Dûl.Collect Thardúth implements (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected the mysterious Thardúth implements from Emax Dûl.

You should return to Sorkamâl the Forbearing in Nashûbu.Talk to Sorkamâl the Forbearing'I have a request, ${PLAYER}, if you are returning to the city above.

'I have heard from some of our soldiers that the Ordâkhai sorcerers near the great temple were wielding strange implements that seemed to bolster their magic. They described them as pitch-black metal rods, sharpened to a point on one end. It seems likely to me that these were made by the Thardúth, and the Utûgi brought them into the city as a gift for their Ordâkhai allies.

'The Thardúth still pose a grave threat to the people of Shagâna, and we must learn what we can about their power. Please, if you find any, bring them to me for study.''Have you collected the implements?'

You hand Sorkamâl one of the chests. She opens it and gingerly inspects the black rod inside.

'I feel uneasy just being near this, ${PLAYER}. This is powerful dark magic, indeed. Thank you for gathering them for me. I hope it can better instruct us in how to face these foes in future battles!'Rahâzi has come to call on Mizâdi, and not a moment too soon. For she is shaken, her army defeated, her spirit frail. In this moment Rahâzi can feel the heavy weight of many lives in Mûr Ghala and Shagâna - they all hang in the balance.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma when you are ready.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma when you are readySpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma. Ingarûma is located south of Hanamíku, high on a hill-top overlooking Imizíla.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingarûma'We lost! We lost... everything! And it is all my fault!''We have a plan. That is all I need.''There are no words.'Mizâdi asks you to accompany her on her journey to Numûru's memorial, to remember him properly.Join and speak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for Numûru.Speak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for NumûruPlace the memorial stones you've collected on top of the existing stones.Place the memorial stones upon the cairn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for Numûru.Speak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for NumûruPlace Numûru's sword and armour in front of the memorial.Place Numûru's sword in front of the memorialPlace Numûru's armour in front of the memorialSpeak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for Numûru.Speak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for NumûruSpeak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for Numûru.Speak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for NumûruSpeak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for Numûru.Speak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for NumûruPay your respects to Numûru, and the other fallen Subuzûri.Pay your respects to Numûru, and the other fallen SubuzûriSpeak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for Numûru.Speak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for NumûruSpeak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for Numûru.Speak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for NumûruSpeak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for Numûru.Speak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for NumûruSpeak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for Numûru.Speak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for NumûruSpeak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for Numûru.Speak with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for NumûruSpeak once more with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for Numûru.Speak once more with Mizâdi by the memorial cairn for Numûru'I would ask one last favour from you, my friend. That you walk with me, as I pay my respects to Numûru, and all of the fallen Subuzûri.''I feel so old. I have seen so much war, and so much bloodshed. I have seen enough for three lifetimes, and I do not yet have silver in my hair.''Please - do the honours. Place his sword and armour in front of the memorial.''I hate it. I hate war. I hate what it brings out of me - and I hate that I am burying another man who cared deeply for me, and I for him.''Let us pay our respects, to Numûru, and all of our fallen heroes.''I must go back - go back to Shagâna. That is where I am needed. To help my people and shield them from the shadow of war, that it may never visit Shagâna again, at least in my lifetime.''I bid you farewell, my friend. You have been a steadfast companion to me, and one I have come to rely on and greatly appreciate.''You will always have a place in my halls, a warm bed and a cold drink. Find me, when next you come to Shagâna. I would see you again, in happier times.''Thank you for coming with me, ${PLAYER}. You should put the stones you collected on top of the ones I've gathered.''Yes, Kirí followed me here. I believe he knew what I was doing, and who it was for.'

Mizâdi looks at you, hesitating for a moment.

'Would you take him? I believe his days of adventuring are not yet over. I believe Numûru would have wanted him to go on some adventures with you.'The Kintai of Sul Madásh welcome the assistance of you and the others against their ancient enemy, Sívigush. Irsinith directs you to enlist Viznak's further assistance.Irsinith enlists you to gain Viznak's aid in learning more about the missing section of the map. Return to him at Sul Madásh.Speak with Viznak at the Sul Madásh in AdagímViznak directs you to scour the area in the south-east section of Adagím in search for something out of the ordinary. He believes that you will find a fungal growth very different from the others near the location not on the maps.Collect a peculiar-looking mushroom from south-east AdagímYou discovered a mushroom at the foot of the mountains in south-eastern Adagím. The mushroom was certainly different and out of place from the rest. Return the mushroom to Viznak at the Mother's Hill.'Viznak's counsel shall be of great value.

'Seek him out, and ask by what signs we might discern whether the 'Blight Lady' has come to this place, drawn to a hidden wellspring of the Earth-terror.''We must hurry. Go to the place on the dwarf map. Look for Uruks, look for trolls, and look for morvul! If you see blighted fungi different from others, collect one for me.''This is not good. Look at the gills. They are very different. None of the fungus here is like this. The ground here is too moist. This fungus is from the north.'Bârshud is no more, but the work is not yet complete. His forces need to be scattered to the winds, and Imizíla taken.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi within Imizíla.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi within ImizílaDefeat Ordâkhai and destroy barricades within Imizíla to force out the remaining Ordâkhai.Defeat Ordâkhai & destroy barricades within ImizílaDefeat Ordâkhai and destroy barricades within Imizíla to force out the remaining Ordâkhai.Defeat Ordâkhai within Imizíla (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy Ordâkhai barricades within Imizíla (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rally faltering Subuzûri within Imizíla and defeat the remaining Ordâkhai bóra.Defeat Ordâkhai bóra & rally faltering Subuzûri in ImizílaRally faltering Subuzûri within Imizíla and defeat the remaining Ordâkhai bóra.Defeat Ordâkhai bóra in Imizíla (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Rally faltering Subuzûri in Imizíla (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Imizíla.Find and speak with Shâra Mizâdi in ImizílaFind and speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Imizíla.Find and speak with Shâra Mizâdi in ImizílaSpeak with Razâl in Imizíla.Speak with Razâl in ImizílaSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Imizíla.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Imizíla'What happened to Sudûgul? I lost sight of him in the confusion.

'Perhaps Razâl knows where he went?''I agree with Razâl. We will return to bring Sudûgul to justice, but for now, let us savour this victory, with as dear as the cost was.

'This battle is won, the remaining Ordâkhai are in retreat. Let us head back to Ingarûma.''Yes, I saw Sudûgul. He went into the crypts of Pagru-kirít with a few of Bârshud's guards.

'We should take caution, however - we should take a large force of adventurers - we know not what dangers lurk within the Garden of Corpses.''Your distraction worked well - the Ordâkhai are in disarray. Join our Subuzûri, and take the fight to the Ordâkhai to drive them from Imizíla forever.'Sigileth wishes to tell you about her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.Sigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.Learn the severity of Corudan's injuriesSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.Follow Sigileth's account of her return from the FearwaterSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.Hear what Cúridwan had to say about Corudan's injuriesSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.<rgb=#00FF00>Shiver</rgb> at the thought of the unnatural coldSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.Hear what Cúridwan had to say of the unnatural chillSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.Hear what Sigileth believed of the spiritSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.<rgb=#00FF00>Hail</rgb> the spirit, if spirit it beSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.Listen to Sigileth's accountSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.Listen to Sigileth's accountSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.Listen to Sigileth's accountSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.Ask Sigileth what she believes happenedSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.Hear the remainder of Sigileth's accountSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.Hear what Corudan had to sayThe wound Nakási gave to my brother was deep; it worsened with travel, soaking through our makeshift bandages.'Corudan lost a great deal of blood at Kasukhín before we could stem its flow, and that would explain a chill of the body.

'But for you to feel it as well makes me think there may be another cause, an outward cause. This cold is not natural.''Hers may not... but mine do. You say this may not be Silirtas... but if it is, I have to speak to her! I have to tell her I am sorry!''I urged you to come with us, Silirtas, to face a great and unknown evil. I thought despite every danger that lay ahead of us, if any need perish, it would be Sigileth of Lórien. I thought I could keep you safe! I am so sorry!

'When you were slain by Azagath before the door of Utug-bûr, I fell into despair. I thought I too must die to atone for that terrible deed, for robbing you of the life you might have had; only the voice of  drew me out of that darkness.

'Her/His words made me realize something, dear Silirtas. Every moment of every day, for every person in this Middle-earth, is a gift: not of treasure, but of choice. Every point in time gives you the opportunity to decide how you choose to use that moment. You chose to fight the fading of your people. You chose to venture with an Elf and a  you had known for less than a day to combat an evil of the Elder Days. Those choices were yours, Silirtas, and I am inspired by them! I celebrate them!

'But I have learned there is one more choice you might make, dear one!'Sigileth wipes the tears from her eyes.

'I have said my part. I believe Silirtas heard my words... but I cannot know for certain.''That is... a curious sight...

'In what direction do these animals travel?'You have to rescue Lakhêpi the Far-faring from the brigands of Aptíku... and perhaps from herself!Lakhêpi the Far-faring is likely somewhere within the brigand camp of Aptíku, and may need your help!Search for Lakhêpi inside the brigand camp of AptíkuYou found Lakhêpi the Far-faring inside Aptíku, but she does not appear to be in any immediate danger.Observe Lakhêpi within the brigand camp of AptíkuYou found Lakhêpi the Far-faring inside Aptíku, but she does not appear to be in any immediate danger.Talk to Lakhêpi inside the brigand camp of AptíkuYou found Lakhêpi the Far-faring inside Aptíku, but she does not appear to be in any immediate danger.Watch the reaction of the brigands to your activity inside AptíkuYou found Lakhêpi the Far-faring inside Aptíku, but she does not appear to be in any immediate danger.Talk to Lakhêpi inside the brigand camp of Aptíku'Let us be on our way, friend helper. We will return to Hanamíku while these friends of Mashdagâl remain friendly to us... a state that may not long last!

'It might be different if you chose the life of a brigand... but I deem that is not your story! Am I mistaken?''This is an amusing circumstance, friend helper, you are going to laugh at this one. I was observing this camp from a safe distance, as I promised you I would, but in my eagerness I stepped upon a dry twig and was seized by the scouts of Aptíku! Well, theirs is the business of banditry, and should I hold it against them if they believed I might carry treasure of some worth to them? I confess the only valuables upon my person are located within the cache of my mind: the stories I have accumulated!

'That might not have been of great interest to them, but when I spoke the name of my last assistant, the man who aided me before you became my helper, they recognized it! His name was Mashdagâl, and while he abandoned me in An Shêru for reasons of his own, it turns out he was once a member of this camp of highwaymen!

'Because of my friendship with Mashdagâl, they agreed to let me leave in exchange for a tale. I wove them a recent yarn that might be of interest to them, concerning the great wealth accrued by a king of bandits and his instructive end... and now you are here, and we can laugh about this misunderstanding. They may be brigands, but if we treat them kindly they will do the same with us.''Hmm. I think this truce will last only for so long as they believe you might join their band, and as I deem the life of a highwayman is not the life you intend to lead, we had best hasten on our way.'A summer thunderstorm has come to Minas Tirith alongside messages that spur the onset of a new adventure.The Ranger Orthonn is eager to speak with you inside the Splintered Shield.Talk to Orthonn in the Splintered ShieldOrthonn and Dagoras have invited you to <rgb=#00FF00>sit</rgb> by the table in the Splintered Shield.Listen to the conversation in the Splintered Shield concerning the cause for this meeting.Listen to Orthonn and Dagoras in the Splintered ShieldOrthonn sighs heavily and shakes his head.Talk to Orthonn in the Splintered ShieldListen to the conversation in the Splintered Shield concerning the cause for this meeting.Listen to Orthonn and Dagoras in the Splintered ShieldThrymm Red-beard has come to the Splintered Shield and overheard your conversation with Orthonn and Dagoras.Talk to Thrymm Red-beard in the Splintered ShieldOrthonn has come to a decision.Listen to Orthonn's decisionOrthonn has some words for you before you depart.Talk to Orthonn in the Splintered ShieldYou and your companions begin your journey toward Mordor.Travel with your companions toward MordorDagoras has called a halt on the road that runs through Ithilien.Talk to Dagoras beside the road that runs through IthilienYour companions are resting beside the road that runs through Ithilien.Talk to Thrymm Red-beard in IthilienTalk to Orthonn in IthilienDagoras is ready to resume your journey toward Mordor.Talk to Dagoras and continue your journey toward MordorYou and your companions continue your journey toward Mordor.Travel with your companions toward MordorYour companions have entered Mordor, and now you continue your journey toward Seregost.Talk to Orthonn in Dor AmarthYour companions have entered Mordor, and now you continue your journey toward Seregost.Ride with your companions through Dor AmarthThrymm has paused midway through Dor Amarth with some questions for you.Talk to Thrymm Red-beard in Dor AmarthYou and your companions continue your journey toward Agarnaith.Travel with your companions toward AgarnaithA white horse stands unattended in Agarnaith, within view of the keep of Seregost.Examine the unattended steed outside SeregostYou are not the only ones to have come to Agarnaith on this day.Remain alert in the swamps of AgarnaithYour friend Harthalín has come to survey the keep of Seregost in the swamps of Agarnaith!Talk to Harthalín in AgarnaithYour companions introduce themselves to Harthalín and inquire about her mission at Seregost.Listen to the conversation of your companions and HarthalínHarthalín has agreed to answer your questions.Talk to Harthalín in AgarnaithDagoras is in Agarnaith, thinking about what is to be done.Talk to Dagoras in Agarnaith'This is my favourite of the many taverns that can be found in the White City, ${PLAYER}. It will be no hardship to wait out the rain and thunder beneath this roof!''Lhaereth oft escapes justice with winged speed, only to reappear somewhere else. I am put in mind of a river-channel blocked by fallen trees and brush; after enough rain-fall, the river bursts forth elsewhere!

'Through your efforts and those of others, we have dammed the river of Lhaereth's evil, but for so long as she lives she will not abandon her works of malice. Faeron and Rhadrog fear the Lady of Blight may return to her keep of Seregost and renew her attempts to create a Second Great Plague with which to threaten Gondor.'You tell Thrymm that you are only lately returned, and he laughs heartily.

'From the talk I have overheard, it sounds as if you will not be here long! Well do I understand the need for combat and for excitement. Why, that is what has brought me to the Splintered Shield nearly every day since the wedding of the King of Gondor! But I am not supposed to speak of it. Know only that these muscles will tire before my martial spirit, and if that happens the grave must accept me!

'But the war is done, and it seems we shall be beset by peace! I cannot return to my own land and my own wedding if I believed danger still threatened. Share with me your secret worries and Thrymm will aid you in besting them!'

With Orthonn's permission you share with Thrymm the fears of Faeron and Rhadrog, and he eagerly insists that he accompany you to Seregost.'Our mission is urgent, but if its success depends upon the departure of one storm-cloud, we have already failed. Trust that we have time enough!

'If we must return to Mordor, let us do so wearing dry clothes!''We have travelled far already, but there is much further to go. Let us stop for a few moments to let both horse and rider rest.''One last adventure, ${PLAYER}, and I will return to Wildermore and wed my Cyneberg. I seek not to delay that happy day, but if danger brews anew in Mordor no man of Rohan could remain idle, and Thrymm Red-beard less than any!

'My betrothed will understand. Is she not a shieldmaiden of Rohan, and no stranger to battle herself? What courage she displayed when the terrible giant Núrzum blanketed Wildermore in ice and snow! Why, if it was Cyneberg who overheard your talk in the Splintered Shield and not Thrymm Red-beard, I believe she would be the one riding to Mordor with you on this day!'

Thrymm pats the neck of his steed.

'I borrowed this fine fellow from the stables of Minas Tirith with the permission of the grooms there, and gave to him the caparison of a horse of Rohan that perished on the Pelennor. Stylhóf I have named him, for though he was not bred of Rohan I wanted him to have a Rohirric name: "Steel-hoof" is its meaning. He carries the name, and me, very well indeed!''When last we came this way, we marched toward the unknown. None of us knew what awaited us at the Black Gate. Even having been there and seen it with my own eyes I cannot fully believe what transpired: the fall of Sauron and the defeat of his armies!

'New masters thought to rule Mordor in the days following the destruction of Sauron, but none could match that Dark Lord in power or potency. And that is a good thing for Gondor, and for all of Middle-earth, but we must not underestimate their evil or their desire to do great harm. The reports I have heard of Lhaereth's contagions...'

Orthonn shudders.

'Well, let us make sure she has not returned to Seregost to perfect them. She may not rival Sauron in power, but if she is not his equal in hatred I deem she may at least approach that vile one in malice, and in evil intent!

'Gwaebad will carry me beyond the Black Gate and into Mordor. We are not afraid.''I am in no hurry to return to Mordor, ${PLAYER}, for the challenges we faced in Minas Morgul remain etched in my memory... but I know this mission is important.

'We must pass by the Black Gate and return once more to Mordor if we are to learn if Lhaereth has come back to Seregost. Our ride continues.''The hush is peculiar.

'Has this become an empty land, or do its occupants hide from us, lying in wait and watching us as we pass?''I would rather fight a score of foes than wait for an equal number of minutes, ${PLAYER}! It has always been thus!

'When I agreed to come with your scouting party I believed there would be fighting! Let us hope Seregost does not disappoint!

'Of course I am not wishing Lhaereth's evil upon Middle-earth! You know my meaning, ${PLAYER}. This infernal quiet has me on edge. Let us continue onward, and perhaps this appalling silence will soon be broken!''Yes, I know ${PLAYER}, and I would name us friends! My name is Harthalín, and I fought beside the Last Alliance of Men and Elves at the Battle of Dagorlad, three thousand years ago. I believed Sauron was destroyed, but it was not so. Through some sorcery Sauron survived to trouble Middle-earth.

'When I received word that the Dark Lord had been defeated once again, only months ago, I disbelieved it and returned to this land. It was then that I met ${PLAYER}, and we worked together to put an end to any of Sauron's still-living schemes.

'I believe now that the Dark Lord is truly gone, and that many of his servants have joined him in death. Many, I say... but not all.''It was a dream, ${PLAYER}, a dream that filled me with a sense of foreboding. Three times have I dreamed this dream, but familiarity has not made its meaning more clear to me, nor its presence more welcome. The phantasmal images chill me to my very bones, though I have stood with courage against some of Middle-earth's most frightening terrors.

'I dreamed of a stone chamber, a chamber with neither entrance nor exit. I knew not how I came to be there, and while the dream persisted I could sense no means of leaving the chamber. Only waking could free me from that place, but while I was held by that dream it was no dream at all, and seemed as real to me as anything I have experienced in all my years of life. There was an evil about that inaccessible chamber; it lay heavily upon the stones, but I could not identify its source.'

Harthalín shakes her head to clear away the ill-feeling memory.

'My people are not quick to disregard the meaning of dreams. When that same dream returned on subsequent nights, I bent all my thought upon deciphering it. If the chamber with no doors is not a real place, what might it represent? I believed it might represent the keep of Seregost, accessible only by the air or by those who might climb such a great height. And so I made the climb thinking Lhaereth might have come back to Seregost, and some force for good wanted me to confront her. I searched the keep for any sign that she might have returned and begun anew the work she had halted.''It is good to learn that Lhaereth has not returned to Seregost, but unless I am mistaken we have discovered further dangers!

'I will ride back to Minas Tirith and bring these tidings to the King. Doubt not that he will dispatch scouts to these new lands, for Gondor must learn if servants of Sauron are active elsewhere as they were on Gorgoroth!

'Go forth in safety, and trust in your companions! We do not know what dangers await you in the further reaches of Mordor!'The barracks of Emax Dûl have been abandoned by the city guards, but they still contain a bounty of weapons and equipment. Let us claim them for Shâra Mizâdi's cause!You have arrived in the Emax Dûl guard barracks.

You should talk to Numûru.Talk to NumûruThe barracks appear to have been abandoned.

You should look around and find the armoury.Find the armouryYou have found the armoury.

You should collect Ordâkhai weapons.Collect Ordâkhai weapons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You are being ambushed by Ordâkhai!

