You should defeat the Utûgi.Defeat the Utûgi'Let us return to Nashûbu. I will send a group to gather the remaining weapons.''The barracks look... abandoned? Hmm.... Let's look around. See if you can find the armoury, and keep an eye out for any Ordâkhai.''An Utûgi captain and his party now block our path. I see no other option but to fight through. Are you ready?'Inside the tombs there is a dank chill in the air and bones piled high - a mountain of the dead. Over our own footsteps we can hear the sounds of rustling. So much rustling. The Dead - or something worse - is restless in these tombs.Move forward in the tombs of Mut-hûru to investigate any signs of Bârshud or Sudûgul.Move forward in the tombs of Mut-hûru to investigateListen to Mizâdi and Numûru's conversation.Listen to Mizâdi and Numûru's conversationListen to Bârshud and Sudûgul's conversation.Listen to Bârshud and Sudûgul's conversationListen to Bârshud and Sudûgul's conversation.Listen to Bârshud and Sudûgul's conversation<rgb=#ff0000>Do not let Bârshud see you</rgb>Fight off the wights in the tomb!Fight off the wights (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Make your escape from the tombs of Mut-hûru.Make your escape from the tombs of Mut-hûruMake your escape from the tombs of Mut-hûru.Make your escape from the tombs of Mut-hûruOur glorious victory is close! I can practically taste it. We just need to take Imizíla and Bârshud - and his forces - will soon fall.Join the conversation with Mizâdi and Numûru.Join the conversation with Mizâdi and NumûruJoin the conversation with Mizâdi and Numûru.Join the conversation with Mizâdi and NumûruSpeak with Mizâdi near Imizíla.Speak with Mizâdi near ImizílaDefend Mizâdi from the Ordâkhai counter-attack!Defend Mizâdi from the Ordâkhai counter-attackDefend Mizâdi from the Ordâkhai counter-attack!Defend Mizâdi from the Ordâkhai counter-attack<rgb=#ff0000>Mizâdi must not falter</rgb>Join Mizâdi and Numûru once more near the main gate of Imizíla.Join Mizâdi and Numûru near the main gate of ImizílaJoin Mizâdi and Numûru once more near the main gate of Imizíla.Join Mizâdi and Numûru near the main gate of ImizílaJoin Numûru and the Subuzûri to take the main gate.Take the main gate with NumûruSpeak with Mizâdi to determine what to do next.Speak with Mizâdi to determine what to do next'I understand Numûru's concerns, but I will not let Bârshud slip from my grasp again. He will die this day.''I - we - fall back! Everyone - fall back to Ingarûma!Bârshud has taken everything from me. And I will have my vengeance, paid in the blood price.Move forward into Bârshud's fortress.Move forward into Bârshud's fortressKill Bârshud's guards within Imizíla.Defeat Bârshud's guards (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})<rgb=#ff0000>Mizâdi must not falter</rgb>Move forward to confront Bârshud in his throne room.Move forward to confront Bârshud in his throne roomListen to the conversation in Bârshud's throne room.Listen to the conversation in Bârshud's throne roomDefeat the risen Numûru within Bârshud's fortress in Imizíla.Defeat the risen Numûru<rgb=#ff0000>Mizâdi must not falter</rgb>Listen to Mizâdi and Bârshud's conversation.Listen to Mizâdi and Bârshud's conversationListen to Mizâdi and Bârshud's conversation.Listen to Mizâdi and Bârshud's conversationSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi about what to do next.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi about what to do nextListen to Mizâdi and Rahâzi's conversation.Listen to Mizâdi and Rahâzi's conversationListen to Mizâdi and Rahâzi's conversation.Listen to Mizâdi and Rahâzi's conversation'Oh, Numûru, you deserved so much better than this.'As the palace of Emax Dûl succumbs to the control of Thothril the Entangler, many civilians have become trapped. It is our duty to free them before they are driven to madness.You have arrived inside the servant's living quarters of the palace.

You should talk to Razâl.Talk to RazâlYou have arrived inside the servant's living quarters of the palace.

You should investigate the area.Investigate the servants' quartersThothril the Entangler has begun to take over the minds of the servants in the palace.

