You should defeat Head Servant Sintáhi.Defeat Head Servant Sintáhi'It is done. Let's get back to Nashûbu.''We have arrived unseen! Now, we need to assess the servants' condition here. I just hope we are not too late!''Thothril the Entangler has already begun driving these people mad! We need to save who we can, and fast! However, I fear some of them may be too far gone to save....''That seems to be everyone who is still sane. We must now deal with the head servant. She seemed practically fanatical in her devotion to Thothril, and will only drive others to madness if she is left alive. Let's end this and get out of here.'This will be the perfect site for a camp. It just needs some hard work, a couple new tents - and fewer brigands.Enter Ingarûma and make your way inside the camp.Enter IngarûmaDefeat brigands within Ingarûma and destroy their hastily constructed fortifications.Defeat brigands within Ingarûma (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Destroy hastily constructed barricades (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Find and defeat the brigand chief Zalûd within Ingarûma.Find and defeat the brigand chief Zalûd within IngarûmaFind and defeat the brigand chief Zalûd within Ingarûma.Find and defeat the brigand chief Zalûd within IngarûmaBuild new camp-fires and construct new tents in Ingarûma.Build new camp-fires in Ingarûma (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Construct new tents in Ingarûma (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Plant Mizadi's banner at the highest point in Ingarûma to signal to the others that it is now safe to arrive.Plant Mizadi's banner at the highest point in IngarûmaThe fate of some members of the Kindred of the Coins remain a mystery, and for now can only be guessed at by wondering minds.Guard-captain Gadâr stands prepared to defend you within Dâr Laja.Talk to Gadâr within Dâr LajaGadâr has sworn to protect you. You should stay close to him.Follow Gadâr and remain under his protectionJaith has entered Dâr Laja with information about what transpires in the city.Talk to Jaith inside Dâr LajaYour guards have left Dâr Laja to prevent the uprising from entering the Meeting-hall and doing you some harm. You should return to the main hall and stay away from the entrance!Return to the safety of the main hall of Dâr LajaKhôltekh motions for you to speak to him.Talk to Khôltekh in the main hall of Dâr LajaThe catacombs of Umbar-môkh may allow you to flee the uprising and escape to safety!Flee through Umbar-môkh to safety!Khôltekh has led you into Umbar-môkh, through which you must find safety!Talk to Khôltekh in Umbar-môkhKhôltekh hopes to lead you through Umbar-môkh to safety!Follow Khôltekh through Umbar-môkh to safetyTemámir soldiers bar your passage.Talk to the Temámir guardsman barring your passageTemámir soldiers bar your passage.Temámir soldiers bar your passageKhôltekh had better have an explanation for this insult!Talk to Khôltekh and demand an explanationKhôltekh nods in the direction of the waggons to the north.'You have nothing to fear, my Lady. The doors of Dâr Laja are strong, and the men who guard them are even stronger! None of the shouting throng will get inside.''The area from Dâr Laja to Bith Gabâr is packed with residents of the city, a shouting throng. Many in the crowd carry weapons, but for now they have not wielded them against us. I think that will not change, but I cannot say that with certainty.

'You must stay inside, my Lady. It is not safe for you out there. I fear we cannot protect you if you leave the safety of the Meeting-hall!''Dâr Laja is not safe for us, Hármelak. I know you trust in your guardsmen to keep the unruly throng at bay... but I have not that faith in them.

'The city has come alive with anger, and that fury is directed at you... at us. If we remain here, I believe we will be slain.''Most of the crowd has not yet thought to look for us in Umbar-môkh. We can follow these passages to safety!''Hold it right there, Hármelak.'

The Temámir meaningfully grips the haft of his spear and nods in the direction of Khôltekh.

'I will not use this unless I am commanded to do so... but I will obey the order if it is given.''Spare me your indignation, Hármelak: you know what happens to those who gamble with the lives of others without taking care to slant the odds sufficiently in their favour. The Song of Waves and Wind proved very useful, and it may be that Gondor lies in ruin even now, but you failed to manage the people of the city, and they have turned upon you. That they think to also hold me accountable for your blunder is... unfortunate.

'But the memories of the people are short. You will be kept safe and unharmed until such time as it is politically advantageous for the Temámir to produce you.

'The waggons to the north will transport you safely out of the city and beyond reach of the crowd that calls for your head. This is much finer treatment than you would receive from anyone else; let us say it is in remembrance of the tyrants we overthrew, and the Kindred we led together, if only for a short time.'I come to call on Mizâdi, and not a moment too soon. For she is shaken, her army defeated, her spirit frail. In this moment I can feel the heavy weight of many lives in Mûr Ghala and Shagâna - they all hang in the balance.Join Mizâdi, Rahâzi, and Razâl's conversation inside Mizâdi's tent.Join Mizâdi, Rahâzi, and Razâl's conversationListen to Mizâdi and Rahâzi's conversation.Listen to Mizâdi and Rahâzi's conversationGrab the map from the pile of scrolls in the corner of the tent.Grab the map from the pile of scrollsPlace the map on the table in front of Mizâdi and Rahâzi.Listen to the conversation between Mizâdi, Razâl, and Rahâzi.Listen to the conversation between Mizâdi, Razâl, and RahâziListen to the conversation between Mizâdi, Razâl, and Rahâzi.Listen to the conversation between Mizâdi, Razâl, and RahâziSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi inside the tent.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi inside the tent'We have much to do, and still more to plan.'The palace of Emax Dûl has fallen under the control of one of the Thardúth of Damudûr, Thothril the Entangler. Many important records and tomes are still stored in this historic Nêshakari fortress. We must recover them, before they are destroyed in the fighting!You have arrived in the royal living quarters.

You should talk to Sorkamâl.Talk to SorkamâlSorkamâl fears valuable tomes may be destroyed in the fighting in Emax Dûl.

You should collect historical tomes in the royal living quarters.Collect historical tomes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})You have collected as many tomes as you can carry.

You should talk to Sorkamâl.Talk to SorkamâlSorkamâl would like to check one more location before you leave.

You should investigate the Sai's bed-chamber.Investigate the Sai's bed-chamberYou have found a strange broken statue near the Sai's bed.

You should investigate the artifact piece.Investigate the artifact pieceSorkamâl is curious to learn more about the broken artifact.

You should collect the remaining artifact pieces.You have collected the pieces of the artifact.

You should assemble the artifact by placing the pieces on the bottom section.Assemble the artifactAn Ordâkhai sorcerer has appeared and threatens you!

You should defeat Dúrkhamos the Far-reaching.Defeat Dúrkhamos the Far-reachingThe statue you assembled exudes a fell aura.

You should destroy the assembled Thardúth statue.Destroy the Thardúth statue'We have saved what we can. Let us be gone from this place, before some other foul sorcerer ambushes us or any other statues come to life.''What a beautiful palace this is! It is unfortunate that such ugly cruelty has been allowed to reside inside it....

'Come, we should scour this place and retrieve as many tomes as we can carry. The guards and servants are already acting strangely, perhaps because of this 'Thothril the Entangler' I keep hearing so much about. We should gather what we can and leave, and quickly.''That is as many tomes as we can carry without weighing us down. There is one more place I would like to look before we leave: the Sai's bed-chamber. I believe it is in the rear of the area. Anything of higher value will likely be found there.'Travelling in these lands, I have made bonds with many whose stories are like mine. The tyranny and depravity of Ordâkh has armed us with a common resentment. As rebellion gathers at my back and allies join my table, we plan to besiege Emax Dûl.The leaders of the rebellion have gathered in Ahâba.

You should talk to Mizâdi to begin the meeting.Talk to MizâdiThe leaders of the rebellion have gathered in Ahâba to plan their attack.

You should listen to the conversation.Listen to the conversationAhâba is under attack!

You should defeat the attacking Ordâkhai!Defeat the attacking OrdâkhaiSomeone approaches in the darkness.

You should listen to the conversation.Listen to the conversation'Please, hear my words. I wish only to save my family.''Good, you are here right on time. Our meeting can now proceed.

'Despite our growing numbers, this will still be a difficult battle. Let us hear how everyone thinks we should proceed.'You embark on a journey back to Viznak and learn that travel through Mûr Ghala grows more harrowing by the moment.Make your way to Viznak in Adagím.Make your way north-west toward Viznak's encampmentMake your way to Viznak in Adagím.Continue your journey west through AdagímMake your way to Viznak in Adagím.Search among the trees to the north-west for safe passage to ViznakMake your way to Viznak in Adagím.Defeat DúrvenelInform Viznak that you were coming to visit him in Adagím.Speak with Viznak'You come see me in Sul Madásh.''You strong, but you lucky I was looking this far west. Or, you likely dead. Meet me back at the Sul Madásh. We talk there.'Emax Dûl, the ancient Nêshakari stronghold overlooking Idagâl, has long been known to be an impenetrable fortress. Many invasions have failed at its gates. The prince of Ordâkh and his forces are counting on this to protect themselves from the growing rebellion just outside their walls, but unknown to them, the fortress has a weakness.Razâl is standing by to begin the infiltration plan.

You should talk to Razâl when you are ready to begin.Talk to RazâlRazâl is with you and ready to begin.

You should enter the secret cave system.Enter the secret cave systemYou and Razâl must find a way into the gate-house to open the gates of Emax Dûl.

You should explore the caves with Razâl and find the entrance to the gate-house.Find the entrance to the gate-houseYou have found the gate-house.

You should defeat the guards in the gate-house before they can signal the alarm.Defeat the guards in the gate-houseYou have successfully taken control of the gate-house.

You should find and use the lever for the main gate.Use the gate leverMizâdi's forces have begun the invasion of the city.

You should exit the gate-house to the streets of Emax Dûl.Exit the gate-houseMizâdi's forces are fighting for control of Emax Dûl.

You should find Mizâdi somewhere up ahead.Find MizâdiMizâdi has cornered Góramul Sai at the steps to the palace.

You should help your allies defeat Góramul Sai.Defeat Góramul Sai'We hold the city, but Bârshud and Góramul Sai have eluded me. We must take a moment to catch our breath, assess our casualties, and then pursue the prince.''Kotráka Saiya says the secret way into the city is through here. The two of us will enter the cave system, find the way to the gate-house, and open the main gates to the city, allowing our forces through.

'Everyone is counting on us. Let us go!'You have come with Guardsman Khârdab to try and save both Pasumín the Toy-maker and the children of Hanamíku from the Ordâkhai.You have come with Guardsman Khârdab to an encampment of the Ordâkhai to rescue Pasumín and the children of Hanamíku.Talk to Khârdab outside the encampmentGuardsman Khârdab has stayed behind to hold off the pursuing Ordâkhai while you continue further into the encampment in search of the children and Pasumín.Continue further into the encampment in search of the childrenYou have found Pasumín within Nakársong, but the toy-maker has suffered many grievous wounds.Talk to Pasumín within NakársongPasumín has succumbed to the wounds he suffered, but his duty is not yet complete: you must stand in defence of the children!Defend the children of Hanamíku from the Ordâkhai of NakársongYou have defended Tebût and his friends from the Ordâkhai of Nakársong.Talk to Tebût in NakársongKhârdab has rejoined you, and desires to know if the children and the toy-maker are safe.Remain on your guardKhârdab has rejoined you in the depths of Nakársong.Talk to Khârdab in Nakársong'Let us return to Hanamíku before more Ordâkhai come.''If the children intended to reach the area where the lions are kept, we may have to fight past numerous soldiers to reach them. Fear no foes! Time now is our greatest enemy, for Pasumín has not raised a sword in anger for many years, and the Ordâkhai will not hesitate to cut him down alongside the children!''I have done... what I could... ${PLAYER}...

'You must... save them now...''Oh no...'

Khârdab surveys the bodies within Nakársong and shakes his head sadly.

'So he is slain... I feared it would be so. The soldier that Pasumín once was returned to save the children of Hanamíku from death, but that grim reckoning has carried away the man he had become.''I did not mean for this to happen, ${PLAYER}!

'Why did Pasumín come after us? We thought if we were caught by the Ordâkhai then the Hamâti soldiers might save us... but he was just a toy-maker! Why would HE wield a blade to defend us? Did he not know he would perish?'The party has begun, and now everyone has a chance to make merry and forget their troubles, if only for a night.Numûru told you to enjoy the party! Sample the various unique dishes within the party.You hear Numûru calling you from upstairs - perhaps you should find him?Speak with Numûru upstairs at the partyNumûru looks like he would like to speak with you.Speak with Numûru upstairs at the partyGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi.Guard the door for Numûru as he speaks with MizâdiGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi.Guard the door for Numûru as he speaks with MizâdiYou see an over-eager party-goer coming this way. Turn them away!You see an over-eager party-goer coming. Turn them away!Guard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi.Guard the door for Numûru as he speaks with MizâdiGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi.Guard the door for Numûru as he speaks with MizâdiYou see an over-eager party-goer coming this way. Turn them away!You see an over-eager party-goer coming. Turn them away!Guard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi.Guard the door for Numûru as he speaks with MizâdiGuard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi.Guard the door for Numûru as he speaks with Mizâdi'One final ask, my friend. Could you stand watch here, and gently turn away any over-eager party-goers?

'It is quite important that I say what is in my heart to Mizâdi without interruption. Will you help me with this?'Pasumín has been laid to rest outside the village of Hanamíku.Guardsman Khârdab stands in the cemetery of Khabur Pâshu near Hanamíku.Talk to Guardsman Khârdab at Khabur PâshuGuardsman Khârdab stands in the cemetery of Khabur Pâshu near Hanamíku.Listen to Guardsman Khârdab at Khabur PâshuGuardsman Khârdab stands in the cemetery of Khabur Pâshu near Hanamíku.Talk to Guardsman Khârdab at Khabur PâshuGuardsman Khârdab stands in the cemetery of Khabur Pâshu near Hanamíku.Stand with Guardsman Khârdab at Khabur PâshuTebût and his friends have come to the cemetery of Khabur Pâshu near Hanamíku.Talk to Tebût at Khabur PâshuTebût and his friends have come to the cemetery of Khabur Pâshu near Hanamíku.Listen to Tebût's questionTebût and his friends have come to the cemetery of Khabur Pâshu near Hanamíku.Give Tebût your answer to his questionTebût and his friends have come to the cemetery of Khabur Pâshu near Hanamíku.Stand at Khabur Pâshu as Tebût and his friends visit Pasumín's graveGuardsman Khârdab stands in the cemetery of Khabur Pâshu near Hanamíku.Talk to Guardsman Khârdab at Khabur Pâshu'I have grown cold. Let us return to the village.''When Pasumín came to live in Hanamíku, many years ago, he left his old life behind and started anew, using his skills as a woodworker to repair the buildings and fences of the village. But it was the carving of wooden toys for the children that brought him the most joy; whenever I saw him engaged in that pursuit I saw the light in his eye, and I knew the deeds of his past were far from his thoughts.''Everything seems so unreal, ${PLAYER}. We watched the Hamâti soldiers training, and we were captivated by their strength and their force of arms. Their swords shone so brightly! How could they lose against the cowardly Ordâkhai?

'But they were not the ones who did battle at Nakársong! It was the toy-maker Pasumín who fought for us, and it was he who fell defending us! He was no soldier! He was just a toy-maker! Why would he do battle with the Ordâkhai? Why did he fight for us?

'We were cruel to him, ${PLAYER}, and he died to save us. But we did not mean for it to happen.''The children of Hanamíku will remember this day, ${PLAYER}, and Pasumín will be with them always. Even when they are grown they will not forget what he sacrificed. He meant more to them than I knew, and I believe his memory will now guide their steps.

'May it keep them safe in these dangerous days.'You speak to Khârdab of an adventurous life lived in the wild, where death seemed a constant companion. He nods sadly.

'The life you have chosen is a hard one, ${PLAYER}. Not all would choose such.'Mûr Ghala emerges from the yoke of oppression, but tyranny and danger persist. Forward thinkers seek assistance from any who would advance the cause of freedom in the awakening land.You were directed to speak with a Steward of Mûr Ghala to expand the breadth and impact of your assistance in the land. You should seek the counsel of Lejâl in Zajâna or Calúrmin in Sul Madásh.Speak with the Steward of Mûr Ghala, Calúrmin, at Sul MadáshSpeak with the Steward of Mûr Ghala, Lejâl, at Zajâna'Mûr Ghala stirs from long slumber, yet the shadows of night do not flee swiftly. Though we speak now of places marred by blight and infested by ancient foes, know that where embers yet smoulder, flame may rise anew.

'Our scouts remain vigilant, but they are few, and the fires of strife may kindle faster than they can be quenched. Speak with a Steward of Mûr Ghala, either Lejâl in Zajâna or Calúrmin in Sul Madásh. They shall guide you in where your strength may best serve the land and her people.''Mûr Ghala stirs from long slumber, yet the shadows of night do not flee swiftly. Though we speak now of places marred by blight and infested by ancient foes, know that where embers yet smoulder, flame may rise anew.

‘Our scouts remain vigilant, but they are few, and the fires of strife may kindle faster than they can be quenched. Speak with a Steward of Mûr Ghala, either Lejâl in Zajâna or Calúrmin in Sul Madásh. They shall guide you in where your strength may best serve the land and her people.''Mûr Ghala stirs from long slumber, yet the shadows of night do not flee swiftly. Though we speak now of places marred by blight and infested by ancient foes, know that where embers yet smoulder, flame may rise anew.

‘Our scouts remain vigilant, but they are few, and the fires of strife may kindle faster than they can be quenched. Speak with a Steward of Mûr Ghala, either Lejâl in Zajâna or Calúrmin in Sul Madásh. They shall guide you in where your strength may best serve the land and her people.''From the ashes of strife, new hope takes root. Yet renewal is not without trial. Loyalists to the yoke of tyranny still walk among us, servants of the All-seeing Eye, whose hearts remain black with malice. Where they tread, peril follows.

'They raid and burn; they slaughter without mercy, clinging to the vestiges of a crumbling dominion. As the jázga cornered and wounded, they strike with desperate fury, more dangerous now than before.

'Our scouts, though vigilant, report stirrings of wickedness in places where the foulest take shelter, and where unrest secretly brews. This knowledge we pass to those who would stand with our cause, to drive out the last shadows of the long night. And not only in battle, but in the mending of what was broken. We find our strength for hearth and home must be restored if the land is to flourish once more.

'If your heart is willing, reward shall not be withheld, nor honour forgotten. Visit me each day and I will direct your efforts.''From the ashes of strife, new hope takes root. Yet renewal is not without trial. Loyalists to the yoke of tyranny still walk among us, servants of the All-seeing Eye, whose hearts remain black with malice. Where they tread, peril follows.

'They raid and burn; they slaughter without mercy, clinging to the vestiges of a crumbling dominion. As the jázga cornered and wounded, they strike with desperate fury, more dangerous now than before.

'Our scouts, though vigilant, report stirrings of wickedness in places where the foulest take shelter, and where unrest secretly brews. This knowledge we pass to those who would stand with our cause, to drive out the last shadows of the long night. And not only in battle, but in the mending of what was broken. We find our strength for hearth and home must be restored if the land is to flourish once more.

'If your heart is willing, reward shall not be withheld, nor honour forgotten.  Visit me each day and I will direct your efforts.'Track down and defeat every formidable enemy in Idagâl.Track down and defeat every formidable enemy in Idagâl.Defeat Kasâshu the GrinderDefeat ErshubâtDefeat Akílu the FeasterDefeat GírkhashDefeat UmanûguDefeat Mórobul the World-treaderDefeat SúlkhorDefeat Brikóno the MarauderDefeat Imtushâl the Gall-spitterDefeat many kergrim lurking deep within Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many kergrim lurking deep within Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many kergrim in Hatokáli FellsDefeat a great many kergrim lurking deep within Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many kergrim lurking deep within Hatokáli Fells.Defeat a great many kergrim lurking deep within Hatokáli Fells.Defeat a great many kergrim in Hatokáli FellsDefeat many kergrim throughout Idagâl.Defeat many kergrim in Idagâl.Defeat many kergrim in IdagâlDefeat a great many kergrim throughout Idagâl.Defeat many kergrim in Idagâl.Defeat a great many kergrim in Idagâl.Defeat a great many kergrim in IdagâlHaving captured the Dragon, Mizâdi now asks for you to speak with him and find out what he knows about Bârshud.Speak with Khórpon Bóro in Hanamíku. He can be found near the courtyard with vines within Hanamíku.Speak with Khórpon Bóro in HanamíkuSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in HanamíkuSpeak with Khórpon Bóro in Hanamíku.Speak with Khórpon Bóro in HanamíkuSeek out a tool-maker in Hanamíku. You may find one near the markets.Gather iron from deposits in the hills west of Hanamíku.Mine ore for Unagâr west of Hanamíku (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Unagâr, the tool-maker in Hanamíku.Defeat wasps near Unagâr's home near the road, west of Hanamíku.Defeat wasps outside of Unagâr's house (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak once more with Unagâr the tool-maker in Hanamíku.Speak with Unagâr the tool-maker in HanamíkuPresent the key to Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku. Hanamíku can be found in Pahar Hatokáli, within Mûr Ghala.'He knows something about Bârshud. For someone called 'the Dragon', he has been weeping quite profusely. Perhaps that's common among dragons, I know not.

'Speak with him - he is across the way there. Some of our Subuzûri are keeping a close eye on him, although I have little worry he will attempt an escape. I believe he knows something important about Bârshud. Please, find out anything you can from him.''Thank you for all your hard work getting this, friend. With this, we have what we need to find what Bârshud was after, and with luck, him as well.''I will tell you what I know. Swear to spare my life!

'I have heard rumours of Mizâdi - they say she is honourable. If she swears to spare me, I will tell you everything I know about Bârshud. I have information. He visited Bolo Thúki on his way south.''He wants mercy? I doubt that he deserves such clemency, but we seldom need to make deals with the best of Men, do we?

'Very well, tell him I will spare his life in exchange for what he knows about Bârshud. He leaves Hatokáli though, and heads further south. I do not want him in Mûr Ghala.''Very well. I have heard rumours of the Shâra. None of those rumours claim that she is dishonorable. I will help you in exchange for safe passage out of these lands.

'I bear on my person a mould for a key. It was given to me by Bârshud, should I need to enter the depths of Mut-hûru. That is where he is going - the tombs south of here. I know not why.

'You will find the mould in my tunic. Yes, there. You need only to bring it to a tool-maker, someone that can forge iron. It is a heavy door - it will require quite a bit of metal for such a key.''A key? You have a mould for it?

'Yes, and quite a large one you'll need, looking at that mould. I do not have the iron on hand for it. There is some in the mountains west of here. Be warned, it is dangerous - a band of thieves keeps their camp in the mountains to the west.

'There is another matter, that of payment. We will breach that topic once you have brought me the iron I need for the key.''Ah yes, that is more than enough iron for the key.

'As I said, however, there is still the matter of payment. I do not want your coin. You see, I live just outside of Hanamíku, to the west. This past month, I have been harried day and night by huge stinging wasps. They wait outside my home. Such pests they are! Kill those cursed wasps. By the time you return, I shall have your key forged and ready for you.''Just in time. There it is, quite heavy too.

'No, I do not require proof. You travel with Shâra Mizâdi, I trust you are honourable and true to your word, as she is.

'I shall sleep soundly for the first time in months - thank you, friend. I hope the key brings you that which you seek.'The Khemozêl Clan has posted a task to collect blood-coated axes. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire blood-coated axes for the Khemozêl Clan.Wanted: blood-coated axes from Draugardh. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: blood-coated axes from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Khemozêl Clan has posted a task to collect blood-soaked claws. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire blood-soaked claws for the Khemozêl Clan.Wanted: blood-soaked claws from Draugardh. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: blood-soaked claws from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Khemozêl Clan have posted a task to collect blood-stained hides. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire blood-stained hides for the Khemozêl Clan.Wanted: blood-stained hides from Draugardh. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: blood-stained hides from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Khemozêl Clan has posted a task to collect bloody goo. This can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire bloody goo for the Khemozêl Clan.Wanted: bloody goo from Draugardh. Gather it to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: bloody goo from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Khemozêl Clan has posted a task to collect deformed ears. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire deformed ears for the Khemozêl Clan.Wanted: deformed ears from Draugardh. Gather them 