tors.Wanted: sun-scorched sword sheaths from Mûr Ghala.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Explore enemy camps, settlements, and lairs in An Shêru in Mûr Ghala.Explore enemy camps, settlements, and lairs in An Shêru in Mûr Ghala.Find DamudûrFind Naxar DâlFind the Crypts of Khâb DakuFind Spoiler's CragFind ZakhûrFind the Spent-lodesFind AbníshuFind the Seething-wellsFind the Pools of TaridímFind the Roost of the AnzûriFind OnabóhaFind the Beast-fieldsFind UruthúshFind the Arch of AdazârFind the Slopes of ShâlahinFind GebarakórFind Kôth RauFind LâkindarExplore enemy camps, settlements, and lairs in Idagâl in Mûr Ghala.Explore enemy camps, settlements, and lairs in Idagâl in Mûr Ghala.Find the Haunt of Kidu-bâlaFind DurígaFind the Fane of ShahûruFind Gnasher's DelfFind Nax ShalâlFind UshumûtFind the Wither-watchFind JolakhúroFind Emax DûlFind Karmu RâxFind the ScardelveFind the Tombs of Khâb IshilFind Esh MêkagDissatisfied with each of the options, Kishâtal is desperate to find some other solution to his problem.Kagûlu the Armsman is by the forges at the war camp of Ingarûma.Talk to Kagûlu the Armsman at the war camp of IngarûmaKagûlu the Armsman has suggested one more weapon that might be to Kishâtal's liking.Pick up the club Kagûlu suggestedKishâtal is down the slope to the south-east of the forges in the war camp of Ingarûma.Kishâtal has decided to test out this last suggestion at the Orc camp of Roz Káskrauz, located to the east of the war camp.Defeat Orcs alongside Kishâtal at Roz Káskrauz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Kishâtal has returned to the war camp of Ingarûma.Talk to Kishâtal at the war camp of IngarûmaKagûlu the Armsman is by the forges in the war camp of Ingarûma.Talk to Kagûlu the Armsman in the war camp of Ingarûma'Will you return to Kagûlu the Armsman and ask him if he has any other ideas? I know in my heart that if I attempt to use the axe or the spear on behalf of Shâra Mizâdi, I will serve her less well and endanger her conquest! What then will Aradír the Overseer have to say? I shudder to think of it!''Will you return to Kagûlu the Armsman and ask him if he has any other ideas? I know in my heart that if I attempt to use the axe or the spear on behalf of Shâra Mizâdi, I will serve her less well and endanger her conquest! What then will Aradír the Overseer have to say? I shudder to think of it!''I see from your expression that Kishâtal liked neither the axe nor the spear. That will not be a problem, for I have had another idea. There is one more type of weapon I would have him try.

'I speak of the heavy club. I left one leaning against the bench there. Bring it to him and suggest he use it.''I left a heavy club leaning against the bench there. Bring it to Kishâtal and suggest he use it.''I left a heavy club leaning against the bench there. Bring it to Kishâtal and suggest he use it.''A heavy club? I suppose I will try it, ${PLAYER}, but I tell you that the fault lies with the durability of Kagûlu's arms!

'But I will humour him. Let us do battle with the Orcs that dwell at Roz Káskrauz to the east, and I will see if this club is more to my liking.''Let us do battle with the Orcs that dwell at Roz Káskrauz to the east, and I will see if this club is more to my liking.''This is the one, ${PLAYER}! At first I did not believe anything could replace the sword as my preferred weapon... but this heavy club has done it! It was so effective against the Orcs that I could not believe I have not used one all my life!

'Please tell Kagûlu I appreciate his help, and I will use this club from now on. He has solved this problem to my satisfaction, and now Aradír the Overseer should have no reason to complain any further!''Please tell Kagûlu I appreciate his help, and I will use this club from now on. He has solved this problem to my satisfaction, and now Aradír the Overseer should have no reason to complain any further!''Kishâtal has found his new weapon? I am pleased to hear it.

'He will need to swing that club very, very hard if he intends to break it in the same way he broke his swords. That would not be impossible, but I think he should be satisfied with this as his weapon for some time.

'And now he can stop spreading the rumour that my weapons are of low quality! Yes, I knew of his words, and they were falsehoods. I would stop at nothing to disprove them, and the heavy club was to be my next and final option. Either he would wield it, or I would knock him upon the head with it!

'It is for the best it did not come to that, I think.'Numûru has a secret and delicate task for you - to help him gather flowers and fashion a necklace for Mizâdi.Gather flowers matching Numûru's description from the countryside south of Hanamíku.Gather flowers south of Hanamíku (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with the jeweller Kutímu about fashioning a necklace from the stone Numûru gave you. Kutímu can be found within Hanamíku.Speak with the jeweller Kutímu in HanamíkuPick up drying fish to feed to cats outside of Kutímu's house. Kutímu's house can be found south of Hanamíku, near Kirzâmur.Pick up drying fish near Kutímu's house (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Feed Kutímu's cats outside of his house near Kirzâmur.Feed Kutímu's cats outside of his house (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak once more with the jeweller Kutímu now that all his cats have been fed. Kutímu can be found within Hanamíku.Speak with the jeweller Kutímu in HanamíkuSpeak with Numûru in Hanamíku. Hanamíku can be found in Pahar Hatokáli, within Mûr Ghala.'I have a somewhat delicate task, my friend. I was hoping for your aid.' Numûru's voice drops to a hushed whisper.

'I know not how to say this, but as you may have guessed, my heart flutters for Mizâdi. I wonder if you would help me express how I feel to her.' Numûru gently opens his fist to show a gemstone of some beauty.

'Would you help me fashion a necklace for this gemstone, and collect some of Mizâdi's favourite flowers? I have seen some growing south of here, near the farm.

'Oh, and ${PLAYER}? This is to be absolutely secret. I trust you to not breathe a word of this to anyone, you understand?''Thank you, my friend. I trust you to keep this secret. Not on your life do you tell Mizâdi, understand?''Yes, what is it?

'Well that is quite the gemstone, rare to see one of such quality in these parts. Your mysterious friend wants a necklace, you say? I can fashion one for him, but it will take me the better part of the afternoon.

'But my cats would go hungry. That just won't do! I live near Kirzâmur to the south. Feed my cats for me, and I will make this necklace for your friend.''Too many cats?! I've never heard such an absurd concept. I'm looking to adopt more, actually, if you know of anyone looking to give any kittens away.

'Anyway, your necklace is ready for your friend. Now, if you'll excuse me, I need to see about getting some fresh fish from the local fisherman before I have an adorable mutiny on my hands.'Defeat many fell Orcs in the fallow marshes of Adagím.Defeat many Orcs within Adagím.Defeat many Orcs within AdagímDefeat a great many fell Orcs in the fallow marshes of Adagím.Defeat many Orcs within Adagím.Defeat a great many Orcs in Adagím.Defeat a great many Orcs in AdagímDefeat many Orcs throughout Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many Orcs throughout Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many Orcs in Hatokáli FellsDefeat a great many Orcs in Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many Orcs in Hatokáli Fells.Defeat a great many Orcs in Hatokáli Fells.Defeat a great many Orcs in Hatokáli FellsSlay many Orkish foes throughout Mûr Ghala.Slay many Orkish foes throughout Mûr Ghala.Complete Orc-bane of Adagím (Advanced)Complete Utûgi-bane of An Shêru (Advanced)Complete Utûgi-bane of Idagâl (Advanced)Defeat many Ordâkhai throughout An Shêru.Defeat many Ordâkhai throughout An Shêru.Defeat many Ordâkhai throughout An ShêruDefeat a great many Ordâkhai throughout An Shêru.Defeat many Ordâkhai throughout An Shêru.Defeat a great many Ordâkhai in An Shêru.Defeat a great many Ordâkhai in An ShêruDefeat many Ordâkhai in Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many Ordâkhai in Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many Ordâkhai in Pahar HatokáliDefeat a great many Ordâkhai in Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many Ordâkhai in Hatokáli Fells.Defeat a great many Ordâkhai in Hatokáli Fells.Defeat a great many Ordâkhai in Hatokáli FellsDefeat many Ordâkhai in Emax Dûl and throughout Idagâl.Defeat many Ordâkhai in Emax Dûl and throughout Idagâl.Defeat many Ordâkhai in IdagâlDefeat a great many Ordâkhai in Emax Dûl and throughout Idagâl.Defeat many Ordâkhai throughout Idagâl.Defeat a great many Ordâkhai in Idagâl.Defeat a great many Ordâkhai in IdagâlDefeat many Ordâkhai in Zajâna and throughout Kighân.Defeat many Ordâkhai throughout Kighân.Defeat many Ordâkhai throughout KighânDefeat a great many Ordâkhai in Zajâna and throughout Kighân.Defeat many Ordâkhai throughout Kighân.Defeat a great many Ordâkhai in Kighân.Defeat a great many Ordâkhai in KighânThe Utûgi have been found in Emax Dûl, ensuring the will of their masters is completed.The Utûgi have arrived to regain control of Emax Dûl for their Thardúth masters.

You should defeat the Utûgi and their captain, Achárbam, the Blood-hand, in Emax Dûl.Defeat Utûgi in Emax Dûl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Achárbam, the Blood-handThe Utûgi's efforts in Emax Dûl have been disrupted.

You should return to Razâl at Nashûbu.Talk to Razâl'The Utûgi have been spotted in the streets of Emax Dûl! The Elder Orcs must have come to try to ensure the Thardúth's will is enacted. In this case, that must mean keeping the city under Ordâkhai control!

'They seem to have set up a stronghold on the south side of the city, near the great temple. See what you can do to keep their power in check!''You have cleared the Utûgi from the city? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. That is one fewer foe attempting to thwart our war-effort! I have a feeling that this is not the last we have seen of those cursed things, however....'You must rescue Kotráka Saiya's children from inside Emax Dûl before she will show Mizâdi the secret way into the city.To safely enter Emax Dûl, you must be escorted across the bridge by Kotráka Saiya.

You should talk to Kotráka Saiya at the bridge-fort when you are ready to go.Talk to Kotráka Saiya to be escorted to the palaceYou have arrived inside the palace.

You should talk to Kotráka Saiya.Talk to Kotráka SaiyaYou need to secure the safety of Kotráka Saiya's family by getting them out of the palace.

You should find Kotráka Saiya's three daughters and son, Otibúk and speak to loyal guards nearby.Secure Lokóya and AdúriSecure OtibúkFind Khêjiba in the girls' bedroomYou need to secure the safety of Kotráka Saiya's family by getting them out of the palace.

You should find Khêjiba somewhere in the palace royal quarters.Find KhêjibaKotráka Saiya's sister, Barkhuráni, will not allow her to leave with the children.

You should defeat Dark Priestess Barkhuráni.Talk to Dark Priestess BarkhurániKotráka Saiya's sister, Barkhuráni, will not allow her to leave with the children.

You should defeat Dark Priestess Barkhuráni.Defeat Dark Priestess BarkhurániYou have secured the safety of the royal family.

You should talk to Kotráka Saiya.Talk to Kotráka SaiyaYou have secured the safety of the royal family.

You should return to the entrance of the royal quarters and speak to the servant standing by.Return to the entrance of the royal quartersKotráka Saiya will now hold up her end of the deal and show you the secret way into the city.

You should speak to Kotráka Saiya and meet up with your allies.Talk to Kotráka SaiyaMizâdi has set up camp at the secret entrance to the city.

You should talk to Mizâdi at Nashûbu.Talk to Mizâdi'For our plan to work, Kotráka Saiya must show us the secret way inside the city. She will only do this if we secure her children.

'You will enter the palace with the princess and her guards, find her family, and get them out. Since the Ordâkhai do not yet know we have taken the bridge, you should be able to cross as part of her entourage and enter the city. I am sorry to place you in such peril, ${PLAYER}, but she requested that you be the one to join her.

'Do not attempt to cross without her accompaniment! The Ordâkhai archers will surely shoot you from the far side of the bridge.''We have arrived. We must find my children and get them out, before anything happens to them.

'Help me with this, and I will show you the secret way into the city. You have my word.''Come with me. You will enter the palace as my personal guest. I know not how much resistance we will face inside.''Some of the palace guards are still loyal to me, but not all. We must tread carefully until my children are safe!

'My three daughters should be in their bed-chamber, or nearby, but I am most worried for my son, Otibúk. He is still bed-ridden, and we will need the guards' help to carry him to safety.''My Saiya! We have done as you asked and kept only those loyal to you stationed near your children. Some of the other guards have attempted to enter, but we have so far kept them away. Khêjiba ran off when we tried to keep her here, however. Please forgive me, your highness.'

Kotráka Saiya tells the guard to safely escort her daughters to the entrance.

'As you wish! We will do so when it is safe.''My Saiya! We have kept your son secure. However, something is amiss among the guards. I believe those loyal to your sister are attempting to gain control of the royal quarters!'

Kotráka Saiya tells the guard to move her son to a safe location when they can.

'As you wish, your highness. We will move him when we can safely do so unseen.''Mother? What is happening? The guards are being strange and saying I can't leave.'

Kotráka Saiya tells her daughter that she should listen to the guard, and he will help her leave the palace.

'Leave? No! Why do we have to leave?''Are you here to take the children, ${CLASS}? What lies have you spread to convince my sister to abandon her empire, husband, and sister?''We have done what we can. I trust my people to get my children to safety. Let us return to the entrance. I now must keep my end of the deal.''My servant will go and show your allies the way to the secret caves. She can move more quickly through the city than we can. They will have arrived before us, most likely.

'Come, let us leave this place, before my sister or her guards find us.''As I thought, your people have arrived before us. Now that we are out of danger, I am beginning to feel the weight of my decision. My children are safe, but I have lost my husband and my sister both....

'I will work with Shâra Mizâdi to disappear somewhere with my family for a time. I cannot bring myself to wish you luck in a war against my own husband, but I do hope we meet again, ${PLAYER}. I owe you a debt of gratitude.''The royal family is secure. I swear this oath: with us they will be safe! Kotráka Saiya will be allowed to choose her own fate following this bloody war.

'Now, we have everything we need to prevail.''My Saiya, everything has been arranged.'

Kotráka Saiya tells the servant to go to Mizâdi and share the location of the secret entrance to the city.

'At once, your highness. I will go with haste!''Are you here to take the children, ${CLASS}? What lies have you spread to convince my sister to abandon her empire, husband, and sister?'Collect a water bucketDefeat the wood-trollsReturn to the water bucketsCollect another water bucketDefeat the wood-trollsReturn to the water bucketsCollect another water bucketDefeat the wood-trollsTalk to Bhôd-buri-MêjTalk to Meldir in Dhol TêgThe ancient crypts of Pagru-kirít were built for Kishâsu the Knowing below his great tower in the second age. Sudûgul now plans to use the corpses filling the crypts to raise an army of the Dead for Bârshud. We must catch him and put an end to this!Defeat Kishâsu's Risen within Pagru-kirít, The Garden of CorpsesDefeat Kishâsu's Risen within Pagru-kirít, The Garden of CorpsesThe ancient crypts of Pagru-kirít were built for Kishâsu the Knowing below his great tower in the second age. Sudûgul now plans to use the corpses filling the crypts to raise an army of the Dead for Bârshud. We must catch him and put an end to this!Sudûgul plans to raise an army of the Dead for Bârshud.

