You must enter the garden and stop him.Defeat Kishâsu the KnowingDefeat Khardâmu Blood-swornDefeat UshkudâshThe ancient crypts of Pagru-kirít were built for Kishâsu the Knowing below his great tower in the second age. Sudûgul now plans to use the corpses filling the crypts to raise an army of the Dead for Bârshud. We must catch him and put an end to this!Complete Pagru-kirít, The Garden of Corpses -- Tier 3The ancient crypts of Pagru-kirít were built for Kishâsu the Knowing below his great tower in the second age. Sudûgul now plans to use the corpses filling the crypts to raise an army of the Dead for Bârshud. We must catch him and put an end to this!Complete Pagru-kirít, The Garden of Corpses -- Tier 3Two armies descended upon Hanamíku in recent days, one led by Bârshud and one commanded by Mizâdi.Swords and bags dropped by fleeing soldiers can be found on the road south of the village of Hanamíku.Collect discarded swords south of Hanamíku (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect discarded bags south of Hanamíku (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})The Hamâti soldier Urbâru cradles his wounded arm south of the village of Hanamíku.Talk to Urbâru by the road south of HanamíkuAlgarâsh stands by the southern entrance to the village of Hanamíku.'Hold a moment, friend. Know you of the danger that has come to Pahar Hatokáli in recent days?

'These are the hills upon the southern slope of Mûr Ghala, the Ridge of Plenty, and they descend to the Hatokáli River. These were quiet lands for some time, but two armies have of late trespassed upon the fells! Soldiers of Ordâkh hastened from Emax Dûl and trampled through our village on their way south. They pillaged what they could, and I understand they did great harm to Ebnûr's farm just across the way.

'But these soldiers had not the time for leisure! They were pursued by a second army, this one claiming to fight on behalf of Hamât; its leader has taken up residence for now in Hanamíku. They clashed with the Ordâkhai on the road just to the south, leaving weapons and bags scattered behind them. Collect them, if you will, and see if you might learn more of the conflict between these two armies.''The Ordâkhai soldiers were pursued by a second army, this one claiming to fight on behalf of Hamât; its leader has taken up residence for now in Hanamíku. They clashed on the road just to the south, leaving weapons and bags scattered behind them. Collect them, if you will, and see if you might learn more of the conflict between these two armies.''The Ordâkhai soldiers were pursued by a second army, this one claiming to fight on behalf of Hamât; its leader has taken up residence for now in Hanamíku. They clashed on the road just to the south, leaving weapons and bags scattered behind them. Collect them, if you will, and see if you might learn more of the conflict between these two armies.''You are no stranger to me, traveller. I have seen you in conversation with Shâra Mizâdi, and know you for a friend of Renewed Hamât. We have pursued Bârshud's forces here to the southern slope of Mûr Ghala, but he will escape no further! He cannot cross the Hatokáli River at speed, and if we maintain the pursuit we will pin him between our swords and the rushing waters!

'I sustained an injury to my sword-arm as we caught the retreating Ordâkhai just outside the village, but once I have spoken with Dunaïl and obtained a bandage, I will be ready once again to fight! No, do not trouble yourself. I will get it myself. You should aid the people of the nearby village, for we are quite occupied with the Ordâkhai and have not the time to slow down and aid them with anything else!''You should aid the people of the nearby village. We are quite occupied with the Ordâkhai!''Thank you for these, my friend. It has been some time since we have had need of swords, but there has been an increase of bandit activity in the hills, and if these Hamâti soldiers are unable to defeat the Ordâkhai...

'Well, I shall not dwell upon it. The people of Hanamíku are made of stern stuff, and will not wilt in the sun as might some others! We will fight, if we are called upon to do so. I see it is the same with you.'Adagím struggles to survive against ancient threats and new, and you are called to assist the people with its continued defence.Complete the continuing daily and weekly quests to assist the people of Adagím.Complete the quest Daily: Aiding a Gentle HarvestComplete the quest Daily: Managing the LandComplete the quest Daily: Pillagers in the MistComplete the quest Daily: Taken in the NightComplete the quest Daily: Waste Not...Complete the quest Daily: Woven in the RotComplete the quest Daily: ...Want NotComplete the quest Daily: Spare Them from Their FateComplete the quest Daily: The Blight-keepersComplete the quest Daily: The Blight-fungusComplete the quest Daily: Assessing the BlightComplete the quest Weekly: The Scourge of AdagímAn Shêru awakens from a long slumber and her people strive to rejoin the world. You are called to assist them.Complete the continuing daily and weekly quests to assist the people of An Shêru.Complete the quest Daily: Keeping Up with the GrindComplete the quest Daily: Acid for Acquiring AssetsComplete the quest Daily: A Threat from Ancient TimesComplete the quest Daily: Restore the Barricade of LightComplete the quest Daily: More Iron from AboveComplete the quest Daily: More Wood for TradeComplete the quest Daily: Keeping Up InspectionsComplete the quest Daily: Polishing Crystals to Send BelowComplete the quest Weekly: The Terror of An ShêruIdagâl is the setting of a battle for the heart of Harad, and you are called to assist in defending the land.Complete the continuing daily and weekly quests to assist the people of Idagâl.Complete the quest Daily: Keep Quiet the Anguished WindComplete the quest Daily: Finding More of the FlockComplete the quest Daily: Coercive RecruitmentComplete the quest Daily: Gathering More FruitComplete the quest Daily: Collecting the Treasures of NísakaComplete the quest Daily: Controlling the Drake PopulationComplete the quest Daily: Staving Off InfestationComplete the quest Daily: Sweep the Streets for StragglersComplete the quest Daily: Menace Among MenComplete the quest Weekly: The Malevolence of IdagâlKighân desires to rebuild their ancient glory, and you are called to assist the people with its restoration.Complete the continuing daily and weekly quests to assist the people of Kighân.Complete the quest Daily: A Kit for Rune-readingComplete the quest Daily: The Keys to Our PastComplete the quest Daily: More Nakhód JúraComplete the quest Daily: Taking the Fight to ThemComplete the quest Daily: Recovering RelicsComplete the quest Daily: The Cure Among the TyrantsComplete the quest Daily: Continuing Care and FeedingComplete the quest Daily: An Even Stickier HarvestComplete the quest Daily: Continuing to Stem the Blighted TideComplete the quest Daily: Lay Them to RestComplete the quest Daily: Respect for the DeadComplete the quest Weekly: The Curse on Kighân<rgb=#FF0000>Kneel</rgb> to remain hiddenObserve the WargsContinue east to Khel WeroTalk to Bhôd-buri-Mêj at Khel WeroNumûru has gotten swept up in the idea of a party to raise morale for both the citizens of Hanamíku and the Subuzûri, and asks you to aid him.Speak with Ishumâni, the skilled woodworker within Hanamíku.Speak with Ishumâni, the skilled woodworker within HanamíkuGather cords of wood and young saplings to replenish the woodworker Ishumâni's stock of wood. Fresh wood can be found near Kirzâmur, south of Hanamíku.Gather cords of wood (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Gather young saplings (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Ishumâni, the skilled woodworker within Hanamíku with your freshly gathered supplies.Help construct the new wooden supports and dance stage within Hanamíku.Build wooden supports in Hanamíku (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Build a dance stage in HanamíkuSpeak with Numûru in Hanamíku. Hanamíku can be found in Pahar Hatokáli, within Mûr Ghala.Speak with Numûru in Hanamíku'We are almost ready for the feast! Just a few more things to do.

'Ishumâni, one of the local woodworkers, came to me concerned because some of the wooden supports holding up the buildings of Hanamíku have burned out and need to be replaced.

'Just as importantly, we need a dance stage for outdoor guests if we are to have a proper feast!

'I spoke with Ishumâni. She is willing to help provide wooden planks and support pieces for both projects. Will you speak with her?''Yes, I think that's done it! Looks quite a bit better than before.

'I believe we are finally ready for the feast!''You are seeking wooden supports and planks for a dance stage? Yes, I spoke with Numûru about this. I have what I need here, but it will require most of my stock to do so.

'If you are willing to replenish my stock by gathering it out in the wilds, I will work on those supports and planks whilst you are away. There should be some in the scrub woods to the west of Hanamíku.''Excellent, excellent! Here are the planks you need, and the wooden beams.

'Please no, I do not require payment. I have slept soundly each night because of Mizâdi's presence, and that of her forces. That is payment enough.'Hulâda has decided what should be done with the blade that has now become his property.Kagûlu the Armsman is by the forge in the war camp of Ingarûma.Chief Provisioner Dunaïl stands by his tent in the war camp of Ingarûma, and will have the cloth Kagûlu requested.

Fallen branches to stoke the flames can be collected by the trees on the sloping path out of the war camp, to the north of the forges, but Kagûlu warned you to exercise patience and not jump down the cliff.Collect fallen branches from the base of trees on the sloping path out of the war camp (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Talk to Chief Provisioner Dunaïl in the war camp of IngarûmaKagûlu the Armsman is by the forge in the war camp of Ingarûma.Talk to Kagûlu the Armsman in the war camp of IngarûmaYou should stoke the fires of the forges at Ingarûma.Having stoked the fires of the forges at Ingarûma, you now have only to wait.Heat billows from the forgeHulâda has come to the forges at the war camp of Ingarûma.Talk to Hulâda at the war camp of IngarûmaKagûlu the Armsman is by the forges of the war camp of Ingarûma.Talk to Kagûlu the Armsman at the war camp of Ingarûma'The sword belongs to me now? Then I say it should go to Kagûlu the Armsman so he can give it to another soldier in Shâra Mizâdi's army. It is too painful a reminder to me of my cousin Hulûrmakh for me to wield it.

'Bring it to Kagûlu so it can be put to better use. If it belongs to me now then I can determine what is done with it... and I want it not.''Bring the sword to Kagûlu so it can be put to better use. If it belongs to me now then I can determine what is done with it... and I want it not.''Hulâda did not want the sword? Hmm.'

You tell the armsman that Hulâda thinks the sword should be given to another soldier in Mizâdi's army. Kagûlu strokes his beard.

'Ugu-muhatap-zamânya may have been a name above this blade's station, but it has already seen much service in war. I think it will not last much longer as it is. The only use to which I would put it now is to melt it down and make of it a new weapon.

'That will require hotter flames. Fetch me some fallen branches from near the trees that grow on the sloping path out of Ingarûma. I caution you to use patience and take the long way down! Do not jump down the cliff!

'I will also need a cloth with which to clean the blade. I am sure Chief Provisioner Dunaïl will have one I can use, if you ask him.''I am waiting for these items. Take your time.

'Fetch me some fallen branches from near the trees that grow on the sloping path out of Ingarûma. I caution you to use patience and take the long way down! Do not jump down the cliff!

'I will also need a cloth with which to clean the blade. I am sure Chief Provisioner Dunaïl will have one I can use, if you ask him.''How can I help you?

'A clean cloth? Yes, of course. I have one right here.''You have brought me the items I requested?

'Very good. Now stoke the flames and we will get this process underway.''Stoke the flames and we will begin the process.''What have we here?''I have changed my mind, ${PLAYER}! I would like to keep the sword as a memento of my cousin. I do not wish to wield it... but I want to keep it all the same.

'Silly name and all. Is that odd?'

You assure Hulâda that it is perfectly reasonable, and he thanks you for your words.'I am not surprised by this turn of events. After all, I gave you some extra chores for this very reason: I suspected Hulâda might change his mind and desire to keep the sword. I thought it would be wise to delay its destruction for awhile, in the event I was correct. And I was!

'I think Ugu-muhatap-zamânya's days of bringing death are done, and that is probably for the best. Thank you for your part in seeing this through, ${PLAYER}.'Zalûd the Maker of Plans recognized one of the swords you took from the Ordâkhai. Did it once belong to a soldier in Mizâdi's army?Kagûlu the Armsman is by the forges in the war camp of Ingarûma.Show the familiar blade to Kagûlu the Armsman in the war camp of IngarûmaKagûlu told you to seek Hulâda, the only living relative of the blade's owner, last told to scout the zizanu nests at Ukh-bâra in the swamps to the south-east of Ingarûma.Find Hulâda somewhere near Ukh-bâra, south-east of IngarûmaHulâda stands by the edge of Ukh-bâra, the swamp-lands where the zizani make their nests in Pahar Hatokáli.Hulâda asked you to defeat the zizani at Ukh-bâra while he considers what to do with his slain cousin's sword.Defeat zizani at Ukh-bâra (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Hulâda stands by the edge of Ukh-bâra, the swamp-lands where the zizani make their nests in Pahar Hatokáli, trying to decide what to do with his slain cousin's sword.Talk to Hulâda at Ukh-bâra'I think this sword belonged to... what was his name? Hulûrmakh? Yes, that was it. I remember because he gave the sword an unusual name. If this is the same blade, there should be a small inscription somewhere....'

Zalûd squints at the flat of the blade.

'It is here, but it is too small for me to read it. Bring the blade to Kagûlu the Armsman and ask him if Hulûrmakh still lives. I suspect he does not, for a soldier of Ordâkh possessed his blade, whatever it may be called.''Bring the blade to Kagûlu the Armsman and ask him if Hulûrmakh still lives. I suspect he does not, for a soldier of Ordâkh possessed his blade, whatever it may be called.''You have something to show me?'

Kagûlu studies the weapon you recovered from one of the Ordâkhai.

'Yes, this sword belonged to one of our soldiers, a man named Hulûrmakh. He had me inscribe a name upon the blade, and I remember how difficult it was to make the name fit: Ugu-muhatap-zamânya, the death-bringer-of-enemies. Alas, it would appear from your report that his enemies gave him death first.

'His cousin fights also for Shâra Mizâdi. His name is Hulâda, and the sword now belongs to him. You should look for him by the zizanu nests at Ukh-bâra to the south-east.''His cousin fights also for Shâra Mizâdi. His name is Hulâda, and the sword now belongs to him. You should look for him by the zizanu nests at Ukh-bâra to the south-east.''Yes?''That is my cousin Hulûrmakh's blade! When they told me he fell in battle with Bârshud's forces, I never thought to see it again. Never has a weapon had so ill-fitting a name! Death-bringer-of-enemies? Poor, foolish Hulûrmakh.'

You tell Hulâda that the sword properly belongs to him now, and he snorts.

'I do not want it. Well, let me think about it. Help me complete my mission here at Ukh-bâra by thinning the numbers of zizani, and I will decide what should be done.''Help me complete my mission here at Ukh-bâra by thinning the numbers of zizani, and I will decide what should be done with my slain cousin's sword.''I have decided what is to be done with my cousin's blade.'Zalûd the Maker of Plans knows that depriving the Ordâkhai of their weapons will harm their ability to fight against Mizâdi's soldiers.Zalûd the Maker of Plans asked you to defeat Ordâkhai throughout Pahar Hatokáli and take their swords.Collect swords from Ordâkhai throughout Pahar Hatokáli (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Zalûd the Maker of Plans is in the central tent of the war camp of Ingarûma.'The Ordâkhai cannot fight if they lack weapons to wield. Take their swords from them and you will see it is so.''The Ordâkhai cannot fight if they lack weapons to wield. Take their swords from them and you will see it is so.''I told you it was so. Without swords to wield, the Ordâkhai must lose the will to fight Shâra Mizâdi.

'Wait...

'I recognize this blade you have brought to me. This is one of ours.'The robbers of Duríga prey upon the already-desperate Esh Mêkag escapees.The brigands at Duríga have stolen food from the escapees at Dur Nâgu.

You should reclaim the stolen rations and defeat the leader of the brigands, Râhasham the Exiled.Collect stolen rations (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Defeat Râhasham the ExiledYou have reclaimed the stolen rations and defeated the brigand leader.

You should return to Kâbtam in Dur Nâgu.Talk to Kâbtam'Are you here to help, or just another scavenger here to take what little we have?

'Apologies.... I should not be so quick to judge, but we are all on edge because of our lack of supplies. If you truly are here to help, you can reclaim our stolen food for us.

'The robbers camped nearby in Duríga attacked late in the night and took our packaged rations. I fear they will only return to take more if they are not stopped. Some of them looked like Ordâkhai, but they did not attempt to take us back to Esh Mêkag. Perhaps they are deserters, but they still seem to be our enemies.''These are the stolen rations.... You actually reclaimed them for us? I... do not know what to say. It has been so long since anyone showed us kindness.'Explore friendly settlements, structures, tombs, and other important points of interest in An Shêru in Mûr Ghala.Explore friendly settlements, structures, tombs, and other important points of interest in An Shêru in Mûr Ghala.Find Gadim-ûnFind Jiret-menêshFind Khanâg GurExplore friendly settlements, structures, tombs, and other important points of interest in Idagâl in Mûr Ghala.Explore friendly settlements, structures, tombs, and other important points of interest in Idagâl in Mûr Ghala.Find AhâbaFind the Dawn-wardenFind NashûbuFind Dur NâguFind the Hamâti Forward CampYou have turned over every stone, discovered every encampment, and defeated every foe in An Shêru in Mûr Ghala.Complete quests in An Shêru in Mûr Ghala.Complete Explorer of An ShêruComplete Slayer of An ShêruComplete Tales of An ShêruYou have turned over every stone, discovered every encampment, and defeated every foe in Hatokáli Fells in Mûr Ghala.Complete tasks and challenges in Hatokáli Fells in Mûr Ghala.Complete Explorer of Hatokáli FellsComplete Slayer of Hatokáli FellsComplete Tales of Hatokáli FellsYou have turned over every stone, discovered every encampment, and defeated every foe in Kighân in Mûr Ghala.Complete quests in Kighân in Mûr Ghala.Complete Explorer of KighânComplete Slayer of KighânComplete Tales of KighânYou have gone to every corner, defeated every foe, and been a champion for the peoples of Mûr Ghala.Go to every corner, defeat every foe, and be a champion for the peoples of Mûr Ghala.Complete Renewing AdagímComplete Rejuvenator of KighânComplete Rejuvenator of An ShêruComplete Renewer of IdagâlYou have turned over every stone, discovered every encampment, and defeated every foe in Idagâl in Mûr Ghala.Complete quests in Idagâl in Mûr Ghala.Complete Explorer of IdagâlComplete Slayer of IdagâlComplete Tales of IdagâlIn the forgotten caves of Hurum Kâna, a scoundrel makes his home. The self-styled brigand king, Bârlat the Bold strikes at caravans and travellers on the nearby Great Road. The Doorwards of Zajâna have tasked you with bringing Bârlat to justice. But what secrets could the caves - and Bârlat - be hiding, deep in Hurum Kâna?Complete 'The Treasure Caves of Hurum Kâna -- Tier 1'Complete 'The Treasure Caves of Hurum Kâna -- Tier 2'Complete 'The Treasure Caves of Hurum Kâna -- Tier 3'Complete 'The Treasure Caves of Hurum Kâna -- Brigands'You have turned over every stone, discovered every encampment, and defeated every foe in Adagím in Mûr Ghala.Complete quests in Adagím in Mûr Ghala.Complete Exploring AdagímComplete Slayer of AdagímComplete Tales of AdagímSorkamâl wishes to return to the royal living quarters in the palace to secure precious tomes.With Emax Dûl becoming embroiled in fighting, Sorkamâl is concerned that items of great historical value will be lost.

You should talk to Sorkamâl and complete 'Instance: Return to the Royal Quarters'.Complete 'Instance: Return to the Royal Quarters'You have retrieved what you could from the royal living quarters of the palace.

You should talk to Sorkamâl.Talk to Sorkamâl'${PLAYER}, I have another request, if you would care to join me in the battlefield.

'With the palace becoming embroiled in fighting, and a malignant entity taking over the minds of those inside, I am concerned that items of great historical value will be destroyed. Emax Dûl is truly ancient, dating back to the Nêshakari dynasties. We must act to protect any old records left inside, or they will be lost forever!''We have saved what we could, but it is impossible to save everything. I can only pray that when Shâra Mizâdi enters the palace to defeat the Sai, it will not be too heavily damaged to recover the rest.

'When this is all over, I will return to the Palace of Ekal-nêbi to ensure this precious history is preserved for future generations, and that all other remnants of the Thardúth's influence are destroyed.''Are you ready to return to the palace? We must move quickly!'Ebnûr's son Namtâru will not be truly happy until his father's most valuable possession is retrieved from the Ordâkhai who stole it.The shovel with the valuable gemstone embedded in it was taken to the Ordâkhai camp of Bolo Thúki.Retrieve Ebnûr's stolen shovel from the Ordâkhai camp of Bolo ThúkiOne of the Ordâkhai at Bolo Thúki has apparently pried the valuable gemstone from the haft of Ebnûr's shovel!One of the Ordâkhai at Bolo Thúki has apparently pried the valuable gemstone from the haft of Ebnûr's shovel! You should keep searching for it.Defeat Ordâkhai at Bolo Thúki and search for the stolen gemstoneEbnûr's son Namtâru at the farm of Kirzâmur will be pleased that you have recovered the stolen shovel and its valuable gemstone.Ebnûr wishes to speak with you now that you have returned triumphantly to Kirzâmur.'My father's prized possession was stolen by the Ordâkhai when they passed through Kirzâmur: a shovel with a valuable gemstone embedded in the haft. The gem is clear and sparkles in the light, like a diamond, and its worth is greater than all of Kirzâmur. He is too proud to ask for its return... but I am not!

'They will have carried it off to their camp to the south-east. Retrieve that shovel and perhaps then I will agree that we have been made whole... but not before then!''The Ordâkhai will have carried it off to their camp to the south-east. Retrieve that shovel and its valuable gemstone and perhaps then I will agree that we have been made whole... but not before then!''The Ordâkhai will have carried it off to their camp to the south-east. Retrieve that shovel and its valuable gemstone and perhaps then I will agree that we have been made whole... but not before then!''The Ordâkhai will have carried it off to their camp to the south-east. Retrieve that shovel and its valuable gemstone and perhaps then I will agree that we have been made whole... but not before then!''I was not certain you would be able to do it, but you did it! We are in your debt, ${PLAYER}, and can never repay you this kindness! A hundred thanks, my friend!

'See, father? Now it is as if the Ordâkhai were never here. What would you do without me? You would lose your entire fortune, that is what!''It is only a bit of glass. It is not a gemstone at all, and while it sparkles like a diamond, its true worth to me is one of memory. My wife Ayâri is many years in the ground now, but she fashioned that shovel and its incomparable decoration for me when we first came to Pahar Hatokáli and built our home here at Kirzâmur.

'Namtâru has long believed that if our fortunes run ill, we could sell that shovel and make a new start, and I have not told him otherwise. But even were it a diamond embedded in that shovel, I would not part with this gift of his mother Ayâri. It is simply too precious.

'Thank you for returning it to me, ${PLAYER}. You are truly a friend of Ebnûr, and Namtâru, and I know you would have been a friend too of Ayâri. You are welcome at Kirzâmur at any time.'Málacál has asked that you travel to the east of Sul Madásh and help her and her hunters thin the number of blighted wood-trolls that can be found.Málacál has asked that you travel to the east of Sul Madásh and help her and her hunters thin the number of blighted wood-trolls that can be found.Defeat wood-trolls east of Sul Madásh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Return to Málacál near Sul Madásh and report your success of defeating wood-trolls in eastern Adagím.Return to Málacál'${CLASS}! There are sightings of more dangerous wood-trolls in the east and they make great trophies for the guild.

'They are coveted monsters to fell. Gather allies and hunt them down.''Welcome back, ${CLASS}. I trust you return with your head held high and some felled wood-trolls under your belt?

'We are sure there will be more to hunt soon. Your efforts are seen and rewarded by the guild.'Sálunath has asked you to defeat a monstrous and dangerous wood-troll named Agáthar who can be found roaming the marshes east of Sul Madásh.Sálunath has asked you to defeat a monstrous and dangerous wood-troll named Agáthar who can be found roaming the marshes east of Sul Madásh.Defeat Agáthar the BereftReturn to Sálunath in Sul Madásh and inform her of your triumph over Agáthar the wood-troll in Adagím.Return to Sálunath in Sul Madásh'Greetings, ${CLASS}. I have a challenging task that needs to be done by a group of strong-willed adventurers like yourself.

'To the east of Sul Madásh roams a monstrous wood-troll called Agáthar. He preys on any who try and travel within his marshes. It would bring a great relief to our settlement if you can defeat this threat and allow us to further search for the cause of this blight.

'It will be a difficult fight to take such a foe down. I suggest you rally some allies if you aim to fight him instead of trying it alone.''You return. I must say that is unexpected.

'None who have challenged Agáthar before have done so. You have achieved a great feat this day.'Nazâkh has asked you to hunt the great jázga plaguing eastern Kighân known as Bloodtooth. It is recommended you fight her with a large fellowship, as Bloodtooth is quite dangerous.Nazâkh has requested your aid in defeating Bloodtooth, a great jázga who roams east of Zajâna. Nazâkh says she has been seen near the watering hole of Dân Shatagan, north-east of Zajâna.Defeat Bloodtooth and collect her mighty fangBring Bloodtooth's fang to Nazâkh in Zajâna to collect your reward.'You look like a dangerous sort. I have a dangerous job that needs doing, if you're up for a challenge.

'There is a great beast to the east of Zajâna, a jázga of enormous size. She plagues our caravans and our travellers along the Great Road. Locals have taken to calling her Bloodtooth. Some say her mouth is marked in red, though stained by nature or blood I know not.

'It would be a great boon to Kighân to see her defeated. She is quite formidable, larger and tougher than any jázga I've ever seen. It will take a sizeable group - more than a single challenger - to meet her vigour in combat.

'Will you help us see her defeated?''You did it? I thought you were marching to your death, but that tooth is the size of my fist, so it must be true.'Defeat many scorpions prowling throughout Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many scorpions prowling throughout Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many scorpions in Pahar HatokáliDefeat a great many scorpions prowling throughout Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many scorpions prowling throughout Hatokáli Fells.Defeat a great many scorpions prowling throughout Hatokáli Fells.Defeat a great many scorpions in Pahar HatokáliExplore friendly settlements, structures, tombs, and other important points of interest in Adagím in Mûr Ghala.Explore friendly settlements, structures, tombs, and other important points of interest in Adagím in Mûr Ghala.Find Sul MadáshFind LaivárthFind Sâr MarsagFind the Folly of NagakhêdiFind Tûl AmaRazâl has been out scouting again, this time looking for Bârshud's new camp and a suitable forward camp for Mizâdi. He has requested your aid in his search.Speak with Razâl in Hanamíku about scouting Bârshud and a forward camp to the south.Speak with Razâl in HanamíkuRazâl has asked you to scout various points south of Hanamíku to get the lay of the land and figure out where Bârshud may be. The first location is Roz Káskrauz, high up in the hills.Scout Roz Káskrauz for signs of BârshudRazâl has asked you to scout various points south of Hanamíku to get the lay of the land and figure out where Bârshud may be. Next is Imizíla, where Razâl suspects Bârshud to be. Imizíla is below Roz Káskrauz, to the south.Scout outside Imizíla for signs of BârshudRazâl has asked you to scout various points south of Hanamíku to get the lay of the land. Finally he asked you to scout Ingarûma as the potential site of a forward camp for Mizâdi's forces.Scout Ingarûma for camp suitabilityYou are beset by brigands! Fight them off!Fight off the marauding brigands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Speak with Razâl in Hanamíku. Hanamíku can be found in Pahar Hatokáli, within Mûr Ghala.Speak with Razâl in HanamíkuSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku'That was a delightful diversion, but now we must press our advantage. Razâl has been out scouting to the south.

'We need to move our forces further south - I believe Bârshud has moved again, and we need to be closer to his forces, for both scouting and logistical reasons. Work with Razâl to try to figure out Bârshud's location, and a good place for our new camp.''I trust Razâl's instincts. If he says that camp spot is a good one, that is word enough for me.

'Thank you again for braving danger in our service.''Yes, I believe I may know where Bârshud is. There is a fortified encampment south of here. It is an obvious defensive stronghold. Imizíla is its name.

'The locals say the Ordâkhai used to use it as a fortress - so it makes sense Bârshud would take it up once more for the Ordâkhai.

'The locals fear it - they say the Dead walk freely beneath the city, and sometimes escape, harrying and killing the living that they meet, especially at night.

'I know not the truth of these rumours, but we must scout this location, as well as the new location for our forward camp. The area is quite dangerous, and you have a sure hand. Will you help me scout these areas?''Yes, up on the hill. That will give us easy watch over both the valley and the southern fort. I think that location is ideal. Well done, ${PLAYER}.'Explore friendly settlements, structures, and other important points of interest in Kighân in Mûr Ghala.Explore friendly settlements, structures, and other important points of interest in Kighân in Mûr Ghala.Find SormedânFind Ingar-garâshFind the city of ZajânaFind Sen ChatâkFind the groves of GatúrFind Khamósh-engarFind the treasure caves of Hurum KânaFind the Court of LarinâstaFind the KalmakhílaExplore friendly settlements, structures, tombs, and other important points of interest in Pahar Hatokáli in Mûr Ghala.Explore friendly settlements, structures, tombs, and other important points of interest in Pahar Hatokáli in Mûr Ghala.Find HanamíkuFind IngarûmaFind ShûmadirFind KirzâmurFind Nar MakâruFind Sakhar KishâsyaFind Pagru-kirítFind Gates of EshkhâbulFind the Roaring HatokáliFind Khabur PâshuViznak is concerned that the Blight Lady has come to these lands. He directs you to return to Rhadrog and Faeron at Zajâna.Viznak directs you to return to Rhadrog and Faeron in Zajâna, convinced that the Blight Lady they pursue has arrived here in Adagím.Speak with Rhadrog at ZajânaAfter speaking with Rhadrog, he is resolved to seeking out Lhaereth and asks that you inform Faeron at the fountain in Zajâna.Speak with Faeron near the fountain in Zajâna'You must hurry to my bodyguards. They will want to know. They may want to help. Be quick, I will wait here and study more.

'They are still in Zajâna.''That wretched imp yet finds new ways to confound my expectations. If indeed there is truth in the rumour that Lhaereth has come, seeking to reap some vile gain from the pestilence that defiles this land, then we must learn her whereabouts with all speed. Go now—tell Faeron what has passed. I shall make ready to depart.''Our road southward has not been in vain. If the tidings prove true, then the one we have long hunted may at last be near. Let us turn our path east and press on into the very heart of the blight.'My family and I only recently arrived in Emax Dûl. Life was not so different at first, trading one palace for another, but recently something has changed. Of late I felt a growing unease, as if something was hidden from me. Two days ago, I decided it would be necessary to act, to save the lives of my children.You are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.

You should approach Góramul Sai and listen to the conversation.Eavesdrop on your husband's conversationYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.

You should talk to Góramul Sai in the banquet hall.Talk to your husbandYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.

You should hear what Dark Priestess Barkhuráni has to say to Góramul Sai.Listen to the conversationYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.

You should talk to Dark Priestess Barkhuráni in the banquet hall.Talk to your sisterYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.

You should find Otibúk in the southern bed-chamber.Check on your sonYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.

You should use Icy Glare on Ratúlko the Bloody to let him know how you feel.Use your Icy Glare on RatúlkoYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.

You should find Otibúk in the southern bed-chamber.Check on your sonYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.

You should find your daughters in the northern bed-chamber.Check on your daughtersYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.

You should find Khêjiba. She is hiding somewhere in the royal living quarters.Find Khêjiba in the central gardenYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.

You should return Khêjiba to the northern bed-chamber.Talk to LokóyaYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.

You should find Góramul Sai in your shared bed-chamber, to the rear of the living quarters.Find your husbandYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.

You should use your Diplomatic Words to convince Góramul Sai to leave.Use your Diplomatic Words to convince your husbandYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view.

You should hear Góramul Sai's response.Listen to your husband's wordsGóramulâ's eyes welled with tears. Somewhere inside, he knew he was losing the fight, both for Mûr Ghala and for his own mind.

'Kotráka... I am sorry.''I assume you overheard some of that. Mizâdi's rebels approach from the East while the upstart servants of Aradûn approach from the West. Our enemies are nearly at our doorstep. We must strike before they form an alliance and encircle Emax Dûl.

'But do not worry, I will oversee our forces and ensure we are victorious. We cannot abandon Emax Dûl. We cannot fail the Hûl. We cannot abandon Emax Dûl. We cannot fail the Hûl...'

Góramul seems momentarily entranced. He snaps back to normal when he hears someone else enter the room.I inquired as to just who this dark ally is, and why I was not made aware of an important guest in the palace before this.

'My apologies, sister! I would have thought your husband would have informed you. If he has not explained, he must not want to trouble you with it, and I would not want to displease the Sai.

'All you need to know is we have a powerful ally on our side, who will ensure a prosperous future for us and the empire.'

She flashes an innocent smile, but does not elaborate any further.Otibúk's condition is much the same. His whole body glistens with sweat, fighting both his wounds and an ever-returning fever. He occasionally thrashes in the bed, softly moaning. Is he having nightmares of the battle? I could not know, and was being consumed by my helplessness. How can a mother watch her son suffer so?My daughters should be in bed at this hour, but I noticed that my youngest, Khêjiba, was missing. I asked my eldest, Lokóya, if she knew where she was.

'She said she was bored and went to explore. I tried to stop her, but she ran off before I could block the door. I think she went to the garden. Sorry, mother. Please don't be too angry with her.'I asked Khêjiba who she was speaking to, growing increasingly concerned.

'I don't really know. We call her the Pale Lady. She talks to me sometimes.'

I was alarmed, and asked if my other daughters knew about her.

'Yes. She talks to all three of us. I've seen her staring at Otibúk before, too. Do you think she can help him?'I asked Lokóya if she knew about the Pale Lady. She turned white as a sheet at the mention of the name.

'I... Yes. I don't know what she is or what she wants. She has appeared to all of us. Aunt Barkhuráni warned us not to mention her to anyone, so I haven't....'

She starts to cry.

'Mother, I'm afraid to leave our bedroom! Can we please go back to Ordâkh?'I demanded answers. Yes, my husband is the crown prince, but something was deeply wrong, and I would not allow it to threaten my children.

'You forget yourself, Kotráka. I have everything under control.'Slay many foes in Hatokáli Fells in Mûr Ghala.Slay many foes in Hatokáli Fells in Mûr Ghala.Complete Brigand-bane of Hatokáli Fells (Advanced)Complete Kergrim-bane of Hatokáli Fells (Advanced)Complete Orc-slayer of Hatokáli Fells (Advanced)Complete Ordâkhai-bane of Hatokáli (Advanced)Complete Scorpion-slayer of Hatokáli (Advanced)Complete Snake-slayer of Hatokáli (Advanced)Complete Zizanu-slayer of Hatokáli (Advanced)Defeat many snakes throughout Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many snakes throughout Hatokáli Fells.Defeat many snakes in Pahar HatokáliDefeat a great many snakes throughout Hatokáli Fells.Defeat a great many snakes throughout Hatokáli Fells.Defeat a great many snakes throughout Hatokáli Fells.Defeat a great many snakes in Pahar HatokáliDefeat many infected spiders in the foetid fens of Adagím.Defeat many spiders in Adagím.Defeat many spiders in AdagímDefeat a great many infected spiders in the foetid fens of Adagím.Defeat many spiders in Adagím.Defeat a great many spiders in Adagím.Defeat a great many spiders in AdagímDefeat many spiders throughout Kighân.Defeat many spiders throughout Kighân.Defeat many spiders throughout KighânDefeat a great many spiders throughout Kighân.Defeat many spiders throughout Kighân.Defeat a great many spiders in Kighân.Defeat a great many spiders in KighânLakhêpi the Far-faring is in the village of Hanamíku, waiting to hear about the tales you have encountered in Pahar Hatokáli.Lakhêpi is waiting to hear a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>.Lakhêpi is waiting to hear a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>Lakhêpi is in the village of Hanamíku, where she considers the stories you have brought to her.Talk to Lakhêpi in the village of HanamíkuLakhêpi is waiting to hear a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>.Lakhêpi is waiting to hear a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>Lakhêpi is in the village of Hanamíku, where she considers the stories you have brought to her.Talk to Lakhêpi in the village of HanamíkuLakhêpi is waiting to hear a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>.Lakhêpi is waiting to hear a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>Lakhêpi is in the village of Hanamíku, where she considers the stories you have brought to her.Talk to Lakhêpi in the village of HanamíkuLakhêpi is waiting to hear a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>.Lakhêpi is waiting to hear a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>Lakhêpi is in the village of Hanamíku, where she considers the stories you have brought to her.Talk to Lakhêpi in the village of HanamíkuLakhêpi is waiting to hear a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>.Lakhêpi is waiting to hear a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>Lakhêpi is in the village of Hanamíku, where she considers the stories you have brought to her.Talk to Lakhêpi in the village of HanamíkuLakhêpi is waiting to hear a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>.Lakhêpi is waiting to hear a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>Lakhêpi is in the village of Hanamíku, where she considers the stories you have brought to her.Talk to Lakhêpi in the village of Hanamíku'I can tell by the light in your eyes that you have encountered many possible inspirations for new stories throughout Pahar Hatokáli, friend helper!

'Tell me a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>!''Tell me a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>!''He gave up the life of a soldier to make toys for children, but that life pursued him, no matter how he ran from it. In the end, he gave his life to protect the children of Hanamíku.

'A tragic end, but given the choice again I believe he would change nothing. He was a soldier, a toy-maker, and a hero.

'A story worth the telling.''Tell me a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>!''Ebnûr's son Namtâru believed his farmer father possessed a shovel with a diamond embedded in the haft? I am not certain anyone would believe this story, but I see the comic potential within, and perhaps something else: the value we give to our possessions is not always measured in coin. Indeed, they may be far more precious to us than the value for which they would sell.

'An amusing tale, and a valuable message.''Tell me a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>!''Will you say the name of the sword again? Ugu-muhatap-zamânya?'

Lakhêpi the Far-faring sighs.

'I make my living with my words, but I am never going to remember that name. I will need to change it to something else. But one thing is clear: the sword had many bearers, seven by my count, and there is a tale in there somewhere.

'Aye, seven. Hulûrmakh who lost it to the man of Ordâkh, who lost it to you, who gave it to Hulâda, who gave it back to you, who gave it to Kagûlu the Armsman, who gave it back to Hulâda.

'Hmm. Perhaps I will be able to remember the name of the sword after all!''Tell me a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>!''This man Kishâtal is a soldier? Because this story sounds to me as if you are trying to find him a wife. All I have heard is "He is so strong he breaks every sword he uses." I suppose he is handsome as well?

'It may be the kernel of a story about a comic marriage, but it will need some more work. Still I thank you for it. What else have you experienced, friend helper?''Tell me a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>!''I feel as if this story you have told me teeters right on the edge of something darker. Mohóto's deception is an interesting tale of its own... but what of the man with the beautiful face who spoke to him of the treasure in the first place?'

Lakhêpi shivers.

'I think I would not tell this story. There is something about the man no one knows that fills me with unease.''Tell me a <rgb=#00FF00>story</rgb>!''Yes, this story is the most complex of all. To the people of Pahar Hatokáli, Shâra Mizâdi is a shining figure who fights before a willing army to free them from the shackles of Ordâkh: she is a symbol of freedom.

'But she is a woman too, and one who has suffered grief and sorrows enough to cause many others to give up her mission. Yet she fights on. I cannot say if her story is a triumph or a tragedy. I wonder what she would say herself?'

Lakhêpi the Far-faring gazes at you expectantly, and you spread your arms wide: you have exhausted the stories you collected. She smiles.

'You have done well, friend helper. These stories will keep me going for many days to come, and I thank you for them, and for your friendship. In honour of that friendship, I will keep the worrying tales of Mashdagâl's ancient mind-tamperers to myself. It is the least I can do.'The story-teller Lakhêpi the Far-faring has come to Pahar Hatokáli, the Hatokáli Fells, in search of new material for her songs and tales.Lakhêpi the Far-faring asked to meet up with you outside Kakidûr, the brigand camp west of the village of Hanamíku.Meet up with Lakhêpi outside the brigand camp of KakidûrLakhêpi the Far-faring is outside the brigand camp of Kakidûr, west of the village of Hanamíku.Talk to Lakhêpi outside the brigand camp of KakidûrLakhêpi asked you to defeat brigands at their camp of Kakidûr and to pick up weapons you find lying about, all while paying attention to details that might make for interesting stories of the place.Defeat brigands at Kakidûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect abandoned Ordâkhai swords at Kakidûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Collect makeshift weapons at Kakidûr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Lakhêpi the Far-faring is outside the brigand camp of Kakidûr, west of the village of Hanamíku.'Greetings to you, adventurer. Yes, I see you for what you are: a voyager across many lands and a doer of great deeds! I am a travelling story-teller. The name Lakhêpi the Far-faring is known far and wide across Shagâna and Jarmát; she sings songs and tells tales to put food in her belly and a roof over her head. She is I, and I am her!

'But I have run into some trouble of late, for I was turned away from Emax Dûl due to some... recent unpleasantness. I need some new stories, for I have used up my supply and none will pay to hear tales they have already heard time and time again! May I hire you to help me come up with some new songs? My previous companion refused to come with me into Idagâl, and now I am without a helper.'

You agree to assist Lakhêpi as you can, and she smiles.

'Wonderful. First I would like to visit the brigand camps of which I have heard the villagers speak. They are located upon the hills to the west! Let us meet up on the slope below the lowest of the camps.''First I would like to visit the brigand camps of which I have heard the villagers speak. They are located upon the hills to the west! Let us meet up on the slope below the lowest of the camps.''Here we are!''The brigand camps sprawl across the heights above us, friend helper. No doubt there will be weapons scattered about each of these holdings, and if you bring some of them to me I will be able to learn about the history and goings-on of these brigands. You will want to face the villains yourself, of course.

'Spare no details as you go among their camps! The details make all the difference!''The brigand camps sprawl across the heights above us, friend helper. No doubt there will be weapons scattered about each of these holdings, and if you bring some of them to me I will be able to learn about the history and goings-on of these brigands. You will want to face the villains yourself, of course.

'Spare no details as you go among their camps! The details make all the difference!''Let us see what you experienced among the brigands, friend helper!'

Lakhêpi studies the weapons you recovered and listens to your account of the battles you fought.

'Very interesting, very interesting indeed! These swords are of Ordâkhai make, but so too are there weapons of more rustic bent. Also, you engaged in combat not with trained soldiers but with opponents less-skilled in battle than those of Ordâkh. These camps have changed hands in recent days. That will be a useful detail to use in my stories.'Your adventures in Pahar Hatokáli may provide sufficient material for your story-telling friend, Lakhêpi the Far-faring.You should continue to aid the people who dwell among Pahar Hatokáli, the Hatokáli Fells.Complete 'A Nose For Adventure'Your adventures in the Hatokáli Fells may provide sufficient material for Lakhêpi the Far-faring.Learn the story of a soldier who tried to leave his past behindLearn the story of a farmer's cherished possessionLearn the story of a sword changing hands seven timesLearn the story of a man too burly for his own goodLearn the story of the man no one knowsThe denizens of An Shêru have many tasks, big and small, for you to accomplish.Complete quests in An Shêru in Mûr Ghala.Complete quests in An Shêru in Mûr GhalaThe denizens of Hatokáli Fells have many tasks, big and small, for you to accomplish.Complete quests in Hatokáli Fells in Mûr Ghala.Complete quests in Hatokáli Fells in Mûr GhalaThe denizens of Idagâl have many tasks, big and small, for you to accomplish.Complete quests in Idagâl in Mûr Ghala.Complete quests in Idagâl in Mûr Ghala.The peoples of Mûr Ghala have many tasks, big and small, for you to help them accomplish.Complete quests in Mûr Ghala.Complete quests in Adagím in Mûr Ghala.Complete quests in Kighân in Mûr Ghala.Complete quests in An Shêru in Mûr Ghala.Complete quests in Idagâl in Mûr Ghala.Defeat many Tarsâri in the Blade-horn and throughout Kighân.Defeat many Tarsâri throughout Kighân.Defeat many Tarsâri throughout KighânDefeat a great many Tarsâri in the Blade-horn and throughout Kighân.Defeat many Tarsâri throughout Kighân.Defeat a great many Tarsâri in Kighân.Defeat a great many Tarsâri in KighânThe Têtikir have posted a task to collect blood-coated axes. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire blood-coated axes for the Têtikir.Wanted: blood-coated axes from Draugardh. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: blood-coated axes from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Têtikir have posted a task to collect blood-soaked claws. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire blood-soaked claws for the Têtikir.Wanted: blood-soaked claws from Draugardh. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: blood-soaked claws from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Têtikir have posted a task to collect blood-stained hides. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire blood-stained hides for the Têtikir.Wanted: blood-stained hides from Draugardh. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: blood-stained hides from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Têtikir have posted a task to collect bloody goo. This can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire bloody goo for the Têtikir.Wanted: bloody goo from Draugardh. Gather it to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: bloody goo from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Têtikir have posted a task to collect deformed ears. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire deformed ears for the Têtikir.Wanted: deformed ears from Draugardh. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: deformed ears from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.The Têtikir have posted a task to collect wind-cracked sword sheaths. These can be turned in for a reward.You have accepted a task to acquire wind-cracked sword sheaths for the Têtikir.Wanted: wind-cracked sword sheaths from Draugardh. Gather them to earn a reward suitable for collectors.Wanted: wind-cracked sword sheaths from Draugardh.You have turned in a stack of trophies for a modest reward suitable for a collector such as yourself.Defeat Draugrim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Talk to Meldir at Dhol TêgTalk to Mêj-dhug-MêjThe herbalist Unûza has asked for your help picking reeds from the shoreline she can weave into bandages for Mizâdi's soldiers.The reeds Unûza requires can be found along the shoreline of the Hatokáli River.Collect shoreline reeds for Unûza (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Unûza is not far from the river in south-west Pahar Hatokáli.Chief Provisioner Dunaïl stands by his tent in the war camp of Ingarûma, and will appreciate the bandages.'Greetings, traveller. I know you for a friend of Shâra Mizâdi, for I have seen you from afar.

'My name is Unûza, and I am an herbalist from Urmâkh. Yes, I am a long way from home, but for Shâra Mizâdi I would travel even further! I have come to the banks of the Hatokáli River to pick reeds I can weave into bandages for the army. Will you help me? I find the work goes faster with more helping hands.''I have come to the banks of the Hatokáli River to pick reeds I can weave into bandages for the army. Will you help me? I find the work goes faster with more helping hands.''While you picked those reeds, I have finished weaving another batch of bandages. See how efficiently the work progresses?

'Can I ask you to bring the bandages I have finished to Chief Provisioner Dunaïl in the war camp of Ingarûma? That way I will not need to stop my weaving just yet.''Can I ask you to bring the bandages I have finished to Chief Provisioner Dunaïl in the war camp of Ingarûma? That way I will not need to stop my weaving just yet.''More bandages from Unûza? Very good, ${PLAYER}! This delivery is well-timed, for I have found that injuries from the many clashes with Bârshud's forces threaten to outpace the speed with which I can replace the needed bandages!

'So long as Unûza keeps weaving, we will keep ahead of the demand! Thank you for doing your part as well, ${PLAYER}.'Doorward Azagâya has requested your aid in defeating a self-styled brigand king, Barlat the Bold. He makes his home in the caves of Hurum Kâna.Speak with Katâl outside the caves of Hurum Kâna. Hurum Kâna can be found in Kighân to the north of Zajâna, just off the Great Road.Speak with Katâl outside Hurum Kâna'There is a brigand on the Great Road, one self-styled brigand king, that I would have words with you about.

'He calls himself Bârlat the bold, 'Brigand King of Hurum Kâna'. He has claimed the areas south and west of Zajâna as his 'kingdom'. He has been harassing and attacking travellers on the road for supposed taxes. This obviously cannot be allowed to continue. He is little more than an organized ruffian, despite his delusions of grandeur.

'There is a merchant who frequently travels through that area, Katâl, who has asked for our aid in defeating this Bârlat and bringing peace to the Great Road. 

'Will you meet with Katâl?''Yes, I know of this Bârlat. Quickly, quickly, off the road and I would have words with you.'Some of the Ordâkhai cravenly fled west of the village of Hanamíku, and hide now upon the hillside.Craven Ordâkhai hide upon the hillside west of the village of Hanamíku. Napísh believes you might frighten some of them from hiding if you shake some of the bushes in which they hide.Defeat craven Ordâkhai on the hillside west of the village of Hanamíku (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})Napísh stands by the western entrance to the village of Hanamíku.Talk to Napísh by the western entrance to the village of Hanamíku'Ordâkhai soldiers streamed through the village. I saw many of them looking behind them with expressions of great fear, and they stumbled over their feet. Later I learned what pursued them: another army, this one led by a woman they name the Shâra of Renewed Hamât. She brought great strength of arms to bear against the Ordâkhai, and they feared to face her warriors.

'But in their fright some of these cravens looked not where they were going, and failed to follow the great bulk of their retreating fellows! These few stumbled west out of the village, instead of south, and now they hide among the bushes on the western slope. I ask you to find and defeat these craven Ordâkhai, for if they regain their courage after Shâra Mizâdi has moved on with her army, they may threaten Hanamíku.

'You will find them upon the hillside to the west. If you shake some of the bushes in which they hide, you may frighten more of them from hiding!''You will find these cravens upon the hillside to the west. If you shake some of the bushes in which they hide, you may frighten more of them from hiding!''I am impressed you dealt with the craven ones so easily! They will not now threaten the safety of Hanamíku, and for that I am grateful!

'I can tell you have faced greater dangers than these Ordâkhai, but I am glad you have done this on behalf of my village, though it little test your skills. Greater glory awaits you elsewhere, I doubt it not!'Now that you know there are Ordâkhai leaders nearby, Mizâdi asks for your aid in capturing one or both of them.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in HanamíkuGo to the outskirts of the Ordâkhai camp near Hanamíku, Bolo Thúki. Bolo Thúki can be found south-east of Hanamíku.Go to the outskirts of Bolo Thúki, the Ordâkhai encampmentDefeat the Boxer and the Dragon in Bolo Thúki, and convince one or both to return to Hanamíku.Defeat the Boxer in Bolo ThúkiDefeat the Dragon in Bolo ThúkiSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku. Hanamíku can be found in Pahar Hatokáli, which is south of Idagâl, within Mûr Ghala.Speak with Shâra Mizâdi in Hanamíku'They call the tall one the Dragon. The short one is the Boxer. They earned their names for their ferocious and merciless nature in combat.''You've captured the Dragon? That is quite the feat, my friend.

'We have much to ask - let us hope he is a talkative dragon.''The Dragon and the Boxer? Such colourful names these Bóra have.

'Yes...' Mizâdi thinks for a moment. 'We must attempt to capture one or both of these Bóra. They are our best chance of finding Bârshud and learning what he is plotting. I know you are quite skilled at infiltrating the Ordakhai without being seen. Would you go to Bolo Thúki and attempt to convince one or both of these Bóra to aid us?'The prince has retreated into the Palace of Ekal-nêbi. He must be pursed and defeated for Mizâdi to claim victory.Mizâdi has requested your help tracking down and defeating Góramul Sai inside the palace.

You should complete 'Ekal-nêbi, the Fallen Palace' on any difficulty using the Instance Finder.Complete 'Ekal-nêbi, the Fallen Palace' on any difficultyGóramul Sai has been defeated, and Thothril the Entangler has retreated.

You should talk to Mizâdi.Talk to Mizâdi'I will lead a small force into the palace and present Góramul Sai with a choice: surrender... or die. I would like you to be a part of that force, ${PLAYER}. Gather your strongest allies, and meet me inside the threshold. We must face the prince, and learn the true identity of this... Thothril the Entangler.''We have won! The Sai lies dead, the Thardúth retreats, and Emax Dûl is finally ours! Now, I must turn my attention back to the hunt for that snake, Bârshud.

